window.FWN_KEYBOARD_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_KEYBOARD_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2701,"title":"Chapter 2701: Chapter 2653: Repaying Gratitude With Enmity","paragraphs":["Bi Linglong’s concern wasn't unfounded. Any rational politician knew what the right thing to do was. Sparing such a person and having them around was a ticking time bomb.","Zu An, as a transmigrator, knew that better than anyone. There were too many examples in history. Dorgon from the Qing dynasty had accrued tremendous power, but despite his many years of dedication, he'd still failed to conquer a woman with a child. Furthermore, he was also a regent.","Sensing Zu An’s hesitation, Bi Linglong continued with a hushed voice, “Ah Zu, I know this would make it hard for you to face Concubine Bai. You can entrust it to your subordinates and blame it on the Shadow Group and Zhao Yuan. It wouldn’t be surprising if they pulled something while you were trying to rescue the imperial grandson. Concubine Bai wouldn’t be able to blame it on you.”","Zu An shook his head. “I know you’re doing this for me, and under normal circumstances, I should heed your advice. However, I don’t have to worry about such things anymore. Others don’t have the power to threaten me. You don’t have to be too worried about it.”","Bi Linglong was taken aback. She belatedly remembered the strength he had displayed—he seemed more like a god than a mortal. Unlike the other politicians in history, he didn’t have to worry about others stabbing him in the back, as no one could threaten him anymore.","Despite knowing that, Bi Linglong remained worried. “But I still think that...”","Zu An gently grabbed her hand and said, “Linglong, I don’t want to be a cold-blooded machine of politics. If that’s how I treat Concubine Bai and her child today, won’t I do the same to the rest of you if a conflict of interest occurs in the future?”","Bi Linglong was startled. A gentle smile slowly formed on her lips. “I understand. I was too narrow-minded. You’re more like a being of flesh and blood than the others.”","Being from a major clan and selected to be the crown prince consort from a young age, she often dealt with hypocritical officials who wanted to exploit her value. Over time, she'd become a political machine that acted to prioritize her interests and constantly questioned others’ motives. It was a tiring way to live, but she hadn't thought there was anything wrong with that...","...until she met Zu An.","His unusual way of handling situations and his incredible vibrance had made her realize what it meant to be human. That was the trait that had attracted her. She hadn’t expected him to remain the same despite having grown so much.","She suddenly felt fearful. Earlier, she hadn’t realized that she had tried to change the man whom she loved so much. It was a relief that he'd held onto his beliefs.","Many people had seen her entering Zu An’s room. While there were no lack of rumors speculating her relationship with Zu An, she still felt embarrassed dwelling in the same room with him for too long. Then, it just so happened that a guard reported Concubine Bai’s request for an audience, so she took this opportunity to take her leave.","While she was heading out, she passed by Concubine Bai, and directed an amicable smile at the latter. She felt apologetic to the latter for her earlier suggestion.","Concubine Bai reflexively responded with a smile of her own. Before she entered the room, she couldn’t resist the urge to look at Bi Linglong’s departing figure. Worry flickered in her eyes. Even though the two ladies were amicable on the surface, there was bad blood between them due to their rivalry in the Eastern Palace. This seemed to be the first time Bi Linglong was taking the initiative to smile at her. Why did she smile at me? And why do I sense an apology in her gaze?","Concubine Bai had dwelled in the imperial palace for many years, and her association with the Devil Sect and the Shadow Group made her extremely sensitive to her surroundings. A thought surfaced in her mind. In truth, this worry had been on her mind all this time, but she knew Zu An and didn’t think he was such a person. But a person’s conviction can be slowly eroded by pillow talk, and my son’s birthright must be extremely troublesome for them.","Her heart was gripped by nervousness. The first thing she did upon seeing Zu An was to drop to her knees.","Zu An was dumbstruck. “Concubine Bai, what are you doing?”","Tears glimmered in Concubine Bai’s eyes. “Big brother Zu, please spare the child’s life. I’m willing to devote my life to you to repay this favor.”","She didn’t address him as the regent—she was hoping to use their ties to move him.","The women of the imperial palace can’t be underestimated. Concubine Bai must have realized the danger her child is in.","“Concubine Bai, you need not do this. I won’t make things difficult for a child.” Zu An tried to pull her up to her feet.","But Concubine Bai remained on her knees. “Big brother Zu, I’ll take my child into the mountain forest and live out our lives in seclusion. We won’t become a threat to you.” She had seen far too many broken promises in the imperial palace to believe his words.","Zu An smiled. “You don’t have to do that. It wouldn’t do for a child to live in seclusion in the mountains.”","Seeing Zu An’s refusal to budge, sorrow welled up in Concubine Bai’s heart, and tears flowed from her eyes. “Big brother Zu, I know his existence itself is a threat, but he’s my flesh and blood. I don’t know what to do either. Wuuu... ”","The tear stains on her cheeks when she first walked in had been a performance. As an elite assassin, she knew there was nothing more formidable than a woman’s tears. She knew how to use her frail appearance to her advantage to evoke a man’s desire to protect. But she was truly undergoing a mental breakdown now. She understood the severity of the matter, and she could find no reason for Zu An to spare her child. As she spoke, she lost her confidence and eventually succumbed to despair.","Seeing the weeping Concubine Bai, Zu An sighed. “You must be curious about what Linglong told me earlier.”","Concubine Bai cried even harder. She could fathom a guess, as she would have made the same suggestion had she been in Bi Linglong’s place.","“She advised me to spare you and your son. She said that I’m already powerful enough not to have to worry about the two of you. It would also settle the rebellion,” Zu An consoled her.","“Ah?” Concubine Bai was dumbstruck. She hadn’t expected her long-time rival to speak up for her.","Zu An pulled her to her feet and wiped off her tears. “We've known each other for many years. Do you seriously think I'm a vicious person?”","Concubine Bai finally believed his words. She hugged him in delight as she said, “Thank you, big brother Zu.”","Feeling her tears on his robes, Zu An knew she was letting her true emotions through. He didn’t push her aside, and instead patted her shoulder to console her.","Concubine Bai suddenly lifted her head and looked at Zu An with teary eyes. “Big brother Zu, I want to have your baby.”","Zu An was stunned. Hold on! I helped you out of goodwill, but you’re lusting over my body?"]},{"number":2702,"title":"Chapter 2702: Chapter 2654: Unexpected Request","paragraphs":["Zu An smiled awkwardly. “You don’t have to do that. I’m helping you based on our past ties and my principles. What would I be if I took advantage of your weakness to exploit you?”","“You aren’t exploiting this. I’m doing this of my own volition,” Bai Rouxue hurriedly explained. “And I’m not doing this to repay your favor either, but... but...”","Seeing her stuttering and reddened face, Zu An asked, “But what?”","Bai Rouxue mustered her courage to look at him. “For as long as I could remember, I was a tool for the Devil Sect, and I later became the Shadow Group’s Holy Maiden. My life has always been about completing the missions issued to me. I've never lived for myself before.","“I didn’t like that dumb crown prince, but I had to marry him for my mission. But he was too slow-witted to understand the affairs between a couple. Zhao Han emphasized the tradition of having the oldest son succeed the throne to curb King Qi, who was in the line of succession, but that meant the crown prince couldn’t be changed.","“However, the crown prince was too dumb to leave descendants behind. Zhao Han thought it would be better to have an intelligent imperial grandson to placate the officials, so he turned his eyes to me.”","Pain and resentment flickered across Bai Rouxue’s face. Tears began streaming down her cheeks.","Zu An sighed. “It’s over now. You don’t have to think about that anymore.”","Bai Rouxue sobbed as she continued recounting the past. “Big sister Linglong should have been the ideal choice. She was the crown prince consort, so it would grant further legitimacy to the imperial grandson if he descended from her. However, she happened to be away then...”","She laughed miserably. “Now that I think about it, she was from a noble lineage. Zhao Han would have had to think twice about her backing before making a move on her. It’s much easier to trample on people without a background like me.”","Zu An sensed the resentment in her words and said, “You must have suspected that Linglong was aware of this, or was perhaps even one of the masterminds. That must have been why you've been on bad terms all these years.”","“I dared not think that, and the matter has long passed too. There’s no point thinking about all those things.” Being a spy in the imperial palace, Bai Rouxue had always been treading on thin ice, so she dared not express her emotions lest it give her away. This was her first time venting.","“You've misunderstood her. You aren’t the only sacrifice here.” Zu An told her about how Zhao Han had planted a sliver of his soul in Zhao Ruizhi’s body so that he could possess it later, and Bi Linglong was the empress he had chosen.","Bai Rouxue was horrified. “Zhao Han, that bastard!”","Zu An fully agreed with her. “He was indeed a bastard.”","“I've misunderstood big sister Linglong for so many years!” Bai Rouxue felt ashamed of herself, especially when she thought about how Bi Linglong had spoken up for them earlier.","“Don’t think too much about it. It’s all over now. You can make peace with her from now on.” There was something Zu An was intrigued about. “If you hate Zhao Han that much, why do you still care about that child?”","Bai Rouxue revealed a wretched smile. “My life has been dark for a long time. I didn’t like the child at the start, but he was still the child I conceived after ten months of hardship. Over time, he became my pillar of emotional support. He was the reason I held on for so many years.”","Zu An understood where she was coming from. That child had been her light for many years now. She couldn’t just give up on him.","“But I have another reason to hold on now.” Bai Rouxue looked at Zu An with a reddened face. “I thought you were a special man from the first time I met you, but even so, I didn’t expect you to take such a huge risk to save me when Zhao Han sentenced me to death...”","She'd had a good impression of Zu An all along, and that incident tipped the scales. She would have long since confessed to him if not for her involvement in the Shadow Group. But after everything that had happened afterward, she had to swallow down those words.","“You and Zhao Yuan played me like a fool back then,” Zu An remarked bitterly. Zhao Yuan had confronted him several times back then, nearly bringing the matter of him harboring Bai Rouxue to light. It was only now that he realized they'd been in cahoots.","Bai Rouxue was apologetic. “Zhao Yuan planned to abandon me. He figured having the imperial grandson in his hands was enough for him. He didn’t expect you to rescue me. He decided to go along with you and play the role of a loyal subject. Zhao Han had already sensed his impending doom then, and he knew the Shadow Group Master was likely hiding in the imperial palace, so he was suspicious of everyone. Zhao Yuan’s maneuvers won him Zhao Han’s trust.”","Zu An was impressed. It was amazing that Zhao Yuan had succeeded in fooling the cunning Zhao Han, who had the world dancing in the palm of his hand then.","Bai Rouxue lowered her head sorrowfully. “Big brother Zu, you have many gorgeous women, whereas I'm a woman with a child. I know I’m beneath your notice.”","Tears streamed down her cheeks yet again. It was supposed to be a performance to evoke pity, but sadness swiftly welled up in her heart. Why didn’t I meet him first?","She and Bi Linglong had been the crown prince’s consorts, and they'd met Zu An at the same time. She had also been closer to Zu An back then. So why had he ended up together with Bi Linglong, while she landed in this plight?","She would have felt envious in the past, but now that she knew Bi Linglong had nothing to do with her fate and had spoken up on her behalf, she couldn’t bring herself to hate the latter anymore. She could only blame her harsh fate.","Zu An tried to wipe her tears, but he quickly retracted his hand when he realized it was too intimate. Instead, he said, “Don’t put yourself down. You’re gorgeous too. You and Bi Linglong are known as the capital’s two flowers.”","“But you don’t like me.” His consolation only further stoked Bai Rouxue’s sadness.","“Who says I don’t like...” Zu An blurted out, only to realize the inappropriateness of his remark. He'd intended to say he thought she was beautiful, but that didn’t sound right either.","But Bai Rouxue’s eyes lit up. “Really?”","Her hopeful eyes stifled Zu An’s explanation. He couldn’t bring himself to pop her bubble.","Bai Rouxue smiled radiantly. “Don’t worry, big brother Zu. I don’t covet a proper title. I’ll always be waiting for you. It’ll be enough for me if you visit me whenever you miss me.”","Just then, a guard reported Murong Qinghe’s arrival. Bai Rouxue took this chance to flee with a reddened face. Murong Qinghe noticed Bai Rouxue’s flustered look, which prompted her to look at Zu An with questioning eyes.","Zu An knew she was having a misunderstanding, but it was tough to explain this. So, he cleared the air with a light cough and asked, “Qinghe, do you need something from me?”","Murong Qinghe hesitated before finally gathering her courage. “Brother-in-law, can I hug you?”","Zu An was speechless."]},{"number":2703,"title":"Chapter 2703: Chapter 2655: Request","paragraphs":["“This... doesn’t seem appropriate,” Zu An replied awkwardly. Despite having once undergone the most intimate ritual, that was due to Chu Youzhao’s scheming. She was the Chu clan’s daughter-in-law, so it wouldn’t do for him to carelessly hug her.","“My request might be unusual, but I truly wish to hug you.” Murong Qinghe was already embarrassed to make that request, and insisting on it sapped all her courage dry.","A thought surfaced in Zu An’s mind. “Did you argue with Youzhao?”","He had rushed here from the capital when he sensed that Phoenix Pass was in danger, so he hadn't had time to drop by the Chu manor. As such, he hadn’t met Chu Youzhao yet and didn’t know how their relationship had progressed over the years.","“You should know why there’s a conflict between us.” Murong Qinghe was from a military clan, after all. She quickly overcame her embarrassment and regained her courage.","“It has been years since we last met, so how could I know?” Zu An could fathom a guess, but it wouldn’t be good to speculate without speaking to Chu Youzhao first.","“Is that so?” Murong Qinghe murmured before abruptly leaping into his arms to embrace him.","It was so abrupt that Zu An’s protective ki layer reflexively activated, jolting her back. He hurriedly reined in its strength, but it was still too much for her to bear. With a dull thud, Murong Qinghe spewed fresh blood. She collapsed on the floor, severely injured.","Zu An was both angry and worried. He rushed forward to circulate her ki and treat her injuries while exclaiming, “What are you doing? You would have been dead if I hadn’t held back in time.”","Instead of saying a word, Murong Qinghe took this chance to embrace him. Tears flowed down her eyes as she muttered, “It was indeed you that night...”","Zu An was stunned and awed by her intuition. She can tell just from a hug?","“I’m sorry. It was an accident...” he tried to explain, but he didn’t know how to go about it.","“I know. It’s all big brother Chu... No, it was big sister Chu’s arrangement,” Murong Qinghe replied miserably.","“You already know?” Zu An was taken aback.","“How can I not know? She might have fooled me at the start, but the truth became apparent after I was married. Besides, that night was... I didn’t think too much at the start because I was too embarrassed, but in hindsight, that couldn’t have been big brother Chu’s body.” Murong Qinghe wiped her tears. “Since then, big brother Chu has never shared a room with me. I thought he was scorning me and was heartbroken. Fortunately, big brother Chu hinted at the truth to me because he was worried I would resort to something extreme. It was only then that I realized what happened on the night of my marriage.”","“Why did you still test me earlier?” Zu An was curious.","For some reason, Murong Qinghe’s face reddened further. “Youzhao refused to tell me that man’s identity, but it wasn’t difficult to figure out what happened that night. Given my years of ties with Youzhao, I doubt she would just find anyone to take advantage of me.”","“You are the closest man to her, and you happened to be in the neighboring courtyard that night. I tried asking her if it was you that night, but she didn’t give me an answer. That’s why I needed to verify it myself.”","Zu An was intrigued. “You were able to tell with just a hug?”","Murong Qinghe’s face reddened. She turned away. “You wouldn’t know. You aren’t a woman.”","It was too embarrassing for her to say it aloud. That night had been too special for her. There was no way she could forget that sensation.","“I’m sorry. I had too much to drink that night, and I didn’t know Youzhao would do something like that,” Zu An replied apologetically.","“I know. You were a victim too, and she kept you in the dark as well.” Murong Qinghe had already figured out what the Chu clan was planning back then, so she didn’t blame him for it.","The word ‘victim’ sounded off to Zu An. Had it come from him, it would have felt as if he were complaining after taking advantage of her. He asked, “You were hurt the most in this matter. Do you hate Youzhao for it?”","“Of course I do. I hate her for being a woman and not a man.” Murong Qinghe bit her lips. “I should have known earlier. There were times when big brother Chu felt too weak to be a man, but I fancied her for her weak, scholarly disposition.”","Zu An had to concede that the Chu clan had outstanding genes. The three sisters were incredibly good-looking. Chu Youzhao, when disguised as a man, looked like a dashing gigolo. Murong Qinghe wasn’t the only woman who had fancied him then. It could have also been because Murong Qinghe had been in the military for too long and had seen too many coarse men, thus making the gentle and graceful Chu Youzhao more appealing to her.","“Now that I think about it, there were many signs. Big brother Chu asked me several times...” Murong Qinghe suddenly fell silent here.","“What did she ask?” Zu An was intrigued by her peculiar reaction.","“Nothing.”","Murong Qinghe suddenly remembered how Chu Youzhao had once asked her if she would have fallen in love with big brother Zu had she met him first. She hesitated briefly, though she chose Chu Youzhao in the end. Big brother Chu must have been confirming my feelings then.","When she thought about how much Chu Youzhao cared about her, her heart ached.","“Are the two of you on bad terms after talking it out?” Zu An han’t seen Chu Youzhao anywhere in Phoenix Pass.","“I don’t blame big brother Chu. I know she had no choice either. I only blame fate for playing such a prank on us.” Murong Qinghe sighed.","Zu An felt the same too. She’s a good person. She still thinks on Chu Youzhao’s behalf despite having such a thing happen to her.","“Big brother Zu, big brother Chu is a pitiful one too. She has to conceal her identity and live as someone else. Even her marriage was an act.”","“She is a pitiful one. But Linglong ascending to the throne will be the start of all kinsd of changes. I'll push for women's rights, so that they can inherit noble titles and assets. This way, those who face the same plight won’t have to go through the same suffering,” Zu An replied.","Murong Qinghe’s eyes lit up. “Are you doing this for big brother Chu? It looks like her feelings for you didn’t go unreciprocated.”","“Ah?” Zu An was taken aback.","“Youzhao harbors deep feelings for you as well, but she has to play the role of the Chu clan’s young master, and you’re her brother-in-law. She had no choice but to suppress her feelings,” Murong Qinghe said with a sigh. “I did think it was weird how big brother Chu was attached to you. It only made sense to me when I learned that she was a woman.”","“She might have deceived me, but after everything we've gone through, I believe our feelings for each other are real.” Murong Qinghe looked intently at Zu An. “You were the only one she would have chosen to take her place for that night, and I believe she would have rather been the one to accompany you that night.”","Zu An coughed. “I am her brother-in-law, after all.”","Murong Qinghe narrowed her eyes. “That means nothing. Sisters sharing a husband are praised. The previous emperor’s wives are from the Liu clan. Such things are also common among nobles and officials.”","“Why are you suddenly turning the topic to me?” Zu An felt awkward. “What are your plans with Youzhao?”","“We’ll just continue like that. If we part ways, her identity will be exposed. I don’t want to put big brother Chu in a difficult position. Besides, I've already said that I’ll be with her no matter what happens,” Murong Qinghe said with conviction.","It was then that she suddenly changed her tone and said, “Big brother Zu, even though that night... I hope you don’t take me for a casual woman. Don’t look for me again in the future!”","Zu An replied solemnly, “Of course!” I’m also not the kind who will casually take advantage of others.","Then, Murong Qinghe whispered with a reddened face, “But it’ll be fine if big brother Chu agrees to it.”"]},{"number":2704,"title":"Chapter 2704: Chapter 2656: This Is Improper","paragraphs":["Zu An was baffled. What do you mean, it’ll be fine if big brother Chu agrees to it?","Despite being a youngster too, he struggled to understand what was going through the heads of youths nowadays.","Shouldn’t Murong Qinghe be angry at being deceived about her marriage? She looks a bit angry, but she seems to still care for Chu Youzhao a lot. Despite knowing Chu Youzhao is a woman, she still takes her for her lover and husband.","And she’s even willing to let Chu Youzhao get together with other men?","Zu An was confused. Is my understanding of love too narrow?","Seeing Zu An’s reaction, Murong Qinghe realized how culturally shocking her earlier words were. So, she added with a whisper, “You’re an exception. I wouldn’t let big brother Chu be with anyone else.”","“I’m moved by the feelings you have for each other.” Zu An didn’t know how to reply to those words.","“These are my earnest thoughts. I haven’t even told big brother Chu about it.” Murong Qinghe bit her lips. “Brother-in-law, you mustn’t tell big brother Chu about this. I’m still feigning anger at him.”","It took a while before Zu An squeezed out an answer. “Alright.”","This little couple sure knows how to play around.","Murong Qinghe suddenly looked shy. “How much longer are you planning to embrace me, brother-in-law?”","Zu An was speechless.","He impatiently snorted, “I’m treating your injuries!”","Murong Qinghe's injuries from the earlier jolt were so severe that Zu An had only barely stabilized her condition now.","“You’ll have to rest up for the next few days. You mustn’t get into any fights. It shouldn’t take long for you to make a full recovery.” Zu An pulled her to her feet before releasing her. Her body feels young and vibrant, perhaps because she spends her days in the military.","“Thank you, brother-in-law. I was joking with you earlier, though. You can hug me all you want.” Murong Qinghe mischievously blinked at him. She seemed to be in a good mood.","“Scram.” Zu An chased her away with a huff. This lass doesn’t know she’s playing with fire. If it had been in the past, she would have been gushing after being treated by my primordial ki.","Now that Zu An had become the world’s master, he could treat her using the world laws, thus avoiding the primordial ki’s side effects.","Murong Qinghe ran outside. Her head suddenly popped back into the room as she said, “Brother-in-law, don’t forget about our secret agreement.”","Zu An’s eyelids twitched. She looked so wretched earlier that one would have thought she was living in misery all these years, but it looks like she's been enjoying herself in her way.","A smile lingered on Murong Qinghe’s lips even after leaving the room. She murmured, “My dumb brother-in-law.”","What had worried her in recent days wasn't Chu Youzhao, but who it had been that night. Even though Chu Youzhao had implicitly hinted at that person’s identity to her, she dared not believe it until she confirmed it herself. Now that she had confirmed it truly was big brother Zu, it felt as if a boulder had been lifted from her heart. She couldn’t tell if her feeling for him was love, but she wasn’t averse to it.","...","Zu An’s door suddenly opened, and a beautiful figure walked in, asking, “What secrets do you have with little Qinghe?”","Zu An raised his head to see a gorgeous, oval-shaped face. He exclaimed in delight, “Dandan!”","He rushed forth to embrace her. He'd been worried that she had met with danger, because he hadn’t seen her anywhere in Phoenix Pass. Later, he'd learned that she was in charge of transporting rations from Bi Linglong, and wasn’t in Phoenix Pass then.","“Ah Zu!” Zheng Dan hugged him tightly.","It had been three years since they last met. While she was confident in his abilities, she couldn’t stop worrying since he was marching into danger. She had woken up from nightmares countless times, after which she would solemnly pray for him. She had rushed here as soon as she received news that Phoenix Pass was in trouble, only to learn that her lover had descended like a deity and promptly dealt with the rebels. Overjoyed, she headed right over to look for him.","The two of them hugged for a long time before Zheng Dan coyly grumbled, “I can’t catch my breath.”","Zu An was startled. “Was I hugging you too tightly?”","“You’re covered in other women’s perfume.” Zheng Dan’s eyes glimmered. She leaned in and sniffed him. “I smell Linglong’s fragrance. This Hundred Flowers Fragrance smells unfamiliar, but I’m guessing it belongs to that Concubine Bai. Hm? There’s Qinghe’s scent too. Tsk tsk tsk, you’re a beast to go after your sister-in-law.”","“I’m not Giggs,” Zu An huffed. “Don’t talk nonsense. Qinghe was injured, so I was treating her earlier.”","It wouldn’t be good for him to share what had transpired between him and Murong Qinghe, lest he ruin her reputation.","“Your treatment method must have made her swoon.” Zheng Dan knew best just how potent his primordial ki was.","“I'm the world;s master now. I can avoid that side effect when treating others,” Zu An replied awkwardly.","Zheng Dan’s eyes lit up. “I heard from others about how cool you were in that battle, something about you becoming a god. Is it an ability from being this world’s master? Tell me more about it.”","She had been working hard in recent years, evident in the rapid progression of her cultivation, but there was no way she could match the growth of a monster like Zu An. This was a good chance for her to learn about the higher cultivation levels. So, Zu An embraced her and began sharing everything that happened over the past three years with her. Time passed swiftly.","Halfway through, Bi Linglong came in to report about the imperial court’s affairs, only to be quickly drawn in by his stories as well. Her eyes shimmered in excitement, making even the plum makeup between her brows look vibrant. “Compared to what you went through, my life as the empress has been boring. I wish I could have been there with you.”","“Indeed. It feels like everything we've done in the last few years was just playing house.” Zheng Dan felt the same too. She had organized the capital’s underground powers and worked with Little Qien to help Bi Linglong stabilize her position and deal with the rebels. They'd thought that they had done a lot, but compared to what Zu An had faced, it looked like a minor squabble.","“If not for your hard work, the world would have been in chaos. You shouldn’t downplay what you'be accomplished. It hasn’t been easy on you either,” Zu An replied. He had put them through a lot by entrusting everything to them.","“Hmph! I bet you left us here because you didn’t want us getting in the way of you courting other worlds' ladies!” Zheng Dan harrumphed. “I noticed you were vague when talking about the Goddess of Wu Mountain, the Mermaid Queen, and the Sun Goddess... I bet there's something between you and them!”","Bi Linglong nodded in agreement.","Zu An sweated profusely. There was no way to conceal things when someone understood him too well. It took him a long time to placate the two of them.","Bi Linglong suddenly stood up and said, “It’s getting late. I should get going. Dandan, it's been a long time since you last met Ah Zu. There must be many things you’d like to talk to him about, so I won’t impose any longer.”","Unexpectedly, Zheng Dan grabbed her hand and smiled mischievously. “Isn’t it the same for you? There must be many things you would like to say to him as well.”","“Even so, given my identity, I shouldn’t stay here for too long.” Bi Linglong had many sentiments she would like to share with Zu An, but her rational mind held her back. She was now the empress. It wouldn’t do for her to stay over in Zu An’s room under public view, or else the novels in the streets would become even more explosive.","Zheng Dan laughed. “Please! Who doesn’t know you’re the regent’s woman? Now that Ah Zu has displayed his overwhelming prowess, it wouldn’t look out of place for you to be with him. Rather, it would be weirder for you not to be here.”","Bi Linglong’s heart skipped a beat, and her face heated up. She hesitated for a moment before nodding. Then, she stared intently at Zheng Dan.","Having become close friends in recent years, Zheng Dan immediately understood her intention. She angrily lashed out, “Are you chasing me away now? That’s too much! Don’t even think about it. I’m staying here tonight as well!”","Bi Linglong’s face turned bright red. She stood up to leave. “This is improper!”"]},{"number":2705,"title":"Chapter 2705: Chapter 2657: Guilty Conscience","paragraphs":["Zheng Dan moved quickly to grab her arm. “What’s improper about this? It’s been a long time since you last met. Others will understand.”","Bi Linglong got agitated. “That’s not what I’m talking about! I’m talking about... being here with you!”","Zheng Dan’s face turned severe. “I didn’t know you looked down on me, Your Majesty. You must think that I’m not qualified to be your sister.”","Bi Linglong exclaimed, “Don’t mock me with such bitchy words. You know what I mean.”","Shortly after Zu An’s departure, the capital had been in disarray, and the Bi clan had been purged in the previous capital upheaval. While Bi Linglong did have allies, there weren’t many people she could rely on. Sang Qien and Zheng Dan had helped her a lot in recent years. One had wisdom, and the other was skilled at socializing. The two of them had helped her resolve many problems. After working together so many times, they had long become friends. With her wits, she could tell that Zheng Dan was just playing with her.","“If you don’t mean that, why don’t you want to be here with me?” Zheng Dan harrumphed.","“It’s different!” Bi Linglong felt as if she was going to be driven mad. She looked to Zu An for help. “Say something, Ah Zu!”","“I think Dandan’s words made sense,” Zu An replied with a straight face. He secretly shot Zheng Dan a thumbs up. You’re the best!","Bi Linglong was dumbstruck. She was about to explode from anger. “You two are in cahoots!”","“It’s only a matter of time before such things happen. You just have to get used to it,” Zheng Dan replied with a grin.","Bi Linglong widened her eyes in astonishment. “Hold on, you've already... tried it before?”","Zheng Dan smiled back at her without saying a word.","But Bi Linglong caught her drift. The next question that popped into her mind was with whom Zheng Dan had done it together with, only to remember how close she was with Sang Qien. And to think I thought they looked closer than sisters! I finally understand why!","She angrily glared at Zu An. You depraved man!","The maids outside waited for a long time, but the empress didn’t come out. They exchanged perplexed looks.","The empress’ personal maid was worried. Your Majesty, do you still remember your position? You mustn’t be led astray by the regent! She glared at the other restless maids and told them not to fidget around, before arranging for some of them to return first to change shifts.","Some maids were confused. Why do we need to do shifts? It’s just waiting for a couple hours.","Bi Linglong wouldn’t bring powerless maids with her to the battlefields; these people were meticulously chosen because of their ability to double as guards. Standing for a few hours was no trouble for them.","“A few hours?” the personal maid sneered. These people don’t know how ridiculous the regent’s stamina is.","It was a relief that the regent had constructed a barrier around the room to prevent any noise from getting out, or else she wouldn’t know how to deal with the situation.","Some time later, Zhang Zitong rushed back, only to be blocked at the doorway. Startled, she explained, “I have something I need to report to the regent urgently.”","“Commander Zhang, I’m afraid it’s inconvenient for the regent to meet you right now,” the personal maid replied.","Zhang Zitong recognized the empress’ personal maid and asked, “Is Her Majesty inside?”","The personal maid nodded.","Zhang Zitong immediately figured out what was happening inside, and that made her gnash her teeth. The empress pulled the rug out from under me while I was busy with official business. Indeed, all women lust for the regent’s body.","She coughed lightly before ordering, “Guard this place properly. Don’t let anyone other than the empress enter the room, or else I’ll hold you accountable!”","She was their superior, so she had the right to issue commands to them. Hmph, it’s one thing for the empress to claim the regent’s body, but I won’t allow other vixens to join in.","Her arrangement made perfect sense, making it impossible for anyone to see through her motive. Even she herself was impressed by her wits.","The maids exchanged perplexed looks. Considering that Zhang Zitong was their superior, as well as the regent’s and the empress’ aide, they secretly informed her, “The Sang clan’s young mistress is here too.”","Zhang Zitong was speechless. She stared at the room in shock. She knew how much of a vixen Zheng Dan was, but Bi Linglong had always been dignified and demure. To think that Bi Linglong would play along to Zheng Dan’s tune!","The other guards nodded in agreement. They'd been equally shocked earlier too.","Zu An had constructed a one-way sound isolation barrier to avoid being oblivious to the happenings outside, so Bi Linglong heard the conversation outside loud and clear. She angrily bit her lover’s shoulder. “It’s all your fault! How embarrassing!”","The clean reputation she'd maintained over the years had gone down the drain. She wanted nothing more than to hide in a hole right now.","Zheng Dan mischievously blew at her ear. “Who dares tease our empress? You can issue an edict to execute them.”","“The first one I’ll execute is you!” Bi Linglong exclaimed. A ghost must have possessed her to have actually chosen to stay behind!","“Big brother Zu, she’s bullying me!” Zheng Dan shook Zu An’s arm as she lodged a complaint.","Her voice was so cloying that Bi Linglong, despite being a fellow woman, shuddered. Do men like her type? Ugh, I can’t copy that even if I want to.","Zu An was in a good mood. “You can bully her back.”","“Yes, my regent.” Zheng Dan’s hands shot for Bi Linglong’s body, causing the lofty empress to squeal nonstop.","...","The following morning, the radiant sun cast its rays on Phoenix Pass. Peace had returned after yesterday’s battle, and everyone in the city seemed to radiate bliss from their faces. Quite a few people were still discussing the regent’s valiance.","Bi Linglong, who was surveying the surroundings, leaped in shock. She was afraid that someone had heard their voices last night. However, she quickly realized they were referring to Zu An’s battle with Zhao Yuan and the Shadow Group, and she breathed a sigh of relief.","It’s all that vixen Zheng Dan’s fault! I lost my dignity as an empress last night! Does she usually go that far with Sang Qien too?","Thinking about what happened yesterday made Bi Linglong blush furiously. I didn’t think there was such a side to Little Qien beneath her demure front. I should advise Ah Zu to calm down a little lest he hurt his body.","But considering her lover’s unique constitution, her worries were likely to be unfounded.","Zhang Zitong looked at Bi Linglong in admiration. Your Majesty is truly self-disciplined. She didn’t sleep a wink last night, and she could barely walk when she left the room in the early morning. Yet, she still perked herself up and insisted on doing an inspection. Is that her guilty conscience at work?"]},{"number":2706,"title":"Chapter 2706: Chapter 2658: Two Kings and Three Respects","paragraphs":["Bi Linglong had been at her limit. She'd been planning to do a quick customary check before returning to rest, lest she make a fool of herself.","But as time passed, she felt a warm surge of energy rising from her abdomen before diffusing into her limbs and marrows. Incredibly pure natural ki nourished all her meridians, causing her cells to buzz to life. Her exhaustion faded, and she even felt as if her cultivation had advanced a level. She was initially startled, but she soon realized what had happened and blushed.","Ah Zu, as the world’s master, was worthy of being called a god. The things he had in his body were probably more effective than the treasures and spirit springs that cultivators fought over.","She bit her lips. Now that there’s such a function to him too, those vixens will be sticking to him all day long. That made her jealous.","This was the first time the soldiers, who were used to Bi Linglong’s regal air, saw her coy side. Her peachy skin and her vibrant plum blossom mark complemented each other, causing many to stare at her in a daze. Even Zhang Zitong, who had been jealous the entire night, had to concede that Bi Linglong was truly beautiful. Even a woman would be mesmerized by her, let alone that philandering regent.","“Commander Zhang, have you found Concubine Bai’s son?” Bi Linglong suddenly asked while walking on the street.","“Yes. We ambushed one of the Shadow Group’s hideouts in accordance with the regent’s intelligence. The place was heavily guarded by the Shadow Group’s assassins, but the regent provided us with their defense layout. We would be unworthy of being your imperial guards if we still failed at that mission.”","Bi Linglong gestured for others to distance themselves with a wave of her hand. She looked intently at Zhang Zitong before saying, “Commander Zhang, you mentioned the regent several times in your report. I can sense your deep admiration for him. Are you fond of the regent?”","Zhang Zitong’s heart thumped furiously. Oh no, is the empress jealous? Is she going to eliminate potential rivals now?","It was normal for consorts and concubines to scheme against each other and even poison imperial offspring.","Zhang Zitong reacted fast and replied, “You have misunderstood, Your Majesty. I merely respect the regent a lot.”","“Are you certain you aren’t fond of him?” Bi Linglong assessed Zhang Zitong with an unreadable smile. “I’ll tell the regent to assign you to another post and bestow you with a marriage.”","“No!” Zhang Zitong exclaimed.","Looking at Bi Linglong’s playful gaze, she hesitantly added, “Which woman wouldn’t be fond of an unparalleled hero like the regent?”","Bi Linglong was moved by those words too. “Indeed, which woman wouldn’t be fond of him?”","Not only does Ah Zu stand at the peak of power, he is also the strongest man in the world. Most important of all, he’s so suave!","It was not just once or twice she had seen the maids secretly discussing the regent with glowing eyes. Zu An already had enough lovers; the thought of having to deal with more women who approached him with ulterior motives gave her a headache.","“Commander Zhang, I’ll assign you a mission. Make sure to protect the regent well. Don’t let women with ulterior motives get close to him.”","Zhang Zitong was momentarily stunned before her face lit up in delight. “Yes, Your Majesty!”","At the same time, she was perplexed why the empress wasn’t worried about her. The empress must have entrusted me with this mission because she sees me as one of her own. Maybe she has acknowledged that I’d eventually become one of the regent’s women. The thought of that made her excited.","Just then, Zu An’s deep, magnetic voice echoed, “Come here, Zitong.”","Zhang Zitong jolted in shock. She looked around her, but Zu An was nowhere to be found. Am I having auditory hallucinations because I’m missing him too much?","“What are you thinking? Come to the city lord manor right now!” Zu An huffed.","It was only then Zhang Zitong realized that Zu An was talking to her remotely. That awed her. The regent is truly powerful.","Noticing her astonishment, Bi Linglong asked, “What’s wrong?”","Zhang Zitong replied, “The regent has summoned me over. He probably has something to ask me.”","“It’s likely regarding Concubine Bai. I’ll head there with you.” Bi Linglong was concerned about this matter too.","Zhang Zitong couldn’t turn her down, so the two of them went to meet Zu An together.","Looking at the empress’ silhouette, Zhang Zitong chuckled under her breath. This must be a one-of-a-kind situation in history—the empress paying a visit to the regent, though I doubt anyone sees a problem in that after the previous capital upheaval and the recent battle at the Phoenix Pass.","They arrived at the city lord manor, where they saw Concubine Bai seated in the main hall, anxiously waiting for them. When she saw the two of them, she hurriedly stood up and greeted, “Paying respects to Your Majesty.” She nervously looked at Zhang Zitong, her fingers clutching tightly onto her skirt.","“You may dispense with the formalities.” Bi Linglong supported Concubine Bai upright. She happened to meet Zu An’s gaze, which instantly reminded her about what had happened last night, prompting her to avert her gaze. I wonder where Zheng Dan is...","Zu An also remembered the passionate night they'd shared, and his heart tingled. He quickly reined himself in with a cough before asking, “Zitong, how was the mission last night?”","Zhang Zitong had to hold herself back from rolling her eyes. I was going to report this matter last night, but you were busy messing around in your room. Even so, she couldn’t say those words aloud. Instead, she reported what she had just told Bi Linglong in detail.","When she learned her son was safe and sound, Concubine Bai breathed a sigh of relief.","“Take Concubine Bai to meet her child later,” Zu An instructed. “I’ll also entrust you with the concoction of their antidotes. You can go to the Embroidered Envoys and the academies.”","“Thank you, regent!” Concubine Bai was grateful.","“Since Linglong is here too, shall we discuss how we should settle them?” Zu An proposed.","“I am a sinner, so I don’t dare to hope for much. All I ask for is a small courtyard in the capital,” Concubine Bai meekly said.","Bi Linglong’s wariness soared. She wants a courtyard in the capital? That’s as good as telling Zu An to visit her whenever he can! I’d be a fool to give them a house so they could have a tryst with each other.","So, she replied with a smile, “Sister, I can’t wrong you two. You both have special standing. There are similar precedents in history. For instance, there was a system of ‘two kings and three respects’ in the ancient era. Each dynasty conferred the royalties of the previous two dynasties as nobles and granted them fiefs. Given your stature, you can pick any province of your liking, and I’ll confer it to you.”","It had become paramount to change the dynasty. After consecutive rebellions, Zu An knew better than to give the Zhao clan another chance. His kindness would only bring more conflicts to the world. After just having quelled the Zhao clan’s rebellion, his prestige was at an all-time high; few would dare to oppose him at this juncture. He was determined to clean things up for Bi Linglong before leaving this world.","Concubine Bai’s son was the successor of the previous dynasty. His young age and relationship with Concubine Bai made it easier to deal with him than the others from the Zhao clan. Bi Linglong’s proposal was thorough, having considered different aspects of the issue. Her wealth of experience in governance showed in her decision-making."]},{"number":2707,"title":"Chapter 2707: Chapter 2659: Old Ties","paragraphs":["Concubine Bai interjected, “But that’s as good as conceding that the new dynasty succeeds the Zhou Dynasty. Wouldn’t that be unfair to big brother Zu?”","“That’s true.” Bi Linglong agreed.","Zu An had saved the world from the monster invasion, and practically all powers in the world recognized him as their lord. Not even legendary emperors in human history had achieved the same height as him. He didn’t have to inherit the Zhou Dynasty’s mantle; it was beneath him to do so.","Zu An laughed. “Why would it be unfair to me? I’m not the emperor.”","Bi Linglong rolled her eyes. “Who else, other than you, is worthy of being the emperor?”","“You’re doing a good job as the empress.” Zu An shook his head. He had no interest in being the emperor. His eyes were set on the stars, the myriad worlds. Being a nation’s emperor held little significance to him.","“Not at all. It all went up in smoke within two years after you left,” Bi Linglong said with a sigh. She was proud and confident in her governing ability, but there had been many frustrations in recent years that made her realize that there was little she could do alone.","“They only acknowledge me because of you. You’re more suited to be the emperor. With the prestige you command, everyone will bow down to you willingly.”","She had ordered the Embroidered Envoys to spread news about Zu An’s immense accomplishment in driving back the monsters, building up his immense prestige among the populace. In truth, she had been preparing for this day.","“I’ll have to leave for a long time very soon. How can I be a good emperor when I can’t be present?” Zu An looked at Bi Linglong. “Linglong, you’ve already done very well. I believe that you’re a good empress. Now that I’ve cleared up all the underlying risks, you won’t have to worry about another rebellion anymore.”","Bi Linglong knew Zu An wasn’t the type to be bound to one place, and being the emperor would only be a constraint on him. She bit her lips and glanced at Concubine Bai and Zhang Zitong. After some hesitation, she asked, “Big brother Zu, have you considered how the others might feel if you make me empress? Won’t they be upset and dissatisfied?”","She was only one of his many lovers, and his other lovers were outstanding in their own right too. They could be dissatisfied with him giving so much to her. In particular, the big miss from the Chu clan. They might have separated peacefully, but she’s still his legal wife.","Furthermore, there are also other lovers whose capability and beauty don’t pale in comparison to mine. What right do I have to be the empress? What if others turn against me, and this just leads to disharmony in Ah Zu’s household?","Zu An burst into laughter. “You don’t have to worry about that. They’re cultivators, and they have their pursuits too. I’ll help them realize their dreams. Of course, Little Qien and the others can assist you with your work too.”","“But I still don’t think I’m suited...” Had it been years ago, Bi Linglong would have taken the position without hesitation. Back then, she’d prioritized her clan above all else, and she also wanted to exact her vengeance.","But now, all those things felt fleeting to her. She would rather spend her time with her lover.","Zu An interjected, “Have you not considered a bigger problem? If I become the emperor, who should become the empress?”","Concubine Bai and Zhang Zitong were taken aback. They looked at Bi Linglong with gossipy eyes. Neither of them dared harbor thoughts of becoming the empress, but would Bi Linglong, as the current empress, lower herself to be an ordinary concubine?","And if Bi Linglong wanted to be Zu An’s empress, the other ladies wouldn’t necessarily let things slip. Being the nation’s empress was one thing, but being Zu An’s empress was another matter. The latter meant being Zu An’s legal wife; the others wouldn’t give up on that position so easily.","Bi Linglong was also stunned, as she realized how tricky the situation was. If Zu An became the emperor, she would be at a disadvantage competing for the empress seat.","It’d probably go to the big miss of the Chu clan. She is the legitimate wife, after all.","But the thought of lowering herself to serve tea to other women pricked her pride.","Noticing her dilemma, Zu An laughed. “Let’s not dwell on this. It’s too troublesome for me to be the emperor. It’ll be better for you to be the empress and bring prosperity to the people.”","Bi Linglong’s lips twitched, but she decided not to dwell on the topic. She took her leave with Concubine Bai so the two of them could discuss a legal way to settle her and her son without undermining the regent.","After they left, Zu An turned to the long-legged guard off to the side and said, “Zitong, there seem to be words on the tip of your tongue. Feel free to say whatever you have in mind.”","Zhang Zitong hesitated, but she spoke up anyway, “Regent, I don’t think what you’re doing is fair.”","“Oh? How am I being unfair?” Zu An was surprised.","“During the founding of the Zhou Dynasty, the Zhou clan went after the preceding Meng Dynasty’s imperial family. Many Meng clansmen and their subjects died as a result. And yet, you showed such compassion to the Zhao clan.” Zhang Zitong’s eyes reddened.","She must have been reminded about the casualties suffered by her Zhang clan protecting the old imperial grandson. Zu An walked over and patted her shoulder. “You don’t think I’ve killed enough Zhao clansmen yet?”","He hadn’t gone after them out of a grudge, but there was no denying that he had killed many Zhao clansmen.","Zhang Zitong was startled. She belatedly remembered how the regent had previously purged respected and influential Zhao clansmen in the previous capital uprisings. That greatly placated her. “I wasn’t thinking clearly, regent.”","Zu An smiled. “Concubine Bai’s son is a child. We shouldn’t continue the bloodshed for the world’s stability. However, your words do remind me of something. Contact the Hub of Freedom and have them create a list of the Meng Dynasty’s survivors. I’ll acknowledge them and grant them a fief where they can live openly.”","Zhang Zitong’s eyes lit up. “Is that for real?”","“Of course it is. Do you think I’d lie about this?” Zu An huffed.","“I’ll do it right now!” Feeling conscience-stricken, Zhang Zitong meekly looked at Zu An and said, “Regent, I haven’t contacted them since I started following you. You aren’t... testing me, right?”","Zu An replied, “...Do you think I’d need to do something like that?”","Zhang Zitong beamed. “That’s true. But regent, those people would rather have you become the emperor and restore the Meng Dynasty’s glory.”","Zu An shook his head. “Dynasties come and go; this has been the unchanging way of the world. I don’t intend to get involved in such matters, so don’t mention it ever again.”","“Yes, I won’t mention it again.” Zhang Zitong was disappointed.","Zu An relented with a sigh. “Zitong, I’m not going to get involved with the Meng Dynasty, but I won’t forget the Zhang clan’s sacrifice. I’ll build a monument for the Zhang clan so that the world remembers their heroic deeds even after ten thousand years. Also, I’ve never thought of you as a subordinate, so you don’t need to be so uptight around me.”","Those words evoked Zhang Zitong’s past memories, and tears glimmered in her eyes. She kneeled and kowtowed to him. With a hoarse voice, she said, “I thank you on their behalf, regent.”"]},{"number":2708,"title":"Chapter 2708: Chapter 2660: Acquaintances","paragraphs":["Zu An hurriedly pulled Zhang Zitong up to her feet. “You don’t need to do something like that! I owe your Zhang clan a lot. I haven’t properly repaid you yet. Is there anything you want? I’ll fulfill it as long as it’s within my means.”","He wasn’t the real imperial grandson, but it was thanks to the Zhang clan that he’d grown up safely. He was indebted to the Zhang clan for their sacrifice.","Feeling the heat of Zu An’s palms on her arms made Zhang Zitong’s heart race. The regent has touched me! Through her excitement, she heard Zu An’s words, and that made her heart swell in bliss. “Can I ask for anything?”","“You can give it a try. There are very few things that are beyond me now.” Zu An smiled. Despite everything he had been through, he still enjoyed her reverent gaze.","Zhang Zitong’s breathing hastened. Her face reddened as she thought about something, but she suppressed that thought and said, “I wish to continue serving you as your guard. No, not just a guard, but... What was the term you used back then? Yes, secretary. That.”","Zu An was stunned. “You’re already my guard and secretary. That isn’t much of a wish. Why don’t you pick something else?”","But Zhang Zitong shook her head. Her mind was made up. “That’s what I want!”","She knew that Zu An’s pond was filled with ferocious, gigantic sharks, and a shrimp like her would only be swallowed whole if she joined the battlefield. But if she became his secretary, no matter how many lovers he had, she could remain the one closest to him.","Those sharks might even have to fawn over me instead!","The thought of the lofty empress, noblewomen, and holy maidens fawning over her made her so happy that she nearly burst into laughter.","Zu An couldn’t understand her bizarre wish, but since it wasn’t anything difficult, he accepted her request. “Alright. Let me know if there’s anything else you want.” Although, he didn’t think this would be enough to repay the Zhang clan.","“This is enough.” Zhang Zitong grinned merrily.","...","After organizing the rebel army in Phoenix Pass, Zu An and Bi Linglong brought the rebel kings to the capital as prisoners. The political situation immediately stabilized. Many major clans had been secretly liaising with the rebels in search of a way out, but with the rebellion quelled, no one dared to harbor traitorous thoughts anymore.","It also helped that Bi Linglong had publicly burned the letters she obtained from the rebel army, declaring that she would only punish the masterminds. That won her tremendous support from the people.","Zu An entrusted all administrative work to Bi Linglong, including the clean-up and the transition of dynasties. Meanwhile, he went to the courtyard on top of Mount Yuquan and gathered all the teachers there.","Other than Second Senior Drunken Sword Immortal Xiao Yao, who was wandering the world, Sixth Junior Painter Yu Yanluo, who was with the Fiend races, and Ninth Junior Bard Shang Liuyu, who was with the Ocean races, the rest were all present.","“Paying respect to the libationer!” All of them bowed to Zu An.","To them, his position as the libationer was more important than his post in the imperial court. They keenly noticed that Jiang Luofu hadn’t returned with him, and that made their hearts sink in sorrow.","Zu An knew they had misunderstood, so he quickly told them about the events during the trip and where Jiang Luofu was likely to be.","“A universal deity?” The crowd was startled.","They were the old libationer’s disciples, masters of their respective fields. They were knowledgeable. But learning about universal deities and the battle against Zhao Yuan at the Phoenix Pass made them realize that they were still frogs in a well.","Even so, this only sparked their enthusiasm to get to the bottom of things.","Knowing they were a bunch of obsessed academics, Zu An warned them, “Don’t recklessly dive into this. Catching the attention of a universal deity is more likely to bring destruction, though if you happen to be suited for their path, it is possible for them to bestow you with power instead, such as in Zhao Yuan’s case.”","Qi Yaoguang blinked. “Is the libationer telling us to look into deities whose dao aligns with ours, so we can have a higher chance of getting acknowledged?”","Zu An nodded. “It would be best for you to avoid getting involved with them, but I know you’re devoted academics. You won’t let an opportunity to uncover the unknown slip past your fingers, so I won’t waste my breath here.”","Yan Xiangu frankly replied, “I’ve been pursuing the heavenly dao for a long time now. I can’t stop now that a path has emerged. It might be fraught with dangers, but I have no regrets dying while in pursuit of the truth.” Despite his emaciated physique, he looked unwavering in his stance.","“Great senior is right!” The others voiced their agreement. They weren’t to give up on their paths for safety.","But Ji Dengtu was more worried about something else. “Why don’t I see Xiaoxi? Don’t tell me you lost Xiaoxi on top of my little aunt?” He lurched forth and grabbed Zu An’s collar. His voice was quivering.","The others frowned. If anyone else dared to treat the libationer in such a manner, they would have intervened right away, but Ji Dengtu had a special relationship with him.","“Brother Zu, what about my big sister?” Xie Xiu asked. A third-generation disciple like him wasn’t qualified to attend this meeting, but he was Zu An’s friend and Xie Daoyun’s little brother, so Zu An had called him over too. He was only speaking up now because he hadn’t dared to interject when his elders were talking.","Yan Xiangu also asked, “Indeed, Libationer. Is Daoyun safe?” He, too, was worried about his disciple’s safety.","“You don’t have to worry. They’re safe. I’ll bring them over right now.” Zu An wasn’t angry even though Ji Dengtu’s saliva was splattering all over his face. They had, after all, forged a strong bond over erotica back then.","The crowd was perplexed. Right now? How? Are they in this room too? But we went out to welcome the libationer together earlier. He didn’t bring anyone else other than the beautiful guard with long legs.","Zu An abruptly paused for a second before saying, “Xiaoxi is fine, but Xie Daoyun’s situation is a little unique. You should prepare yourselves mentally.”","“Ah?” Yan Xiangu and Xie Xiu’s faces paled.","“Ah? Is she crippled, poisoned, or in a coma?” Xie Xiu asked about a series of frightening possibilities.","“That’s not it. She’s fine, it’s just that her appearance has changed.”","“What do you mean, her appearance has changed? Is she disfigured?”","Zu An had no idea how to explain this, so he decided to let them witness it in person instead. Thus, he began communing with the world’s will.","There were a few flashes of light, and several figures suddenly appeared in the house.","“Xiaoxi!” Ji Dengtu nearly burst into tears when he saw Ji Xiaoxi.","There was also the well-endowed Pei Mianman, the innocent yet seductive King Wu Consort, and a woman who was dressed like an ancient shaman but emanated a familiar scholarly air.","“Where’s my big sister?” Xie Xiu panicked when he didn’t see his big sister.","“Xiu’er, it has only been a while. Have you already forgotten me?” Xie Daoyun had been chatting with her Fiend race friends when she was suddenly transported here. She heard her little brother’s words and instinctively reached out to pinch his ears.","“Ah?” Xie Xiu, Yan Xiangu, and the others froze up."]},{"number":2709,"title":"Chapter 2709: Chapter 2661: Seed","paragraphs":["“Huh? Who are you?” Xie Xiu immediately retreated like an alarmed rabbit while staring at her with wary eyes.","Xie Daoyun belatedly remembered that she was still assuming Yumen Beiqing’s appearance. Frustrated, she said, “I’m your big sister. It’s a long story.”","“Brother Zu, who is she?” Xie Xiu refused to believe it. He thought Zu An was making fun of him. He wondered if a mishap had happened to his big sister, prompting Zu An to hire an actress to fool him.","Yan Xiangu was perplexed too. Other than their similar dispositions, he saw no similarity between Xie Daoyun and the woman in front of him.","Xie Daoyun harrumphed. “You brat. You have two moles on your left bottom. You have been afraid of ghosts from a young age, and you always pestered the maids to accompany you because you didn’t dare to sleep alone. You peed your bed even when you were already seven...”","Xie Xiu anxiously interjected, “Stop, stop, stop! I believe you now!”","No one knew about his dark history better than his big sister. An impostor wouldn’t have known about all these things. His face darkened. I shouldn’t have questioned her identity. Ugh, I’m sure news will spread soon, and the reputation I have built up for myself will be ruined.","Xie Daoyun just bowed to Yan Xiangu, and the latter tested her on talismans and formations, specifically knowledge that only they knew. From that, Yan Xiangu confirmed that she was Xie Daoyun... but he still couldn’t understand how her appearance could have changed like that.","“Libationer, what’s going on?”","“She is now the Fiend races’ esteemed Saintess Yumen Beiqing...” Zu An explained.","“That elusive Yumen Beiqing from history?” Those present in this meeting were well-read; they had naturally heard about the legendary Yumen Beiqing. They hadn’t expected her to be Xie Daoyun.","“It is truly baffling. Yumen Beiqing must have been Xie Daoyun’s previous incarnation. An accident might have happened while she was transmigrating into the past using the Nature Jade, resulting in such an outcome,” Zu An summarized the situation.","The crowd was in shock. Had they not witnessed it with their own eyes, they wouldn’t have believed such a thing could have happened.","“I hadn’t expected the concept of past incarnations to be real,” Hei Baizi remarked.","Qi Yaoguang’s eyes twinkled in excitement. “I wonder who my previous incarnation was.”","...","Unlike the curious crowd, Xie Xiu was more concerned about his big sister’s appearance. “Will my big sister have to live out her life with this appearance?”","Zu An was at a loss too. “We might find a solution in the future.”","Xie Daoyun spoke up, “Big brother Zu, it’s not a big deal. After returning to this world, I found out that I’d appear as Yumen Beiqing in the day, but revert to my original appearance at night.”","“Your appearance reverts?” Zu An was overjoyed to hear that.","Xie Daoyun nodded. “I initially thought I had reverted to my original appearance for good, but at daybreak, I transformed into Yumen Beiqing yet again. I wasn’t comfortable with it at the start, but I soon got used to it. I did spend a substantial time as Yumen Beiqing back in the past, so it feels as if both of them are me.”","Zu An deduced that returning to this world might have reawakened Xie Daoyun’s identity, but there was no way to say to be sure whether she would completely revert back in the future.","Xie Xiu was stifled. “Ah? Doesn’t that mean I can only meet my big sister at night?”","Xie Daoyun huffed, “I’m still your big sister in the daytime!”","“But whoever marries you in the future will be marrying two people at once,” Xie Xiu said. He noticed his big sister glancing shyly at Zu An and frowned. “Brother Zu, did you... get together with my big sister while you were in the past?”","Zu An was awed by Xie Xiu’s sharp judgment as a brothel regular. The latter could keenly sense the difference in their intimacy level.","He was about to answer when the furiously blushing Xie Daoyun exclaimed, “You brat! What nonsense are you spouting? I’ll wallop you!”","Xie Xiu fled in a fluster. “You can wallop me, but you should at least inform our father about something this important!”","Zu An’s head hurt. Having too many lovers was troublesome too. I should find time to pay a visit to Lord Xie.","Ji Dengtu took the chance to ask, “Brat, what happened with the Cruel Poison Constitution you mentioned earlier?”","As a renowned physician, he could sense a terrifying poison that sparked fear from the bottom of his heart in his daughter’s body.","“You don’t have to worry. I’ve found a solution for her Cruel Poison Constitution. We’ve gathered ingredients to concoct a pill that will aid Xiaoxi in cultivating the poison dao. This could be a blessing in disguise; her cultivation will grow by leaps and bounds.” Zu An recalled that one of the ingredients was the Defying Spirit Tears, and that caused his heart to squeeze.","“Poison dao?” Ji Dengtu frowned. “Will that prevent her from marrying and having a child?”","As a father, he was more concerned about his daughter’s safety and happiness. He knew that poisonous creatures tended to store poison in their reproductive organs, so he was worried.","“I don’t think so...” Zu An had never considered this, but this solution had been offered by Shennong’s successor and affirmed by a Celestial Emperor. They would have brought it up if there was such a huge downside to the solution.","Ji Dengtu was angered. “What do you mean by ‘you don’t think so’?”","Ji Xiaoxi exclaimed in a fluster, “What are you saying, daddy? I won’t talk to you anymore!”","Being a physician herself, she had also considered this issue. But the Cruel Poison Constitution was too unfathomable; it was already a blessing for her to have found a way to survive, so she didn’t dare to hope for more.","Not to mention big brother Zu is this world’s master. He wouldn’t be fazed by my poison, so that isn’t a problem at all.","There was no way she could explain that in front of so many people, especially given her shy nature. Unable to take the embarrassment, she ran out.","“My good daughter, I was wrong! Let me feel your pulse...” Ji Dengtu chased after his daughter.","Zu An took this chance to settle Pei Mianman and the others in the academy.","Yan Xiangu and the others seemed to have returned to the old days when they first enrolled in the academy, pestering Zu An to tell them more about the ancient era and the deities.","Zu An’s wealth of experience had given him a deeper insight into strength, cultivation, and laws. His answers could always shake Yan Xiangu and the others to their core. Eventually, they decided to gather all the academy’s students to listen to Zu An’s lecture.","Zu An knew he hadn’t been properly doing this job as the libationer, so this time, he tried his best to clear everyone’s doubts in order to sow a huge dao seed here. This way, even if something happened to him in Dreamland, the cultivators of this world would still find a path forward.","The lecture lasted for three whole days. It wasn’t that Zu An refused to continue, but the crowd needed time to digest what they’d already learned.","He had already sown the seed anyway, so it was only a matter of time before it flowered.","Yan Xiangu and the others had only previously recognized Zu An as the libationer because that was the old libationer’s order. They’d respected him, but it was only out of admiration for his strength and character.","Yet now, they were bowing to him as disciples. They viewed him as their mentor from the bottom of their hearts.","Zu An returned to the courtyard. He suddenly sensed something and turned to the side, where he saw a figure dressed in a snowy-white robe."]},{"number":2710,"title":"Chapter 2710: Chapter 2662: A Virtuous Woman Fears A Persistent Suitor","paragraphs":["The courtyard at the peak of Mount Yuquan was tranquil. The lotus pond in the courtyard blossomed all year round, and the red koi swimming in it were as good as spirit pets. Anyone who came here would be awed by the sight.","But the picturesque scenery paled in comparison to the beautiful figure standing in it. She had long, fluttery hair, brows reminiscent of the distant mountains, and a pair of bright eyes. Her fair neck resembled that of a graceful crane, and she wore a white robe resembling snow. Her very presence formed the most picturesque painting.","Moonlight shone on her, and she naturally commanded the limelight.","“Big sister Yan!”","Zu An was overjoyed to see the other party. He hadn’t expected to reunite with her here. She felt familiar to him because he thought about her frequently, but upon further thought, it had been a long time since they last met.","“It was a wonderful lecture. Even I benefited greatly from it. I was your elder, but you can become my master now.” Yan Xuehen had a pleasant voice, but her tone was colder than the night wind.","Even so, Zu An didn’t think too much of it. Her character archetype was that of a snow immortal; he would be more surprised if her personality suddenly changed.","“I dare not be your master. You are my master.” Zu An walked over with a grin.","But Yan Xuehen subtly side-stepped to maintain her distance from him. “The world of cultivation has never been about age or seniority. It’s about how far you have advanced. Your cultivation far surpasses that of the past Zhao Han and the Fiend Emperor. You are qualified to be the master of all experts in this world, including me.”","Sensing her distance, Zu An frowned. He flitted forth and embraced her. “It’s been a while, but you’ve changed quite a bit.”","Yan Xuehen wanted to dodge, but it was beyond her means to avoid him. His warm embrace brought a frown to her face. “You’re using your skills to deal with me now?”","“You wanted to dodge,” Zu An replied brazenly.","“You have reached the peak of humankind, so why are you still acting like a thug?” Yan Xuehen’s voice quivered. She tried to struggle free but to no avail. In the end, she coldly said, “Regent, please have some self-respect. I am Chuyan’s master, and this is the academy’s sacred land...”","Whoosh!","She was kissed before she could finish speaking. To make things worse, the other party made a loud smooching sound, as if pulling a prank on her.","Her fair skin was swiftly dyed red. “You!”","The White Jade Sect’s disciples admired Yan Xuehen’s beauty, but they found her too cold. She never showed any expression. Many had fantasized about how mesmerizing she would be if she smiled, but no one had ever seen her smile, let alone blush.","Yet in front of Zu An, she always showed sides unknown to others.","Looking at her angry yet embarrassed expression, Zu An thought to himself that this was probably the peak of beauty. He couldn’t take it anymore and stole yet another kiss from her.","Yan Xuehen couldn’t struggle free of him, so she put on a stern face and said, “I’m indeed no match for you now, but are you the type of person to take advantage of women like this?”","Zu An chuckled. “Of course I am. For many years now, I’ve dreamt of going onto the streets and teasing fair maidens!”","Yan Xuehen was left speechless, utterly shocked by his shamelessness.","She helplessly replied, “Ah Zu, didn’t we agree to forget about the past and remain as normal friends?”","“This is normal for me.” Zu An was unfazed.","Yan Xuehen was starting to get frustrated. “Do you hug normal friends like that too?”","You have successfully trolled Yan Xuehan for +22... +22... +22...","Zu An wouldn’t hug male friends like that, but he had no qualms with hugging female friends in such a manner. That said, he wouldn’t dare say those words aloud.","Yan Xuehan sighed yet again. “Ah Zu, I am Chuyan’s master.”","“So what?” Chuyan knows about us, but I promised her that I’d keep it from Yan Xuehen. I shouldn’t backstab her now.","“Stop messing around.” Yan Xuehen glared at him.","“If I remember correctly, you promised me a hundred times. Surely a sect master like you won’t renege on your promise, right?” Zu An was helping jog her memory of their previous meeting.","“A hundred times? I only promised thrice...” Yan Xuehen blurted out, only to realize right away she had fallen for Zu An’s scheme. She angrily pummeled her fist on his chest.","Seeing that she had returned to normal, Zu An burst into laughter.","After the two bickered a little more, Yan Xuehen said while gasping for air, “Can’t you release me first? I have something to say.”","She had already glanced outside a couple times, worried that others would request an audience with their libationer.","“Do you still acknowledge the three times?” Zu An took the chance to ask.","Yan Xuehen gritted her teeth. Seeing how he refused to let go, she had no choice but to reply with a “Mm”.","Her embarrassed response further stoked Zu An’s fondness. Yan Xuehen had become colder after several years of absence, but that was due to the advancement of her cultivation rather than their relationship.","She cultivated the Unshakable Daoist Manual, which required one to cast away their feelings. If he’d let her have her way earlier, their relationship could have had to stop here.","Fortunately, the old idiom rang true—even the most virtuous woman feared a persistent suitor.","Yan Xuehen eyed the man beside her with conflicted eyes. A long time later, she asked, “Have you found a way to save Chu Chuyan?”","“I’ve found Chuyan and stabilized her condition for the time being, but it would be a stretch to say she’s living.” When he talked about Chuyan, Zu An’s smile vanished.","“What happened?” Yan Xuehan anxiously grabbed his hand.","“You don’t need to be so nervous. Chuyan currently exists as a soul, and her condition isn’t as bad as you imagine. For the time being, the situation is under control...” Zu An moved to explain about the Naihe Bridge and the Oblivion River.","Even though she was supposed to have cast away her emotions, tears glimmered in Yan Xuehen’s eyes. “Chuyan is suffering there alone. She is too pitiful.”","She suddenly raised her head and declared, “I want to meet her.” She was worried about Chu Chuyan and wanted to see how she was faring.","“That’s the Netherworld. The living can’t get there.”","“Aren’t you the master of this world and the Netherworld? You must have a way!” Yan Xuehen looked at him with hopeful eyes.","Zu An pondered for a while. “There is a way—soul projection—but it’s fraught with dangers...”","Yan Xuehen firmly replied, “I’ll do it!”"]},{"number":2711,"title":"Chapter 2711: Chapter 2663: Condition","paragraphs":["“If you get careless, your soul could disintegrate.” Zu An grimly warned Yan Xuehen.","Upon reaching the Earth Immortal realm, cultivators gained the power to draw their souls out of their bodies. The stronger they were, the further their souls could travel from their bodies.","But that was limited to the mortal world, which was filled with ki that could nourish one’s soul. Even so, they had to be extremely careful of weapons that dealt with the soul, and their bodies had to be protected properly too. A soul, no matter how powerful, would disintegrate if it lost a body to house itself.","The fact that they were heading to the Netherworld, which could potentially corrode their souls, didn't help either.","“No matter how dangerous it is, I have to go. I have been worried about Chuyan all these years. I have browsed countless records but couldn’t find a way to save her. I finally have some news about her now. I won’t be able to rest at ease unless I see her in person.” Yan Xuehen looked anguished.","Judging from her emotional fluctuations, Zu An could tell that this was a knot in her heart. Yan Xuehen thought that their relationship was what had caused Chu Chuyan’s mishap. If she couldn’t resolve it in time, it could grow into an inner demon, and that would be the greatest possible bane in her cultivation method.","Thus, Zu An said, “Alright.”","“When do we make a move?” Yan Xuehen breathed a sigh of relief.","Zu An looked at the night sky and said, “It’s going to be the ‘Zi’ hour[1] soon. The yin energy will be the most concentrated then; it’ll be best to head to the Netherworld at that time.”","He gave Yan Xuehen a brief overview of the Netherworld and the things she had to look out for lest she suffer a fright later on.","Yan Xuehen calmly listened to him. Shortly after, she began meditating under his guidance, and by channeling the method he had imparted to her, her soul began drifting out of her body.","Staring at her face close up, Zu An was mesmerized by her beautiful appearance and her unique transcendent disposition. No wonder even someone as powerful as Zhao Han had courted her back then.","Yan Xuehen suddenly opened her eyes and noticed his scrutiny. That made her face redden. “I have another question. Will it be safe to leave my body here?”","She’d had many suitors, which cultivated her cautious personality. She was worried about leaving her body here after projecting her soul out.","Zu An smiled. “Don’t have to worry. This is the safest place in the academy, and I’ll also set up formations here. No one will be able to reach your body. I’ll also be able to return here right away if anything happens. As long as I focus, I can keep tabs on anything happening in this world.”","Yan Xuehen was relieved. At the same time, she looked forward to reaching his level. “The records detail an unparalleled cultivation level, but for many generations, we cultivators thought it was just the ancestors’ imagination. I never thought you’d reach it.”","“Call me master from now on, and I’ll teach you,” Zu An said with a grin.","“Pui!” Yan Xuehen spat before shyly looking away.","Even though she had said that Zu An was now qualified to be her master, she’d intended it to refer to a solemn impartation of cultivation insights. But judging from Zu An’s tone, he was likely planning to exploit that position to take advantage of her. There was no way she could accept that.","Zu An knew how shy she was and was worried her emotional fluctuation could affect her soul’s stability, so he stopped teasing her. “Are you ready? Let’s begin.”","“All right.” Yan Xuehen closed her eyes. Under Zu An’s guidance, she murmured an incantation, and soon, a faint silhouette stood up from her body.","Yan Xuehen thought it was strange to see her own body sitting on the bed. “Your method of soul projection seems different from projecting the yin soul and the yang soul.”","Zu An altered the surrounding environment to protect her soul while explaining with a smile, “There is a slight difference. The yin soul and the yang soul are just parts of the soul, whereas this soul projection draws out the entirety of the soul...”","Looking at Yan Xuehen’s soul, Zu An was perplexed as to why the projected souls he had seen were all wearing clothes. In theory, souls should have been bare and without adornment.","It must be their subconscious mind at work. They instinctively feel that they should be clothed even when projecting their souls, which results in them appearing that way.","Yan Xuehen was enlightened by Zu An’s talk about souls. I should be able to make a breakthrough in my cultivation if I go into seclusion after I return...","When she saw how earnestly he was taking this, her expression became gentler. He looks dashing when he gets serious.","If she knew what Zu An was thinking, however, her lower jaw would drop to the ground.","“Aren’t you going to project your soul too?” Yan Xuehen asked curiously.","Zu An smiled as he reached out to grab her. “Living beings are forbidden in the Netherworld, but I’m an exception. Come, let me guide you.”","Yan Xuehen didn’t turn him down. Being in soul form left her feeling insecure, and she instinctively wanted to stay close to Zu An. Her body shuddered when she grabbed Zu An’s hand. “This feels weird.”","“Your senses are more pronounced in soul form...” Zu An replied. He was reminded about how his soul had fused with Jiang Luofu’s in the Monster World—that had been an unforgettable experience to him.","I wonder if she’s safe...","Sensing something strange, Yan Xuehen asked, “Are you thinking about other women while holding my hand?”","She regretted blurting that out right away. It was unlike her to say such words.","But Zu An was overjoyed. “I didn’t know big sister Yan got jealous too.”","“I am merely keeping an eye on you on Chuyan’s behalf. As her master, I ought to stop you from philandering while she’s not around,” Yan Xuehen replied coldly.","“Of course, of course.” Zu An could hardly suppress his smile. He leaned closer and said, “I have been feeling lonely now that Chuyan isn’t with me. Master, shouldn’t you take her place and accompany me to keep me from philandering around?”","“How can you be this shameless?” Yan Xuehen exclaimed angrily. She’d never realize a soul could blush as well.","“Shouldn’t you go all the way when helping someone? If you refuse to help, I’ll have to look for other people. You’d have failed your duty to Chuyan, no?” Teasing the ice immortal was more fun than Zu An had thought.","Yan Xuehen blinked. Something felt off about his words, but she couldn’t put her finger on what it was. “Just because I’m keeping an eye on you on Chuyan’s behalf doesn’t mean that I’ll help her with... this.”","“Why? If you take care of me, I won’t have the energy to look for others. You’d be doing Chuyan a huge favor here.”","Yan Xuehen was shocked to find herself moved by his words. This makes sense. It’d be better to keep him by my side than to let him philander outside. I think Chuyan would rather he be with me than other ladies outside. At least we’re close...","That thought made her face redden. She angrily punched the man beside her and exclaimed, “You nearly misled me! You would still have the energy to find other ladies even if Chuyan was with you!”","She had a lasting impression of his neverending stamina. She had spent many nights exhausted over that. It would be impossible to satisfy him with just the two of them.","Zu An’s eyes lit up. “It sounds like you’ve considered it.”","Yan Xuehen was on the verge of dying from embarrassment. She decided to just give in. “If you promise not to look for anyone else other than Chuyan in the future, I can... take care of you on her behalf.”","1. 11PM to 1AM. ☜"]},{"number":2712,"title":"Chapter 2712: Chapter 2664: Don’t Even Think About It","paragraphs":["“Sure!” Zu An accepted without any hesitation.","Yan Xuehen was dumbstruck. She angrily exclaimed, “How can you make a promise you won’t keep?”","You have successfully trolled Yan Xuehen for +66... +66... +66...","She didn’t think Zu An would give up on the forest for Chu Chuyan and her.","“How do you know I can’t do it if you don’t give it a try?” Zu An looked at her with a smile.","Yan Xuehen averted her gaze. She was no fool. Playing along with him was as good as whacking a dog with a meat bun—she would just get gobbled up.","The two of them soon arrived above the sea. Yan Xuehen suddenly said, “I heard you’re on good terms with the Mermaid Queen. Shouldn’t you pay her a visit now that you’re here?”","Zu An was surprised. “I didn’t expect the aloof Immortal Yan to show interest in mortal affairs.”","Yan Xuehen’s heart skipped a beat. “Hmph! Who in the world hasn’t heard of your philandering affairs?”","She would never admit to collecting all the news relating to him over the years. In fact, upon hearing about his return, she had rushed here from the White Jade Sect without rest.","“It isn't safe for a soul to remain outside the body for too long. I need to bring you back as soon as possible lest complications occur.” Zu An wouldn’t be so foolish as to bring a woman to meet her love rival. That would be as good as stomping on his own foot.","Yan Xuehen didn’t intend to meet the Mermaid Queen either; she wouldn’t know how to respond in the latter's presence anyway. Without revealing their relationship, she would be forced to watch their public display of affection as an elder. It was too embarrassing for her to reveal their relationship, on the other hand.","“I heard the Mermaid Queen used to be the Dragon Emperor’s wife? Don’t you already have many lovers by your side? Why do you still go after other people’s wives?” Yan Xuehen thought her dao of clear-mindedness, which she had spent many years cultivating, would shatter when she asked this question.","He already has Chuyan, Miss Pei, the Devil Sect’s Saintess Miss Qiu, and me... Why does he still go after other people’s wives? It’s not just the Mermaid Queen. There’s also the empress and the empress dowager.","She had been reading the novels about the regent’s romances sold on the street.","You have successfully trolled Yan Xuehen for +110... +110... +110...","Her only relief was that she wasn’t in any of those books, or else she would be too embarrassed to face the world.","Zu An felt awkward too. “It was a coincidence. When I first arrived at the Ocean races' territory, someone was impersonating the Dragon Emperor, and she was escaping from pursuers...”","He roughly described his first meeting with the Mermaid Queen by the seaside tavern back then.","That changed Yan Xuehen’s impression of the Mermaid Queen. “It sounds like you aren’t at fault here. But why do you keep bumping into such incidents?”","Zu An was frustrated too. “I don’t know either. It’s the same between us too. You were initially after my life as well...”","The embarrassed Yan Xuehen chomped on him before he could finish speaking. Her face was all red. He’s like a magnet for women.","Before they knew it, they arrived at the abyss leading into the Netherworld.","When she looked at the pitch-black abyss before her, Yan Xuehen was no longer in the mood to bicker with Zu An. The dread she instinctively felt made her lean closer to Zu An.","Zu An wrapped his arm around her waist. “Stay within a meter of me. Living beings are forbidden from the Netherworld. You must be careful not to be afflicted by its death energy.”","“Mm.” Understanding the severity of the situation, Yan Xuehen obediently stayed within Zu An’s arms.","She wasn't averse to physical contact with Zu An, but her position and the habit she had cultivated over many years made her self-conscious about it. But if there was a legitimate reason, she didn’t mind being publicly intimate with Zu An.","Zu An leaped into the abyss with Yan Xuehen in his arms. A light emanated from his body and enveloped the two of them.","Yan Xuehen glanced at the man beside her. She thought about their encounters, and the frost in her eyes melted into tenderness. She embraced him tightly while resting her face on his chest. Even if it’s just for a short while, he belongs to me now.","It didn’t take long for them to land on the ground. Zu An gently said, “We’re here.”","Yan Xuehen looked up and assessed the surroundings. “Is this the Netherworld?”","The world was shrouded in a gray mist. Zu An had told her that was death energy, which could kill any living being upon contact. While she was assessing the surroundings, her body suddenly shivered. She bolted away from Zu An’s arms while staring at him in shock.","“What’s wrong?” Zu An was stunned.","“I don’t know. You suddenly felt very frightening. Every bit of my soul is telling me to stay away from you.” Yan Xuehen had no idea why she had such a feeling. Zu An was powerful, but it wasn't his first time holding her. She shouldn’t have been frightened of him.","However, this was primal fear.","Zu An understood what was going on right away. “I'm the master of the Netherworld, wielding the power insignia of the afterlife. All ghosts in the Netherworld naturally fear me...”","He cast a skill that shrouded him in light, isolating the terrifying pressure he emanated.","Yan Xuehen breathed a sigh of relief. She wiped away her sweat. “I've never felt that scared before. I felt utterly helpless, as if I would live and die at your whim. It was terrifying.”","Zu An leaned in with a smile. “It’s not as if that's never happened before.”","Yan Xuehen’s face turned completely red. “You’re so hateful!”","She also remembered how he had driven her to her limit back then, to a point where she begged him for mercy. Even her voice lost its usual coldness and then became cloying.","Zu An's interjection did dispel much of her fear, however. It quickly dawned on Yan Xuehen that even though he appeared to be teasing her, he seemed to have his own reason for doing so.","They made their way to a black pass. Yan Xuehen looked dazed as she murmured, “Is that the legendary Gate of Hell...”","This place was often mentioned in daoist records and folklore, but it was often shrugged off as a legend. She'd never thought a day would come when she was standing before it.","Zu An nodded. He introduced to her the Netherworld’s buildings, the distant Yin Mountain, and the Yellow Spring.","Yan Xuehen studied her surroundings with curious eyes as she asked, “Why is there no one here? Ah... I mean, why are there no netherworld guards around?”","“There seems to have been a major incident in the Netherworld at some point in history, resulting in the disappearance of the netherworld guards. The place is still functioning thanks to the Netherworld Book of Life and Death and its intrinsic laws managing the ghosts, though.” Zu An remembered about the message left behind by the missing shamans, Ox Head, and Horse Face, and he couldn’t help but worry.","Yan Xuehen sensed his worry and held his hand. “Ah Zu, I have been cultivating hard the past few years too. My cultivation has far surpassed the old Zhao Han. From now onward, I’ll help you no matter what you’re facing.”","Zu An was moved. Yan Xuehen was one of the female powerhouses standing at the peak of the world. Rather than being reliant on others, she would rather help shoulder her lover’s burden. He hugged her and whispered, “Will you help me when I’m with Chuyan...”","Yan Xuehen pushed him aside before he could finish speaking. The utterly embarrassed ice immortal’s complexion had turned completely pink. “Don’t even think about it!”","“I’m talking about cultivation. What are you thinking about?” Zu An looked at her with a mischievous smile.","Yan Xuehen realized she had fallen for his trick and angrily pummeled him. For the first time in a very long time, laughter filled the desolate Netherworld."]},{"number":2713,"title":"Chapter 2713: Chapter 2665: It’s All Acting","paragraphs":["As they walked down the Yellow Spring Road, Yan Xuehen noticed bizarre red flowers growing by the roadside. She stopped to take a closer look. “Are these the legendary Red Spider Lilies? How beautiful.”","“They are indeed beautiful.” Zu An agreed. These Red Spider Lilies were the only plants in the Netherworld. Each time he passed by this sea of flowers, it raised his mood a little despite the stifling atmosphere.","“When Chuyan obtained the Pure World Icelotus’ intent back then, Miss Pei simultaneously obtained the Paramita Butterfly’s intent. Could her Paramita Butterfly be related to these Red Spider Lilies?” Yan Xuehen suddenly remembered something.","“Her Paramita Butterfly does indeed resemble these Red Spider Lilies. I’ll bring her here when an opportunity arises.” With this experience, Zu An would be able to bring Pei Mianman here to view the Red Spider Lilies in the future.","“I’d like to have a look at Miss Pei’s Paramita Butterfly, too.” Yan Xuehen felt goodwill toward Pei Mianman, not just because the latter's was Chu Chuyan’s close friend but also because of their interactions. Compared to the other women whom I haven’t met, Pei Mianman is much better...","“I also hope for such a day to come.” Zu An smiled. Pei Mianman’s Paramita Butterfly was usually hidden in her body. It would only appear on her waist when her blood was racing quickly. The only way for Yan Xuehen to see it would be if we were together in bed...","Yan Xuehen looked at him with a questioning gaze, sensing something amiss from his expression.","The two of them ventured further into the Netherworld. Knowing she would soon meet Chu Chuyan, Yan Xuehen’s initial curiosity about the Netherworld gave way to nervousness. She bit her lips. She was probably the only master in the world who was nervous to meet her disciple.","Soon, they arrived under the Bridge of Helplessness.","When she looked at the blood-colored Oblivion River Water, Yan Xuehen’s face paled. With her sharp eyes, she could see the distorted faces of vengeful spirits within. Has Chu Chuyan been living in such a vile environment?","A seven-colored light glowed under the Bridge of Helplessness, forming an independent space. The racing Oblivion River seemed to avoid that space. But Yan Xuehen couldn’t see anything there.","Zu An belatedly remembered the Bridge of Helplessness’ rules—those standing on the bridge couldn’t see those under the bridge. Thus, he smeared his finger across her eyes.","When Yan Xuehen opened her eyes once more, she could finally see a pure white lotus pad inside the seven-colored light. A beautiful woman was seated on the lotus. She was either cultivating or in a deep sleep.","It formed a stark contrast to the Oblivion River. On one side were the vengeful spirits of hell, whereas on the other side was a heavenly fairy. Her presence somehow dampened the ferocity of the Oblivion River.","“Chuyan...” Yan Xuehen’s voice quivered at the familiar sight. If not for Zu An holding onto her, she might have even stepped into the Oblivion River.","“She’s in a deep sleep.” Zu An patted her hand, as if telling her to calm down.","“How long does she have to remain in that state?” Yan Xuehen’s voice was trembling. She had noticed vengeful spirits in the Oblivion River swiping their claws at Chuyan, wanting to drag her down into the abyss with them. It was just that the seven-colored light stopped the vengeful spirits and disintegrated them.","The seven-colored light and the white lotus appeared to be protecting Chu Chuyan, but there were countless vengeful spirits dwelling in the Oblivion River. Yan Xuehen was worried about leaving her here.","“A thousand years... No, she has 997 years left.” Zu An’s voice was light-hearted, but he didn’t look happy in the slightest. He thought that time was passing too slowly.","“It takes so long?!” Yan Xuehen was agitated. “Aren’t you the world’s and the Netherworld’s master? Can’t you find a way to save her?”","Zu An shook his head. “She chose to spend a thousand years under the Oblivion Bridge in order to not forget me. This is a fundamental law governing the Netherworld; I can't alter it, at least not with my current ability.”","Yan Xuehen sighed. “What a silly child. If you hadn’t become the Netherworld’s master, you wouldn’t have met her and learned about the thousand years of anguish she would be going through.”","It would take an extreme degree of obsession for someone to withstand such a long trial. Many couples who had promised eternity to each other eventually succumbed to the years of suffering under the Bridge of Helplessness, and they could only watch in despair as their other half forgot about them. Their love turned into hatred, and they joined the vengeful spirits dwelling in the Oblivion River.","“Indeed. She’s a fool.” Zu An felt a tight squeeze in his chest when he thought about the worst possibility.","“It’s as if you’re fated for each other. She sacrificed so much for you, and you just happened to become the Netherworld’s master, which granted you the power to protect her.” Yan Xuehen felt apologetic. The greater the feelings they had for each other, the greater the guilt she felt.","Chuyan loves Ah Zu so much. Who am I to get stuck between them?","“What happened between us is fate too.” Zu An sensed Yan Xuehen’s low spirits and hugged her from behind.","Startled, Yan Xuehen tried to struggle free from his arms, protesting, “Don’t mess around. Chuyan is right there!” She couldn’t overcome the mental barrier even though Chu Chuyan was unconscious.","“Don’t worry. She can’t see a thing...” Zu An was halfway through his words when his smile suddenly froze in place. He noticed Chu Chuyan’s eyebrows fluttering.","Then, Chu Chuyan opened her eyes and looked coldly at the two of them.","Zu An: “...”","Yan Xuehen was on the verge of losing her mind. She'd almost struggled free of Zu An’s embrace, but she couldn’t tell when Chu Chuyan had woken up. If she saw what happened earlier...","She eyed the Oblivion River. For a brief moment, she even considered jumping in and ending it for good.","Chu Chuyan was the first to break the silence. “Ah Zu, master...” Her voice was feeble, and she sounded groggy.","Zu An was both alarmed and overjoyed. He grabbed Yan Xuehen and brought her to the lotus pad inside the seven-colored light.","Yan Xuehen shoved Zu An aside as soon as she got a stable footing. She anxiously explained, “Chuyan, don’t think too much into it. Ah Zu wasn’t hugging me. He was just...” Her mind went blank.","“I wasn’t thinking much of it. Flight is forbidden above the Oblivion River. Master, you couldn’t have gotten here if Ah Zu didn’t carry you over.” Chu Chuyan blinked. “Master, are you calling him Ah Zu too? The two of you have gotten much closer.”","Yan Xuehen’s heart beat furiously. She awkwardly twirled her hair to conceal her awkwardness. “Is that so? It just caught on with me after hearing you call him that.”","Zu An nearly burst into laughter. Chu Chuyan was feigning ignorance to tease Yan Xuehen despite already knowing about their relationship. He'd already felt sympathy for Yan Xuehen when Chu Chuyan previously warned him not to give her away.","Yan Xuehen looked conflicted, not knowing that Chu Chuyan was making fun of her.","Unable to bear watching this anymore, Zu An wanted to tip off Yan Xuehen, but when he saw Chu Chuyan’s warning glare, he quickly sealed his lips. Chu Chuyan was going through a lot for him. It wouldn’t hurt for her to find some entertainment to tide her over through a thousand boring years.","Yan Xuehen was oblivious to it. To not give herself away, she quickly changed the subject. “Chuyan, I never expected your seclusion to almost end up as eternal farewell between us.” Her emotions poured out, and tears streamed down her cheeks.","Chu Chuyan knew that emotional fluctuations were taboo to their cultivation; her master had to be truly agitated to behave in such a manner. She thought about the time she had spent with Yan Xuehen, how the latter had taken care of her in the sect, as well as the bizarre experiences she'd had in recent years.","She suddenly felt incredibly aggrieved, diving into Yan Xuehen’s arms and crying, “Master!”","The master and disciple cried for a long time while Zu An watched them in a melancholic mood.","Chu Chuyan had been extremely composed since their last reunion, but she was after all a young lady. It wouldn’t do for her to continue suppressing all these emotions inside her.","However, she had been independent from a young age. She wouldn’t break down even in front of her mother, Qin Wanru. It was only to Yan Xuehen, who was like both a master and a mother to her, that her true emotions would flow out.","After the two ladies vented their emotions, Zu An asked curiously, “Chuyan, weren’t you in hibernation? Why did you suddenly wake up?”","Yan Xuehen tensed up too. What if she saw what happened earlier?","Chu Chuyan rolled her eyes in annoyance. “You still have the cheek to ask that? Why didn’t you wake me up when you came to the Bridge of Helplessness after returning from the past? Were you planning to leave just like that again if I didn’t wake up?”"]},{"number":2714,"title":"Chapter 2714: Chapter 2666: Turning Tables","paragraphs":["“I know it isn’t hard for you to fall into a deep sleep. I feared things would get harder for you if I woke you up, so I chose not to disturb you,” Zu An explained.","“What’s the point of sleeping for a long time if you aren’t around? I’d rather wake up and spend each day with you slowly.” Chu Chuyan glared at him grudgingly. She took his decision not to wake her to heart.","Yan Xuehen was surprised. She had never seen Chu Chuyan speaking in such a manner. The latter had always been cold-natured, and everyone in the White Jade Sect said Chuyan resembled her master the most. Who could have known she could utter such sweet words?","But then again, even her own Unshakable Daoist Heart had wavered, let alone Chu Chuyan’s.","Even so, it feels weird seeing this young couple murmuring such sweet nothings to each other, especially when the man is my man, too. She was shocked when that thought popped into her head. She hurriedly drove it out.","While embracing Chu Chuyan, Zu An noticed Yan Xuehen’s discomfort. He was also feeling uncomfortable, especially since he could tell Chu Chuyan was intentionally doing this as an act in front of her master.","Yan Xuehen will probably explode if she finds out that I helped Chu Chuyan fool her, but if I reveal it now, it’ll also cause an uproar...","He could only try his best to balance both sides. He broke the awkwardness with a light cough and asked, “Chuyan, how did you know I was here?”","Chu Chuyan chuckled. “I’d be as good as dead if I didn’t hear a thing when you were speaking so much. However, it takes some time for me to wake up. A certain fellow had already left when I last woke up, leaving me to deal with this Oblivion River alone.”","Sensing her grudge, Zu An felt apologetic. “I should have just woken you up if I'd known.”","“I was worried you’d leave right after seeing me again, so I set up a formation to wake myself up as soon as you arrived. It’s a relief that I did that, or else you might have left after seeing me once more.” Chu Chuyan eyed Yan Xuehen as she spoke, thinking to herself that Zu An had likely brought the latter here to tour the area.","Haaa, why would someone as incredible as my master fall for this pig?","Yan Xuehen’s heart skipped a beat. Can her formation record information? If so, she would have seen Zu An hugging me earlier... The thought of that was driving her insane, causing her to continue prattling, “Chuyan, I came here to meet you. I only looked for Ah... him to bring me here.”","Chu Chuyan eyed Yan Xuehen in surprise. “Master, you used to hate Ah Zu. Your attitude toward him seems to have changed a lot.”","Yan Xuehen anxiously explained, “I was worried you’d be deceived by his lies—that would have hindered your cultivation. Now that I know him better... I have to admit he’s a decent person. My view of him is different now.”","Chu Chuyan was speechless. You didn’t want me to be deceived, but you ended up getting deceived yourself.","After being kept in the dark for so long, she wanted to return the favor, so she had to keep her thoughts to herself. She harrumphed. “What’s decent about him? He’s full of flaws, especially his philandering ways. His eyes wander the moment he sees someone beautiful.”","Yan Xuehen agreed with those words. That fellow would be perfect if he weren't so lustful.","What Chu Chuyan said next nearly made her heart leap out of her chest. “Master, you’re also incredibly beautiful. I hope Ah Zu hasn’t done anything rude to you?”","“He’s been very proper around me...” Yan Xuehen said with a guilty conscience. She reflexively thought about Zu An’s barbaric ramming, and that made her face heat up.","“Is that so?” Chu Chuyan assessed her playfully before turning back to Zu An. “Ah Zu, you mustn’t bully my master, all right?”","“Of course. I respect Sect Master Yan as my master, too.” Zu An decided to shut his mind down and not think too much about it. These two women are putting their acting skills into play. I could tear up. It’s just that the information asymmetry placed Yan Xuehen in a disadvantageous position right from the get-go.","Yan Xuehen felt as if a storm was raging in her usually calm mind. How can Ah Zu be so thick-skinned as to say such words? He respects me as his master too? Do you ride on your own master?","Chu Chuyan grabbed Yan Xuehen’s hand and gently said, “Master, I can’t be with him for now. You have to help me keep an eye on him, lest I find myself with an army of sisters when I return.”","Yan Xuehen’s guilt was at an all-time high. How can I let down Chuyan’s trust in me? I’m not worthy to be someone’s teacher. I can’t continue hiding this anymore. “Actually, Chuyan...”","Chu Chuyan saw through her intention and interjected, “Ah, I nearly forgot. That fellow wouldn’t be tied down so easily. I heard the stories you shared with me the last time you were here. You got involved with more women in the past, didn’t you?”","Yan Xuehen’s courage was shattered by Chu Chuyan’s interjection, though at the same time, she was also curious about what Zu An had gone through.","“There’s no new woman. They're all people I know,” Zu An replied sheepishly. With two incredibly beautiful women staring at him simultaneously, he was bound to feel guilty even if he had done nothing wrong.","It was fun watching the master-disciple duo playing against each other. No wonder ancient emperors were so fond of inciting infighting among the princes and the crown prince. Otherwise, the princes could unite against them.","“How can you already know people from the past?” Chu Chuyan doubted his words.","“I thought I shared the details with you?”","“I was deeply asleep. I could only sense someone talking to me, but I don’t remember the details.”","Zu An had no choice but to share the details with her again.","Yan Xuehen was flabbergasted. She'd thought their experiences in the dungeon were shocking, but to think that such mystical encounters were commonplace for him. No wonder he grows so quickly!","“Manman was the ancient Goddess of Wu Mountain, whereas Teacher Shang was the ancient Mermaid Queen...” Chu Chuyan was astonished to realize that the people around her had such secret identities.","“Did you meet my previous incarnation? How about my master’s?” Chu Chuyan asked curiously.","Yan Xuehen was alarmed. “Why are you dragging me into this?” But she was intrigued too. Somehow, it feels weird if he got together with someone who resembles me in the ancient era.","“I didn’t see your previous incarnations.”","Chu Chuyan was disappointed. “Looks like Manman and Teacher Shang are more special...”","Zu An huffed, “They might be their previous incarnations, but I’d say that they're different people. Beneath their identical appearances lie completely different personalities.”","“You must have enjoyed it,” Chu Chuyan scoffed.","Zu An was speechless. There’s no way to placate you, is there?","Yan Xuehen burst into laughter. Looks like Chuyan is the only one who can curb him.","She was about to ask more about the deities when Chu Chuyan suddenly said, “Ah Zu, I’d like to talk to my master in private.”","Zu An was curious to know what she was going to talk about, but it wouldn’t do for him to eavesdrop when she was asking for privacy. Thus, he nodded and flew off.","Now that they were alone under the Bridge of Helplessness, Yan Xuehen suddenly felt nervous.","“Master, there’s something weird about you,” Chu Chuyan suddenly remarked.","“What’s weird about me?” Yan Xuehen felt her hair stand on end.","“I’m usually the one nervous around you, so why are you nervous around me now? That’s how the women Ah Zu had outside usually react whenever they see me,” Chu Chuyan assessed her playfully.","“Ah?” Yan Xuehen’s mind went blank. It’s over. She knows."]},{"number":2715,"title":"Chapter 2715: Chapter 2667: A Higher Level","paragraphs":["Many thoughts flashed through Yan Xuehen’s mind. Awkwardness and embarrassment gushed into her mind, overwhelming her.","But Chu Chuyan suddenly grabbed her. “Master, I know you’re worried about me, but you can put your mind at ease. I’m already used to it. It’s not that different from when I was cultivating in seclusion in the White Jade Sect; it’s just a change of environment. You know I prefer quiet. Staying here might be an ordeal to others, but it’s not difficult for me.”","“Ah?” Yan Xuehen blinked. Is that what she wants to say? She finally understood what it meant to have a guilty conscience. After breathing a sigh of relief, her conscience got to her, and she said, “Chuyan, I...”","But Chu Chuyan didn’t give her the chance to speak. “Master, I wasn’t joking about that. I won’t be able to accompany Ah Zu for a thousand years, so can you take care of him on my behalf?”","Yan Xuehen panicked. “How can I take care of him...”","“Ah Zu is strong, but he’s still young. As the saying goes, ‘deity at a whim, demon at another’. Master, you should stay with him and guide him. If he strays down the wrong path, I fear that no one will be able to stop him,” Chu Chuyan said.","The serious talk cleared Yan Xuehen’s mind a little. She solemnly nodded. “Alright.”","As the leader of the orthodox path, the duty to uphold justice was ingrained in her. What Chu Chuyan mentioned could potentially happen, and that would spell a calamity for the world.","Seeing her master’s grim expression made Chu Chuyan snicker on the inside. I know Ah Zu’s personality well. He might stray when it comes to women, but he won’t make a mistake in other matters.","She had only said that to give Yan Xuehen a valid pretext to stay by Ah Zu’s side. When she first learned about her lover getting together with her master, she was angry, but many things had happened since. She'd gone on a long journey and even traveled along the river of time under different identities. This was minor compared to everything she'd been through.","Furthermore, she knew her lover well. He was a philanderer at heart, and it didn’t help that he was handsome and powerful. It would be hard for other women not to be charmed by him. I’d rather my master benefit than other strangers out there. At least we’re keeping it within our lineage. My master is the most outstanding woman in the world. Countless heroes were awed by her back then and courted her. She only remained single for so long due to our cultivation methods and her personality.","Chu Chuyan had previously wondered what man could win over her master, and had even tried finding a dao companion for her. Who could have known that her master, who had shown no interest in other men, would fall for her lover? Should I be proud or angry?","To top it off, those two had only gotten together due to her ‘Snow Lady’ condition back then. It was a trick of fate for her to have playedd matchmaker between her master and her lover.","Many years of interacting with her master gave her a good grasp of her master’s temperament. She knew her master couldn’t overcome her guilt, and it was evident from the other party’s conscience-stricken expression and distracted attitude. This matter had to have been weighing down on her mind.","Intense emotional fluctuation was a taboo for her master’s cultivation method. At this rate, it could become an inner demon.","But Chuyan knew her master cared about her reputation and was easily embarrassed. If she was too direct, it wouldn't be beyond her master to draw her sword and end her life on the spot. So, she had to advance slowly and let her master slowly grow accustomed to this relationship.","Haaa, my lover and my master are hooking up behind my back, and I still have to give them a push. This sure is hard on me. She felt exhausted.","But when she thought about how she was playing her lofty master like a fiddle, she soon smiled with glee. I bet she’ll show the most interesting expression when the truth comes out...","The corners of her lips curled upward. She didn’t feel as indignant anymore.","Yan Xuehen grabbed her disciple’s hand as she vowed, “Chuyan, I’ll find a way to free you.\"","Chu Chuyan wanted to tell her master not to concern herself with something that even Zu An was helpless about, but she was worried that such words would wound her master’s pride. So, she replied with a smile, “Thank you, master.”","The two of them chatted for a long time. By the time she came out to beckon Zu An over, Yan Xuehen’s eyes were red. She said, “She wants to meet you.”","“You cried?”","Zu An instinctively tried to wipe her tears, but Yan Xuehen stepped back while nervously looking at the Bridge of Helplessness. Despite knowing that Chu Chuyan couldn’t see them here, she felt awkward.","Before flying under the Bridge of Helplessness, Zu An cast a spell on Yan Xuehen to protect her soul.","“I told my master to take care of you. She agreed,” Chu Chuyan said with a smile.","“How’s that possible?” Zu An narrowed his eyes skeptically. “Did you tell her the truth?”","“Of course not,” Chu Chuyan scoffed. “She still doesn’t know I know, so don’t you dare tell her. Otherwise, I’ll never forgive you.”","“Fine...” Zu An couldn’t understand what was going through her mind, but he could only go along with her. I’ll leave it up to time to resolve this issue.","Chu Chuyan rested her head on Zu An’s chest. “Ah Zu, I’m worried about your trip to Dreamland...”","“It could be a fortuitous encounter too. Either way, it’s something I’ll have to overcome. We can’t remain stuck here, or else we’ll be helpless if trouble comes knocking.” Zu An thought about the monsters and the Annihilation Beast that had destroyed the Monster World.","This was a Wonderpoint World, but that could still be insufficient against the universal deities. Given that Zhao Yuan and the others had obtained a universal deity’s annihilation energy, his gut feeling told him it was a matter of time before more trouble arrived.","Besides, there was something he wanted in Dreamland.","The two of them cuddled and chatted for a long time. However, it was soon about to be daybreak in the mortal world. Chu Chuyan was worried that Yan Xuehen’s soul would sustain damage if she stayed in the Netherworld for too long, so she reluctantly bade farewell.","While Zu An was taking Yan Xuehen out of the Netherworld, the latter suddenly said, “Ah Zu, about the universal deities you mentioned earlier, I think I came into contact with a similar power before.”","“What?” Zu An was startled. “Which deity did you come into contact with?”","Yan Xuehen was uncertain. “I don’t know. I didn’t see its physical form. It was a pitch-black world with a tinge of white around it. I sensed a peculiar power. It was even stronger than the Absolute Dispassion that I pursue.”"]},{"number":2716,"title":"Chapter 2716: Chapter 2668: A Stronger Fourth Universal Deity","paragraphs":["“A pitch-black world, white light...” Zu An was at a loss. He had never heard of such a deity. He hurriedly asked, “What were the circumstances leading to that encounter?”","Yan Xuehen pondered it. “I was flipping through an ancient notebook in our sect’s library, searching for a way to save Chuyan, when I was transported into that pitch-black world. I felt unprecedented, immense pressure weighing down on me, making me shudder. I also felt a void that could make a person forget everything... It’s hard to describe that sensation with words.”","Zu An continued asking, “What was the ancient record you were reading?”","“The notebook contains the insights of an elder from history whose identity is unknown. Its contents are all over the place, mentioning an even higher level than Absolute Dispassion. That book has been shrugged off as nonsense, left in a corner to collect dust. While searching for a way to save Chuyan, I couldn’t leave a single stone unturned, so I browsed through it too.”","The daoist sects had always thought that the highest level achievable was Absolute Dispassion, but that unknown author claimed there was a higher level. Unsurprisingly, his words were shrugged off as nonsense.","As Yan Xuehen shared the notebook’s contents, Zu An frowned. The details were all over the place, sounding like a lunatic’s ramblings. It was understandable why the text had been so poorly regarded across the generations.","The past Zu An might have shrugged it off as a lunatic’s delusion as well, but now that he had more information about higher levels, he thought about another possibility. “That unknown elder might have unknowingly caught a universal deity’s attention, but the universal deity didn’t favor him and chose not to bestow him power.","“His mind and cultivation weren't strong enough to withstand the universal deity’s pressure, causing him to go insane. That could be why his notebook resembles a madman’s ramblings.”","Yan Xuehen was taken aback. “Is catching a universal deity’s attention that dangerous?”","“That’s also what I’m perplexed about.” Zu An assessed Yan Xuehen. “You might have caught that universal deity’s attention after reading that notebook because your daos are aligned, but you fared much better than that elder—you didn’t lose your mind. However, I don’t sense special powers within you either. It doesn’t seem as if that universal deity bestowed you with power.”","For instance, Zhao Yuan and the Shadow Group’s assassins had been aligned with the Deity of Annihilation’s dao and were bestowed with its power, resulting in the rapid advancement in their cultivation.","Yan Xuehen had grown significantly stronger, but that was the result of her aptitude and the enrichment of the world’s ki. It didn’t seem to be the deed of a universal deity. But if she hadn’t been bestowed with the universal deity’s power, she should have gone insane from the latter’s terrifying pressure. Her current situation was perplexing.","“Even so, something seems to have changed within me. I can sense a higher level than Absolute Dispassion, and my cultivation speed is faster than ever. Sometimes, when I cultivate too quickly, I enter a state of emptiness. It feels as if I've cast aside my human emotions, and everything has become meaningless.”","Zu An widened his eyes in realization. “No wonder you were so distant when we first reunited.”","“Rubbish. It has nothing to do with that!” Yan Xuehen averted her gaze.","“It has everything to do with it,” Zu An replied seriously. “I thought it was because you'd reached a higher level in your Unshakable Daoist Manual, but thinking back on it, it was more likely that you were affected by your audience with the universal deity.”","“But I didn’t meet any deity then.” Yan Xuehen was nervous. They were dealing with deities here, after all. She feared that she would end up in the same situation as that elder.","“That’s why I’m confused...” Zu An pondered about the matter, but he knew too little about universal deities to say for sure. So, he telepathically called out, “My beautiful master, do you know which deity did big sister Yan encountered?”","Mi Li lazily replied, “You only call me when you need me.” She manifested beside Zu An as she spoke, though only Zu An could see her.","“I didn’t want to disturb your rest,” Zu An replied with a fawning smile.","“Aren’t you disturbing me now?”","“Desperate times call for desperate measures. Master, do you know which universal deity Sect Master Yan encountered? Is she in any danger?”","Mi Li sneered, “Tsk. You were calling her big sister Yan earlier, only to draw a line before me and call her Sect Master Yan now. Are you worried that I’d be jealous?”","“Of course. You’re big sister master. How can I call other people big sister too?” Zu An replied earnestly.","“You have a sweet tongue.” Mi Li chuckled. “I overheard your conversation. There is indeed a universal deity who fits that profile, but I can’t say for certain. That universal deity is known to be disinterested in mortal affairs, so I can’t imagine him gazing upon a mortal.” She sounded confused as well.","“Disinterested in mortal affairs?” Zu An narrowed his eyes. “That resembles the state of Absolute Dispassion that Sect Master Yan strives for. Could the alignment in their daos and that elder’s notebook have drawn the universal deity’s gaze?”","“That is possible.” Mi Li nodded.","“Who’s that universal deity?” Zu An asked.","“You’re getting ahead of yourself. Do you think I can carelessly reveal a universal deity’s name?” Mi Li scoffed.","“That’s true.” Zu An nodded.","“But you don’t need to worry. It would make sense for that woman to not be bestowed with power if it was that universal deity who gazed at her. That deity is known to be disinterested in everything. He has never actively bestowed power to his disciples,” Mi Li replied.","Zu An was still worried. “What a wasted opportunity. I've heard that most people only receive a universal deity’s gaze once in their lifetime, and other universal deities steer clear of such individuals.”","Yan Xuehen had a chance to meet a universal deity but didn’t receive any power. Does this mean she won’t be able to obtain the powers of other universal deities either?","“Who says there’s only one chance to receive a universal deity’s gaze? That might be true for most people, but such rules don't apply to special entities. Besides, having a single universal deity isn’t a bad thing. Yan Xuehen’s universal deity is an extremely strong entity, even stronger than the ones you know of.”","Zu An was stunned. The universal deities he currently knew about were the Deity of Memory Meng, Deity of Chaos and Enigma Mi Li, and the Deity of Annihilation. And yet, none of the three was as powerful as the universal deity whom Yan Xuehen had encountered?"]},{"number":2717,"title":"Chapter 2717: Chapter 2669: Forgetting Everything","paragraphs":["“But Sect Master Yan got nothing out of that encounter,” Zu An pointed out.","“Nothing? Just sensing that universal deity’s power is a huge benefit. Yan Xuehen said herself that her cultivation speed is much faster than before,” Mi Li lazily replied.","“Are there any disadvantages to this?” Zu An was still worried.","“There are. Under that universal deity’s influence, Sect Master Yan may lose her human emotions and forget many things. There might come a day when she forgets about you too,” Mi Li gloated.","“What?!” Zu An was horrified. “Are there any solutions?”","“What solutions can I possibly have? This is a universal deity’s dao influence. If I could interfere in that, I’d be a universal deity too.” Mi Li rolled her eyes.","There was a long moment of silence before Zu An raised his head to look at Mi Li. “Does that mean I can only save her if I become a universal deity?”","“Perhaps.” Mi Li sounded unsure. She looked at him playfully. “Despite your carefree attitude, you go all out whenever something involves your lovers. Do you think it’s that easy to become a universal deity?”","“Humans ought to have something to work toward,” Zu An replied.","Mi Li stared at him in a daze before snapping out of it. “That’s a good attitude. I believe you’ll eventually succeed one day.”","Zu An eyed her skeptically. “Are you keeping something from me?”","“What could I be keeping from you?” Mi Li yawned. “You interrupted my sleep. I’m going back into hibernation. Don’t disturb me if there isn’t anything important.” She disappeared in a puff of smoke.","Zu An frowned. He felt there was something amiss about Mi Li’s earlier expression, but there was nothing he could do when the other party refused to speak.","“What’s wrong, Ah Zu?” Yan Xuehen called out.","“Ah, it’s nothing.”","“You were in a daze earlier. Did you figure out which universal deity I met?” Yan Xuehen asked nervously.","After some thought, Zu An decided to reveal some information. “I don’t know that universal deity’s name, but he appears to be a formidable being You probably caught his attention because his dao aligns with the Absolute Dispassion you're pursuing...”","He shared what he had just heard from Mi Li. Yan Xuehen was a top-notch expert and had a strong dao heart. Rather than concealing things from her, it would be better to give her a heads up so she could prepare herself in advance.","“You’re saying I might start forgetting things...” Yan Xuehen’s face paled. Despite pursuing Absolute Dispassion, she was seeking only to forget some human emotions, not to relinquish all her emotions, bonds, and memories.","“These side effects might only start to show as you advance further in that universal deity’s dao,” Zu An explained.","Yan Xuehen was silent for a long while before letting out a sigh. “What’s the point of becoming strong if I have to forget everything? Can’t I pursue a different dao from that universal deity?”","“We don’t know enough about universal deities to know the implications. Don’t worry too much for now. On the whole, this is good news for you. Let’s go with the flow and see how it goes for now.” Zu An patted her hand and consoled her.","“How can this be good news? At this rate, I’ll forget about Chuyan and you...” Yan Xuehen’s face reddened as soon as she blurted those words out.","Zu An was overjoyed. He embraced her and said, “I didn’t know big sister Yan cared so much about me.”","“You’re overthinking it.” Yan Xuehen tried to push him aside out of embarrassment.","But Zu An held her tightly. “Stay close to me. You might get sucked in by the Netherworld otherwise.”","“Nonsense! We’re already out of the Netherworld,” Yan Xuehen grumbled.","Zu An belatedly realized they were currently flying above the sea. He calmly replied, “You’re still in your soul form. The slightest carelessness may result in the dissipation of your soul. We might be out of the Netherworld, but you still shouldn’t let your guard down.”","Yan Xuehen bit her lips and held her tongue, allowing Zu An to hug her as he pleased. But when she felt his breathing against her neck, she couldn’t bear it anymore and complained, “Stop staying so close to me.”","Zu An sighed. “You might forget me in the future. I’m afraid I might lose you if I stray further.”","Yan Xuehen’s heart softened. She also feared this situation. But if I can forget everything, perhaps I can put an end to this ill-fated entanglement...","Her attention was quickly drawn back to the present. “Where do you think you’re touching?!”","“I don’t want to lose you.” Zu An made her anger dissipate with a single line.","There was a long silence before Yan Xuehen replied, “Me neither.”","After hearing her true feelings, Zu An couldn’t hold himself back anymore and sealed her lips.","Yan Xuehen’s body stiffened, but it soon fell limp. A ridiculous thought flashed across her mind. Chuyan told me to take care of him. Does this count too?","But she was more concerned about something else. If I’m going to forget everything in the future, I should cherish every day I have with him.","Jolts washed over her like relentless waves. She was taken aback. “Why does it feel so intense...”","“Souls are more sensitive,” Zu An explained.","“How would you know...” The truth dawned on Yan Xuehen as soon as she asked the question. He must have done this with other women before!","You have successfully trolled Yan Xuehen for +22... +22... +22...","But her fury was swiftly quelled by his tenderness.","Zu An took her to the clouds. It was freezing up there, but cultivators of their level were impervious to the cold. On top of that, the warmth radiating from Zu An’s body made Yan Xuehen feel sluggish.","“How beautiful!”","“How beautiful...”","The two of them remarked in unison.","Yan Xuehen was startled. Her remark was directed at the starry sky, but Zu An’s remark appeared to be directed at her. Unbeknownst to her, Zu An had unfastened her robe.","She clutched her belly and crossed her legs out of embarrassment. With the starry night sky reflected in her eyes, she whispered, “Only two more times.”","Zu An nearly burst into laughter. He hadn’t expected her to be keeping count, though he knew that she was the kind of person who couldn’t put down her pride unless given a legitimate excuse.","“Alright.” Needless to say, he wouldn’t argue about the validity of their agreement right now.","Yan Xuehen tightly embraced the man before her while staring at the stars in a daze. Somehow, she felt bolder than usual. The rules and restrictions she usually imposed on herself faded away. Her cheeks reddened like peach blossoms. With a wave of her hand, she wrapped them in a layer of fog.","Zu An was surprised. “Aren’t you blocking the beautiful night sky?”","“It feels weird to do it in the wild...” Yan Xuehen’s voice grew meeker with each word. She knew it was unlikely for others to bump into them at this altitude, but she felt insecure.","Zu An agreed with her. Who knows if there are entities in the sky looking at us? So, he wove the clouds together to form a miniature world around them.","Yan Xuehen was surprised by the familiar scenery. “It’s the White Jade Sect!” Even her room had been reconstructed in full.","“Would you feel more comfortable being in your room?” Zu An asked with a tender smile.","Yan Xuehen felt embarrassed. You’re making me more nervous with this atmosphere. But she knew he meant well, so she chose not to say anything to dampen the mood.","Zu An also projected his soul and walked over to her side.","Yan Xuehen felt her head spin. This fellow has no sense of shame. I was wearing clothes when I projected my soul, but he...","“Since you don’t want to be in your room, let’s head to the White Jade Sect’s other landmarks,” Zu An said with a mischievous laugh. He lifted her and carried her to the square in front of the sect hall."]},{"number":2718,"title":"Chapter 2718: Chapter 2670: I’ll Never Forget You","paragraphs":["Despite knowing this wasn't the real White Jade Sect, the sight of the familiar square still made Yan Xuehen nervous. “What are you doing?”","“I knew Sect Master Yan wouldn’t allow me to do it in the White Jade Sect, so I could only construct another one.” Zu An gleefully toured the area with her in his arms. “Does it look similar?”","Similar? It’s identical! Yan Xuehen thought to herself. She was awed by his ability to remember the details despite having only been there once.","But recalling his purpose for recreating this scene made her embarrassed and angry. He's the god of this world now, yet he’s using his powers for such nonsense!","“Don’t do it here. It feels weird.” Yan Xuehen’s fair skin was now so red that it looked as if blood would ooze out of it.","“Is it because there are no disciples here? That isn’t a problem.” Zu An waved his hand, conjuring figures wearing the White Jade Sect’s uniforms and carrying the White Jade Sect’s swords.","Yan Xuehen was stunned. She felt as if she had really returned to the White Jade Sect, especially when two nearby disciples noticed her and walked over to greet her.","“Paying respects to Sect Master Yan.”","Yan Xuehen was so embarrassed that she hurriedly buried her head in Zu An’s arms, not daring to reply. If there were a hole in the ground, she would have leaped into it without any hesitation.","She knew that these figures were fake, evident from their spiritless eyes, but Zu An’s ability to reconstruct the White Jade Sect and its disciples was still ridiculous. The thought of the usually stoic Sect Master Yan being carried into the White Jade Sect’s most sacred hall and bullied in front of its disciples made her tremble nonstop.","“Are they not real enough for you? Unfortunately, I can’t construct real humans yet. Why don’t I take you back to the White Jade Sect? We should be able to get there in the blink of an eye,” Zu An whispered to her.","“No!” Yan Xuehen exclaimed. She would die of shame if she returned to the White Jade Sect in her current state.","But when she saw Zu An’s mischievous grin, she knew right away that he was teasing her.","“You!” Yan Xuehen was so angry that she bit his shoulder. He’s terrible! No wonder Chuyan was fooled by him!","You have successfully trolled Yan Xuehen for +55... +55... +55...","Zu An laughed. With a wave of his hand, the surrounding ‘White Jade Sect disciples’ dissipated. “Looks like you’re satisfied with this place.”","Yan Xuehen gritted her teeth. She couldn’t say she was dissatisfied, or else Zu An would probably just bring her back to the White Jade Sect. He had always been fearless and brazen, and now that he had grown this strong, no one could stop him anymore.","She thought about Chuyan’s request and earnestly lectured him, “Ah Zu, with great power must come great responsibility. You mustn’t use your abilities on such nonsense.” She thought that she had to correct Zu An lest he go overboard. It would be a huge pity if he went down the wrong path.","Zu An kissed her ear and whispered, “I’ll stop messing around... if you promise me.”","The sensation made the sensitive Yan Xuehen shudder. After hearing his words, her face heated up. “How can you threaten me? How are you any different from the Devil Sect then?”","Zu An burst into laughter. “Oh, there is a huge difference. Countless Devil Sect experts have dreamed about taking advantage of the leader of the orthodox sects, the White Jade Sect’s Immortal Yan. None of them have succeeded to date, but I did.”","Yan Xuehen groaned in agony. This fellow is so shameless that there’s no reasoning with him!","“Fine. Do whatever... you want. But you mustn’t speak like that ever again.”","“It’s a deal.”","...","Yan Xuehen had never observed the White Jade Sect from this angle, but very soon, she learned the number of glass tiles on top of the White Jade Sect’s gates, the number of bricks in front of the hall, and the number of candles and incense sticks inside the hall...","In the end, she mustered her final sliver of demureness and meekly said, “You've already used up the three times I promised you...”","Zu An was amused. “This only counts as once.”","Yan Xuehen became agitated. “How can this count as once? From the gate until now...”","She was too embarrassed to continue speaking. This fellow is like a demon king!","Seeing the lofty immortal revealing such mortal emotions further stoked Zu An’s excitement. He hugged her tightly in his arms. “I’ll make sure you never forget about me.”","Yan Xuehen realized that his actions were driven by the fear that she might forget him one day. That filled her heart with tenderness. She gently accepted everything and said, “Ah Zu, I’ll never forget you.”","...","Meanwhile, Pei Mianman looked at the ethereal fairy from the peak of the academy’s Mount Yuquan. “Sect Master Yan?”","She'd been in the Devil Sect when Zu An suddenly transported her here. It was to let Ji Xiaoxi and Xie Daoyun reunite with their family members. She was heartened by the sight, but she was also envious of the kinship they shared.","She'd wanted to have a private chat with Zu An, but the latter had gone on to lecture for three straight days in the academy. She couldn’t find an opportunity to approach him.","She'd excitedly rushed over here to look for Zu An when he finally concluded his lecture, but when she entered, the latter was nowhere to be found. Instead, there was a beautiful woman.","She'd thought that Zu An was hiding a lover, but at second glance, she realized that the woman was Yan Xuehen and was taken aback.","She knew Yan Xuehen was Chu Chuyan’s master, and she was aware of Yan Xuehen’s resounding reputation in the Dao Gate and among the orthodox sects. However, her impression of Yan Xuehen shattered when she bumped into her getting steamy with Zu An.","“Sect Master Yan?” Thinking it would be inappropriate to just turn around and leave, Pei Mianman tried calling out to her. Is she here for a secret liaison with Ah Zu? But he isn’t here.","But the other party didn’t respond, leaving Pei Mianman perplexed. With her cultivation, even if she was asleep, she should have awakened when I called out to her.","Taking a closer look, she noticed Yan Xuehen’s snowy skin had turned red, and her breathing was ragged. She seemed to be moaning in pain.","“Is she having a cultivation deviation?” Pei Mianman was taken aback. Be it for Chu Chuyan or Zu An, she couldn’t turn a blind eye to this.","She thought about treating Yan Xuehen to stabilize her condition, but she was worried that her intervention could worsen the situation instead. This made her panic.","Yan Xuehen was panicking too. She could vaguely hear sounds, and that made her pale in horror. “Ah Zu, I think there’s someone next to my body.”","Zu An smiled. “Don’t worry. You’re fine.”","He already knew that it was Pei Mianman, which was why he hadn’t activated the formations.","But Yan Xuehen was still worried. “There really is someone there! It seems to be Miss Pei.”","Knowing he couldn’t hide it anymore, Zu An projected the situation inside the room with a wave of his hand. “See, you aren’t in danger. She won’t hurt you.”","Yan Xuehen nearly fainted. She was already embarrassed about doing it with Zu An, and it definitely didn’t help that a junior was looking at her! Her soul was thousands of kilometers away, but the soul and the body were intricately linked.","If Pei Mianman figures out what’s going on, I should just smash my head into a block of tofu!"]},{"number":2719,"title":"Chapter 2719: Chapter 2671: Exposed","paragraphs":["Zu An was startled when he sensed the anomaly in her body. He had no choice but to give in. “All right, let’s rush back.”","Yan Xuehen angrily bit him. “I’ll never forgive you if she finds out about us!”","Zu An looked at her. “She's already seen us together.”","“You still dare to speak!” Yan Xuehen felt as if she would lose her mind. This fellow sounds so gleeful about that!","“Relax. She won’t notice anything amiss,” Zu An said with a smile. All of a sudden, however, his expression stiffened. Why is she here?","A beautiful figure flitted across the moonlit sky. The academy’s defensive formations didn’t affect her in the slightest. It didn’t take her long to arrive at Mount Yuquan’s peak.","The formations Zu An had constructed around the courtyard were about to automatically attack her when she harrumphed. “Is this how you treat a guest?”","Sweat rained from Zu An’s forehead. He quickly halted his formations remotely.","The beautiful figure nodded in satisfaction. “That’s more like it.” She walked into the courtyard.","Sensing something amiss, Yan Xuehen hurriedly asked, “Who is it?”","Zu An had no idea how to explain, so he said, “Take a look for yourself.”","He projected the situation in the courtyard into the air, revealing a long-haired, red-robed beauty.","Yan Xuehen was speechless. She furiously pummeled Zu An’s body. “Return right now! That demoness will figure it out if she sees it!”","The red-robed beauty was Sect Master Yun Jianyue. Unlike Pei Mianman, Yun Jianyue was a master of seductive arts. With her wealth of experience, she could figure out what was going on at a glance.","The two had been archenemies for many years now. The thought of Yun Jianyue learning about her relationship with Zu An sent shivers down Yan Xuehen’s spine.","Zu An laughed. “Don’t worry. No one's thoughts will go in that direction. Besides, Manman will stall her.”","Yun Jianyue entered the courtyard.","A vigilant voice echoed from within. “Who is it?”","Pei Mianman rushed out, only to be taken aback when she saw the red-robed beauty. “Sect Master Yun!”","Yun Jianyue hadn’t expected someone else to be in the courtyard. Her face heated up. Good thing I didn’t say anything intimate earlier. I’d die of embarrassment if others knew about it. “Miss Pei.”","Looking at the long-haired silhouette under the moonlight, Pei Mianman had to concede that Yun Jianyue was truly gorgeous, especially with her imposing disposition as the master of the Devil Sect. That sparked her vigilance. Why would she visit Ah Zu in the middle of the night? There’s no way that lustful Ah Zu can resist a beauty of her caliber!","In the past, she would have never thought of that, but what happened with Yan Xuehen made her realize that everything was possible. She asked, “What brings Sect Master Yun here?”","Yun Jianyue had met Pei Mianman before, but each time they met, she couldn’t help but wonder what the latter had eaten to grow so big. She had an impressive figure too, but it was lacking compared to this young lady.","She keenly sensed animosity in Pei Mianman’s words. I won’t stoop to getting into a catfight with my disciple’s friend. The only one who's a match for me is that stone cold woman... but there’s no way that woman would have anything with Ah Zu.","She had considered matchmaking Zu An and Yan Xuehen so she wouldn’t be the only one to die of embarrassment if her relationship with Zu An was exposed. Unfortunately, she hadn’t had a chance to do so thus far.","“I heard Zu An had returned, so I came here to ask about Honglei.”","Pei Mianman secretly breathed a sigh of relief. “Don’t worry, Sect Master Yun. Ah Zu has managed to save Honglei—I met her a few times myself. She’s still in a feeble state, as the immortal medicine isn’t enough to heal her impaired soul. She needs plenty of rest to recover, but she should be almost well now.”","Yun Jianyue was overjoyed. “That’s wonderful news. I’d like to meet her. Where’s Zu An? It’s been a while since I arrived, so why is he not here?”","“Ah Zu isn’t here.” Pei Mianman was perplexed about that as well.","“He isn’t here?” Yun Jianyue was confused. She sensed another presence inside the courtyard, but there were too many defensive formations here to tell who it was.","She'd thought that Pei Mianman had been messing around with Zu An, and had come out here to drive her off. She could understand why Pei Mianman would do that, but she couldn’t accept Zu An implicitly allowing it to happen.","Her anger surged. “Regent, don’t you think it’s inappropriate for you to remain hidden when a friend has come to visit?”","Zu An sighed. She must be truly angry to address me as ‘regent’.","Yan Xuehen was perplexed. Why is Yun Jianyue angry?","“Sect Master Yun, you've misunderstood. Ah Zu isn’t inside...” Pei Mianman explained.","The lack of response from Zu An further stoked Yun Jianyue’s anger. She thrust her palm, destroying the windows by the side. “Putting on airs with me? Regent...”","She froze before she could finish speaking. The person in the room wasn't Zu An, but someone else beyond her wildest imaginations. “Ice sculpture, what are you doing here?”","But Yan Xuehen didn’t respond.","Pei Mianman walked up to her with a frown. “Sect Master Yun, do you now believe me when I say that Ah Zu isn’t here?”","“Where is he? And why is this woman here?” Yun Jianyue’s head was spinning.","“I don’t know either. I just arrived.” Pei Mianman was worried. “I tried calling out to Sect Master Yan, but she hasn't responded. Now and then, her face turns red and her breathing becomes ragged, as if she’s suffering cultivation deviation.”","Yan Xuehen’s reputation as an ice-cold beauty was so striking that it was unthinkable for her face to turn red.","“Her face turns red?” Yun Jianyue narrowed her eyes in doubt. She walked over to inspect Yan Xuehen’s condition.","Yan Xuehen trembled. Her mind turned blank. “I’ll kill myself if she finds out about it!”","She looked so serious that Zu An didn’t dare continue teasing her. With a flash of rainbow light, they returned to Mount Yuquan.","Yan Xuehen returned her soul to her body. She tried to stand up and walk away, but her legs caved in and she fell to the side. Fortunately, Pei Mianman quickly grabbed her arm to support her. “What’s wrong, Sect Master Yan?”","Yan Xuehen's face was burning red. She dared not reply, fearing that her voice would sound too coy and give her away.","Yun Jianyue’s gaze alternated between her and Zu An. Looking at Yan Xuehen’s perplexing behavior, a thought popped into her mind. “What were the two of you... doing?”"]},{"number":2720,"title":"Chapter 2720: Chapter 2672: Different Intentions","paragraphs":["Yan Xuehen was scared out of her wits. Having dedicated her life to fighting Yun Jianyue, she would be lucky if she got away with a tattered reputation after stealing her disciple’s man.","Zu An spoke up and said, “I took Sect Master Yan’s soul to the Netherworld to visit Chuyan.”","“Soul projection?” Pei Mianman widened her eyes in realization.","“Can a living person’s soul enter the Netherworld?” Yun Jianyue asked in astonishment.","“It shouldn’t have been possible under normal circumstances, but with my current strength, I can bring a person in, though it’s only limited to the soul,” Zu An replied gleefully. He had to be the only human in the world capable of this feat.","“That’s wonderful! I want to go to the Yellow Spring Road to examine those Red Spider Lilies.” Pei Mianman was overjoyed. She hadn’t been able to do much with her Paramita Butterfly. Taking a look at the Red Spider Lilies could help her reap some benefits. She turned to Yan Xuehen and asked, “Sect Master Yan, did you see the Red Spider Lilies? Are they beautiful?”","Yan Xuehen had enough time to regain her composure. “Yes, they are unforgettably beautiful.”","Pei Mianman’s eyes twinkled in excitement. She was already imagining how romantic it would be for her to stroll through a field of Red Spider Lilies with her lover.","But Yun Jianyue wasn’t that easily fooled. She eyed the two of them and asked, “Are you sure that’s all?”","Zu An replied with a smile, “What else could there be?”","Yun Jianyue pushed on with narrowed eyes, “A person’s senses are heightened in soul form. Did you do anything impolite to the ice sculpture?”","Before Zu An could reply, Yan Xuehen harrumphed. “What do you mean by that, demoness?” She was nowhere as confident as she appeared, but she knew it would appear more suspicious if she didn’t fight back when her archenemy was slandering her.","Zu An secretly shot Yan Xuehen a thumbs-up. Who could have thought the cold Yan Xuehen would be such a wonderful actress? Is acting second nature to all women?","Yun Jianyue burst into laughter. “What else could I mean? I don’t believe you two didn’t get intimate while he was escorting you to the Netherworld.”","Yan Xuehen replied with a cold face, “Indeed, but we have nothing to hide.”","There was no way to hide this matter. The other women would know right away when Zu An took them to the Netherworld. It would be unwise to lie about this matter. Please forgive me, founder of daoism...","For some reason, she had been lying more than ever after meeting Zu An.","Zu An was worried that Yan Xuehen couldn’t cope with the situation alone, so he helped to explain, “She needed to remain within a meter of me in the Netherworld, so some physical contact was inevitable. I’d never disrespect Chuyan’s master.”","That single line made the three women present blush.","Yan Xuehen thought about how she had been thoroughly taken advantage of.","Yun Jianyue felt conscience-stricken. She was Qiu Honglei’s master, after all. Hmph, this won’t do. I must make sure that stone cold woman suffers the same plight before our relationship is revealed, or else I’ll become a laughingstock.","Pei Mianman alternated her gaze between Zu An and Yan Xuehen. She knew that the two of them had a thing, so she decided to quietly watch their performance. I’m not surprised by Ah Zu’s acting skills, but Yan Xuehen usually appears so dignified and upright. I didn’t expect her to be such a good liar too.","Yan Xuehen was starting to feel uncomfortable. She quickly replied, “Regent, thank you for bringing me to meet Chuyan. I should return to my seclusion now. I shan’t impose on you any further.”","She turned around and left.","Zu An panicked. He couldn’t bear for her to leave so quickly.","However, Yun Jianyue moved even faster. “Ice sculpture, we have known each other for many years now. Isn’t it impolite of you to leave just like that? You should stay a few more days.”","Yan Xuehen’s face reddened. More like being played with for a few days if I choose to stay. But she refused to give in. “I have nothing to say to you. Or are you looking for a fight?”","“Sure. I’ve been wanting to challenge you to a fight—my cultivation has advanced a fair bit recently. You won’t chicken out, will you?” Yun Jianyue sneered.","Yan Xuehen couldn’t stop herself despite knowing it was a taunt. “Hah, of course not.”","“Then let’s fight right now.” Yun Jianyue rolled up her sleeves.","Pei Mianman secretly laughed. The leader of the Devil Sect and the leader of the orthodox sects, yet they're acting like a pair of countryside aunties.","Yan Xuehen looked away. “Not now. My soul is still affected by the Netherworld’s death energy. I’ll need some time to recuperate.”","Her legs were still trembling from the earlier ordeal. She wouldn’t be a match for the demoness in her current state.","“Fine, I shan’t take advantage of your weakness. I’ll wait a few days for you here till you’re ready to challenge me,” Yun Jianyue replied.","Zu An also interjected, “Sect Master Yan, you should stay here a couple days more. There are many things regarding Chuyan and the universal deities that I need to discuss with you.”","Yan Xuehen snorted in her mind. What an obvious lie. In truth, she couldn’t bear to leave either, so she used her duel with Yun Jianyue as an excuse to stay.","Zu An settled her down in the neighboring room. This was the old libationer’s residence. Out of respect for the old libationer, there were no other residences in the vicinity other than his.","Yan Xuehen didn’t want to interact with anyone else in the academy. She figured that Ah Zu wouldn’t mess around when there were other people in the courtyard, so she agreed to it. She quickly found an excuse to take her leave and rest in her room.","I feel as if my body is in tatters even though it was just a union of souls...","Yun Jianyue looked at Yan Xuehen’s fleeing silhouette and frowned. “Something feels off about the ice sculpture.”","Pei Mianman, who had guessed the truth, looked at Zu An and snorted.","Feeling conscience-stricken, Zu An asked Yun Jianyue about the reason behind her visit.","“What else? I’m here to look for my darling disciple. Do you think I’d be here for you?” Yun Jianyue couldn’t reveal their intimate relationship as Pei Mianman was around too.","Zu An smiled sheepishly. “I just visited Honglei not long ago. She’s on the verge of a full recovery.”","“I can’t rest at ease until I see her in person.” Yun Jianyue was nervous. Qiu Honglei had left home and met with a mishap after witnessing her affair with Zu An. This matter had been weighing on her mind.","Zu An nodded. He understood how she felt, so he took off his pendant. A cave paradise soon manifested in the courtyard. He brought the two women inside.","A beautiful figure rushed out from the place and leaped into Zu An’s arms. “You heartless thing. You haven’t visited us for a long time now. Did your feelings change?” She pummeled him as she spoke.","Zu An felt a headache settling in. That tone... It can only be Black Jing Teng.","When they saw the beautiful lady dressed in black lace acting coyly around Zu An, Yun Jianyue and Pei Mianman’s faces darkened.","You have successfully trolled Yun Jianyue for +66... +66... +66...","You have successfully trolled Pei Mianman for +66... +66... +66..."]},{"number":2721,"title":"Chapter 2721: Chapter 2673: Laying It Out","paragraphs":["Black Jing Teng noticed the other two women present and pouted in displeasure, but she quickly changed her expression and coyly nuzzled against Zu An’s chest. “Ah Zu, why don’t you bring them in to play together? I don’t mind it.”","Yun Jianyue was speechless. What do you mean by play?","Pei Mianman was startled. Of all people, Miss Jing has to crack a joke with Sect Master Yun. That’s a bona fide demoness there!","But she quickly remembered that Jing Teng was a sealed demoness herself and chuckled under her breath.","Zu An felt a headache setting in. “Stop messing around. I brought them here to visit Honglei.”","Black Jing Teng huffed. “You still dare to speak about that! Our agreement is for you to occasionally drop by and nourish us if we help you take care of her. We fulfilled our end of the bargain and even gave our house to her, yet you hardly visited us at all.”","Yun Jianyue snorted at Zu An. “Take your time nourishing her. I’ll check on Honglei.”","You have successfully trolled Yun Jianyue for +77... +77... +77...","Pei Mianman rolled her eyes too. “I’ll check on Honglei too.”","You have successfully trolled Pei Mianman for +77... +77... +77...","While Zu An was feeling stressed out, Black Jing Teng visibly turned white.","“Little sister, you’re kicking up a fuss again.” White Jing Teng’s disposition was conspicuously different. She was elegant and dignified, completely unlike the eccentric woman from earlier.","Yun Jianyue and Pei Mianman instinctively halted their footsteps. They knew that the two sisters were sharing a body, but it was still shocking to see it.","White Jing Teng directed a nod at the two women. “Pardon us for earlier. She’s still young and immature. I hope you won’t hold it against her.”","Yun Jianyue and Pei Mianman were rendered speechless. Aren’t you the same age as your little sister? And the two of you are old enough to be our ancestors!","But it didn’t seem appropriate to hold a grudge when White Jing Teng was earnestly apologizing to them, so they replied, “Of course not, Miss Jing.”","Black Jing Teng angrily protested inside, “What do you mean, immature? Those two women are our love rivals! Why are you being so polite to them? We should reveal Yun Jianyue’s affair with Ah Zu and have those two cows fight it out, so we can sit back and reap the benefits.”","They had noticed the intimate interactions between Zu And and Yun Jianyue the last time the latter came to visit Qiu Honglei. It wasn't hard to guess their relationship from that.","White Jing Teng suppressed her little sister’s urge to drop the explosive news, and instead gracefully smiled at the two women. “Come, let me take you to Miss Qiu.”","At the same time, she reasoned with her little sister, “That’s too shallow. They'd soon realize that we were driving a wedge between them. Have you considered how Ah Zu would view us?”","Black Jing Teng was dissatisfied. “Are you going to watch as Ah Zu flirts with them?”","“Why resort to despicable means when we can just watch it play out?” White Jing Teng replied with a mysterious smile. “This is a hidden card that only we know about. We should hold onto it for now.”","Black Jing Teng was taken aback. “Big sister, you’re more evil than me.”","...","Jing Teng led the way. Looking at her graceful gait, Pei Mianman murmured, “That waist and that bum... If I were a man, I wouldn’t be able to stand it.”","Yun Jianyue was worried too. Ah Zu has so many top-notch beauties around him. How can Honglei fend against them alone? Should I lend her a helping hand?","Her face heated up as soon as that thought popped into her mind, and she cursed at herself. Jianyue, when have you become as hypocritical as that stone cold woman? Do you truly intend to help Honglei?","The door to the distant wooden cottage creaked open, and a beautiful figure walked out. “Big sister Jing, Ah Zu...”","Qiu Honglei had been resting when she heard voices outside, so she came out to take a look. Halfway through her greetings, she noticed Yun Jianyue and froze up. “Master...”","Her heart was plunged into turmoil. She didn’t know how to face Yun Jianyue. Should I call her master or big sister?","She had always respected her master, and her master took good care of her too. But whenever she recalled the sight of her master and Zu An getting together above the Lake of Hatred, her heart still hurt.","Pei Mianman was unaware of the tension between the master and disciple. She rushed forward to support Qiu Honglei. “Honglei, you've gotten skinnier. It feels as if you'd topple over in a stiff breeze. Was the food I brought you not to your taste?”","Pei Mianman had accompanied Zu An several times when he visited Qiu Honglei. The two of them knew each other from their time at Brightmoon City. There had been conflicts between them then, but after everything they had been through, those had been long forgotten.","“Manman~” Qiu Honglei grabbed Pei Mianman’s hand and smiled. “I haven’t had much of an appetite recently.”","They had quickly grown closer due to the frequent visits.","“That’s how it is when recovering from an illness. Try going for some bland food first and rest well,” Zu An said.","Qiu Honglei nodded. She knew her master was here too, but she didn’t know how to face her.","Pei Mianman didn’t notice the anomaly between them. “Honglei, Sect Master Yun is here to visit you. She's been here before, but you were still unconscious then.”","Qiu Honglei’s heart quivered. In the end, she called out, “Master~”","She couldn’t talk about her master’s relationship with Ah Zu here, as there were others around.","“Honglei!” Unable to hold herself back anymore, Yun Jianyue embraced Qiu Honglei. “I’m sorry for putting you through so much misery.”","The guilt she had been suppressing for many years poured out, and tears streamed down her cheeks. She believed that if not for her affair with Zu An, her disciple wouldn’t have left the Devil Sect and met with a mishap.","Feeling the moisture on her shoulders, Qiu Honglei remembered the care and concern her master had shown her. Had things gone awry, they might have never met again. That caused her to burst into tears as well. “Master...”","Seeing this, Pei Mianman turned to Zu An and said, “We should give them some space.”","As he knew about the situation between them, Zu An was hesitant.","White Jing Teng nodded too. “It has been a long time since the two of them met. They must have a lot to say to each other. We shouldn’t disturb them.” She took the lead by walking away.","Zu An could only follow suit. He wished Yun Jianyue good luck before leaving as well.","Yun Jianyue felt nervous. She had never been so nervous, not even when she was faced with mountains of corpses and seas of blood, or even Zhao Han. She'd never thought she would be afraid to face her disciple.","The door closed, and the room plunged into silence. The crying master and disciple stepped away from each other and straightened their postures.","It was Yun Jianyue who first broke the silence. “Honglei, I've been worried about you. It’s a relief that Ah Zu found the immortal medicine and saved you.”","“Ah Zu is indeed capable,” Qiu Honglei muttered. “How else could he have won your heart?”"]},{"number":2722,"title":"Chapter 2722: Chapter 2674: Battle Plan","paragraphs":["Yun Jianyue’s expression stiffened. She bitterly said, “I’m sorry, Honglei.”","Seeing her proud master apologizing in such low spirits softened Qiu Honglei’s heart. “Master, can you construct a formation to prevent sounds from getting out?”","Yun Jianyue knew that Qiu Honglei was going to lay things out. She was flustered, but she didn’t turn down the request. “Alright.”","She constructed a barrier. “They can’t listen to our conversation anymore.” Though I won’t be able to stop Ah Zu if he wants to eavesdrop.","Qiu Honglei looked at her. “Master, how did you... get together with Ah Zu?” That was what she was most curious about. Her master wasn’t the type to stoop to stealing her disciple’s man.","“I sustained severe injuries during Lu Sanyuan’s rebellion. To save me, Ah Zu...” Yun Jianyue began.","Qiu Honglei interjected before Yun Jianyue could finish speaking. “I know about that. He did it to save you, and I don’t blame either of you for that. But that wasn’t your first time, right? You know what I’m getting at.”","Yun Jianyue’s face heated up. She had imagined this situation countless times and thought about how to deal with it, but now that she was faced with it, she found that her mind went blank instead. In the end, she sighed and replied, “It started with a misunderstanding...”","She explained what had happened after Zu An absorbed Sir Fu’s ki.","Qiu Honglei’s face darkened. “Ah Zu forced himself on you?”","Yun Jianyue shook his head. “He was suffering from an inner demon from his breakthrough to essence form stage, but I couldn’t have helped him if I wasn’t willing too.”","Qiu Honglei’s heart swelled with jealousy upon learning the full story. “You were already together that early on. I was the third party...” Even though I came first...","Yun Jianyue anxiously exclaimed, “That’s not it, Honglei. I got in between your feelings. I'm the despicable one.”","“Master, don’t put yourself down. It’s beyond humans to control their feelings.” Qiu Honglei sighed. “It’s all Ah Zu’s fault for being a philanderer.”","Yun Jianyue looked at her worriedly. “Honglei, you can punish me however you wish to, but you’re currently in a feeble state. You shouldn’t bottle up your feelings. You’ll only hurt yourself.”","Qiu Honglei smiled. “Master, do you know what I’m the angriest about?”","Yun Jianyue bitterly replied, “I failed to uphold my duties as your master and stole your man. Anyone would be angry about that.”","“That’s not it,” Qiu Honglei replied, much to Yun Jianyue’s bewilderment. “I’m angry that you chose to keep it from me.”","Yun Jianyue was speechless.","“It’s one thing for Ah Zu to keep it from me, but master, why did you keep it from me too?” Qiu Honglei’s eyes glimmered, making it impossible to tell how she was feeling.","“How could I talk about that?” Yun Jianyue was frustrated as well. “I wanted to shrug that incident off as a beautiful mistake and erase Ah Zu from my life, but things happened afterward...”","Qiu Honglei sighed. “Ah Zu is indeed an unforgettable man, not to mention he’s shameless and tenacious. He wouldn’t give up on a beauty like you.”","“You know him well.” Thinking about how the culprit behind this mess had escaped scot-free made Yun Jianyue grit her teeth in anger.","You have successfully trolled Yun Jianyue for +33... +33... +33...","“Master, it’s one thing if this happened to Chuyan and Sect Master Yan, but I’m disappointed that you were so indecisive and even chose to hide it from me.” Qiu Honglei sounded aggrieved. “We are the Devil Sect’s demonesses, practitioners of the Bewitching Dance! We should be free from the shackles of social convention. We've seen plenty of such things from the sisters around us. Do you think I’d be fazed by your relationship with Ah Zu?”","“I have disappointed...” Yun Jianyue noticed something amiss halfway through her sentence. “Ah?”","Qiu Honglei bit her lips. “I mean it, master. I would have been jealous and angry if I were Ah Zu’s only woman, but he’s a philanderer! He has countless lovers, and they're all beautiful and outstanding women. I can’t deal with them alone. We could have worked together if you had told me earlier. The other women out there wouldn’t have stood a chance against us!”","Yun Jianyue blinked. She tried touching Qiu Honglei’s forehead. “Are you serious?”","“Of course!” Qiu Honglei exclaimed. “Such things are common in our Devil Sect! There are also similar instances between fellow disciples, blood-related sisters, and even... You're the master of the Devil Sect, so why are you following the hypocritical conventions of the orthodox sects?”","Yun Jianyue awkwardly replied, “But it’s a different story. Our sect members do those things to attain greater power or to vent their lust, whereas we...”","“True love, huh?” Qiu Honglei interjected.","Yun Jianyue couldn’t take it anymore. “Fine, you’re even teasing me now! Don’t you feel the same toward Ah Zu too?”","“Of course I do,” Qiu Honglei replied with tender eyes. “I believe Ah Zu feels the same about us too. So, we can’t let Ah Zu do worse than those scum in our sect. Good people deserve to be bullied.”","Her twisted logic left Yun Jianyue’s head reeling. “Honglei, you have a novel perspective.”","Qiu Honglei crossed her arms. “Master, Ah Zu is always looking to fool around. If we were going to have another sister, do you think I’d prefer it to be a stranger or you?”","Yun Jianyue’s heartbeat hastened. “Honglei, do you really not mind?”","“What I mind is you not telling me the truth. We could have stopped other vixens from slipping in through the cracks.” Qiu Honglei lay in her master’s arms with a tear flowing down her cheek.","How could she not mind? But the other party was her master. Yun Jianyue had taken good care of her, doted on her, taught her how to cultivate, and provided her with a safe shelter.","While disciples of the Devil Sect were indignant that the orthodox sects labeled them as demonic, deep down, they knew that it was a fitting label. The Devil Sect believed in the survival of the fittest, and the ends justified the means. With Qiu Honglei's beauty, were it not for her master’s protection, some elder in the Devil Sect would have long used her as a cauldron for nourishment.","For the longest time, her master was her sky. It was home to her wherever her master was. Having been orphaned at a young age, Yun Jianyue was more than a master to her. She didn’t want her master to be burdened by guilt for the rest of her life and perhaps even leave an inner demon behind. Their ties couldn’t be allowed to fracture over a man.","Although, she meant what she had just said too. Zu An was indeed a terrible philanderer. Rather than benefiting outsiders, she would rather let her master in on the pie.","Yun Jianyue tightly embraced her disciple. Having raised Qiu Honglei, she could see through the latter’s intentions. She murmured under her breath, “Thank you, Honglei.”","All of a sudden, Qiu Honglei frowned. “Oh no!”","Yun Jianyue was stunned. “What’s wrong?”","“We can’t let others know about this, especially not Sect Master Yan and Chuyan. Otherwise, we’ll never be able to lift our heads in front of them.”","Yun Jianyue had fought with Yan Xuehen all their lives, whereas Qiu Honglei and Chu Chuyan were rivals, as they were both the Holy Maidens pushed forth by their respective sects.","“Don’t worry, I’ll keep my distance from Ah Zu to keep them from learning about it,” Yun Jianyue replied.","Qiu Honglei rolled her eyes. “Master, do you think I’m trying to pressure you using the same hypocritical tactics that those orthodox sects? It goes against our Devil Sect’s style to retreat in the face of a challenge. We should be proactively making a move instead!”","Yun Jianyue’s heart stirred. “You mean...?”","Qiu Honglei’s eyes twinkled. “We’ll drag Sect Master Yan down too. Let’s see who mocks whom then. We're the Devil Sect’s demonesses; such things are no big deal to us. They, on the other hand, pride themselves on their principles. They're the ones who will be shamed!”"]},{"number":2723,"title":"Chapter 2723: Chapter 2675: Master and Disciple United","paragraphs":["Yun Jianyue’s eyes lit up. “As expected of the disciple I raised. You had the same thought as me!”","Qiu Honglei was surprised. “You also thought of that, master?”","Yun Jianyue nodded awkwardly. “I couldn’t stand the thought of being mocked by that ice sculpture for the rest of my life, so I thought I’d make her like me. Neither of us can mock the other then. I didn’t think that deeply into it, but I guess it’d indeed be more embarrassing for them.”","Qiu Honglei was enthused. “Master, how’s your progress?”","Yun Jianyue frowned. “My gut feeling tells me something is off about that ice sculpture and Ah Zu, but I can’t put my finger on it.”","“Tell me about it. What feels off?” Qiu Honglei asked with widened eyes.","Yun Jianyue shared the earlier incident, especially how unnatural Yan Xuehen looked when she returned to her body. “Their explanation made sense, but something seems to be off.”","Qiu Honglei nodded in agreement. “Indeed. How can Ah Zu not be tempted by someone as beautiful as Sect Master Yan? I didn’t think about it back then, but if he dares to touch even you, master, what else would he dare not do?”","Yun Jianyue’s eyebrows shot up. “You lass! You’re making fun of me!”","Qiu Honglei hugged her arm and coyly replied, “Master, I’m just stating facts here. Don’t take it to heart.”","Yun Jianyue continued, “Ah Zu has always been fearless and brazen. It is indeed likely for him to have made a move on that ice sculpture. But I've known that ice sculpture for many years. She isn’t the type who would get involved with her disciple’s man...”","Qiu Honglei grudgingly murmured, “Master, are you conceding that you’re inferior to Sect Master Yan in that aspect?”","Yun Jianyue harrumphed. “You said it yourself. We’re the Devil Sect’s demonesses. It’s more like us to be daring in that regard. How can you say I’m inferior to her?”","“Master, you've finally regained your usual flair.” Qiu Honglei chuckled as she leaned against Yun Jianyue and enjoyed the warmth they shared. This isn’t that bad either. I can be with master forever, and we can work together to deal with love rivals too.","“Honglei, what should we do to make that ice sculpture accept Ah Zu?” Yun Jianyue was vexed. She'd harbored that intention for a long time now, but she hadn’t found a way to achieve that.","“Shall we work together to knock out Sect Master Yan, strip her bare, and put her on Ah Zu’s bed? I don’t believe Ah Zu can hold himself back.” Qiu Honglei’s eyes twinkled.","Yun Jianyue looked at her disciple with a frown. She’s even more extreme than me.","“That won’t work. That ice sculpture is no weaker than me. If we work together, we can defeat her easily, but capturing her is a different story. Besides, I doubt Ah Zu will fall for it. He is lustful, but he isn’t the type to take advantage of others in their moment of weakness, not to mention that ice sculpture is Chu Chuyan’s master.”","Qiu Honglei nodded. Ah Zu is indeed not that kind of person.","“Should we injure Ah Zu and have Sect Master Yan offer herself to save him, just like what you did back then?” Qiu Honglei proposed.","Yun Jianyue gritted her teeth. She’s doing this on purpose, isn’t she? “Ah Zu is now so powerful. How can we injure him?”","“That’s true.” Qiu Honglei nodded. “Since there’s nothing we can do about Ah Zu, should we try drugging Sect Master Yan instead? Our Devil Sect’s Yin Yang Path has some potent medicine. Even you nearly fell for it back then, master. You should have some of it on you, right?”","Yun Jianyue was speechless.","Fang Zhonghe from the Devil Sect’s Yin Yang Path was fond of concocting such medicine, and she did have some on hand. However, she still turned down the tempting proposal. “That won’t do. That ice sculpture practices the Unshakable Daoist Manual; the medicine might not work on her. Even if it works, Ah Zu can heal her. We have to find a way to make her do it willingly. Otherwise, she’ll claim we schemed against her, and it won’t be fun to mock her after.”","Qiu Honglei giggled. “Master, I have to say you’re wrong. Considering Sect Master Yan’s personality, there’s no easy way around this, so we’ll have to do it step by step. Ah Zu can cure her poison, but that will require physical contact. Sparks are bound to arise from that. Even if they observe etiquette, their relationship won’t be as pure as it used to be.”","Yun Jianyue’s eyes lit up. “Your suggestion makes sense. Why didn’t I think about that?”","Qiu Honglei nuzzled against Yun Jianyue with an excited grin. “Master, when are we doing it?”","“You focus on your recuperation. Leave this matter to me,” Yun Jianyue replied. She already had an idea in mind.","When Yun Jianyue left the room, Zu An walked over and whispered, “Big sister Yun, how is it?”","Yun Jianyue knew what he was getting at, so she let out a sigh and said, “Honglei is still angry at me.”","Zu An gently comforted her. “It can’t be helped. You’re more than a master to her, and such a thing happened. Don’t worry too much. She just needs time for her feelings to settle down.”","Yun Jianyue was secretly delighted. She was probing Zu An to see if he had eavesdropped on their conversation, and it seemed the latter hadn’t. This made things easier for her. She said, “I’m thinking of staying here to accompany Honglei. Is that fine with you, regent?”","Zu An was overjoyed to hear that news. “Of course.”","Yun Jianyue’s expression suddenly turned serious. “Don’t let others know about our relationship, lest it affect Honglei.” Especially not Yan Xuehen.","“That goes without saying,” Zu An replied. “There aren’t many rooms in the courtyard. I’ll have to place you next to Sect Master Yan.”","“That would be best.”","“???”","“I mean, we are already familiar with each other.”","“You aren’t planning to fight and tear the courtyard down, are you?”","“Don’t worry, I won’t go that far.”","...","Black JIng Teng was observing the two of them from afar. They sure know how to act.","Zu An noticed how she had looked at the two ladies. He'd been planning to head out to settle Yun Jianyue into her room, but it wouldn’t be appropriate for him to just leave right now, as he hadn’t visited Jing Teng in a while. So, he decided to gather them together in the room and share what happened with them.","Qiu Honglei saw her master returning and initially thought their secret ploy had been exposed. She only breathed a sigh of relief afterward, upon learning that wasn’t the case.","“Shouldn’t we call the ice sculpture here to listen too?” Yun Jianyue asked.","Zu An shook his head. “I’ve already shared it with her on our way to the Netherworld.” I doubt the shy Yan Xuehen is in the mood to meet anyone after what happened earlier.","“You must have chatted a lot on the way,” Yun Jianyue replied with a tinge of jealousy.","Black Jing Teng asked, “Big sister, could there be something between Ah Zu and that Yan woman?”","White Jing Teng telepathically replied with a graceful smile, “It doesn’t matter. We’ll just watch the show.”","Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei were initially distracted, as they were busy considering how to scheme against Yan Xuehen, but their attention was soon drawn to Zu An’s story. Even though he had returned safe and sound, their hearts still thumped anxiously when they heard about his close shaves. In particular, they were shocked when they learned about universal deities.","Yun Jianyue remarked, “Actually, I sensed a powerful will summoning me a while back. I don’t know if it was one of the universal deities you talked about.”"]},{"number":2724,"title":"Chapter 2724: Chapter 2676: A New Universal Deity","paragraphs":["“What?” Zu An was taken aback. Yan Xuehen had previously received an audience with a universal deity and was on her way to forgetting everything. Who knew what kind of side effects Yun Jianyue would suffer? “Which universal deity did you encounter?”","He figured he could look after her if it was Mi Li, but on second thought, Yun Jianyue’s dao was nothing like Mi Li’s. The chances were unlikely.","Yun Jianyue’s face reddened. She began to stutter.","“Master, there are no outsiders here. Who is it?” Qiu Honglei said. The other two ladies here were fellow ‘sisters’, so there was no need to hide things from them.","Yun Jianyue hesitantly replied, “I didn’t see the universal deity; I merely sensed his presence. He seemed to be the Deity of Desires. I might have caught his gaze due to the special nature of my cultivation skill.”","The others exchanged glances. No wonder she’s embarrassed. It is indeed... embarrassing.","The awkward looks made Yun Jianyue more self-conscious. “Don’t misunderstand. There are more desires than just lust, such as greed, jealousy, and gluttony. They're all different types of desires...”","The others played along with her and nodded.","Yun Jianyue finally caved in and exclaimed, “Fine! I caught his gaze because of what you’re thinking. I’m the first person in the Holy Sect’s history to master the Voice of the Devil, after all.”","It was hard to tell who succumbed and laughed first, but the others began trembling uncontrollably too.","Zu An tried his best to suppress his laughter as he asked worriedly, “Has there been anything different since? Have you gained any new abilities, and do those abilities come with side effects?”","“I have indeed gained a new ability.” Yun Jianyue bit her lips. “I can stir a person’s lust much more easily now.”","Qiu Honglei was stunned. Hold up, that makes it easier for us to pull off our plan! To think I was worried about whether the Yin Yang Path’s medicine would work on Sect Master Yan!","“Really?” Jing Teng was intrigued. “How does it compare to Ah Zu’s special ki?”","The mention of that ki made all the women present blush. All of them had been victims of that.","“It’s compa...” Yun Jianyue was about to answer that it was comparable when it struck her. “Ah Zu’s special ki? What’s that?” I almost let it slip. I am Honglei’s master and Ah Zu’s elder. I shouldn’t know what effects his special ki has.","Qiu Honglei quickly added, “Ah Zu’s ki is rather unique. It’s normal that you don’t know about it, master.”","Jing Teng narrowed her eyes. Interesting. They 've already patched things up?","Black Jing Teng scoffed, “That master and disciple duo are so perverted. We were at odds for so long when we fell in love with Ah Zu at the same time.”","White Jing Teng sneered, “Is it? I thought you were primed to snatch whatever good things I have.”","Black Jing Teng was indignant. “Pui! I was the first one to go after him!”","While the two sisters were arguing, Pei Mianman asked, “Does it work on both sexes?”","Yun Jianyue’s face reddened. “It does...”","Qiu Honglei suggested, “Shall we give it a try?”","“On whom?” Yun Jianyue asked.","Ah Zu is out of the question. His ox-like stamina is no joke. What if he runs amok?","Honglei isn’t an option either. She’s still recovering.","Jing Teng is a senior, and for some reason, I’m a bit intimidated by her.","Thus, she turned her gaze to Pei Mianman.","When she realized that everyone was looking at her, Pei Mianman blushed. “Hold on. Why are you looking at me?”","Yun Jianyue hugged Pei Mianman. “Manman, why don’t you give it a try? Ah Zu is here anyway. He can help you if anything happens.”","Pei Mianman’s face was so red that it looked as if one could squeeze blood from it. This was too embarrassing!","Qiu Honglei blinked in confusion. “Master, when did you become so close to Manman?”","Their closeness didn’t seem feigned, but one was the Devil Sect’s master whereas the other was a second-generation disciple of the Dao Gate. That was quite an uncanny combination.","Sensing her confusion, Pei Mianman replied with a grin, “Ah, I haven’t told you yet. Honglei, your master and I are cousins.”","“Sisters?” Qiu Honglei was baffled.","Yun Jianyue nodded. “Manman’s mother is from the Yun clan too. She is my and Yuqing’s aunt. That makes Manman and me cousins.”","Pei Mianman hugged Qiu Honglei and mischievously said, “Honglei, now that I’m your master’s sister, shouldn’t you call me aunt?”","Qiu Honglei felt giddy. I merely slept for a while. How did my master become my sister, and my sister become my elder?","Yun Jianyue snatched her disciple back. “Manman, Honglei is still recovering. Let’s talk about this another day.” If we really wanted to go down this rabbit hole, we would all be fellow sisters.","Black Jing Teng remarked, “What a messy relationship they have.”","White Jing Teng agreed. “Indeed...”","Black Jing Teng took this chance to take control of their body. “Since no one wants to be the test subject, I’ll sacrifice myself.”","From her black stockings, the crowd knew that the little sister had taken control.","Black Jing Teng had a volatile personality, but she was the ideal test subject among them. Yun Jianyue accepted her offer and placed her finger on the latter’s body.","Black Jing Teng was still smiling when her face suddenly turned red. Her knees began knocking together. She looked toward Zu An with teary eyes. “Ah Zu~”","Her coy voice induced goosebumps in the other women. The others wondered if this was how she spoke whenever she was in heat with Zu An.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. He suppressed his lewd thoughts and focused on investigating Yun Jianyue’s new ability. “How are you feeling? Are you able to control yourself? When did the ability start taking effect...”","Unfortunately, Black Jing Teng was in no state to answer his question. She instinctively nuzzled against him. “Ah Zu...”","The others were stunned. Yun Jianyue’s ability is formidable!","Jing Teng had fallen to her ability despite not being an entity made out of flesh and blood.","Yun Jianyue coughed. It would be inappropriate to continue staying here, so she said, “I shan’t interrupt the two of you. I’ll take a rest outside first.”","Qiu Honglei’s face reddened too. “Master, it has been a while since I saw the outside world. Why don’t you take me outside?” It would be awkward to stay here and hear her lover getting steamy with another woman.","Pei Mianman quickly spoke up too. “Honglei, I’ll support you.”","The three women tactfully left the cave paradise.","Black Jing Teng pushed Zu An to the ground, her eyes glistening with lust. “There’s no one to disturb us now.”","Zu An was speechless. Why do I feel like a tool here?","Many years ago, when he was still a shut-in, his greatest wish had been to have a harem. Now that his wish had been fulfilled, he realized that having a harem wasn't easy at all. It was only recently that he'd had an unforgettable, soulful interaction with Yan Xuehen, but now, he had to deal with Jing Teng.","Even horse breeders wouldn’t push their steeds this far!"]},{"number":2725,"title":"Chapter 2725: Chapter 2677: Chill","paragraphs":["Yun Jianyue took Qiu Honglei to the lotus pond outside to enjoy the mountain breeze and the academy’s night scenery while chatting about recent affairs.","Qiu Honglei’s heart swelled with bliss. While Zu An occasionally took her out to breathe in some fresh air too, she had been too weak to admire the world’s beauty. Now that she was on the verge of a complete recovery, everything looked different to her.","While they were chatting, Yun Yuqing rushed over after hearing the news. Xie Daoyun and Ji Xiaoxi were busy having their family reunion, while Yan Xuehen was still overcoming her awkwardness. She was the only one left on the mountain peak.","She brought a thin blanket with her and wrapped it around Qiu Honglei. “Honglei, you’re still recovering. You mustn’t catch an illness at this point.”","“Thank you, Aunt Qing.” Qiu Honglei had known her master had a younger sister, but there had been no need for her to interact with Yun Yuqing as the two sisters had been estranged. But now that her master and Yun Yuqing had patched things up, she had to make sure to maintain etiquette.","Yun Yuqing was gorgeous. Qiu Honglei thought, No wonder she was known for her beauty back when she was King Wu’s consort, and Ah Zu fancies her.","This complicated relationship made Qiu Honglei feel awkward. Yun Yuqing was her aunt, but both of them were Zu An’s lovers, which made them sisters. But if they looked at it in terms of who had gotten together with Zu An first, she should have been Yun Yuqing’s older sister instead. But she couldn’t bring herself to tell an elder to call her ‘big sister’.","My seniority has been slipping while I was unconscious. Ugh, what a huge waste. Even Manman has become my aunt, and now there’s another, Yun Yuqing. How vexing!","She was tempted to drag Chu Chuyan here to experience the same frustration.","Yun Yuqing smiled. “Don’t call me aunt. That sounds weirdly old. We’re a family now. You can call me big sister instead.”","Qiu Honglei replied with a smile, “Shouldn’t you be the one to call me big sister?”","Yun Yuqing’s smile froze up, but she quickly replied, “That works too. It’d be great to have a big sister look after me.”","Yun Jianyue couldn’t take it anymore and interjected, “Preposterous. What are the two of you doing?” If Yun Yuqing calls Honglei big sister, won’t I have to start calling Honglei big sister too? There’s no way I can do that!","Pei Mianman could hardly hold her laughter in. “It’s right anyway. You can call her aunt, and she’ll call you big sister. I don’t see a conflict here.” It doesn’t affect my standing anyway.","Qiu Honglei hugged Yun Yuqing’s arm and coyly said, “Aunt Qing, don’t mind me. I was joking.”","It belatedly struck her that she would be putting her master in a tough spot if Yun Yuqing called her ‘big sister’. By the same logic, she would have to call Chu Chuyan ‘big sister’ in the future too. They were both the Holy Maidens of their respective sects, and the victor between them hadn’t been decided yet. She would bring shame to the Devil Sect if she admitted defeat in this field. That was unacceptable to her.","This little hiccup helped to mellow the mood, and the group chatted harmoniously.","Worried that Qiu Honglei couldn’t take the cold, Yun Jianyue had been grabbing her disciple’s hand and transmitting ki to her.","Pei Mianman smiled. “Leave it to me.” She conjured a flickering black flame at her fingertip and lit a few bonfires. It didn’t take long for the gazebo to become warm.","“Thank you, Manman.” Qiu Honglei could feel the concern others were showing her, and it brought warmth to her heart.","She had heard plenty of stories about her Devil Sect peers fighting over men. They would go as far as to beat their rivals to death. It was good that they didn’t have to scheme against each other for Zu An’s favor. I wonder where Ah Zu found these wonderful women.","Yun Jianyue showed interest in Pei Mianman’s black flames. “These flames carry the racial traits of the Devil races, but it isn’t as simple as that. It’s truly incredible...”","Just like that, they chatted for the entire night. It was only when they heard the roosters’ calls and saw the brightening hue on the horizon that they exchanged bewildered looks.","“They aren’t done yet?” someone in the group suddenly said.","All the women sighed. The man in the room was their lover, after all. The thought of him spending the night with another woman still sparked their jealousy, especially since they showed no signs of stopping.","“I’ll go check things out. It’s about time for Honglei to rest anyway,” Yun Yuqing said.","Qiu Honglei’s face reddened. “I’m fine. I can rest with master.” She didn’t want to be used as an excuse here.","Yun Jianyue wanted to discuss the details of their scheme against Yan Xuehen with Qiu Honglei, so she played along and said, “I’ll bring Honglei into the room to rest first.”","Just then, the cave paradise opened. Zu An staggered out while holding the walls for support. When he saw the women staring at him, he quickly straightened his posture and awkwardly asked, “You aren’t asleep yet?”","The women felt anger boiling within them. Yun Jianyue couldn’t lower herself to complain, so she glanced at her disciple and urged her to say something.","Qiu Honglei thought about the lengths Zu An had gone to save her and the meticulous care he'd shown her over the years. She couldn’t bear to say anything to him, so she turned her gaze to Yun Yuqing. Isn’t this the time for you to speak up?","Yun Yuqing felt indignant. Unlike you people, I was King Wu’s consort. We might not have done anything, but it makes it hard for me to complain about Zu An’s philandering ways. She turned her gaze to Pei Mianman.","Pei Mianman was speechless. You’re backing down now after all your big talk? But she was indeed displeased, so she asked, “Same to you. Aren’t you tired after doing it until now?”","Her words made Zu An feel even more awkward. Before he could say a word, Pei Mianman stood up and left. “I’ll head back in to rest.”","Qiu Honglei nodded. She didn’t want to get involved in their fight.","Yun Yuqing took her leave too. While she was walking by Zu An, she remarked with a chuckle, “Don’t go overboard lest you hurt your body.”","Now that he was alone, Zu An rubbed his waist. Black Jing Teng is a little temptress. She’s far more brazen than her big sister, daring to do everything. Each time she’s at her limit, she pushes White Jing Teng out to take the blow and returns only after resting up.","Isn’t it peculiar how, despite sharing the same body, the two sisters regain their stamina whenever they switch personas? How in the world do they do it?","He had to concede that his experience with Jing Teng was one-of-a-kind. The seamless transition between the dignified big sister and the eccentric little sister was an experience that couldn’t be described with mere words.","Under the influence of Yun Jianyue’s ability, White Jing Teng had been far more proactive than usual. She'd even pulled out her trump card—white stocking on one leg and black stocking on the other, simultaneously showcasing the traits of both sisters. It had quite the visual impact.","That, together with his earlier experience with Yan Xuehen, had driven Zu An to his limit. I mustn’t mess around like that anymore.","Meanwhile, Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei discussed their plan in their room.","Qiu Honglei was worried. “Ah Zu mentioned that Sect Master Yan has obtained a universal deity’s power too, further dampening her emotions. Master, will your ability work on her?”","“I’d have to give it a try to know.” Yun Jianyue was excited to pull one over her long-time rival.","In the neighboring room, Yan Xuehen felt a chill running down her spine. How weird. Why am I feeling cold?","She was aware of the earlier gathering in the gazebo, and she'd considered heading out to meet them. However, she'd decided against it in the end. They're all that fellow’s lovers. That demoness happens to be their kin, but what reason do I have to join the group?"]},{"number":2726,"title":"Chapter 2726: Chapter 2678: Battle","paragraphs":["In the neighboring room, Qiu Honglei eyed the wall and asked, “Master, could Sect Master Yan have overheard our words?”","Yan Xuehen was a renowned expert in the world of cultivation. It wouldn’t be surprising if she had the means to eavesdrop on their conversations.","Yun Jianyue proudly replied, “Don’t worry, I'm here. If she can overhear our conversation that easily, I might as well surrender to her.”","Qiu Honglei’s heart was put at ease. Master and Sect Master Yan have always been equally matched. There should be no problem if she said so. “Master, I’m also worried about something else. You saw Ah Zu’s earlier condition too. Miss Jing is simply too... energetic. I’m worried that Ah Zu’s body won’t be able to take it.”","Yun Jianyue frowned. “You’re worried about that fellow? He’s built like a bull!”","Lewd memories flashed through Qiu Honglei’s mind, and her face reddened. “But I've never seen him so weak before.”","Yun Jianyue nodded. “That’s true. We can’t underestimate those two sisters.”","The two of them fell silent. Considering their master-disciple relationship, it felt weirdly awkward for them to be talking about their lover’s prowess in bed.","Yun Jianyue changed the subject with a cough. “Your worry isn’t unfounded. It won’t be good if he fails to perform after we've drugged that ice sculpture. Let’s nourish him well tomorrow and keep an eye on the other women, lest they make a move.”","Qiu Honglei’s face reddened. “I’ll have to trouble you for that, master. It’s not convenient for me to move around, as I’m still recovering from my injury.”","Yun Jianyue rolled her eyes. “There’s nothing difficult about that. You can stall Miss Pei by chatting with her. Leave Yun Yuqing to me. As for Miss Xie and Miss Ji, they shouldn’t be a problem since they're busy with their family reunion.”","Qiu Honglei thought those words made sense. Master and Manman might be cousins, but they are from different generations. There are more common topics between me and Manman.","They continued discussing their plan to deal with Yan Xuehen. They were both intelligent individuals, and it didn’t take them long to devise a feasible ploy.","Zu An had barely rested for two hours when the teachers and students from the academy began streaming in to visit him. He couldn’t tell them that he was exhausted from his night activities, so he could only muster his energy to deal with them. Fortunately, he'd recovered most of his energy with just two hours of rest.","After he was done dealing with the academy’s affairs, Yun Yuqing entered the room with a bowl of chicken soup. “Ah Zu, you have been working hard recently. You need some nourishment.”","Zu An had expended too much energy in recent days, and the aroma of the chicken soup whetted his appetite. He took two sips, and his eyes lit up. “Did you make this? It’s delicious!”","“I can brew one for you every day if you like.” Yun Yuqing thought about how Yun Jianyue had secretly offered her pointers. Blood is indeed thicker than water.","She had never thought about personally cooking for Zu An. She'd been born into affluence and her family had plenty of chefs serving them. They had never needed to cook for themselves. But Yun Jianyue had told her that if she personally cooked for Zu An, the meaning would be different.","Yun Yuqing hadn’t expected that her elder cousin, despite being a feared demoness, had such a meticulous side. Even she hadn’t thought about brewing chicken soup to nourish Zu An.","Zu An took a few more sips. “It has a unique taste. What did you add to it?”","“Ginseng, deer antler, epimedium, cistanche, morinda root, eucommia bark, cynomorium, goji berry, red dates...” Yun Yuqing recounted the herbs she had used. This was Yun Jianyue’s recipe. The Devil Sect’s demonesses sure are knowledgeable.","Zu An was speechless. No wonder I feel a heat in my stomach after drinking the contents. He put the bowl aside and said, “There’s no need to add so many herbs.”","“Ah? You don’t like it? Big sister Yue says it’s beneficial for you.” Yun Yuqing was stunned.","Zu An was taken aback. So, it was Yun Jianyue’s idea? What is she planning, feeding me so much nourishment? Does she also intend to...","Yun Yuqing picked up the bowl and personally fed him. “Ah Zu, you need nourishment. You have been working hard in recent days, including lecturing in the academy...”","Zu An wanted to turn her down, but his stomach rumbled. He was feeling hungry, so he took the bowl and continued drinking. By the time he was done, his body felt warm.","Exclamations suddenly echoed outside.","“They're fighting!”","Alarmed, Zu An rushed out. Standing atop two of Mount Yuquan’s peaks were a black figure and a white figure—Yun Jianyue and Yan Xuehen.","“What are you doing?” Zu An shouted. I know you're rivals, but do you have to come to blows each time an opportunity arises?","Yun Jianyue replied, “This is between me and her. Ah Zu, you stay out of it. We agreed on this battle yesterday. I don’t mind postponing it another day if she hasn’t rested enough.”","“There’s no need for that.” Yan Xuehen’s voice was as cold as ever.","She'd had to postpone the fight yesterday because her legs were wobbling from Zu An’s pounding. She would have embarrassed herself if they fought there and then. But a night of rest coupled with Ah Zu’s rich ki nourishment put her in a better state than ever. She was determined to teach Yun Jianyue a lesson and let everyone in the academy know that the demoness was beneath her.","It was rather perplexing how, despite practising the Unshakable Daoist Manual, she couldn’t control her emotions whenever Yun Jianyue was involved.","The tense atmosphere between the duo stirred a commotion in the academy. Yun Jianyue and Yan Xuehen were renowned figures in the world. In particular, Yan Xuehen was viewed as a fairy and enjoyed great popularity. A showdown between these two was a huge deal. News quickly spread in the academy, and soon, even people from the capital rushed over.","“Waaa, Sect Master Yan’s skin is as smooth as rumored. No wonder she’s known as a fairy!”","“Of course! Don’t you know that back then, she was lauded as the number one beauty in the world of cultivation?”","“You’re blaspheming the fairy! Fairy Yan is devoted to pursuing the dao. She has no interest in such mortal comparisons.”","“I didn’t expect Sect Master Yun to be that beautiful.”","“Indeed. I have always heard she was a demoness who doesn’t hesitate to kill others, so I thought she would be a hideous monster with a bulky body. I didn’t expect her to be so beautiful. In terms of looks, she surpasses even Fairy Yan.”","“Nonsense. You clearly don’t have an eye for beauty. Nothing can surpass Fairy Yan’s transcendent beauty.”","...","Just their presence was enough to divide the crowd into two factions.","Yun Jianyue finally made her move. She unleashed a crescent moon that flowed in a beautiful arc before slicing through the mountain peak Yan Xuehen stood on.","Yan Xuehen flitted into the sky, avoiding the attack. At the same time, frost enveloped the mountain Yun Jianyue stood on.","Zu An’s eyelids twitched. At this rate, they’ll destroy the academy!"]},{"number":2727,"title":"Chapter 2727: Chapter 2679: Losing Control","paragraphs":["Zu An raised his hand and enveloped the nearby mountain peaks in a thin golden layer before shouting, “Please fight within this arena. Don’t go overboard in the fight.”","There was no lack of experts among the spectators in the academy, and they were all astonished by the strength of the golden layer. The academy often held tournaments as well, in which they inscribed similar formations on the dueling rings to prevent the shockwaves from destroying the academy’s buildings and harming innocent spectators. But the formations only spanned the size of a training field at most, and even so, they were always prepared days in advance.","However, the libationer had constructed such a massive formation in the blink of an eye, and it was strong enough to withstand attacks from top-notch experts like Sect Master Yan and Sect Master Yun.","The morning sun shone on the peaceful mountain valley, cloaking the lush mountain peaks in a golden sheet.","Two beautiful figures glared at each other in midair. Their brief clash had left the two of them shocked. They'd both thought that given their recent breakthroughs and the power bestowed by their respective universal deities, it would be an easy fight, but the other party had also grown beyond their imagination.","Under their glares, the air became so tense that it felt almost viscous. Upon sensing their murderous intent, the birds residing in the mountain forests fled in fear.","Yan Xuehen raised her hand, and her Flying Snow Sword emerged from its sheath. Its blade resembled a slender ice crystal that glimmered brilliantly under the sun. The light reflected could easily affect most opponents, but it wasn’t enough to even faze Yun Jianyue.","Yun Jianyue responded by lighting an ancient lantern. The flame inside the lantern was tiny, looking as if it would be extinguished at any moment, but its gentle brilliance instantly enveloped all the nearby mountain peaks. Even the sun paled in comparison to it. It felt as if the day had suddenly turned into night, and the ancient lantern was the moon.","Yan Xuehen’s Flying Snow Sword was no longer as brilliant as before, but she didn’t lose her composure. The sword vibrated, transforming the gentle mountain breeze into a powerful frigid gale. Snow began raining from the sky, cloaking the mountain peaks.","She slowly made her way toward Yun Jianyue, her every step leaving a beautiful ice crystal pattern. The air between her and Yun Jianyue froze. The incredible cold was reminiscent of a prison; it could even freeze the body and blood of a top-notch expert. On top of that, sharp ice crystals manifested out of thin air and whizzed toward Yun Jianyue.","“Your Snowflake Sword has advanced another level,” Yun Jianyue said with a chuckle. She gently stepped on an ice crystal before her silhouette blurred like fleeting moonlight.","The omnipresent ice cage could indeed trap all things tangible, but how could it imprison moonlight? Yun Jianyue’s body was incredibly fluid, dodging the incoming ice crystals with graceful movements.","Awed exclamations echoed from the academy. The younger students gulped.","“How beautiful...”","As someone who had mastered Bewitching Voice, Yun Jianyue’s every gesture and chuckle could siphon away a person’s soul. Now that she had received the Deity of Desires’ bestowment, even without her intentionally seducing them, normal people couldn’t hope to resist her charms.","As she flitted across the air, Yun Jianyue left silhouettes in her wake. By the time she appeared once more, she was already standing in front of Yan Xuehen. Her crescent glaives were as thin as a cicada’s wings, looking as if a glowing silver fluid was flowing within them; they seemed to be imbued with the moon’s power. They moved in a perfect arc, forming yet another full moon in the sky.","But the top-notch experts present sensed the danger of the full moon—it was formed by compressing immense force together. It surreptitiously swept toward Yan Xuehen’s waist, slicing through the raging snowstorm that was protecting her.","Yan Xuehen channeled the Flying Snow Sword, choosing to counterattack instead of dodging. Its sword tip precisely struck the edge of the full moon.","A weaker cultivator would likely have chosen to strike the moon’s body, but its weak spot lay in its perimeter. There was a crisp sound, and the moon shattered into specks of light.","Awed exclamations echoed outside the mountain valley. None of the spectators thought they could resolve this crisis as gracefully as Yan Xuehen.","Qiu Honglei tensed up. “Will master be alright?”","Yun Yuqing patted her head and said, “Don’t worry. Big sister won’t lose that easily.”","Yun Jianyue dashed through the specks of light and swiftly approached Yan Xuehen like a specter. It was as if she had cast aside her corporeal body, her steps leaving behind graceful black afterimages. No more than a handful of people in the academy could see her true body.","The earlier full moon attack had been a feint. She'd known that Yan Xuehen could unravel her attack, but the shattered specks of light would seep into the latter's body and slow her ki circulation for an instant. That was more than enough time for her to strike.","Yun Jianyue quickly weaved a tight moonlight net resembling a lover’s embrace with her crescent glaives. Her slashes were imbued with the ancient lantern’s moonlight energy, granting them incomparable sharpness and a tinge of law that affected its target’s movements and mind.","The mountain valley turned into her moonlight domain. No one except for Zu An could make out her silhouette, for every beam of moonlight was her!","Yan Xuehen’s expression turned grim. She held the Flying Snow Sword in front of her while manifesting swords of ice behind herself. The crisp buzzing of a blade echoed in the air. Her hair and robe fluttered as snow shrouded her body, forming a massive avatar of ice.","As she swung her blade down, the avatar behind her fused into her Flying Snow Sword, and she unleashed a powerful burst of blue sword ki that sliced the moonlight in two. The sword ki even reached the clouds on the horizon, cutting them in half as well.","All the spectators stood up and craned their necks to look at the distant blue hue with shocked eyes. If not for Zu An’s barrier, the capital could have been sliced in half as well.","Even Zu An was taken aback. The earlier slash had nearly shattered his barrier. It was a relief that he had reacted quickly and reinforced it. He had used his godlike powers to isolate this area into a mini world, but Yan Xuehen’s sword had the power to slice through that world! Her growth far surpassed his wildest imaginations.","“Master!” Qiu Honglei grabbed her sleeves. Even Yun Yuqing wasn’t as confident as before.","“Don’t worry, she’s fine,” Zu An said.","The brilliant moonlight in the mountain valley suddenly turned red. Even the moon in the sky transformed into a blood moon. A coy laugh echoed from the blood moon. “Ice sculpture, I didn’t expect your swordsmanship to have reached this level. I underestimated you.”","The crowd looked over. A beautiful figure was seated in the blood moon. Her sleeves had disappeared due to the earlier sword slash, but her fair arms, coupled with her amazing figure, left her oozing with seductive charm.","Zu An’s head hurt. This woman is unknowingly emanating the Deity of Desires’ power, and it’s affecting everyone in the academy!"]},{"number":2728,"title":"Chapter 2728: Chapter 2680: Mutually Injured","paragraphs":["It would be disastrous if everyone in the academy and perhaps even the capital went on a rampage, so Zu An took out his Violet-Gold Alms and lightly knocked on the bowl. A calming reverberation echoed through the academy, calming the fervent minds of the crowd.","The crowd widened their eyes in astonishment. They were all thinking, What got over me? I wanted to charge over as if I had lost my mind. No wonder she’s known as a demoness. Just looking at her made me lose control of myself.","The older students silently circulated their ki to calm themselves while instructing their juniors to close their eyes and not look anymore.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. The Violet-Gold Alms protected one’s soul from beguilement and damage. Yun Jianyue’s desire energy likely fell under the field of beguilement.","It was fortunate Yun Jianyue hadn't actively channeled that power, and the desire energy was divided across many individuals over a huge area, so its effect on each individual was limited. Thanks to that, the Violet-Gold Alms easily shook them out of their daze. Otherwise, they would have been in trouble.","Yun Jianyue was startled by the chaos, but she proceeded to laugh coyly afterward. That seduced quite a few people in the crowd yet again, so Zu An had to raise the frequency of his knocking on the Violet-Gold Alms to dispel the effects.","Qiu Honglei was perplexed. While master is skilled in the art of seduction, she doesn’t like to resort to that, which is why she usually puts on a fierce appearance. Yet she's now embracing the character of a temptress. Is it because Ah Zu opened her horizons, or is it the influence of the Deity of Desires?","Yan Xuehen frowned too. “Demoness, you have changed.”","“Aren’t you the same too? Your sword isn’t as emotionless as before. Did you recently meet someone you fancy?” Yun Jianyue chuckled coyly.","The spectators didn’t think much of it; they thought this was just a way for the demoness to shake Fairy Yan’s mind.","But Yan Xuehen felt conscience-stricken. Her expression turned cold, and she thrust her blade toward the blood moon. A resounding buzz echoed from her sword as blue frost rippled into her surroundings. Everything in the vicinity froze, and ice crystals reminiscent of diamonds dangled in midair.","“Why are you in such a rush?” Yun Jianyue chuckled, though her eyes narrowed ferociously.","The blood moon behind her suddenly flowed like a fluid, gushing forth and devouring the ice crystals in its way. The malevolent blood sea and the frigid ice crystals clashed and eroded each other. A thick fog broke out into the surroundings. It felt as if hell had manifested on earth.","Many spectators turned pale in fright. Their earlier lewd thoughts had vanished without a trace.","Zu An laughed. So, fear can dispel lust. He wondered whether to bring Yun Jianyue to the Netherworld to see the different hells. It could help her achieve a breakthrough in her Corpse Mountain Blood Sea domain. But on the other hand, that could affect her ‘desire’ dao cultivation.","Yan Xuehen’s reckless attack put her at a disadvantage in this clash. Her skirt was nicked, revealing her fair legs.","The crowd trembled in excitement. It was just her thighs, but the demure Sect Master Yan had never revealed them before.","Black streaks appeared on Zu An’s face. I feel like I’m the one losing even though they're the ones fighting. He could only console himself with the thought that the ladies in his previous world were dressed far more scantily than this.","The two women in the sky didn’t have the leisure to think about such things. They continued clashing inside the fog.","Yan Xuehen lived up to her reputation as the strongest expert of the Dao Gate. She knew she had slipped up and opted to maintain a defensive posture to slowly regain her momentum.","A while later, Yun Jianyue fully fused with the blood moon. All the moonlight and blood light converged together to form a single line. It pierced through the thick fog and locked onto Yan Xuehen, leaving her no room to escape.","Yan Xuehen’s expression tightened. As she became one with her sword, her Flying Snow Sword buzzed louder than ever. A beautiful blue hue reminiscent of ten-thousand-year-old ice glowed around her. Whatever the blue hue touched froze over.","The clash between the blades produced a sound that couldn’t be fully described with words. It resembled the call of a phoenix, or the clash between two stars.","Everyone’s hearts shuddered. This sight inexplicably deepened their understanding of the sword and the saber.","Time seemed to stop at this moment. There was no earth-shaking explosion; just the intersection and destruction of their energies and laws. The mountain range was split in two. One half turned into an ice field, whereas the other was dominated by the blood moon and sea.","The two women harrumphed before retreating a hundred meters away. Trails of blood seeped from the corners of their lips.","Yun Jianyue’s hair and clothes were coated in white frost. Even her breath immediately froze into ice crystals.","Yan Xuehen’s face and body turned red. A blood moon vaguely manifested on her body.","Alarmed, Zu An quickly stepped in between them and declared, “Let’s end this fight here. There’s no point continuing the fight, as your abilities are comparable to each other. At this rate, it’ll only end in mutual destruction.” His voice was firm and left no room for negotiation.","The crowd wasn’t surprised, as Zu An was unquestionably the strongest expert in the world. Most cultivator ranking boards didn’t include his name, as it was meaningless to do so. The gap between the first and the second place was too huge. Thus, his verdict was credible.","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue were both on close terms with Zu An, and they themselves knew that he was speaking the truth, so they clasped their fists and took their leave.","It was only when Zu An lifted the barrier that the crowd realized that there was a clear boundary within the mountain range. On one side were red trees and flowers, and molten flowing earth resembling the blood moon. On the other side was a pristine ice field. The vibrant mountain peaks had turned barren as a result of the fight.","Zu An turned to the crowd and said, “I believe most of you have gained something from witnessing the fight, but calm down and slowly unravel what you have learned. I’d recommend you go into seclusion to ponder hard. You may go now.”","With a wave of his hand, the desolate mountain peaks became verdant once more.","The crowd was awed. They bowed to him before taking their leave. As they left, they couldn’t help but discuss the battle and Zu An’s miraculous restoration of the mountain peaks.","Zu An quickly returned to the courtyard and first made his way into Yun Jianyue’s room. Qiu Honglei was so anxious that she was on the verge of crying, whereas Yun Yuqing was helping Yun Jianyue channel her ki to heal her injuries.","“You’re severely injured...” Zu An wanted to help her, but Yun Jianyue stopped him with a look.","“Don’t reveal our relationship. I have Yuqing and Honglei here to aid me, but the ice sculpture is alone. You should help her instead,” Yun Jianyue secretly relayed a message to him via her ki.","Zu An was taken aback. “Do you mean it?”","“Of course! Now that Chuyan isn’t with her, she’s alone. What do you expect her to do alone?” Yun Jianyue quickly replied. “As much as I want to defeat the ice sculpture, I don’t intend to take advantage of her weakness.”","“But you’re severely injured. Yuqing’s ki might not be enough.” Zu An was still worried.","“Manman is over there. Call her over to help me. The two of them should be enough to treat my injuries,” Yun Jianyue said.","Zu An agreed. Yun Yuqing and Pei Mianman weren't strong enough individually, but if they combined their strength, they could handle it. Besides, Yan Xuehen needed help as well, so Zu An told Yun Jianyue to take care before rushing to the neighboring room.","Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei exchanged expectant looks."]},{"number":2729,"title":"Chapter 2729: Chapter 2681: Anxious","paragraphs":["Qiu Honglei was taken aback. She sent a voice transmission and asked, “Master, have you already used your ability on Sect Master Yan?”","When she saw the two of them fighting, her heart had nearly leaped out of her chest. She'd been worried danger might befall her master. Yet her master had still managed to use that kind of ability in that tight situation?","“Of course. Why else would I push myself so far?” Yun Jianyue was gleeful because she had gotten to Yan Xuehen.","“Master, don’t take such risks ever again!” Qiu Honglei glared at Yun Jianyue. The thought of her master becoming severely injured made her shudder in fear.","“Don’t worry, I've been through plenty of danger in my life. I know what I’m doing.” Yun Jianyue harrumphed, unhappy that her disciple didn’t share her excitement in having succeeded in their plan.","“What are you murmuring about over there?” Yun Yuqing asked.","“Nothing. Just something worth celebrating.” Yun Jianyue smiled like a sly fox.","“Tell me about it,” Yun Yuqing realized her big sister had been less ferocious but more seductive recently.","“I’ll tell you when the time is right.” Even in her moment of glee, Yun Jianyue knew some things couldn’t be said out loud.","“Tsk. Stingy!” Yun Yuqing was dissatisfied, but there was nothing she could do about it.","Meanwhile, Zu An entered the neighboring room and saw Pei Mianman treating Yan Xuehen. Pei Mianman was relieved to see Zu An. “Ah Zu, you came just in time. Sect Master Yan is severely injured, and I’m afraid I alone am unable to treat her.”","Zu An nodded. “Leave her to me. You help your big sister.”","“Ah?” Pei Mianman was taken aback. Her gaze alternated between the two. Wouldn’t it be inappropriate to leave a man and a woman alone like this? She knew about their relationship, but the others were still oblivious to it. If she left the room, it could stir rumors.","Zu An harrumphed. “Your big sister is calling you over. Yuqing can’t treat Sect Master Yun alone, so they need you there to help her.”","Yan Xuehen opened her eyes. “Thank you, Manman.”","Pei Mianman pouted. I thought Yan Xuehen was a reserved person, but she’s driving me out now? This adulterous couple! They can’t wait to fool around as soon as Chuyan is gone! She finally replied, “We’ll be right next door. Call us if you need anything.”","She couldn’t reveal her knowledge about their relationship, so she could only subtly remind them to take note of their surroundings. If they were too loud, the others could hear what was happening from next door. She shot a glare at Zu An before leaving the room.","You have successfully trolled Pei Mianman for +66... +66... +66...","Zu An was startled. He'd come here to treat Yan Xuehen, only to be treated as a pervert.","He walked up to Yan Xuehen and carefully grasped her hand. “Is there a need for the two of you to go this far and get yourself injured like that?”","Yan Xuehen tried to withdraw her hand, but Zu An refused to release it. She thought about the extreme intimacy they had shared yesterday and decided to let him do as he pleased. “Hmph, why don’t you go reprimand that demoness instead?”","“It’s not a reprimand. I’m just worried about both of you,” Zu An gently replied.","“You’re rather concerned about the demoness.” Yan Xuehen glanced at him. With her sharp instincts as a woman, she sensed something amiss.","Zu An was alarmed. He couldn’t give Yun Jianyue away without her agreement. “What are you thinking? Aren’t I here to treat your injuries?”","Yan Xuehen felt a tinge of sweetness in her heart. At least I’m better than the demoness in this regard.","But her face heated up right after. How can I harbor such thoughts? She would mock me if she knew about this.","“It’s a good thing I was around, or else you’d have gone down together,” Zu An said worriedly as he channeled a steady stream of warm ki into her body to treat her injuries.","It hurt him no matter who got injured, not to mention there was a good chance of the two of them going down together. The thought of that frightening possibility made him tempted to reveal his relationship with both of them. That way, he could become their battlefield instead. But considering their relationship as long-time rivals, that would be a huge mess too.","“So be it. I can’t lose to that demoness!” Yan Xuehen harrumphed.","Zu An burst into laughter. “You’re usually unfazed by everything, but you lose your composure as soon as Yun Jianyue is involved.”","Yan Xuehen frowned. “I don’t know why either. Perhaps we were enemies in our previous lives.”","Her emotions went haywire whenever she thought about the demoness. That reminded her of something, and she eyed Zu An warily. “Doesn’t your recovery ki carry the power of the Golden Phoenix? Are you sure it’s fine?”","Her vigilant attitude made Zu An laugh. “Have you forgotten I'm now the god of this world? I can erase the side effects of my ki in this world. Don’t think too much and focus on recuperating from your injuries.”","“Mm.” Yan Xuehen breathed a sigh of relief and began channeling her ki.","With Ah Zu’s help, I should recover faster than the demoness. Just you wait and see!","The thought of that brought a smile to her lips.","But why does Ah Zu’s ki feel so hot...","In the neighboring room, Yun Yuqing pinched Yun Jianyue’s waist and said, “Focus, big sister! At this rate, you’ll suffer a cultivation deviation!”","Yun Jianyue smiled sheepishly. She was too focused on the situation next door to focus on her own treatment. Yun Yuqing and Pei Mianman were top-notch experts as well; they could sense the anomaly in her condition.","“Don’t worry, I’ll be fine even if the treatment is delayed.” Yun Jianyue was overflowing with curiosity, but Zu An had constructed a barrier to isolate noises from the neighboring room, so she was unable to hear what was happening on the other side.","She had to time herself well to catch them in the act. If she moved too early, it would alert them and make them vigilant. If she moved too late, they would snap out of her ability.","She thought hard about it and decided to wait a little longer. Ah Zu shouldn’t be that fast.","She'd even confirmed that Ah Zu had drunk plenty of the nourishing chicken soup with Yun Yuqing beforehand. He should have recovered his stamina, which was squeezed dry by the Jing Teng sisters last night.","Yun Yuqing suddenly asked, “Do you think... they'll do something next door?”","The room plunged into silence.","Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei thought their ploy had been exposed.","Pei Mianman wondered if she had accidentally let the news slip. Even though she was angry when she learned that Zu An had gotten together with Yan Xuehen, she wasn’t so tactless as to infringe on their privacy. Although, she'd secretly revealed it to Chu Chuyan so that the latter wouldn’t be hurt too deeply.","The reactions were so huge that Yun Yuqing felt embarrassed. “It goes without saying that I trust Sect Master Yan’s character, but she’s so beautiful, and Ah Zu is... I fear that Ah Zu might make a move in the heat of the moment...”","Pei Mianman replied with a straight face, “Don’t worry, Ah Zu won’t force himself on others. Nothing will happen unless Sect Master Yan is willing.”","She wasn’t lying. She knew Ah Zu’s character well, and judging from her expression back then, Sect Master Yan was clearly a willing party. This is in line with Ah Zu’s character, but I must say that Sect Master Yan is a bit hypocritical.","Yun Yuqing chuckled. “Then I guess nothing can possibly happen. Sect Master Yan is such a reserved person!”","Yun Jianyue exchanged amused looks with Qiu Honglei. Well, you never know!"]},{"number":2730,"title":"Chapter 2730: Chapter 2682: How Can I Resolve the Situation","paragraphs":["In the neighboring room, Yan Xuehen’s injuries recovered at a visible pace under the effects of Zu An’s ki. It wasn't her first time witnessing this, but she was still awed by his pure ki.","“I doubt I could ever cultivate my ki to this extent.” Yan Xuehen, despite being a proud person, couldn’t help but feel demoralized. She felt that she couldn’t reach this level even if she continued cultivating for a hundred or even a thousand years.","Zu An smiled. “Don’t put yourself down. I only reached this level because I obtained this world’s Law Beacon and became its master. Unless you obtain a Wonderpoint World’s Law Beacon as well, it’ll be hard for you to reach the same level as me. On top of that, this power is only limited to this world.”","His concern warmed Yan Xuehen’s heart. “I understand. Thank you for your reminder.”","The most important thing to a cultivator was their dao heart. If their dao heart wavered, their cultivation would collapse.","“There’s no need for words of gratitude between us. It sounds so distant.” Zu An tenderly organized Yan Xuehen’s unkempt hair. When he saw her pale face, his heart ached.","Yan Xuehen embarrassedly eyed the wall and said with a hushed voice, “Be careful, they're just next door. I... won’t be able to face anyone if they learn about it.”","She could have constructed a barrier to hinder Yun Jianyue’s prying eyes if she was in her normal state, but now that she was severely injured, she didn’t have the strength to maintain such a barrier.","Zu An burst into laughter. “Don’t worry. I’m not that careless. They can’t hear anything next door.”","Yan Xuehen breathed a sigh of relief. A second later, she murmured, “You seem awfully experienced. You must have done such things often.”","The vibrant expressions on the cold beauty made Zu An’s heart quiver. She’s truly as beautiful as a fairy. “Are you jealous?”","“Jealous? I’m helping Chuyan keep an eye on you,” Yan Xuehen replied with a straight face. As she recovered from her injuries, her face regained its redness, making her look coy.","“Indeed. You’ll have to take care of me more now that Chuyan isn’t around.” Zu An wasn’t bothered by Yan Xuehen’s more vibrant expression; he attributed it to her feeling vulnerable due to her severe injuries. Besides, they were in an intimate relationship. It was normal for her to be more vibrant when there were no outsiders around.","“How should I take care of you?” Yan Xuehen stared at him with eyes brimming with emotions. Zu An was moved.","“Chuyan is my wife. Since you’re taking care of me on her behalf, it’s only right for me for you to take care of me like a wife caring for her husband.” Zu An grabbed her hand. Despite her frosty exterior, her hand was warm and soft like fine jade. Yan Xuehen is truly blessed by the maker.","“There are plenty of people taking care of you like a husband. Didn’t the Jing Teng sisters take very good care of you just last night? Yun Yuqing even prepared a bowl of chicken soup for you earlier—it was filled with tonics that boost your vitality,” Yan Xuehen sneered as she shook his hand off.","You have successfully trolled Yan Xuehen for +33... +33... +33...","Zu An burst into laughter. I didn’t expect her to be keeping track of these things despite appearing so aloof. She must have been keeping an eye on everything happening around me. He pulled Yan Xuehen into his arms and asked, “Big sister Yan, are you jealous?”","His masculine aura made Yan Xuehen shudder. She instinctively pushed Zu An aside. “Stop it. You’re here to treat me. You can’t stay here for too long, or else they’ll suspect something.”","“Don’t worry, they don’t know how long it’ll take for me to treat you.” Zu An sensed her tone loosening up.","“Aren’t you planning to treat the demoness later? She’ll know right away.” Yan Xuehen sneered. Ah Zu came here first because I’m closer to him, but Yun Jianyue is Miss Qiu’s master, making her Zu An’s friend. He won’t turn a blind eye to her plight.","“I’ll go slower later. They won’t notice a thing,” Zu An scoffed. She gets easily affected whenever Yun Jianyue is involved.","“Are you sure you wouldn't be going slower to spend more time with her? She might be my nemesis, but I have to concede that she’s gorgeous, not to mention she’s the only woman in the history of the Devil Sect to have mastered the Bewitching Voice. Countless men would kneel under her skirt at a wag of her finger. You saw how the crowd reacted during our duel earlier.”","Yan Xuehen blushed after saying those words. It sounds like I’m jealous, but I’m just stating facts!","Zu An was both surprised and overjoyed. While Yan Xuehen would give in to him in a moment of passion, she was still demure on the whole. She had never acted so coyly to him before. The change in her attitude delighted him.","“Do you think I’d have to resort to such underhanded means?”","“Sure, sure. All it takes is a word from you—princess and holy maidens would line up for a chance to serve you,” Yan Xuehen scoffed as if she had just downed an entire vat of vinegar. “Who knows? That demoness might throw herself at you too.”","She suddenly narrowed her eyes and asked, “Has that demoness ever tried to seduce you?”","She had never considered this possibility, but Zu An’s words reminded her. With Ah Zu’s standing, which woman could resist him now? Yun Jianyue is a demoness from the Devil Sect, and she specializes in seducing men. He’s a philandering pig, and Yun Jianyue is so beautiful...","All those thoughts spurred her panic.","“What are you thinking? Sect Master Yun is Honglei’s master. How could we have such ties?” Zu An secretly wiped away cold sweat. Yun Jianyue had also sternly warned him not to divulge their relationship, or else she would turn against him. Thus, he had no choice but to lie to Yan Xuehen.","But he knew it was only a matter of time before the truth came to light, and that gave him a headache. How am I supposed to resolve the situation then?","Both Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue would blame him for keeping secrets from them. It wouldn't be beyond them to fling their sleeves and leave him for good.","“And I am Chuyan’s master!” Yan Xuehen harrumphed. Her face reddened right after she blurted out those words. She tugged her clothes as she felt inexplicable heat rising from her body.","“It’s different. That was a coincidence.” Zu An could only explain it that way, but he was soon mesmerized by her beauty. Her glistening lips made his mouth go dry.","While he was thinking about how to approach her without angering her, she suddenly leaned in on her own volition and gently kissed him.","“Ah Zu, you can’t get together with that demoness. I don’t know what I’ll do otherwise.” Yan Xuehen looked at him with pleading eyes.","Zu An’s heart quivered. Do I have to continue deceiving her and resolve this issue in the future? But both sides have warned me not to reveal our relationship. What am I supposed to do?","“If you’re struggling to resist that demoness’ seduction, you can... look for me. I’ll take care of you on Chuyan’s behalf,” Yan Xuehen said as she shyly buried her face in his chest, not daring to look at him anymore."]},{"number":2731,"title":"Chapter 2731: Chapter 2683: From Hell to Heaven","paragraphs":["“Really?” Zu An was exhilarated. He had never expected Yan Xuehen to be so proactive.","Yan Xuehen’s heart was beating quickly. She also hadn’t expected herself to utter such bold words. She sensed something was amiss, but somehow, she didn’t think her words were excessively overboard even though they stepped on the line.","And I’d let Chuyan down if Yun Jianyue gets to him.","From a personal standpoint, she also didn’t want there to be anything between Zu An and Yun Jianyue, or else just the thought of it could anger her to death.","“Of course.” Her voice was barely audible, but it couldn’t escape Zu An’s ears.","He burst into laughter as he pulled her into his arms. His cold lover felt a lot warmer than usual.","Yan Xuehen felt dazed. She normally wasn't averse to being intimate with Zu An, but something just felt off today.","Zu An leaned in and kissed her. She moaned and reciprocated the kiss. He thought that he had finally melted the ice beauty’s heart. She’s so much more proactive than usual.","Yan Xuehen felt bliss surging into her heart. I was deceiving myself all this while by putting distance between us. This passionate kiss felt like the most intoxicating wine in the world. She felt as if she was going to melt from the heat.","And this intoxication effect was as much physical as it was psychological. The realization of that made her embarrassed. What's come over me? Forget it. It's already happened anyway. There’s no reason for me to continue pushing him away. Till Chuyan returns, I’ll help her fulfill her duties as his wife...","The thought of Chuyan jolted her heart. She suddenly felt a wave of intense shame.","She had practiced the Unshakable Daoist Manual, after all. Clarity returned to her head, and she belatedly realized how intertwined their bodies were. Taken aback, she exclaimed, “Ah Zu, are you sure... you didn’t use that golden phoenix ki on me?”","“Of course not.” Zu An was stunned. He thought she was just embarrassed. “Calm down, big sister Yan. It’s a normal reaction in the heat of passion. I like you, and you like me too. That’s all that matters.”","Yan Xuehen was confused. He has no reason to deceive me. He might be lustful, but I trust his character. He won’t use such despicable means to take advantage of me. Could this be my true will...","It’s all Ah Zu’s fault! He messed around too much after we returned from the Netherworld. Otherwise, I wouldn’t be feeling this way with just a mere touch.","The thought of what happened in the Netherworld made her heart beat even faster. Her usually cold eyes overflowed with tenderness and shyness.","The two of them naturally fell on the bed together. Out of embarrassment, Yan Xuehen put down the blinds as Zu An pushed her down.","...","A while later, Yun Yuqing’s anxious voice echoed, “Bad news, Ah Zu! Something happened to big sister Yun!”","Qiu Honglei’s anxious voice followed. “Master is at her limit!”","They barged into the room without waiting for a response. The door was locked, but a normal lock couldn’t hope to stop the two of them.","Pei Mianman looked upon the situation worriedly. She knew about Zu An and Yan Xuehen’s relationship. Things would get troublesome if the two of them were doing something intimate in the room. But Yun Jianyue’s injuries had suddenly worsened. She couldn’t find a way to help her, so she had no reason to stop these two women from seeking Zu An’s help.","Yan Xuehen exclaimed in horror. She anxiously sat up and grabbed a blanket to cover her body, but her smooth shoulders and exquisite collarbones remained exposed. On top of that, her fair skin was dyed red. Anyone witnessing this scene would know what had happened right away.","Looking at the three women who had barged into the room, her face turned pale. It’s over!","It was one thing for her reputation to crumble, but the White Jade Sect’s honor would be sullied, and Chuyan would become a laughingstock too. On top of that, Yun Jianyue would mock her to no end. The thought of that filled her heart with despair. She instinctively grabbed her Flying Snow Sword to slit her throat. She could think of no solution other than ending her life and cleansing her shame with her blood.","But Zu An moved faster than her. He grabbed her sword and exclaimed, “Big sister Yan, what are you doing?”","Yan Xuehen’s eyes were cloaked in despair. “Ah Zu, let me die.”","Zu An quivered upon seeing her current state. I considered coming clean with them, but now, I’m glad I didn’t do so. “Don’t worry, big sister Yan. They didn’t see anything.”","“How could they have not seen anything? They...” Yan Xuehen pointed at the three women who had just barged into the room, only to raise her eyebrows in astonishment.","None of the three women were moving. Their postures were fixed at the moment they barged into the room—their legs and hands hung in mid air, and their expressions were frozen in place. They looked like three statues. But Yan Xuehen could tell they were living beings. Not even the greatest sculptor in the world could create a masterpiece as lifelike as this.","Zu An explained, “I paused their time. They haven’t realized what’s going on in here.”","“Really?” Yan Xuehen was overjoyed. It felt as if she had been lifted from hell into heaven.","“Of course.” Zu An smiled. “With my recent breakthrough and my grasp of the World Law Beacon, I am god in this world. I can do things beyond your wildest imagination. Pausing their time is nothing in comparison.”","Yan Xuehen blinked as spirit returned into her eyes. “Are there no restrictions?”","“Of course there are. I could easily pause their time because they're standing next to one another, so the implications on the world’s cause and effect are limited. But if I expanded the scale to the academy and the capital, the implications would be so great that they could plunge this world into chaos or even unravel it,” Zu An explained.","Yan Xuehen looked at Zu An with envious eyes. “I can’t imagine how anyone can defeat you in your current state. Even universal deities must only amount to this much, no?”","Any cultivator would dream of attaining the abilities Zu An wielded.","Zu An shook his head. “My abilities are only limited to this world. I won’t be able to use them outside of this world. In comparison, the universal deities can exert their unparalleled powers across the myriad worlds.”","Yan Xuehen was startled. She wanted to further discuss this topic, but the cold wind blowing against her skin was a reminder of her current plight. She felt so embarrassed that she quickly put on her clothes.","Zu An frowned. “You don’t need to be in such a rush. Time flows differently for us right now. We can... stay like that for a little longer, and it would only be an instant for them.”","Yan Xuehen spat. “No way!”","Even if the three women couldn’t see it, it was still as good as a public execution for her to get steamy with him in front of them.","“Why did you all suddenly go quiet? Did you see something?” Yun Jianyue’s voice suddenly came from outside."]},{"number":2732,"title":"Chapter 2732: Chapter 2684: Doubt","paragraphs":["Yan Xuehen had barely breathed a sigh of relief when she heard her nemesis’ voice. She was so nervous that she could almost feel her heart leaping up her throat. She anxiously put on her clothes, but she was in such a fluster that she buttoned them incorrectly.","Zu An was amused by her panic. He reached forth and helped her rebutton.","But that only made Yan Xuehen more nervous. How can I explain this if she witnesses this sight?","“Don’t worry, she won’t be able to get in,” Zu An reassured her.","Yan Xuehen realized Zu An must have used his time stop ability again and exhaled in relief. Her face reddened. “I’ll do it myself...” I’ll probably run out of strength quickly if I let this fellow tidy up my clothes for me.","Zu An watched her put on her clothes with a grin. He found it a beautiful scene to behold. Yan Xuehen was so embarrassed by his intense stare that she turned away from him.","“Are you ready?” Zu An asked.","“Stop!” Yan Xuehen hurriedly interrupted him. Under Zu An’s perplexed gaze, she quickly channeled her cultivation method. After a few circulations, her redness receded, and she regained her usual icy mountain-like coldness.","Zu An was startled. He thought about her earlier act of passion, and the sharp contrast made his heart skip a beat. No wonder so many people in my previous life enjoyed the dere tropes! There's an inexplicable charm to it.","“Don’t you give me away later!” Yan Xuehen glared at Zu An as she instructed him.","“Don’t worry, I’m a veteran myself,” Zu An promised, thumping his chest.","Yan Xuehen felt a twinge of jealousy. “You must have a lot of experience doing this.”","Zu An was speechless.","When Yan Xuehen was finally done with her preparations, Zu An snapped his fingers, and time reverted to normal for the others in the residence.","“Ah Zu, my master...” Qiu Honglei said as her eyes swiftly scanned the room. She was stunned when she saw a fully-clothed Yan Xuehen resting on a chair and Zu An sitting a distance away, remotely treating her injuries.","Her master had hinted for her to head over to catch them in the act, thinking Zu An and Yan Xuehen should have started on the 'action'. She'd felt embarrassed and wanted her master to do it instead, but she couldn’t defy her master and had no choice but to half-reluctantly, half-excitedly head over.","She'd thought a huge scandal was awaiting her, but it was the opposite of what she expected. After my master boasted so much about her ability...is this all? Master, you’re so unreliable!","Meanwhile, Pei Mianman was perplexed. She knew about Yan Xuehen and Zu An’s relationship. Even if they dared not do anything in the room, they wouldn’t be so distant from each other as if they were strangers. Alhough this wasn’t a good time to raise her doubts.","“How’s your master?” Zu An asked.","Qiu Honglei felt a tinge of guilt under Zu An’s gaze. Fortunately, Yun Yuqing spoke up. “A problem cropped up with big sister Yun’s injuries. I don’t know why, but her condition suddenly worsened. We had no choice but to seek your help.”","“Are you sure? She looks fine to me,” Zu An said as he looked at the doorway.","Qiu Honglei and the others turned around and saw Yun Jianyue rushing over. “What’s taking all of you so... long?”","Yun Jianyue froze when she saw everyone looking at her. She quickly scanned the room and saw Yan Xuehen properly clothed, emanating her usual ice sculpture aura. She was stunned. How is this possible?","“Big sister Yun, how are you...” Yun Yuqing was bewildered.","Yun Jianyue quickly cleared the air with a laugh. “Somehow, I managed to calm the energy rampaging inside my body. I was worried you would disturb their treatment, so I rushed over to stop you. Looks like I came too late.”","Yun Yuqing breathed a sigh of relief. “I’m glad you’re fine, big sister.”","Yun Jianyue responded with an unnatural smile. She was feeling conscience-stricken.","Qiu Honglei wished there was a hole she could jump into. I’d be too embarrassed to face Ah Zu if he learns about our plan.","Pei Mianman alternated her gaze between the two pairs—Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei, and Zu An and Yan Xuehen. She could already guess the reason behind Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei’s anomalous behavior, but she couldn’t understand how Zu An and Yan Xuehen were so prim and proper.","What made Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei suspect them of being in a relationship? If I hadn’t witnessed it myself, I wouldn’t have believed that the icily cold Sect Master Yan would have an affair with Ah Zu.","She considered warning Zu An about it, but on second thought, she realized this had nothing to do with her. I should just enjoy the show. The thought of that brought a smile to her face.","After the farce settled down, Yun Jianyue and the others quickly returned to their room. Yan Xuehen looked at their departing silhouettes and murmured, “Ah Zu, I think the demoness is after me.”","“Don’t think too much into it. It’s just an accident.” Zu An had come to the same conclusion, but he was on close terms with Yun Jianyue too. He had already made an exception by siding with Yan Xuehen once. If he continued that way, he wouldn’t be able to face Yun Jianyue anymore.","“Ah Zu, are you sure you didn’t use your special ki on me?” Yan Xuehen asked.","“I didn’t. It was just a natural reaction in the heat of the moment,” Zu An reassured her. No wonder Yan Xuehen was acting abnormally earlier. Yun Jianyue must have used her ability. What’s that woman up to?","After returning to her room, Yun Jianyue found an excuse to send away Yun Yuqing and Pei Mianman before asking her disciple with a hushed voice, “Honglei, are you sure you didn’t see anything when you entered the room?”","“Both of them were properly dressed and observing propriety. I told you Ah Zu was a gentleman.” Qiu Honglei had intended to complement Yan Xuehen too—she acknowledged the latter's character even though they were enemies. It was unlikely their plan would ever come to fruition. However, she decided otherwise lest she agitate her master.","“Gentleman...” Yun Jianyue was baffled. My silly disciple, you must now know how wild he is. He grabbed my hair and rode me like a horse!","She was confident that Zu An was incapable of resisting Yan Xuehen’s allure, and she had successfully planted her desire energy in Yan Xuehen. So what went wrong?","A thought suddenly popped into her head. “You were away for quite a while. Did you really not see anything at all?”","Qiu Honglei was baffled. “You went over shortly after we went there.”","“Nonsense! You were away for at least ten minutes. That’s why I came over to look for you,” Yun Jianyue refuted.","“That can’t be. You came over shortly after we arrived at Zu An’s room. That’s why Yuqing and Manman were baffled. You can ask them if you don’t believe me.” Qiu Honglei was confused by her master’s remark.","It wasn't without reason that Yun Jianyue was one of the world’s top experts. After a moment of contemplation, she smacked her thigh and exclaimed, “I get it now! There really is something between them!”"]},{"number":2733,"title":"Chapter 2733: Chapter 2685: We Have the Upper Hand","paragraphs":["“What makes you say that, master?” Qiu Honglei was confused. After what happened earlier, she didn’t harbor any hopes.","Yan Xuehen appeared to be unfazed by the mundane, and for many years, she had been uninterested in romantic relationships. On top of that, she was Chu Chuyan’s master. It was unthinkable for there to be anything between her and Zu An.","“Think about it. You were there for ten minutes, but it felt like an instant to you. No one else could have affected your senses under Ah Zu’s watch. Only he himself is capable of that.” Yun Jianyue’s eyes flickered with a brilliant light.","“Does Ah Zu wield such an ability?” Qiu Honglei was baffled. She had been unconscious for so long that she had no idea what abilities Ah Zu currently wielded.","“He has mentioned many times that he’s the god of this world, and that there’s nothing he’s incapable of.” Yun Jianyue started getting excited halfway through her sentence as if she had discovered uncharted territory.","“Master, you’re saying...” Qiu Honglei quickly guessed what her master was driving at.","“Indeed. Why would Ah Zu warp your senses if they were innocent? Thinking back, it felt unnatural how distant they seemed,” Yun Jianyue sneered.","“Sect Master Yan is cold-natured; she avoids physical contact with men. Ah Zu is a gentleman, so it would make sense for him to observe propriety,” Qiu Honglei pointed out.","“What poison did that fellow feed you to make you think that he’s a gentleman?” Yun Jianyue huffed. “Besides, it’s not as if he's never hugged that ice sculpture before. Do they need to maintain such a distance between each other?”","“They hugged before?” Qiu Honglei was stunned.","“Of course! He hugged me with one hand and her with the other.” Yun Jianyue had a dangerous look in her eyes. Why didn’t I think about that earlier? If he dares to lay his hands on me, there’s no reason he wouldn’t dare lay his hands on that ice sculpture!","She had been too convinced that nothing could happen between him and that ice sculpture beforer, but that fellow’s flirting skills surpassed common sense. He could very well have his way of dealing with Yan Xuehen.","“Ah?” Qiu Honglei was baffled. A man in the world actually simultaneously held my master and Sect Master Yan in his arms?","“Have you forgotten about it? It was when we had a showdown against Zhao Han in that dungeon. Zu An held us both in his arms, but things were urgent back then, so I didn’t think too deeply into it. There could have been something between them then.” As she spoke, Yun Jianyue got increasingly excited. “Think about it. That ice sculpture is someone who would rather die than violate propriety. I should have known when she allowed Ah Zu to touch her!”","Qiu Honglei was baffled. Hold on, you've already been sharing a husband since then? She still found it hard to believe that the lofty Yan Xuehen would get together with Zu An. “This is all your conjecture. We don’t have any proof.”","“That’s disappointing.” Yun Jianyue paced around the room with a vexed heart.","“Master, are you sure your ability is that potent? Sect Master Yan looked completely unfazed earlier.” Qiu Honglei was still reeling from the awkwardness of barging into their room earlier.","“If that fellow helped her, it would have been easy enough for the ice sculpture to overcome this crisis. How dare that fellow collude with the ice sculpture to deceive me? Doesn’t that mean he cherishes the ice sculpture more than me?” The furious Yan Jianyue suddenly looked deflated, and her face turned pale.","Qiu Honglei was horrified. “What’s wrong, master? Did your injuries relapse? I’ll look for Ah Zu right away!”","She was about to rush to the neighboring room when her master grabbed her.","“I’m fine. It’s just that... I've fought with that ice sculpture all my life, but I still lost to her in the end. And it was a crushing defeat.” Yun Jianyue looked forlorn, as if her life had lost all meaning.","Do I have to prostrate myself to that ice sculpture in the future? The thought of having to serve tea to the other party made her feel so terrible that she would rather die. Qiu Honglei was already a step behind Chu Chuyan, with the latter claiming the title of Zu An’s official wife. If she lost to the ice sculpture too, that would spell a complete loss for them both, master and disciple!","Yun Jianyue felt so awful that she wanted to hug her disciple and cry, but she was worried the ice sculpture would overhear and make fun of them.","Qiu Honglei knew about the rivalry between her master and Yan Xuehen, so she could immediately guess how her master was feeling. She chuckled. “Master, you don’t need to be so pessimistic. Things aren’t as bad as you think.”","“What do you mean?” Yun Jianyue grabbed Qiu Honglei’s arm like a drowning man clutching onto a straw of hope.","Qiu Honglei laughed on the inside. My master usually puts on a domineering front, commanding deference from the world. Yet she seems like a fragile-hearted girl here. “Think about it, master. While it’s true Ah Zu didn’t tell you about his relationship with Sect Master Yan, he also didn’t tell Sect Master Yan about his relationship with you.”","Yun Jianyue’s eyes lit up. “Indeed! That ice sculpture would have used that to mock me if she knew about my relationship with Ah Zu! You’re right. That ice sculpture definitely doesn’t know about my relationship with Ah Zu!”","Seeing her master had regained her fighting spirit, Qiu Honglei continued, “Ah Zu chose to withhold the truth from both parties, which shows that he isn’t biased. Rather, now that we've figured out the truth about Sect Master Yan while the latter is still kept in the dark, we have the upper hand!”","The more Qiu Honglei spoke, the angrier she felt. She puts on a holier-than-thou attitude as if the secular world is beneath her, yet she turns out to be a bitch who steals her disciple’s man.","She snuck a glance at her master and secretly apologized for inflicting collateral damage on her. My master is from the Devil Sect, so it’s understandable for her to do that. But Sect Master Yan is the leader of the orthodox sects, and she often preaches kindness, morality, and propriety. Doesn’t she feel ashamed at all?","Yun Jianyue burst into laughter. “Well said, my good disciple! We have the upper hand now!”","She excitedly hugged her disciple and kissed her. “I didn’t raise you all these years in vain! That ice sculpture’s precious disciple isn’t around to help her. As long as we join hands, she won’t be a match for us!”","Qiu Honglei looked perplexed. Her master had taught her many seduction skills, and they had once boasted that either of them could easily make any man in the world fall head over heels for them. And yet, they now had to join hands to fight for a man.","Yun Jianyue suddenly thought about something and harrumphed. “Hmph! What’s Ah Zu thinking by keeping both sides in the dark? Does he intend to use this information asymmetry to keep us fighting while he reaps the benefits of both sides?” That thought irked her.","Qiu Honglei gave the matter some thought before shaking her head. “Ah Zu isn’t that kind of person. He probably doesn’t know how to approach this matter. The world knows you've been fighting with that Yan woman for a lifetime now. If he revealed the truth, it would be one thing for us since we’re from the Devil Sect, but that Yan woman, who prides herself on being the leader of the orthodox sects, might end her life out of shame.”","Yun Jianyue’s eyes lit up. “That’s not a bad idea. Let’s hash it out with that ice sculpture. Let’s see if she can keep up her act!”","Qiu Honglei anxiously stopped her. “We mustn’t do that! If something happens to that Yan woman, Ah Zu will blame us. Taking a step back, what if she simply denies it? We don’t have any evidence, and with her stellar reputation, the world is more likely to believe her than us.”","Yun Jianyue frowned. “You’re right. She's kept up that pretense for so long that it's given her a lot of credibility. The whole world has fallen for her stink act.”","She scoffed, “Our Devil Sect is known for our seduction arts, but I think that ice sculpture’s skills surpass ours. Look at how she's charmed the entire world!”","Qiu Honglei agreed too. The master and disciple continued grumbling about Yan Xuehen for a long time before both of them let out a sigh.","“What should we do next?” Qiu Honglei asked.","Yun Jianyue pondered before replying, “After today’s incident, that ice sculpture and Ah Zu will be guarded against us. We won’t be able to find evidence ourselves.”","“Should we ask Aunt Yuqing for help?” Qiu Honglei asked.","Yun Jianyue shook her head. “That won’t do. She’s my little sister. They'ill be guarded against her, too.”","She spent a moment in thought before asking, “What about Miss Pei?”"]},{"number":2734,"title":"Chapter 2734: Chapter 2686: Coming Clean","paragraphs":["“Manman?” Qiu Honglei frowned. “I don’t think it’ll work. She's been good friends with Chu Chuyan since their time at Brightmoon City. There’s no way she would help us deal with Chu Chuyan’s master.”","“Just because they're good friends doesn’t mean they're on good terms. If they are that close, why would Manman get together with Ah Zu even though he’s married to Chuyan?” Yun Jianyue pointed out.","“There must be a reason behind that.” Qiu Honglei rolled her eyes. “Didn’t you get together with Ah Zu despite knowing my relationship with him too?”","Yun Jianyue was speechless. Gah, it feels like I've shot myself in the foot.","Qiu Honglei quickly grabbed Yun Jianyue’s arm and said, “Master, I’m kidding. Manman is your younger cousin, so she should be closer to us. Let’s do as you say and ask her for help.”","Yun Jianyue’s complexion finally improved. This lass would have never dared to joke with me like that in the past. It’s all Ah Zu’s fault!","“You ask her. I’m not close with Manman, and you've known her longer.”","Qiu Honglei was baffled. “She’s your younger cousin! How are the two of you not close?”","Yun Jianyue replied sheepishly, “I can’t shrug off the feeling that she’s a junior. It’s embarrassing to talk about such matters with her. It’s better for you to do it.”","Qiu Honglei belatedly remembered that others still didn’t know about her master’s relationship with Zu An, so she had no choice but to take on the job. I must have owed my master a lot in my previous life. Not only did I get my man taken by her, but I even have to cover her ass.","So, Qiu Honglei went out and visited Pei Mianman’s room.","Pei Mianman rushed over to support her. “Honglei, you should take it slow. You've only just recovered.”","Her concern brought a smile to Qiu Honglei’s face. “Thank you, Manman, but I am still a cultivator. I’ve been resting too much in recent years, so I’d like to walk around more.”","The two of them exchanged some pleasantries. Pei Mianman sensed that Qiu Honglei had come with a purpose, so she probed about that.","Qiu Honglei was put on the spot, but she still replied, “Manman, what do you think about Ah Zu and Sect Master Yan?”","Pei Mianman was taken aback. “Why do you suddenly ask that?” Have they figured out Ah Zu’s relationship with Yan Xuehen?","Qiu Honglei didn’t notice her anomalous response. “I just think that they look too distant.”","Pei Mianman breathed a sigh of relief. “Do they?” More like negative distance.","“Didn’t you see how Ah Zu was sitting five meters away from Sect Master Yan when treating her earlier in the day? I’m worried there’s a conflict between them.” Qiu Honglei wasn't so foolish as to reveal that she suspected them of having an affair right away.","Pei Mianman scoffed in her heart. I bet Ah Zu didn’t expect his cautiousness to backfire on him.","“Sect Master Yan values propriety and avoids physical contact with men. Ah Zu probably kept his distance because of that.” Pei Mianman couldn’t help but recall intimate images of the duo as she said those words. Honestly, I can’t understand how Yan Xuehen fell for Ah Zu.","Yan Xuehen hadn't just been putting on an act all these years. She was true to her reputation, but Zu An had somehow managed to melt even the icy mountain.","Qiu Honglei was aware of Yan Xuehen’s reputation, and she knew no one would believe her if she said that Yan Xuehen had seduced her disciple’s man. On the contrary, people would think that she was slandering Yan Xuehen. /Thus, she could only remark, “Sect Master Yan is simply too powerful, so much so that my master went all out and accidentally released her desire energy in the duel. We were worried that she would be affected, but fortunately, she looked fine earlier on. Her self-discipline is truly formidable.”","She didn’t voice her suspicion, but instead subtly revealed the key phrase ‘desire energy’. She knew Manman was smart enough to draw a link. She’s Ah Zu’s woman and Chuyan’s best friend. She wouldn’t turn a blind eye to this matter!","Unsurprisingly, Pei Mianman’s complexion darkened. I was wondering why she and Ah Zu looked so formal in the room. I bet something indescribable must have happened in there earlier. They must have used some method to deceive our eyes...","They chatted a while longer before Qiu Honglei took her leave, knowing that Pei Mianman had to be harboring doubts now.","After she walked out the door, she hid in the corner and secretly observed Pei Mianman. It was only when the latter rushed out of the door that she finally left with a satisfied smile. I am indeed a Devil Sect demoness. Somehow, I feel excited doing this.","Meanwhile, Pei Mianman finally found Zu An. The latter was sending off a few imperial court officials who had come to visit.","Zu An smiled and stepped forward with open arms to embrace her. “Manman, you’re here.”","Pei Mianman stepped aside and avoided his embrace.","“What’s wrong, Manman?” Zu An was taken aback.","“Ah Zu, I won’t say anything about your philandering ways, but why do you have to get involved with Sect Master Yan, of all people?” Pei Mianman finally let it off her chest.","Zu An replied bitterly, “Would you believe me if I said it happened by coincidence?” He knew Pei Mianman had seen them that day.","“It doesn’t matter what I think. The question is whether others believe you or not.” Pei Mianman took a deep breath. “How much longer do you intend to conceal this matter?”","“I don’t know.” Zu An sighed in resignation. “You also know Yan Xuehen’s position. It doesn’t matter to me whether this gets revealed or not, but I fear she won’t be able to take the backlash. She might just end her life out of shame.”","“You two should never have overstepped your boundaries!” Pei Mianman was both angry and agitated.","Yan Xuehen’s reputation was too resounding. She was the leader of the orthodox sects, the incarnation of justice, the divine fairy who practiced the Unshakable Daoist Manual... It would be no exaggeration to say that the world already saw her as a saint.","The higher a person stood, the greater they stood to fall. It would be a huge scandal if she were exposed to be in a relationship with a man, not to mention that it was her disciple’s man. Even Pei Mianman felt stifled thinking about it, let alone Yan Xuehen.","Zu An asked, “Manman, why are you suddenly asking me about this?”","“You shouldn’t have done it if you didn’t want others to know,” Pei Mianman coldly uttered. “I’m here to warn you that others have started suspecting your relationship with her. It won’t be long before they arrive at the truth. You should mentally prepare yourselves for that.”","Then, she left without giving him a chance to ask further questions. She wasn't going to betray Qiu Honglei.","Zu An fell into deep thought. He could guess what was going on.","Qiu Honglei and Yun Jianyue barged into the room earlier today to catch us. I was still overjoyed when they patched things up, but to think they would join forces to pull this off right after.","Did they find out about me and Yan Xuehen?","No, that can’t be. If she had conclusive evidence, Yun Jianyue would have confronted Yan Xuehen right away. They're probably just suspecting it...","Should I pull both sides together for a show of hands?","No, that won’t do. Their situations might be similar, but Yun Jianyue is from the Devil Sect and has less regard for her reputation. Yan Xuehen is at a disadvantage..."]},{"number":2735,"title":"Chapter 2735: Chapter 2687: A Shocking Question","paragraphs":["It had been a long time since Zu An felt so frustrated over a problem ever since his breakthrough. He felt an unprecedented sense of helplessness. He thought for a long time but couldn’t come up with a solution, so he decided to just take it one step at a time.","Since Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei suspected Yan Xuehen, Zu An thought he should warn the latter, or else she would be disadvantaged when dealing with them.","Yan Xuehen was appalled by his return, worrying that others would notice their relationship. However, when she learned the reason behind his return, she was shocked. “Huh? Is there something wrong with the demoness? Why is she doing that?”","She had doubted Yun Jianyue at the start, but she dropped her suspicion after Zu An promised her that nothing was amiss. From the looks of it now, the demoness had indeed come prepared.","“It’s all your fault. She must have started suspecting us after our trip to the Netherworld.” Yan Xuehen thought about the things he had done along the way, and her face turned so red that one could almost squeeze blood out of it.","She couldn’t even stand upright then. Given how sharp the demoness was, she was bound to have sensed that something was amiss.","“I suspect she intends to drag you down.” Zu An was aware of their relationship, and that allowed him to better guess her thoughts.","Yan Xuehen calmed down and thought about it. “Yes, you’re right. The demoness is capable of that. She probably plans for us to embarrass ourselves, so she can mock me for that...”","She felt stifled. I should be angry about that, but it just so happens I have an affair with Zu An. The demoness hit the nail on the head by chance!","Zu An couldn’t help but wonder if the two women would gang up against him if they learned about each other’s relationship with him. The ensuing drama that could arise from that made him shudder.","“What’s wrong?” Yan Xuehen was perplexed by his response.","“It’s nothing. We should tread carefully for now. She’ll probably let it slip when she fails to find any evidence,” Zu An consoled her.","“Easier said than done!” Yan Xuehen hissed. “She wields desire energy now. Who knows when she’ll use it against me?”","It finally made sense why she had been so affected earlier.","“You have something similar to void energy too. You fell for her trap because you were unguarded, but now that you know what she’s up to, you should be able to neutralize her desire energy with your void energy,” Zu An replied.","Yan Xuehen nodded. Fighting spirit blazed in her eyes. “I’d like to see whether my dao is stronger, or hers!”","Zu An thought, They're truly a match made in heaven. Neither side refuses to admit defeat.","Yan Xuehen suddenly narrowed her eyes. “I’m in too much of a disadvantage if I remain in a passive position. This won’t do. I should fight back too!” She could turn a blind eye to such things when it came to anyone else, but somehow, she couldn’t let herself lose when it came to Yun Jianyue.","Zu An was rendered speechless. Yun Jianyue’s action has already left me flustered. If Yan Xuehen makes a move too, given their wits, they might quickly realize our relationship, and that would spell the end of the world!","He said, “I’ll take her away with me. That way, she won’t be able to deal with you.”","Yan Xuehen turned to him. “Where do you plan to take her?” There was a tinge of jealousy in her voice.","“Her Corpse Mountain Blood Sea Domain resembles the Netherworld. That would be the perfect excuse to take her on a tour in the Netherworld. She won’t suspect a thing,” Zu An replied.","“You want to take her to the Netherworld?” Yan Xuehen raised her voice. “That means she would have to project her soul and stick close to you?”","Zu An was astounded. He was in an intimate relationship with Yun Jianyue, so he didn’t think much about embracing her. But to Yan Xuehen, who didn’t know about their relationship, that was overstepping a boundary.","He coughed. “What are you thinking? I’m also bringing Manman with us to observe the Red Spider Lilies. With her around, nothing can possibly happen.”","Yan Xuehen exhaled in relief. The atmosphere won’t be as chummy with someone else around. However, she still felt jealous. “Our previous duel ended with a draw. With her wits, it’s likely that she’ll advance her domain to a higher level after your trip to the Netherworld. By then, I might no longer be a match for her.”","She glared at him grudgingly as if blaming him for helping an outsider against her.","“I’m doing this to stop her from going after you.” Zu An lifted her chin. “Big sister Yan, you look so adorable when you’re jealous.”","“Who’s being jealous?” Yan Xuehen looked away in embarrassment. Why do I keep acting like that in front of Zu An?","To conceal her awkwardness, she changed the topic. “Forget it. Take her to the Netherworld if you want to, but can you leave Miss Jing here to accompany me?”","“Why are you looking for her?” Zu An was worried that a fight would ensue.","Yan Xuehen harrumphed. “I can’t end up lagging behind that demoness. Miss Jing has deep ties with the Dao Gate, and her knowledge runs deep. There are many things I’d like to consult her on. It might help me take a step forward.”","She also wanted to go to the Netherworld to meet Chuyan, but she dropped that thought because she was worried that Yun Jianyue would see through them. I can get Ah Zu to take me to the Netherworld whenever I want anyway. There’s no need for me to go with her.","Zu An’s heart was put at ease. “That’s a good idea. Jing Teng does command vast knowledge.”","Other than Mi Li, Jing Teng was the most knowledgeable person around him. Her wealth of life experience and experience in suppressing the giant tomb made her a living encyclopedia. Besides, Qiu Honglei was still too frail to head to the Netherworld. It would be good to leave Jing Teng here to take care of her.","Zu An paid a visit to Yun Jianyue and Pei Mianman to inform them about his plan.","Yun Jianyue wanted to plot against Yan Xuehen, but she knew advancing her cultivation was more important, so she agreed with Zu An's decision. Meanwhile, Pei Mianman could guess Zu An’s intentions, but she didn’t hesitate to accept the offer because she wanted to see the Red Spider Lilies in person.","Thus, Zu An quickly made preparations before taking Yun Jianyue and Pei Mianman’s souls to the Netherworld.","Yan Xuehen took this chance to consult Jing Teng about her dao. But Jing Teng didn’t seem interested in engaging with her.","Yan Xuehen sensed something was amiss and asked, “Miss Jing, is there something on your mind?”","Jing Teng replied, “Miss Yan, I have a question. Do you think a master can share a husband with her disciple?”","Yan Xuehen’s face turned pale."]},{"number":2736,"title":"Chapter 2736: Chapter 2688: Suspicion","paragraphs":["Yan Xuehen’s face paled in horror. She'd thought that the demoness had only guessed the truth coincidentally, but who could have thought that even Jing Teng, who spent her days in the cave paradise, had figured it out too? Didn’t that mean the other ladies knew about it too? They're probably just keeping quiet about it out of respect for me.","She felt as if she had been plunged into an ice chamber. She reached for her sword to end her life once and for all.","Jing Teng eyed her sword and asked, “What are you doing? Even if you’re not on good terms with Yun Jianyue, you shouldn’t make a move against her while her soul isn’t around.”","“Ah?” Yan Xuehen was baffled.","“I knew I shouldn’t have told you that!” Jing Teng glared at Yan Xuehen as if the latter were a despicable rat who took advantage of other people’s weakness.","Yan Xuehen was bewildered. She noticed Jing Teng’s stockings turning black—it was the younger Jing Teng who was talking to her.","“You’ve misunderstood. I wasn’t going to make a move on Yun Jianyue.” Yan Xuehen knew the younger Jing Teng was eccentric like a demoness and didn’t want to provoke her.","Black Jing Teng smiled. “I knew you weren’t that kind of person. You wouldn’t resort to such underhanded means even when dealing with someone who stole your disciple’s man.”","Yan Xuehen was speechless. Aren’t I the one who stole my disciple’s man? Who are you referring to?","“I didn’t expect a lofty expert like Yun Jianyue to do something that despicable, but what’s more maddening is how Qiu Honglei let things slip despite it all. She continues to maintain close ties with her,” Black Jing Teng huffed.","“You’re saying Yun Jianyue...” Yan Xuehen narrowed her eyes. It was plenty obvious what Black Jing Teng was driving at.","Many thoughts surged into her mind, and the doubts she'd previously harbored suddenly made sense. She'd always thought there was something amiss between Zu An and Yun Jianyue—they looked like friends, but they seemed extremely comfortable with each other. She had previously attributed that to Yun Jianyue’s eccentric personality as a demoness and didn’t think in that direction, but if even she could get together with Zu An, there was no reason the demoness couldn’t do so as well.","Zu An had hugged them both in the dungeon back then, but she hadn’t suspected a thing due to the urgency of the situation. But now that she thought about it, the demoness had never come into contact with other men in her life, let alone allowing someone to grab her waist.","No wonder Ah Zu maintains a neutral stance and covers up for her. So that’s the reason...","As shock washed over her heart, Jing Teng’s stockings reverted to white. She apologetically said, “Please don’t misunderstand, Miss Yan. My little sister was talking nonsense.”","Yan Xuehen had gotten used to the two sisters’ role switching. “Your little sister wouldn’t make such a remark out of nowhere. You must know something.”","White Jing Teng was put in a spot. Knowing the other party wouldn’t let things slip, she acquiesced and said, “I overheard Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei’s conversation. They were talking about something about stealing their disciple’s man. My little sister might have misunderstood because of that. Unfortunately, we don’t know the details about the matter.”","Black Jing Teng angrily roared, “Why aren’t you telling her the truth? That Yun woman stole her disciple’s man—no, she stole our man too! So what if I rat her out?”","White Jing Teng huffed, “A lady doesn’t gossip about others behind their back.”","Black Jing Teng rolled her eyes. “I've never been a lady. You can keep your holier-than-thou attitude and watch in resignation as someone steals your man!”","“Ah Zu has never been a devoted man. Are you only realizing that now?” White Jing Teng retorted.","Black Jing Teng was at a loss for words. “It’s one thing for Ah Zu to be like that, but what’s the deal with that Yun woman? She’s Honglei’s master! How can she do that? I won’t stand for it!” After years of living and chatting together, she had gotten close to Qiu Honglei.","Looking at her furious little sister, White Jing Teng could only change tactics to convince her. “Haven’t you considered that Ah Zu might blame us if we did something? Not only would Yun Jianyue hate us, but Qiu Honglei might not be thankful either. The other ladies would also be wary of us. We'd become everyone's enemy. There wouldn’t be a place for us.”","Black Jing Teng was taken aback. She didn’t mind being hated by the other ladies, but she was horrified by the possibility of Zu An being averse to her.","Seeing that her little sister had calmed down, White Jing Teng turned to Yan Xuehen and continued, “This is probably a misunderstanding. I doubt it’s as my little sister says. Miss Yan, please don’t take it to heart.”","Yan Xuehen responded with a strained smile. She chatted a little longer before excusing herself.","I thought there was an affair between Ah Zu and Yun Jianyue, but it seems like the person Yun Jianyue was talking about is me. In the end, I only went in one big circle.","I guess there’s no way to continue hiding my relationship with Ah Zu. I should talk to him when he returns.","But she recalled Black Jing Teng’s words. Could there really be something between Yun Jianyue and Ah Zu? If that’s the case, Ah Zu won’t tell me the truth, and he won’t help me either...","Yan Xuehen suddenly felt vexed. She decided to have a chat with Xie Daoyun and Ji Xiaoxi. They had been traveling with Ah Zu, so they had a better understanding of what he'd been through in recent years. Unlike Yun Yuqing, those two ladies would be closer to her.","...","Meanwhile, Zu An took Yun Jianyue and Pei Mianman’s souls to the Netherworld. He instructed the two of them to stay close to him to protect them from the death energy.","Yun Jianyue snorted. We’re so close that our ears and hair are pressed against each other, and that ice sculpture still says they're innocent?","Pei Mianman didn’t notice these details, as she had something weighing on her mind. She regretted giving a heads-up to Zu An. It felt awkward for her to share a space with Yun Jianyue now.","Sensing the tension, Zu An said, “You don’t have to worry. I can sense anything that happens at the mountaintop residence. Your bodies will be safe.”","Yun Jianyue smiled. “That’s the safest place in the academy, and that ice sculpture is there too. There’s no reason for me to worry.”","Pei Mianman was surprised. “Aren’t the two of you rivals? Will she protect your body?”","“We are enemies, but I acknowledge her character. She wouldn’t resort to despicable means to defeat me. If our positions were switched, I’d protect her body too,” Yun Jianyue replied without any hesitation.","Pei Mianman was baffled. What a weird relationship they have. I don’t know if they're enemies or friends. She was so intent on cornering Yan Xuehen just a moment ago. Not knowing what to do about this situation, she said, “Ah Zu, I’d like to visit Chuyan first.”","That would be an opportunity for her to catch up with Chuyan and consult her on how to deal with this matter."]},{"number":2737,"title":"Chapter 2737: Chapter 2689: Coming Clean","paragraphs":["Zu An accepted Pei Mianman’s request. He'd previously been worried about bothering Chu Chuyan, fearing that she would be in greater pain if she woke up, but from their previous interaction, he'd learned that she was happy to wake up and chat with people she knew.","Yun Jianyue also spoke up. “I’ll join you.”","Pei Mianman looked at her questioningly, causing her face to heat up. I can’t say that we’re all sisters, right? It’ll help to dampen the blow if we at least get familiar with each other.","Yun Jianyue wasn't afraid of Chu Chuyan, but considering the latter’s special standing, she wanted to avoid unnecessary trouble. To keep Pei Mianman from thinking too much, she explained, “I’d like to see the legendary Bridge of Oblivion.”","Zu An chuckled in his heart. I didn’t expect big sister Yun to have such an adorable side to her.","The two ladies initially had their minds occupied, but they soon found themselves awed by the Netherworld’s scenery.","“I’d never have expected the legendary Netherworld to be our playground.” Yun Jianyue turned to Zu An. This fellow is extraordinary. No wonder he has so many women charmed. At this point, she suddenly glared at Zu An and asked, “Ah Zu, do you have an affair with that ice sculpture?”","It was much more discreet to communicate via souls, so there was no need to worry about Pei Mianman overhearing them.","Zu An sighed. “Would you believe me if I said no?”","“Of course not!” Yun Jianyue harrumphed. You’d obviously cover up for that ice sculpture if there’s something between the two of you.","“See. Why bother asking me if you won’t believe me?” Zu An sighed.","“Looks like there really is something between you two!” Yun Jianyue sneered.","“There isn’t.”","“I’m sure of it!”","“There isn’t.”","...","This argument continued until they reached the Bridge of Oblivion.","The two ladies, despite having gone through a lot, were taken aback. The Oblivion River’s blood-tinged yellow river emanated a bloodthirsty aura that made their souls tremble even from a far distance away. They wouldn’t want to approach it even if no one told them about the Oblivion River’s traits.","Taking a closer look, they saw countless warped faces in the water. Those were the vengeful spirits cursed to suffer in the Oblivion River for eternity. But sitting at the center of this terrifying river of death was a sacred lotus flower. A beautiful figure could be vaguely spotted amid its iridescent lights, adding some vibrancy to the oppressive scene.","“Chuyan is too pitiful.” Pei Mianman bit her lips. She'd already heard about Chu Chuyan’s condition, but the shock of witnessing it in person still left her feeling melancholic.","Even Yun Jianyue, who was accustomed to seeing mountains of corpses and rivers of blood, fell silent. She felt a tinge of regret. Did we go too far plotting against them in the last two days? That ice sculpture is hateful, but her disciple is innocent.","Zu An gently called out to Chu Chuyan. The lotus flower in the Oblivion River blossomed, and its seven-colored divine light gradually expanded. The beauty lying within opened her eyes.","“Ah Zu!” Chu Chuyan was overjoyed to see Zu An. She hadn’t expected them to reunite so quickly.","“Chuyan!” Zu An noticed the joy in her eyes and thought that he should visit her more often.","Chu Chuyan noticed his company and embarrassedly called out, “Sect Master Yun, Manman...” Would they mistake my interaction with Ah Zu as a declaration of dominance?","Yun JIanyue nodded in acknowledgment.","Pei Mianman excitedly called out, “Chuyan!”","She tried to dash to Chu Chuyan’s side. Horrified, Zu An stopped and warned her, “You mustn’t get afflicted by the Oblivion River, or else it’ll wash away your memories and turn you into one of its countless vengeful spirits.”","Chu Chuyan offered the same warning too.","Pei Mianman remarked hoarsely, “Chuyan, you've really suffered.”","She was close friends with Chu Chuyan. While she'd initially had ulterior motives for approaching her, they became friends after years of company. The knowledge that her best friend had to stay in a place like this for a thousand years filled her with irrepressible sorrow.","Chu Chuyan smiled. “Manman, don’t worry about me. I’m protected by the Pure World Icelotus, and Zu An is taking care of me too. It’s not as bad as you think.”","Chu Chuyan’s consolation only made Pei Mianman feel even more melancholic.","Yun Jianyue tugged Zu An’s sleeves and said, “Why don’t we let them chat in private?”","She could have used this opportunity to express concern and forge closer ties with Chu Chuyan, but her pride wouldn’t let her do so. There were no ties between them on the surface, so if she proactively approached Chu Chuyan, it would make her seem like the weaker one.","Zu An could also tell that Chu Chuyan and Pei Mianman had many things to talk about, and their presence here was a hindrance, so he imbued Pei Mianman’s soul with a portion of his energy to protect her before taking Yun Jianyue elsewhere.","After those two departed, Chu Chuyan asked teasingly, “Manman, isn’t Ah Zu caring?”","Pei Mianman’s face reddened. It was inappropriate of her to get together with Zu An, considering that he was her best friend’s man. “Chuyan, I...”","Chu Chuyan raised a hand to stop her apology. “Manman, do you think I’d be concerned about this after everything I've been through?”","Pei Mianman thought that made sense. It was the same for her too. The Myriad Worlds were so humongous that such social propriety just felt insignificant in comparison. “Chuyan, I was being narrow-minded.”","Chu Chuyan smiled. They exchanged some pleasantries before she suddenly asked, “I heard Ah Zu met someone known as the Goddess of Wu Mountain in their previous life. Is that your previous incarnation?”","“That thing makes me feel so stifled. I don’t remember anything about my previous life. It feels like Ah Zu had another relationship behind my back, but that person is somehow ‘me’, so I can’t get mad at that...” Pei Mianman began venting to Chu Chuyan. It felt as if they had returned to their old times in Brightmoon City, when they would spill their hearts to each other.","...","A while later, Pei Mianman suddenly remembered her reason for coming here and asked, “Chuyan, what kind of person do you think your master is?”","Chu Chuyan was taken aback, but she replied with a smile, “My master is a wonderful person. If not for her, my life would have gone down a different path. The world thinks that she’s a lofty ice immortal incapable of human emotions, but I know my master is full of feelings. It’s just that she's sealed away her heart for her cultivation, which makes her appear cold to others.”","Pei Mianman hadn’t expected Chu Chuyan to have such an evaluation of her master. She further probed, “Do you think your master would fall in love with a man?”","“Under normal circumstances, no, but there’s no way to say for certain when it comes to feelings.” Chu Chuyan’s clear eyes seemed to peer right into the truth.","Pei Mianman hesitantly asked, “What kind of man do you think could catch your master’s eye?”","“Someone like Ah Zu,” Chu Chuyan replied.","Pei Mianman was flabbergasted. “You already know about it?”"]},{"number":2738,"title":"Chapter 2738: Chapter 2690: Solution","paragraphs":["Chu Chuyan revealed a faint smile. “You abruptly asked me about my master, and most people wouldn’t talk about my master and romance in the same breath. You wouldn’t have asked such a question if you hadn’t noticed something.”","Pei Mianman felt a mixture of awkwardness and awe. “I was worried you would be hurt, but I didn’t think it would be fair for you to be kept in the dark either. That’s why I hesitated.”","“You’re a good friend,” Chu Chuyan said with a heartened smile. She could tell whether Pei Mianman was trying to drive a wedge between her and her master or was genuinely worried about her.","“How did you know? Did Ah Zu tell you?” Pei Mianman was curious.","“He doesn’t have the guts,” Chu Chuyan scoffed. “I discovered it myself.”","“You aren’t angry at all?” Pei Mianman was surprised by how nonchalant Chu Chuyan was.","“How can I be angry? The two of them got together because of me,” Chu Chuyan remarked with a sigh.","Pei Mianman was taken aback. Is Chuyan into being cuckolded? Did she secretly push me and Ah Zu together back then too? Am I just a toy for those two?","Judging from her expression, Chu Chuyan could tell she had misunderstood. She rolled her eyes and said, “What are you thinking? It’s because I was the Snow Lady at a certain point in spacetime!”","Pei Mianman finally realized what Chu Chuyan was getting at. She sheepishly replied, “Ah, I think you mentioned that before.”","“That’s why I only have myself to blame. After becoming the Snow Lady, I lost my memories and hunted them down, leaving them with no choice but to resort to that to rescue me.” Chu Chuyan had been magnanimous when she consoled her master, but it was still a blow to her. That was why she was ranting to her good friend now.","Pei Mianman secretly chuckled. “Indeed, you can’t blame them for what happened.”","“That’s why I feel so stifled. I want to vent but I can’t find anyone to vent to!” Chu Chuyan smacked her thighs whenever she thought about this.","“So, you’re permitting their relationship?” Pei Mianman was perplexed. “I can’t imagine your master’s reaction to that.”","“She doesn’t know that I know,” Chu Chuyan replied with a sigh.","Pei Mianman was stunned. You’re wilder than I thought!","Chu Chuyan explained, “You know my master too. She’s lofty and cares about her reputation. I’m worried she’ll do something extreme if this matter is revealed.”","Pei Mianman nodded in understanding. “That’s possible.”","Yan Xuehen was too famous. The world saw her as a paragon of purity. No one would accept her getting into a relationship with a man.","Had her partner been anyone else, she could have just weathered the storm and it would all eventually pass. But of all people, her partner was Ah Zu, her own disciple’s husband.","Pei Mianman could already imagine how the world would react. They would say that she appeared pure on the surface but secretly schemed to steal her disciple’s man—making her worse than the Devil Sect’s demonesses.","That was what the world was like. They were much more tolerant of villains than good people. A villain would be praised for doing something good for once, whereas a person who had been good their whole life would be eternally condemned for committing the slightest misdeed.","“That’s why I hid the truth from my master. I told Ah Zu to find a way to help her come to terms with this.” Chu Chuyan felt tired. She was the one being cuckolded, yet she still had to clean up after them.","Pei Mianman was stunned. “So Ah Zu knows that you know!” She gritted her teeth in anger. So Ah Zu had Chu Chuyan’s permission all this time. To think I was worried for him!","Chu Chuyan suddenly tensed up. “Was it not Ah Zu who told you about it? How else did you learn about their relationship?”","Pei Mianman told Chu Chuyan about how Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei had tried to solicit her help to investigate Zu An and Yan Xuehen’s relationship.","Chu Chuyan was so agitated that she stood up from the lotus and nearly fell into the Oblivion River. “This is bad! Sect Master Yun is my master’s nemesis. My master will be in trouble if she learns the truth!”","Pei Mianman interjected, “Despite Sect Master Yun’s reputation as a demoness, I don’t think she’s a bad person after getting to know her. I don’t think she’ll corner Sect Master Yan.”","Chu Chuyan paced around the lotus. “Sect Master Yan can be magnanimous at times, but that's toward others and not my master. My master and her are true mortal enemies. For many years, she's failed to outdo my master. She won’t miss a chance to mock my master. My master can remain nonchalant before anyone but her. Faced with Sect Master Yan’s ridicule, I suspect she would rather die than suffer the shame.”","Pei Mianman’s head hurt. “But Sect Master Yun and Honglei are suspecting their relationship, whereas Sect Master Yan knows nothing about the situation. She’s at a disadvantage.”","Chu Chuyan frowned. She pondered for a while before asking, “Manman, can you help my master? Didn’t Sect Master Yun send you to investigate my master? You placate them for now and find a chance to subtly tip off my master.”","Pei Mianman was conflicted. “Have you forgotten that Sect Master Yun is my older cousin?”","“Aren’t we sisters too?” Chu Chuyan blinked. “Not to mention we’re close friends on top of that. You don’t intend to side with me?”","Pei Mianman was rendered speechless. “Fine, I’ll help you this once. But only this once!” Just thinking about the matter gave her a headache.","“That won’t do,” Chu Chuyan anxiously spoke up. “It doesn’t seem like Ah Zu has unraveled my master’s concerns yet. You need to help him.”","“How can I help?”","“Help them normalize their relationship, so my master can be with him openly.”","Pei Mianman glared at Chu Chuyan begrudgingly. “Chuyan, have you forgotten Ah Zu is my man too? You want me to help another woman claim possession of my man?”","“Manman, I know you’re the best. Please, I’m begging you. I’ll owe you a favor. I’ll help you do one thing in the future too,” Chu Chuyan said coyly.","Pei Mianman was reminded of their days in Brightmoon City. They'd often chatted like that in private too. That softened her heart. “Fine, I’ll give it a try, but this matter is too tricky to deal with. I don’t even know where to start.”","Chu Chuyan fell silent. “I’ve been thinking about ways to normalize their relationship, and I do have an awful idea in mind.”","“What is it?” Pei Mianman was intrigued.","Chu Chuyan’s eyes gleamed. “What if Sect Master Yun got together with Ah Zu too?”","Pei Mianman was speechless."]},{"number":2739,"title":"Chapter 2739: Chapter 2691: Battle Plan","paragraphs":["Pei Mianman was shocked beyond words. Sister, are you really into being cuckolded?","Chu Chuyan embarrassedly explained, “Desperate situations call for desperate measures. I've thought hard, but I couldn’t find a way to unravel the knot in my master’s heart. One day, it occurred to me that my master’s biggest fear is Sect Master Yun. If Sect Master Yun were in the same plight, neither of them could mock the other. That would resolve the issue.”","Pei Mianman took in a deep breath. “Chuyan, I want to ask you a question, but I hope you won’t get angry.”","“What is it?”","“Are you helping your master, or do you want Honglei to experience having her man be snatched by her master too?”","Chu Chuyan’s expression stiffened. It was a long while before she exhaled. “I wouldn’t have realized it if you hadn’t mentioned it. I might really have harbored such a thought subconsciously. Honglei and I are the representative disciples of our respective factions, and we've been competing for the longest time. I never expected that notion to be so deeply embedded within me that I wasn’t even aware of it.”","Indeed. If this matter were to be revealed, my master and I wouldn’t be able to face anyone. Qiu Honglei and I were the top disciples of our respective factions, and there's never been a victor between us. The thought of losing to her here makes me feel uncomfortable.","Chu Chuyan’s frank confession left Pei Mianman at a loss for words. A long time later, she exhaled deeply and said, “I didn’t think you would harbor the same thought as them. It feels like the so-called 'Holy Maiden' and 'Demoness' titles are just a difference in faction.”","Chu Chuyan smiled. “Human hearts are complicated. How can it be easy for a mind to become truly unshakable?”","“But how can I help you with that?” Pei Mianman felt extremely awkward. The person she had to matchmake here was her lover!","“I would have done it myself if I could leave this place.” Chu Chuyan looked at her nearly transparent body in misery.","Pei Mianman’s heart shuddered. She has to remain here for a thousand years. That can’t be easy. The least I can do is to help her with her request... It was still awkward, but she figured she ought to do something for Chu Chuyan. “I can help you, but this is unfair to Sect Master Yun. I feel like I’m corrupting a virtuous maiden.”","“Do you think Sect Master Yun doesn’t have feelings for Ah Zu?” Chu Chuyan asked with bright eyes that seemed to see through all facades.","“Ah?” Pei Mianman was startled. “Do you know something?”","Chu Chuyan shook her head. “I was bored under the Oblivion Bridge, so I began thinking about Ah Zu’s lovers and when each pair got together. I noticed there was something amiss between Ah Zu and Sect Master Yun.”","Pei Mianman was stunned. She hadn’t expected that her usually cold-natured friend would think about such things. “Ah Zu said that you were hibernating.”","“It’s a thousand years. I have more than enough time to hibernate, so I try to wake up every now and then,” Chu Chuyan replied.","“Aren’t you lonely?” Pei Mianman felt worried for Chu Chuyan, especially when she looked at the terrifying surroundings.","“I’m used to being alone,” Chu Chuyan replied with a smile. “Besides, it’s interesting to think about those matters.”","Pei Mianman felt conscience-stricken. Did she also think about when I got together with Ah Zu?","“I thought that if even my master could get together with Ah Zu, no one in the world would be safe from Ah Zu’s charms.” Chu Chuyan said. “The first person that popped into my mind was Sect Master Yun. Considering Ah Zu’s personality, do you think it’s possible for there to be nothing between them?”","“Your argument is weirdly convincing.”","Pei Mianman racked her mind. There was indeed an inexplicable intimacy between Zu An and Yun Jianyue. Given Yun Jianyue’s reputation and position as Qiu Honglei’s master, she had never thought of such a possibility before.","But on second thought, those factors meant nothing at all. Even Yan Xuehen got together with Ah Zu, for god’s sake!","“We don’t have to resort to forceful measures. If they're innocent, given their cultivation, nothing will happen between them no matter how we scheme.” Chu Chuyan smiled.","Those words convinced Pei Mianman. She no longer felt guilty. “Since you've been thinking about this for so long, do you have a plan in mind?”","“Not at all.” Chu Chuyan shook her head. She looked at Pei Mianman and said, “I’m leaving it in your hands. With your wits, I’m sure you’ll find the perfect plan.”","Pei Mianman replied, “...Chuyan, are you messing with me now?”","She'd thought Chu Chuyan had already planned everything out, and that she would only need to execute the plan. It turned out that she was both the brains and the brawn of the operation!","Chu Chuyan felt apologetic. “Manman, I’m not messing with you. There’s only so much I can do without knowing the situation on the ground. The two of them are smart people. Whatever I can come up with here won’t escape their notice. But it’s different for you, not to mention you’re Sect Master Yun’s younger cousin. I’m sure you’ll find a feasible solution.”","Pei Mianman rolled her eyes. “So you also know she’s my older cousin!”","“But I think we’re closer.”","“Tsk. Scram!”","...","While the two of them were chatting, Yun Jianyue was raising the pressure on Zu An. “There must be something between you and that ice sculpture!”","Zu An felt helpless. “You’re overthinking things.”","He was getting goosebumps all over his body. He couldn’t sell out Yan Xuehen unless she agreed to it. It would be the same if Yan Xuehen questioned him about Yun Jianyue too.","Yun Jianyue was confused. She had questioned him many times along the way, but Zu An persisted in his stance. That made her confidence wane. Still, she persisted. “Do you earnestly have no feelings for that ice sculpture? We might be enemies, but I have to concede that her charm is incredible. Countless men in the world fancy her, you know?”","“But she’s Chuyan’s master, after all...” Zu An replied.","“Hah! And I am Honglei’s master.”","“Given Sect Master Yan’s personality, do you think it’s possible?”","“I wouldn’t have considered this possibility if it were any other man, but you are a master at this. Who knows whether she’d fall for you?”","“...”","Zu An coughed. “This is a rare chance to explore the Netherworld. You should be focusing on this Blood Sea Hell instead of such unnecessary things. Manman is calling me.” With that, he flitted off.","Yun Jianyue looked at the Blood Sea Hell before her with a frown.","Zu An flew to the Oblivion Bridge to bring Pei Mianman to the Yellow Spring Road, where she could examine the Red Spider Lilies.","Just as he was relieved to be freed of Yun Jianyue’s interrogation, Pei Mianman suddenly asked, “Ah Zu, is there something between you and big sister Yun?”"]},{"number":2740,"title":"Chapter 2740: Chapter 2692: It’d Be Rude Not to Return the Favor","paragraphs":["Zu An’s heart skipped a beat, but he maintained a straight face. “Why do you ask?”","“Your relationship with Sect Master Yun seems to transcend that of ordinary friends.” Pei Mianman couldn’t tell him that it was Chu Chuyan’s conjecture.","“We've braved life and death situations in dungeons together. We’re bound to be closer than friends,” Zu An replied with a chuckle. “Don’t think nonsense and focus on the Red Spider Lilies. Let’s see if they can resonate with your Paramita Butterfly.”","He had already gotten numb to the grilling. At this rate, he could get PTSD from this. I have to find a way to resolve this matter as soon as possible, or else it’ll remain a huge landmine.","His composed attitude made Pei Mianman wonder if Chu Chuyan had been overthinking things. But she suppressed her doubt, walked into the field of Red Spider Lilies, and examined the flowers close up.","Zu An quietly left the area so that she could focus on her cultivation.","He returned to the Oblivion Bridge to accompany Chuyan. They chatted for a while before he finally asked, “Chuyan, did Manman say something to you earlier?”","“It was just some usual talk between close friends.” Chu Chuyan blinked. “What’s wrong? Did you do something wrong?”","“Of course not...” Zu An replied sheepishly. Maybe I should start revealing the truth about Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue, or else I might go crazy at this rate! His only concern was that the damage to Yan Xuehen would be far greater than to Yun Jianyue.","Yun Jianyue would be embarrassed, but Yan Xuehen would take the brunt of the blow and be condemned by the world. There was no way Yan Xuehen would be able to withstand the shame.","Haa, this is the downside of building up a good guy persona.","Chu Chuyan noticed Zu An’s unnatural attitude but didn’t expose him. Instead, she began chatting with him about other subjects.","Time swiftly flew by. Zu An eventually had to reluctantly bid Chu Chuyan farewell to take Yun Jianyue and Pei Mianman out of the Netherworld, lest its death energy harmed them.","Along the way, he asked, “How was it? Did you grasp anything?”","Yun Jianyue’s cheeks heated up. Her mind had been too set on Yan Xuehen’s affairs for her to calm down, so she replied ambiguously, “I felt something, but I might need a few more trips.”","Pei Mianman replied, “It’s the same for me too, so I might need more time.”","Zu An nodded. “Don’t worry about it. I’ll take you here a few more times before I leave. It’ll be best if you can make a breakthrough by then.”","His words reminded them that he could have to head to Dreamland at any time, and that left them with heavy hearts.","Yun Jianyue harrumphed. “You talk as if you’re leaving a will. It’s just some Dreamland. I’ll charge into even mountains of knives and seas of flames with you.”","Pei Mianman glanced at Yun Jianyue. She wouldn’t have thought much about those words under normal circumstances, but after her earlier conversation with Chu Chuyan, she couldn’t help but think that those words sounded like a confession.","“It’s too dangerous over there, and only I have an invitation letter. You should focus on your training instead. You might be able to help me in the future,” Zu An consoled Yun Jianyue with a smile.","Yun Jianyue felt a twinge of guilt. Her lover was about to embark on a dangerous journey, but her mind was still on bickering with the ice sculpture. Hmph! I guess I’ll let things slip if that ice sculpture lowers her head to me.","Pei Mianman was thinking along the same lines too. Ah Zu is about to leave. I should at least resolve things on this side so he can leave with peace of mind. That made her more motivated to carry out the task Chu Chuyan had entrusted to her.","Zu An brought the two ladies back to the peak of Mount Yuquan and returned their souls to their bodies. As soon as they opened their eyes, they saw Yan Xuehen.","“Ice sculpture, why are you staring at me?” Yun Jianyue felt awkward.","Yan Xuehen smiled. “It’s nothing. It just occurred to me that I know very little about you.”","“What a ridiculous thought,” Yun Jianyue scoffed before leaving to look for Qiu Honglei. She was going to ask her disciple if Yan Xuehen had discovered something.","Zu An was perplexed too. “Sect Master Yan, something feels different about you today.”","“After thinking things through, I’m in a better mood.” Yan Xuehen didn’t mention Yun Jianyue, knowing Zu An wouldn’t admit to it.","White Jing Teng had shrugged off the matter as her little sister’s misunderstanding, but Yan Xuehen was no fool. After she returned to her room and calmed down, she'd quickly realized that the other party couldn’t have been talking about her.","There was no reason for Black Jing Teng to have gone through the trouble to tell her that. She had to have other intentions in mind. Thus, Yan Xuehen had deduced that the Jing Teng sisters must have sensed something peculiar between Yun Jianyue and Zu An, and thus put on an act to pit her against Yun Jianyue.","Well, I shall fall for it!","Her relationship with Zu An had been suffocating her. She was fond of Zu An, but she was terrified about what could happen if their affair was exposed. Despite her wits, she couldn’t think of a solution to resolve this matter. Her stress had nearly caused her to manifest an inner demon.","But upon learning that Yun Jianyue could be involved with Zu An, she'd suddenly seen the light at the end of the tunnel.","So the demoness is guilty too!","Thinking about how they had toyed with her made her clench her teeth in anger.","How could Ah Zu not tell me about his affair with the demoness?!","You have successfully trolled Yan Xuehen for +110... +110... +110...","Zu An was bewildered. Why is she suddenly angry at me? Is she jealous that I spent time with Yun Jianyue and Pei Mianman instead of her?","“The imperial palace sent a letter over. The empress and the empress dowager wish to discuss matters with you. The Qin clan and the Chu clan are also looking for you,” Yan Xuehen said.","Ah, so it’s because of that. Zu An couldn’t say too much as Manman was still around, so he simply exchanged some pleasantries before taking his leave.","After he left, Yan Xuehen turned to Pei Mianman and asked, “Manman, is there something on my face?”","“Sect Master Yan looks more ravishing than ever. Did something joyous happen?” Pei Mianman asked with a smile.","Yan Xuehen’s face reddened. She replied with a tinge of guilt, “Looks are of secondary concern to cultivators. Did you meet Chuyan?”","“I met her. We even talked about you.” Pei Mianman scoffed in her heart. Hah, I see that cultivators are all good actors.","Yan Xuehen’s heart skipped a beat. “What did she say?”","“She said that you’re a good master and that the two of you are on good terms. She told me to take good care of you while she’s away,” Pei Mianman said.","“Chuyan worries too much. I’m not a child anymore. What’s there to take care of?” Yan Xuehen was perplexed.","“You never know.” Pei Mianman smiled enigmatically before taking her leave.","Yan Xuehen felt as if Pei Mianman was trying to say something, but she shrugged it off for the time being as there were more important matters for her to attend to. That demoness used her desire energy to scheme against me. It’s time for me to return the favor.","She had prepared a gift for Yun Jianyue while the latter's soul was out."]},{"number":2741,"title":"Chapter 2741: Chapter 2693: Tit For Tat","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Yun Jianyue entered Qiu Honglei’s room. The latter woke up from her meditation and welcomed her with a smile. “Master, were there any gains from your trip?”","Yun Jianyue shook her head. “I could hardly calm down thinking about the ice sculpture. I felt some inspiration from observing the Blood Sea Hell, but I couldn’t make a breakthrough.”","“Master, don’t push yourself too hard,” Qiu Honglei consoled with a smile. “Such spurs of inspiration happen by chance. There’s no way to force it.”","Yun Jianyue’s heart warmed up. She hugged Qiu Honglei. “My dear disciple is the best. You know how to console me.”","The two of them had previously hugged often. The master doted on the disciple, and the disciple relished in the master’s care and concern. But now that they'd become sisters, it felt weird for them to continue hugging like this. Thus, they quietly parted from each other with unnatural looks.","Qiu Honglei broke the awkward silence and asked, “Master, did you meet Chuyan?”","“I did...” Yun Jianyue told Qiu Honglei what she'd seen underneath the Oblivion Bridge.","Qiu Honglei felt wistful. After learning about the latter's plight, she couldn’t bring herself to continue competing with Chu Chuyan anymore. All she felt was sympathy. The thought of spending a thousand years alone under the Netherworld Bridge could send shivers down anyone’s spine.","After learning about what she had to go through, anyone with the slightest kindness in them wouldn’t harbor enmity toward Chu Chuyan.","“Yan Xuehen is too much, capitalizing on this opportunity to steal her man! How despicable!” Yun Jianyue scoffed.","Qiu Honglei burst into laughter. My master just can’t stop harping about Yan Xuehen. If not for their long-time grudge, I would have thought they were in love with each other.","“It would be a surprise if Sect Master Yan were truly in a relationship with Ah Zu.” Even now, Qiu Honglei still doubted Zu An and Yan Xuehen’s relationship. Her impression of Yan Xuehen as a pure and virtuous person was simply too overwhelming.","“But that ice sculpture behaved weirdly when we returned.” Yun Jianyue thought about her encounter with Yan Xuehen earlier and frowned.","“What happened?”","“I suspect she knows about my relationship with Ah Zu.”","“That can’t be. Only I know about your relationship with Ah Zu, and you wouldn’t tell anyone else.” Qiu Honglei was taken aback.","“I hope I’m overthinking things. That ice sculpture is no fool. By now, she might have figured out that I did something to her,” Yun Jianyue said grimly.","“You have to tread carefully, master. Don’t turn from the hunter to the hunted.”","“Don’t worry, I’m not that dumb.”","“Master, what should we do next?” Qiu Honglei asked.","“I've already used desire energy on that ice sculpture once. She might notice it if I make another attempt, and Ah Zu is no fool either. He might have fallen for it the first time, but he’ll realize it if it happens again.” Yun Jianyue frowned. “We have to plan our next move carefully.”","They brainstormed many ideas, but discarded every one in the end. Ultimately, they couldn’t decide on a course of action.","Seeing that it was getting late, Yun Jianyue retired to her room. She didn’t rest right away, but instead inspected her room. Soon, she noticed a projection mirror fragment planted discreetly in the corner of the room. She would have never seen it if her guard was down.","“That conniving ice sculpture! She planted this thing here to film me and Ah Zu!” Yun Jianyue was glad she had sensed something amiss with the ice sculpture, or else she would have fallen for this ploy.","She scanned the room once more to make sure there were no other projection mirror fragments. Hmph, I won’t give that ice sculpture a chance to film me with Ah Zu. She crushed the projection mirror and drifted off to sleep.","In the neighboring room, Yan Xuehen suddenly opened her eyes and smiled. That demoness is as sharp as I thought, but she still fell for my trick.","She was indeed the one who'd planted that projection mirror fragment in Yun Jianyue’s room, and she had made sure to hide it in a discreet location. But after years of rivalry with Yun Jianyue, she knew how difficult of a foe the latter was better than anyone.","The projection mirror fragment was a feint to lull Yun Jianyue into a false sense of security. She would have never guessed that the projection mirror fragment was just the start of the trap. As soon as she crushed the projection mirror fragment, the trap went into motion.","Yan Xuehen knew her cultivation was, at most, on par with Yun Jianyue's. No matter how meticulous her ploy was, it would have been unlikely for her to completely escape Yun Jianyue’s detection. She was confident in her skills, but she wasn’t arrogant. Thus, she hadn’t done everything by herself, and had instead sought Jing Teng, Xie Daoyun, and Qi Yaoguang’s help.","Of course, Jing Teng wouldn’t admit she was trying to deal with Yun Jianyue, making Yan Xuehen think, Those two are always playing good cop, bad cop; it’s hard to tell what they're thinking.","She'd also consulted Xie Daoyun and Qi Yaoguang for this matter. The former’s aptitude in formations surpassed hers, whereas Qi Yaoguang could provide a mysterious oracular energy that made the formation even more unfathomable. Neither Xie Daoyun nor Qi Yaoguang had thought too much about what Yan Xuehen was up to because of her virtuous image. If anything, they were flattered that she was consulting them, and they'd naturally given their all to assist her.","Therefore, Yun Jianyue wasn't just up against Yan Xuehen alone, but the combined powers of the Jing Teng sisters, the formation master Xie Daoyun, and the mystery master Qi Yaoguang. It wouldn’t be surprising for her to be caught in their trap.","Indeed, Yun Jianyue thought she'd foiled Yan Xuehen’s ploy, so she lowered her guard and went to sleep. She descended into a dream that Yan Xuehen had meticulously woven for her.","In her dream, she saw the sky split apart, and a peculiar ship descended. An envoy on the ship claimed that he would bring Zu An to Dreamland. Everyone was reluctant to part with Zu An, but the envoy suddenly declared that Yun Jianyue was one of the guests as well. It turned out catching the gaze of a universal deity had won her an invitation letter too.","She was surprised and overjoyed. She even shot a provocative look at Yan Xuehen, and the latter’s look of defeat filled her with glee. I finally outdid her at something!","She boarded the ship with Zu An, and the two of them set off to Dreamland. Along the way, they were attacked by an Annihilation Beast. It was comparable to the one who destroyed the Monster World; it made quick work of the ship crew.","She fought hard against the Annihilation Beast with Zu An and managed to drive it off, but the fight left Zu An severely injured. He was on his last breath.","Yun Jianyue wept uncontrollably. “Ah Zu, what do I have to do to save you?”","“Dual cultivation...” Zu An only managed to utter those words before falling unconscious.","Yun Jianyue caught his drift and began taking off her clothes."]},{"number":2742,"title":"Chapter 2742: Chapter 2694: Confession","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Yan Xuehen was in the neighboring room. The air before her rippled like water before forming a mirror. The images in the mirror reflected what Yun Jianyue was experiencing in her dream.","Even Yan Xuehen was awed. I’d have never been able to pull this off without Jing Teng, Xie Daoyun, and Qi Yaoguang’s help. A person reacts the most genuinely in an illusion like this.","She tightly grabbed her sleeves. She had never felt so nervous before. On one hand, she could claim the upper hand against the demoness if she could acquire evidence of Yun Jianyue’s affair with Zu An. On the other hand, she was worried that there was really something between Yun Jianyue and Zu An.","Her relationship with Zu An defied convention and left her constantly nervous, but it also filled her with bliss. There were even times when she felt a sense of superiority over Yun Jianyue. But that meant nothing if Yun Jianyue was with Zu An too. The thought of sharing a man with the demoness made her feel worse than death.","The scenes revealed in the mirror made her breathing hasten.","The relationship between Yun Jianyue and Zu An clearly transcended friendship, but again, given that they'd only had each other in a foreign land, it was normal for them to be more intimate than usual.","When the scene cut to Zu An getting severely injured by the Annihilation Beast and needing dual cultivation with Yun Jianyue to survive, Yan Xuehen's heart pounded nervously. She wanted to see what Yun Jianyue would do here.","When Yun Jianyue unhesitatingly took off her belt, Yan Xuehen's heart nearly leaped out of her mouth. Could they be...","In the other room, Yun Jianyue suddenly stopped her movements. She sensed something was amiss, but she couldn’t put her finger on it. There seemed to be something wrong, but when she thought back on it, everything appeared to make sense.","She glanced at the unconscious Zu An and fell into deep thought.","...","In the imperial palace, the Empress Dowager and Bi Linglong were overjoyed by Zu An’s visit and welcomed him warmly.","Zu An initially chatted joyously with them, but when he learned that neither of them had invited him over, his expression suddenly collapsed. But Yan Xuehen said...","He closed his eyes and focused his senses. He felt a peculiar formation pulsating from the residence on top of Mount Yuquan. He immediately understood what was going on.","He felt angry but amused. It turned out Yan Xuehen had sent him away so he wouldn’t get in the way of her ploy. Who could have thought the upright Yan Xuehen would play such a trick?","I can’t return right away and expose Yan Xuehen, or else it could wound her reputation and evoke suspicion. After some thought, he decided to send a voice transmission to Yun Jianyue. With his current cultivation, he could easily pull that off without alarming Yan Xuehen.","Yun Jianyue already harbored doubt about this dream, and Zu An’s reminder further convinced her that this was a ploy. Her face warped murderously. “Who dares to make a fool out of me?!”","A devastating blood sea and blood moon manifested around her and frenziedly destroyed everything in the vicinity.","Such illusion formations only worked if the other party had their guard down. Once the target realized it was just an illusion, the formation could no longer trap her. Thus, Yan Xuehen’s mirror shattered.","Yun Jianyue traced the ki pulsation to her room and was infuriated. She charged at Yan Xuehen while roaring, “Ice sculpture! I didn’t expect you to be this despicable!”","Yan Xuehen was bewildered. I was just a step off. Why did she suddenly regain composure?","“Hah, who could have expected the proud master of the Devil Sect to be willing to use her body to save someone? Have the two of you been together all this time?” Yan Xuehen was also livid when she thought about what had happened nearing the end of the illusion.","The sheer feeling of shame further fanned Yun Jianyue’s anger. I nearly fell for this woman’s ploy! “Hah, when did I do that? Someone who got together with her disciple’s man shouldn’t be maligning others!”","“Nonsense!”","“Back at you!”","The two of them exchanged jabs while crossing blows. The residence was protected by formations, but how could those formations withstand the shockwaves produced by these two top-notch experts? It didn’t take long for them to destroy the building.","Qiu Honglei, Pei Mianman, and the others rushed over and were horrified. “Master (Cousin Yun), Sect Master Yan, what are you doing?!”","Even the academy’s teachers also rushed over. Now that outsiders were around, both women tacitly chose not to mention Zu An anymore and instead focused on crossing blows. The entire residence was soon leveled.","Many people from the academy felt a pinch in their hearts. This residence had been personally built by the old libationer, and many considered it to be a sacred place. To think it would be destroyed like that!","But no one dared to complain about it. The two women were too terrifying. Their enmity was well-known, and no one wanted to get on their bad side.","Fortunately, a seven-colored light descended from the sky shortly after. Zu An had returned.","“Libationer!” Those from the academy were relieved. If you'd taken any longer, our academy would have been destroyed by those two dinosaurs!","With Zu An standing between them, both Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue stopped their attacks and looked away with a harrumph. It was as if they couldn’t hold themselves if they saw each other’s faces.","“What happened?” Zu An asked.","“You ask her!” Yun Jianyue huffed.","“Says the guilty one!” Yan Xuehen scoffed coldly.","“What do I have to be guilty about?”","“You know it deep down.”","“You think you’re in the right after scheming against me?”","“I’m merely returning the favor.”","...","Xie Daoyun and Qi Yaoguang were baffled. Ah! Sect Master Yan solicited our help to deal with Sect Master Yun!","They'd beenflattered when Yan Xuehen knocked on their doors. They had always looked up to her, so they naturally did everything they could to help her. Who could have thought she would use them against Sect Master Yun?","Mount Yuquan’s residence ended up getting destroyed because of that. We have a responsibility to pay for that.","Zu An sighed. He restored the residence with a wave of his hand.","The crowd had already witnessed plenty of his methods before, but this sight still made their eyes turn red in enthusiasm. They excitedly asked him how he'd pulled it off.","Zu An settled the crowd down before calling Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue over. He intended to mediate between them, but the two women ignored him. They were both already convinced he was in a relationship with the other woman and would side with her, so they returned to their rooms and slammed the door.","Zu An felt his head hurt.","Pei Mianman secretly laughed under her breath. “Ah Zu, I’ll talk to them on your behalf.”","“I’ll be troubling you.” When it came to matters of the heart, Zu An’s strength was of no use.","Pei Mianman first made her way to Yun Jianyue’s room. Since they were cousins, the latter didn’t turn her away.","“There must be something between that ice sculpture and Ah Zu, or else she wouldn’t use such a method to test me.” Yun Jianyue gritted her teeth in anger.","Pei Mianman thought about what Chu Chuyan had told her. She took a deep breath and decided to get to the point. “Big sister, let’s put Sect Master Yan aside for now. Are you in a relationship with Ah Zu?”","Yun Jianyue immediately panicked. “Don’t talk nonsense, Manman. How can there... possibly be anything between me and that fellow? I’m talking about that ice sculpture now.”","Pei Mianman sighed. “Big sister, you can’t cover fire with paper. Can’t you tell me the truth?”","Yun Jianyue’s face flickered with several emotions. Seeing that things had gotten to this point, she decided not to argue her way out of it and instead asked, “How did you find out about it, Manman?”"]},{"number":2743,"title":"Chapter 2743: Chapter 2695: A Mess","paragraphs":["No words could describe the intensity of Pei Mianman’s feelings. She'd just been giving it a try, but who could have expected Yun Jianyue to admit to it?","So I am a fool! Chuyan noticed it from so far away, yet I didn’t realize a thing at all despite being right by Ah Zu’s side!","To add insult to injury, Yun Jianyue is my older cousin! But I didn’t sense a thing at all!","That darned Ah Zu! He’s already with Yun Jianyue and Yan Xuehen, but he didn’t utter a word and let them fight it out!","You have successfully trolled Pei Mianman for +666... +666... +666...","She forced a smile and said, “Cousin, don’t underestimate a woman’s sixth sense.”","She was rational enough to not reveal that she'd heard it from Chuyan, or else the other party would surely blow up. She hesitantly continued, “Does Honglei already know about this?”","Yun Jianyue looked awkward for a brief moment before replying with a subtle “Mm.”","Pei Mianman was stunned yet again. A while later, she sighed and said, “The two of you must be close.” How can you not be close? You’re already close enough to share a man!","However, after having spent so much time with Qiu Honglei, she couldn’t say that she was surprised to hear that answer. She knew how much Yun Jianyue meant to Qiu Honglei.","But that only made her more stifled. So I’m the only one kept in the dark!","“Honglei is a good child. I've let her down.” Yun Jianyue sounded guilt-ridden.","Pei Mianman scoffed in her heart. And I’m your younger cousin, remember? You secretly hooked up with my man. Shouldn’t you feel guilty towards me too?","But it was already chaotic enough without her sticking her foot into it, so she decided to let the master and disciple sort it out by themselves.","Yun Jianyue nervously grabbed Pei Mianman’s hand and said, “Manman, who else knows about this? I don’t mind being embarrassed, but I can’t let Honglei be mocked alongside me.”","“Don’t worry, I’m the only one who knows.” Pei Mianman knew what she was worried about. “At this point, Sect Master Yan only suspects it. She isn’t certain about your relationship with Zu An.”","Yun Jianyue breathed a sigh of relief. As long as that ice sculpture doesn’t know. She quickly added, “Manman, you must know why I requested your help last time now. You have to help me, or else Honglei and I will be in trouble.”","Pei Mianman hesitated for a while but eventually decided against revealing Yan Xuehen’s relationship with Zu An. That would cause so much damage to Chu Chuyan and Yan Xuehen that she had to think things through first.","“Let me calm down first.” She waved her hand as she left the room in a daze.","Chuyan asked me to deal with Yun Jianyue, whereas Yun Jianyue asked me to deal with Yan Xuehen. Does no one remember Ah Zu is my man too?! What the hell is this?!","She headed straight to Zu An’s room. She was going to have a good talk with the culprit behind this huge mess.","“Manman, why were you so angry earlier?” Zu An stepped forward to embrace her, only for Pei Mianman to shove him aside and glare at him coldly.","Zu An was perplexed. “Did something happen?”","“You should know better than anyone else!” Pei Mianman glared at him with so much rage that it wouldn’t be surprising if she ripped off his flesh.","“So you know about it.” Zu An knew she had come from Yun Jianyue’s room, so it wasn’t hard for him to figure out what had happened.","Pei Mianman couldn’t take it anymore. “How could you get together with Sect Master Yun and Sect Master Yan? They're Honglei and Chuyan’s masters! What the hell are you thinking?!”","“The heart defies logic.” Zu An didn’t explain how they had ended up together.","Pei Mianman retorted, “...Big words, but you’re just a pervert, aren’t you?”","Zu An was silent.","Pei Mianman suddenly tensed up. “Hold on. You didn’t do anything with my master, did you?”","Zu An was dumbstruck.","His bewildered expression made Pei Mianman burst into laughter. I’m overthinking things. My master might have been a beauty in her younger years, but she’s no longer this fellow’s type anymore. She quietly asked her master for forgiveness in her mind.","She was feeling extremely conflicted now. On the one hand, she was glad she didn’t have to face the same dilemma that Chu Chuyan and Qiu Honglei had gone through. On the other hand, she was worried that if those two cooperated with their masters, she would be at a disadvantage.","She quickly shook those thoughts away from her mind and asked, “What do you intend to do now? How are you going to settle this?”","Zu An looked lost. “I've been conflicted about this too.”","“What’s there to be conflicted about? Call them together and thrash it out!” Pei Mianman harrumphed. “Can’t you see they're already pouncing on each other, all because of you? If you let things continue at this rate, there’ll be no way to resolve this.”","Zu An’s reluctant expression brought a frown to Pei Mianman’s face. She continued, “Do you enjoy seeing them compete over you so you can relish in the benefits? You bastard!”","Zu An angrily replied, “Do I look like that kind of person? I've considered that. It might be possible for Yun Jianyue—she’s from the Devil Sect and doesn’t conform to conventions, so the world won’t mock her for this—but what about Yan Xuehen? She would have to endure not just Yun Jianyue’s mockery, but the world’s scorn too.”","Pei Mianman was taken aback. She'd forgotten about that issue. So that’s what he’s worried about. I misunderstood him.","She thought hard but couldn’t think of a solution, and that vexed her. “Of all things, why did Yan Xuehen have to build up a pure, virtuous persona?” If you went with that persona, you should have never snatched my man!","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. “Manman, you don’t know how frustrated I was, being unable to find a person to confide in. It's wonderful to have you strategize for me.”","“Who’s strategizing for you? I’m only helping because Chuyan asked me to!” Pei Mianman blurted out in a fit of anger.","“Chuyan?”","Pei Mianman clasped her mouth, realizing she had accidentally given away crucial information. There was no point hiding it anymore, so she told him about Chu Chuyan’s request.","Zu An was moved. “Chuyan...”","“You should be glad to have a wife like her.” Pei Mianman harrumphed.","Zu An knew she was jealous, so he embraced her and said, “It’s my fortune to have your company.”","Pei Mianman wanted to maintain a cold expression, but Zu An was so skilled that she soon succumbed and started laughing. “Stop messing around. It’s itchy...”","They wrestled for a bit before resuming their discussion.","“Why don’t I talk to big sister Yun first? She’s a good person at heart. I don’t think she’ll corner Sect Master Yan,” Pei Mianman proposed.","“Are you certain she’ll spare Yan Xuehen?”","“...”","Pei Mianman thought about their long-time grudge. Yeah, it’s unlikely my cousin would hesitate to use this against Sect Master Yan. Even if my cousin held back, Sect Master Yan could feel insulted that she was ‘spared’ by her rival. Who knows what extreme things she could do?","This frustrated her a lot. She exclaimed, “You deal with your mess!”","She turned around and left. He’s the one reaping the benefits. Why should I clean up after him?"]},{"number":2744,"title":"Chapter 2744: Chapter 2696: The Corruption of the Fairy and the Demoness","paragraphs":["After the heat of her anger faded, Pei Mianman slowly calmed down. Chuyan entrusted this task to me. I don’t want to let her down. So, she began contemplating a plan in her room.","Unlike the others, her spectator viewpoint allowed her to see things from an unbiased perspective. It didn’t take her long to grasp the crux of the matter.","Qiu Honglei and Chu Chuyan have accepted their masters’ actions. Yun Jianyue might use this against Yan Xuehen, but that could still be kept under control. The real problem is how the world would react to this matter.","Yan Xuehen had always been a righteous figure. If this matter became public, she would be condemned, and given her personality, there was a good chance she would end her life to cleanse her shame.","Since that’s the case, we just have to control the story.","A thought popped into her mind. If Yan Xuehen would be condemned here, what if we just move elsewhere? Ah Zu can take them to the Fiend side, where the culture is more open. Yan Xuehen might be less reserved there.","Ah Zu hasn’t seen the little Fiend Empress, Yu Yanluo, and Xue’er for some time anyway...","That thought filled her heart with jealousy. It’s one thing for me to help other women court my man, but to have to push him into the arms of other women on top of that... Unlike Chuyan, I'm not into cuckolding.","She immediately dropped the idea. Since they have to remain here, I can only try the other plan...","A few days passed. Zu An was meditating in his room when an anxious Yan Xuehen suddenly knocked on his door. He was perplexed. It was rare to see such an expression on her. He asked, “What happened?”","Yan Xuehen quickly shut the door, took out a book, and passed it to him. “Take a look at this!”","Confused, Zu An took the book and saw it was one of the trendy novels sold on the streets.","Its title was ‘Fairy Plummets to the Secular World—The Regent Claims the White Jade Sect’s Master and Disciple’. Its cover depicted two cold ladies. They didn't look anything like Yan Xuehen and Chu Chuyan, but the similarity in their dispositions was uncanny. Anyone looking at the cover would immediately be reminded of Yan Xuehen and Chu Chuyan.","Zu An flipped open the novel, and it only further affirmed his guess. It showed how he'd first courted Chu Chuyan, and later, how he'd coincidentally gotten together with Yan Xuehen.","His eyebrows shot up. He had to concede that the author had done a good job of stoking the readers’ emotions. Its content was mostly guesses, but it was somewhat close to the truth. What a prodigy!","But seeing how agitated Yan Xuehen was, he consoled her. “Don’t worry, there are many such novels circulating in the market. There are also books about the empress and empress dowager too. No one will take them seriously.”","“It’s different!” Yan Xuehen’s face reddened. “There have been books about us in the past, but those were obviously fake. No one would take them seriously. But it’s different this time.”","She snatched the book over and flipped the pages. “This, this, and this... It’s exactly what happened to us!”","Zu An took the novel back and carefully scanned it with his divine sense. Only then did he realize that the novel was meticulously written to mix fact and fiction. Outsiders would think it was a mere story, but the involved parties knew better.","“Some of the guesses just happened to hit the mark. Most of the content is still gibberish,” Zu An continued.","“No, the author must be someone around us. Someone familiar with us.” Yan Xuehen clenched her jaws. “It could be that demoness...”","Before she could finish her sentence, the door was suddenly blasted open. Yun Jianyue marched into the room with a book in hand. “Ah Zu...”","She noticed Yan Xuehen and quickly swallowed her words. Instead, she asked, “Ice sculpture, what are you doing here?”","Yan Xuehen keenly noticed Yun Jianyue calling Zu An ‘Ah Zu’. They must be in an intimate relationship. She sneered, “Why can’t I be here? What are you doing here then?”","Yun Jianyue instinctively hid the book behind her. “Hmph! Why should I explain myself to you?”","Her action couldn’t escape her nemesis’ notice. Yan Xuehen exclaimed in shock, “Did you also...”","She belatedly realized how inappropriate her words were and bit her tongue.","Yun Jianyue also belatedly noticed the book in Zu An’s hands and exclaimed, “Someone wrote a story about you too?” She snatched the book from Zu An’s hand.","Yan Xuehen also snatched the book that Yun Jianyue was hiding. She was taken aback when she saw the book title: 'The Demoness’ Corruption—The Regent Conquers the Master and the Disciple at the Lake of Hatred.'","Yun Jianyue’s eyebrows also shot up when she saw the book title, but she was more curious about the book’s contents, so she quickly browsed through it. The same went for Yan Xuehen.","Soon, they had indescribable looks on their faces.","Yun Jianyue harrumphed. “You sneaky ice sculpture! I didn’t expect that beneath your pure and virtuous cover, you were so licentious!”","Yan Xuehen felt a mix of awkwardness and shame, but she didn’t let it show. “Hmph, this book about you goes even further. Is it all true?”","Yun Jianyue was rendered speechless. She couldn’t possibly admit to it before finding concrete evidence of Yan Xuehen’s relationship, so she argued back, “This book is elaborately described. I doubt such details could have come out of nowhere.”","Yan Xuehen obstinately held onto her point. “Are you really in that kind of relationship with him?”","Yun Jianyue was vexed. She wanted to admit it and then use it to mock Yan Xuehen. They might have done the same thing, but by virtue of their positions, Yan Xuehen would be more humiliated than her.","However, she gave up on that notion, fearing that Yan Xuehen would refuse to confess to it. That would put her in a bad position. So, she turned to Zu An and asked, “You tell us who’s in a relationship with whom!”","Yan Xuehen glared at Zu An, warning him not to spout nonsense.","Zu An was vexed. “Those money-minded merchants probably came up with this nonsense based on hearsay. Don’t take it to heart. I’ll investigate this matter and clear your names.”","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue exchanged looks. They felt a twinge of guilt. How can our names be cleared when these are all true? But neither one could lower her head in front of her nemesis.","Yan Xuehen scoffed, “Regent, I hope you can deal with this matter promptly to uphold the White Jade Sect’s honor.” She flung her sleeves and left.","Yan Xuehen’s reaction felt so cold and distant that it made Yun Jianyue doubt herself. Could my guess be off the mark?","That said, she couldn’t be outdone here. “Hmph, our sacred sect also has a reputation to uphold! If you can’t resolve this, I’ll have my men look into it and let the culprit have a taste of our sect’s methods!” With that, she also marched away in a huff.","Her practically tangible killing intent confused Yan Xuehen. Could there truly be nothing between them?","Regardless of how they viewed this matter, the novels had already spread throughout the capital. Everyone was talking about them."]},{"number":2745,"title":"Chapter 2745: Chapter 2697: The Source","paragraphs":["If this world had Google, the two novels would have been the most searched topics in recent days.","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue were among the strongest experts in the world. One was the top figure of the orthodox sects, whereas the other was the master of the Devil Sect. Furthermore, they were both incredible beauties who commanded great popularity. If Yu Yanluo was the dream lover of the secular world, the two of them were the dream lovers of the cultivation world.","Yun Jianyue had many fans. She was the number one goddess in the Devil Sect and the underground world. There were even some in the orthodox sects who had been charmed by her. It wasn't without reason that she was known for her seduction arts.","Countless people had had their hearts broken when she first made her debut as a cultivator. They had known she was a venomous rose, but she was so alluring that they couldn’t stop themselves from falling for her. Who knew how many people fantasized about her in the dead of night?","But it would be heresy for someone from an orthodox sect to fall in love with someone from the Devil Sect, let alone its master. Thus, no one dared to reveal their crush for Yun Jianyue in public, resulting in her appearing to be slightly less popular than Yan Xuehen.","Either one becoming taken would have been explosive news, but to think that they would both be taken at the same time... And to the same man, no less! What was even more shocking was that the man was their disciples’ man too! This was a massive scandal of unprecedented proportions!","Everyone in the capital was shocked beyond words. The first thing they asked each other upon meeting was, “Have you read it?”","In taverns, people argued with puffed cheeks.","“It must be fake! It has to be fake! How can a fairy like Sect Master Yan fall for a man?”","“She might be a fairy, but she’s still a woman. The regent is the greatest man in the world. It isn’t surprising for her to fall in love with him.”","“It’s one thing if it’s any other man, but the regent is her disciple’s husband! How can she steal her disciple’s man?”","“What’s so surprising about that? Take a look at the historical annals! It’s common and even praised for sisters to share a husband in imperial harems and noble clans. Why can’t a master and a disciple share a husband then?”","“Such a line of thought is depraved! You’re a scourge to society!”","“You’re being immature, clutching onto meaningless values. Do you think the guy is taking advantage of them? Across history, those who joined the imperial harem or married into a noble clan as sisters did so to tie down the man.”","“Given the regent’s unprecedented accomplishments and power, it isn’t a stretch to say that he's the most powerful man in history. He’s so famous as a philanderer that the White Jade Sect’s Holy Maiden can’t tie him down alone. That’s why Sect Master Yan had to join the fight to boost their chances at victory. You’re merely looking at the surface!”","“Sure, you’re the only one who gets it. Do you think Sect Master Yan is bothered by such secular things?”","Due to their differences in opinion, both sides quickly came to blows. Supporters of both sides stepped forward to help out, causing the tavern to devolve into chaos.","...","Such incidents were occurring throughout the capital and its surrounding provinces. The contents of the novels were being swiftly propagated all over the world.","In the Chu manor, Chu Youzhao angrily exclaimed, “To think I admired and respected Sect Master Yan so much! I didn’t think she would steal my big sister’s man while my big sister isn’t around!”","Chu Huanzhao shared the same thought. “Indeed! Our brother-in-law is just too outstanding. Those vixens have been finding ways to throw themselves at him.”","The thought of losing her brother-in-law to those women made her so angry that she flailed the Wailing Whip, causing the air to crack. Had she not known she wasn’t a match for them, she would have confronted Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue.","Murong Qinghe interjected, “Those are just rumors. They might not necessarily be true.”","“Which darned merchant came up with these novels? I’ll let them have a taste of my whip if I ever get my hands on them!” Chu Huanzhao flailed her whip around as she grumbled. “They wrote so much about my brother-in-law. Why aren’t they writing about my little aunt then?”","Chu Huanzhao blurted out, “Who says they aren’t? There are plenty of novels like...” She nearly ran back to her room to take out her prized collection.","Chu Huanzhao harrumphed. “Those are old books! There hasn’t been any decent work in the past two years. It's been all about other women.”","Murong Qinghe felt perplexed. She should have gotten angry listening to her ‘husband’ discussing this, but somehow, the thought of her brother-in-law made her blood rush. My brother-in-law is a great man. It’s not a surprise that so many women have fallen for him.","In the mountain behind the academy, a few teachers were gathered in a secret chamber to discuss something important.","Qi Yaoguang was awed. These seniors and juniors of mine usually have their hands full with their research. It’s no easy feat to gather them together, and there are usually latecomers. Yet everyone arrived on time today. They must be dying to gossip.","Seeing how her austere seniors were too awkward to kickstart the conversation, Qi Yaoguang decided to break the ice. “Do you think the rumors about the libationer and Sect Master Yan and Sect Master Yun are true?”","“It’s just nonsense made up by those booksellers for money,” Seventh Senior Wang Shuyang said with a dissatisfied look. He was an honest person, and Zu An’s pointers had helped him open new grounds in agriculture. That led him to think that Zu An was being maligned.","“That’s not necessarily the case.” Yin Shi stroked his beard. “The content is too vivid to be based on just sheer imagination. There are even details we didn’t know about, yet it makes perfect sense. Don’t you find that intriguing?”","“Hmph! What’s there to be intrigued about? It must be real! That little pervert...” Second Senior Ji Dengtu had to swallow his remaining words when he found himself glared at by the others. “It’s not as if you don’t know his personality. He wouldn’t give up on women as beautiful as Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue.”","Zu An had used a lot of his paper to produce top-quality erotica back then. To be honest, the current novels in the market were just repetitions of the works Zu An had produced back then. If you ask me, it might be possible that Zu An wrote those novels himself to let the news out.","I have to keep Xiaoxi away from him. Someone as innocent and pure as Xiaoxi can’t possibly beat a love veteran like him!","“But Sect Master Yan and Sect Master Yun aren’t just anyone, not to mention their disciples are in a relationship with the libationer. This is... unthinkable.” Fifth Senior Hei Baizi spun a go piece between his fingers, looking visibly shaken up.","The wheelchair-bound Fourth Senior Shen Xuzi suggested, “Why don’t we just ask him straight?”","The crowd rolled their eyes. Shen Xuzi has been spending too much time around puppets.","Qi Yaoguang turned to Yan Xiangu. “Big senior, why don’t we ask Daoyun?”","Xie Daoyun was in a relationship with Zu An, and they had been together for some years.","“I’m not sure if that’s a good idea...” Yan Xiangu said, but he still ignited a talisman paper to summon Xie Daoyun over.","The others laughed in their hearts. Who could have thought our austere big senior would be curious about this too?","Xie Daoyun soon arrived at the scene. Her face turned red when she heard their question, and she exclaimed, “I don’t know!”","...","In the imperial palace, Bi Linglong’s expression was colder than the night of the winter solstice. “Have you tracked down the source of those novels yet? Who is behind them?!”","“Yes, we have tracked down the source.” Zhang Zitong had the weirdest look on her face. “But they seem to be from the academy.”"]},{"number":2746,"title":"Chapter 2746: Chapter 2698: Can’t Miss the Opportunity to Mock","paragraphs":["Bi Linglong was speechless. She had thought of countless possibilities, such as a plot to besmirch Zu An by the imperial clan’s survivors, or the Shadow Group, or the Hub of Freedom, but it had never crossed her mind that the books would be from the academy.","The academy was Zu An’s territory! Everyone there respected him, and it was unthinkable for anyone there to pull this off.","“I thought I made a mistake too, but after capturing several booksellers, I was forced to conclude that the books are indeed coming from inside the academy. They each thought they were the exclusive publisher, so they worked overnight to release more goods in the market,” Zhang Zitong explained.","“Did you find out who in the academy is behind this?” Bi Linglong asked.","“That person is highly elusive. They concealed themselves, so none of the booksellers know their identity. It appears that they are a formidable cultivator,” Zhang Zitong reported with a frown. It looked as if she had a theory in mind, though.","Bi Linglong knew what Zhang Zitong was getting at. The academy was Zu An’s territory; no one would dare work against him there.","Is the culprit Ji Xiaoxi or Xie Daoyun... It can’t be Ji Xiaoxi. I've only met her a couple of times, but she doesn’t seem capable of this. Her father is capable of it, but I heard he’s a slave to his daughter. It’s unlikely he would do this.","That makes Xie Daoyun the more likely culprit... but why would she do this? She's already been together with Ah Zu since returning from the ancient era. Did she sense something between Ah Zu and Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue and lose her rationality?","That stoked Bi Linglong’s wariness. If she can deal with Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue today, who knows when she’ll go after me?","She gave the idea more thought and decided against it. Xie Daoyun was the Fiend races’ Saintess in the ancient era. She led the fiends in the fight against the monsters. Someone like that wouldn’t be so reckless.","But if it isn’t her, who could it be? Did Ah Zu spread the news himself?","Zhang Zitong probed, “Your Majesty, do you think the contents of the novels are true?”","Bi Linglong harrumphed. “Of course they're true.”","Zhang Zitong was perplexed. “But I can’t imagine Sect Master Yan and Sect Master Yun being in such a relationship with the regent. Their disciples...”","“That fellow is a walking incubus. Which woman in the world can resist him?” Bi Linglong said vexatiously. That fellow just keeps expanding his harem. How am I supposed to deal with this?","No woman in the world would want to share her lover with others.","Zhang Zitong’s face reddened as she felt a twinge of guilt. I have to admit that the regent is indeed dashing...","“That fellow is a master philanderer! How can Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue withstand his abilities?” The more Bi Linglong spoke, the more frustrated she felt.","Annoyance flickered through Zhang Zitong’s eyes. Why is the regent such a gentleman around me then? I've already hinted toward him many times! Though she would never dare say those words aloud to Bi Linglong.","Sensing Bi Linglong’s anger, Zhang Zitong tried to change the subject. “Should I continue investigating this matter?”","“Don’t bother. Why should we worry about him when he’s not even worried himself?” Bi Linglong turned around and returned to her room. She couldn’t tell if Zu An had intentionally released the news or not. It would be awkward if it turned out to be him.","She considered seeking verification from Zu An, but she was too angry to do so right now.","...","A new novel was released before daybreak. The plot was even more explosive this time, delving into Yan Xuehen’s motive for going after her disciple’s man.","She had fought against Yun Jianyue for a long time, with both sides refusing to admit defeat. However, her disciple was now in a bad condition and couldn’t be with the regent. This was a disaster, as her disciple’s relationship with the regent was bound to cool off at this rate. On top of that, she discovered that Yun Jianyue had gotten with the regent. That sparked her sense of danger. For her disciple’s happiness and her reluctance to concede her charm was beneath her rival’s, she began to seduce the regent.","Realization dawned upon the world. It had previously confused them why the highly respected Sect Master Yan would do something like that, but the explanation, as ridiculous as it was, sounded plausible.","No wonder Sect Master Yan and Sect Master Yun came to blows recently. It was over a man!","On Mount Yuquan, Yun Jianyue nearly blew up after reading the sequel. “Rubbish! She got together with Zu An before me! How could our rivalry be the motivation for their relationship?” She smashed the book into dust.","Qiu Honglei gulped before meekly whispering, “Master, you might have been ahead of her.”","“Impossible! The ice sculpture must have been with Zu An before me! The more I think about it, the more certain I am!” Yun Jianyue paced around the room angrily. “If I ever learn who’s behind these books, I’ll rip them apart!”","Pei Mianman cowered. She coughed lightly and excused herself.","“Help me check out the situation on the ice sculpture’s side.” Yun Jianyue was still relying on Pei Mianman for intelligence, thinking the latter was trustworthy since they shared blood ties.","Pei Mianman was on good terms with Yan Xuehen and Chu Chuyan, so it was easy for her to win their trust.","Pei Mianman’s expression crumbled as soon as she left the room. Ugh, it’s been so tough on me! Do you know how hard I have been working to clean up your mess? And now, I even have to fear for my life!","She shook those thoughts out of her head and went off to meet the next batch of booksellers.","Her series had sparked such widespread interest that demand for her books shot through the roof! It was to the extent that resellers were listing the books at astronomical prices! All the publishers in the capital and nearby provinces wanted a slice of the pie, so there was no lack of collaborators for Pei Mianman to choose from.","As such, the third book was released before the readers could even digest the contents of the first two books. It was even more erotic.","It detailed how Yan Xuehen had seduced the regent while her disciple wasn’t around. She'd approached the regent under the pretext of discussing her disciple’s affair, then moved on to consulting the regent about cultivation. Once they became close, she invited the regent to her room in the middle of the night to discuss secret manuals. The regent didn’t suspect her intentions and did his best to impart everything he knew to her.","But Yan Xuehen intentionally dressed scantily, sometimes appearing before the regent in her pajamas. She dropped hints at every turn of the corner. One night, she spiked the regent’s drink with aphrodisiac. The regent finally succumbed. Their discussions about secret manuals moved onto the bed, and it became a truly intimate sharing session.","The details were so explosive that blood would uncontrollably spurt from one’s nose. Needless to say, the novel caused a huge fuss. No one could have imagined the virtuous and pure Yan Xuehen to be so licentious.","On Mount Yuquan, Yun Jianyue clutched her belly and burst into laughter. “Hahaha, the publishers are doing a good job with the novels! I knew the ice sculpture has been faking it all these years. Someone is finally seeing her true face!”","Qiu Honglei scoffed in her heart. Just moments ago, you were berating the publishers for coming up with nonsense.","Yun Jianyue couldn’t hold back anymore. She grabbed the book and marched off to Yan Xuehen’s room. How can I miss such a good opportunity to mock her?","Yan Xuehen was reading the same book in her room. Like Yun Jianyue, she was concerned about the latest development and had bought the newest sequel right away. The content made her face turn red, and she trembled in anger.","Bam!","Someone kicked her door down. Yun Jianyue appeared by the doorway with an evil smile. “You’re much wilder than I thought, ice sculpture!”"]},{"number":2747,"title":"Chapter 2747: Chapter 2699: Evoking Revulsion","paragraphs":["Yan Xuehen slammed the table. “What nonsense are you spouting, demoness?!”","Yun Jianyue gestured to Yan Xuehen’s book with her chin. “You’re asking the obvious. Aren’t you reading it yourself?”","“This is utter nonsense! How can anyone believe it?!” Yan Xuehen’s face heated up as she hurriedly stowed away the book. She hadn’t expected the other party to catch her with it.","“Is it? I thought it was written quite well. It depicts you accurately,” Yun Jianyue said gleefully.","“Accurate, my ass...” Yan Xuehen was so angry that she uttered curses. She wondered how a human could achieve true indifference. Recent events had been challenging her tolerance.","But the years she'd spent cultivating weren’t in vain. It didn’t take her long to compose herself and retort, “Are you acknowledging the novels’ depiction of you too?”","Yun Jianyue’s smile froze. “Ridiculous! It should go without saying that the parts about me are all lies.”","“What double standards!” Yan Xuehen scoffed. She was feeling humiliated due to the novels, but seeing Yun Jianyue in the same plight comforted her.","“Hah! How much of those novels is about me? Compared to you, the stuff about me is a drop in the bucket?” Yun Jianyue had honed fast wits from years of rivalry with Yan Xuehen. “Besides, I'm the Devil Sect’s demoness. Shouldn’t it be normal even if I rear some male slaves? This is nothing for me!","“You, on the other hand, pretend to be some fairy untouched by secular desires, only to play such games behind everyone’s back. Don’t you feel ashamed calling your disciple’s lover into your room in the middle of the night?” Yun Jianyue clicked her tongue in disdain.","Yan Xuehen couldn’t take the insult. Her flying sword flew out of her sheath, and snow rained within the room. Countless ice shards shot toward Yun Jianyue at the speed of light.","Yun Jianyue was already prepared for this attack. She drew her crescent wheels, and the two of them came to blows.","Boom!","It didn’t take long for the residence to crumble under the shockwaves.","Many people from the academy rushed over to spectate the battle.","“Look, they are fighting again!”","“It must be over the libationer.”","“Shouldn’t the libationer deal with it?”","“How is he supposed to resolve this conflict? He can’t side with either of them. Speaking of which, have you read today’s novel?”","“I did. It’s so explosive! I didn’t expect them to be so wild...”","...","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue’s eyebrows twitched uncontrollably. Even though the crowd had suppressed their voices, their discussions couldn’t escape the pair's ears.","Killing intent flared from Yun Jianyue. Had it been anywhere else, she wouldn’t have hesitated to teach them the consequences of gossiping about the master of the Devil Sect. Even Yan Xuehen nearly went on a rampage.","They would only embarrass themselves if they continued fighting, so they tacitly stopped the fight and flew off, leaving the residence in a mess.","Not long later, a new novel surfaced.","This time, the protagonist was Yun Jianyue. It detailed her frustrations in being unable to surpass her long-time rival—her prestige and popularity even paled in comparison to Yan Xuehen’s—so she decided to go about it from another direction. Since both their disciples were the regent’s lovers, she thought she could at least defeat Yan Xuehen in the field of romance. So, she leveraged her strength as the only person in the history of the Devil Sect to have mastered seduction arts to seduce the regent, to give her disciple a helping hand.","But she had underestimated the strongest person in the world. Not only did her seduction arts fail, but she even suffered a backlash and uncontrollably fell in love with the regent. Due to the special nature of her seduction arts and the regent’s charm, she became his plaything.","She was the Devil Sect’s most outstanding demoness. Her looks, figure, and skills were impeccable. Even the regent was infatuated with her. The book elaborated about how Yun Jianyue used the techniques passed down through generations of the Devil Sect’s Holy Maidens to please the regent. It also depicted the regent’s immense strength and how he made her submit.","Yan Xuehen, who had still been brooding over the last book not long ago, was overjoyed. She happily took the book to Yun Jianyue’s room. Meanwhile, Yun Jianyue was throwing a tantrum after reading the book’s contents.","This culminated in yet another huge fight. They learned their lesson and fought in the suburbs. There were fewer spectators this time, but their clashes caused such a huge commotion that it inevitably drew experts over.","Even Zu An rushed over to check on them, fearing they would kill each other.","When they saw Zu An, the two ladies felt conscience-stricken. They felt as if the crowd was looking at them and Zu An with gossipy eyes, which prompted them to escape despite Zu An calling them to stop. They were worried the crowd would assume the rumors were true if they exchanged even a single word with Zu An here.","Zu An shook his head bitterly. The crowd looked at him with eyes of awe, admiration, disdain, and so on.","Zu An returned to Mount Yuquan’s residence and called Pei Mianman over. “You're behind the commotion, right?”","Pei Mianman stuck out her tongue. “Look how hard I have to work to clean up your lousy mess!”","“What are you thinking? How can you make those things public?” Zu An was frustrated. The capital and the academy were in an uproar. Many people had secretly approached him to verify if the rumors were true. Just dealing with those people was troublesome enough.","“Do you intend to hide it forever?” Pei Mianman asked. “It’s only a matter of time before everyone finds out, so we might as well take the initiative to reveal it. At least we’ll have some control over the situation this way.”","“Control?” Zu An was starting to get an idea of what was going on.","Pei Mianman nodded. “That’s right. Haven’t you noticed how, despite the huge commotion this scandal has caused, there aren’t many people criticizing Yan Xuehen or Yun Jianyue?”","“No criticisms? There are plenty of people saying they're shameless!” Zu An had been paying close attention to the crowd’s responses.","“I was the one who spread those criticisms,” Pei Mianman calmly replied.","Zu An was speechless.","“Someone else would have said those words either way. I’d rather take control of the narrative and make the criticisms even uglier. That would evoke the crowd’s revulsion and encourage them to speak up for the two,” Pei Mianman replied.","“The 50-cent army!” Zu An was shocked. He hadn’t expected Pei Mianman to learn these tricks by herself. She would have been a marketing genius in the modern era!","Pei Mianman had no idea what the ‘50-cent army’ referred to, but she continued her explanation. “I intentionally exaggerated the contents of the novels. The first two books are 30% true, but the subsequent ones are less than 10% true. Some people are even questioning the credibility of the novels now.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. All the talk about Yan Xuehen dressing scantily and drugging him just sounded too far-fetched. The recent book about Yun Jianyue was highly exaggerated too. Its content was explosive enough to draw eyeballs, but the smarter ones had already calmed down and shrugged off the books as the publishers’ money-making scheme.","Pei Mianman continued, “Under such a setting, the extreme rhetoric I sowed on the streets would evoke the masses’ revulsion. Even those who truly intend to besmirch Sect Master Yun and Sect Master Yan will be ignored. The masses are beginning to understand and even side with them. When the time is ripe, I’ll give it one last push so that the masses will come to terms with this matter.”","Zu An was awed. “Manman, you’re a genius!”","Pei Mianman dodged his embrace and harrumphed. “With your wits, you should have thought about that too; it’s just that you didn’t dare to take the gamble.”","Zu An fell silent. He had indeed been worried about the situation going out of control.","“It’s too early to celebrate. I've dealt with the public opinion for you, but you’ll still have to find a way to make them come to terms with this matter,” Pei Mianman coldly pointed out."]},{"number":2748,"title":"Chapter 2748: Chapter 2700: Choose One","paragraphs":["In the coming days, the discussion about the novels only intensified, and it spread like wildfire across the world. All manner of talk and rumors surfaced. Some said Yan Xuehen was shameless. Some remarked that Yun Jianyue was a demoness and the root behind this mess. Quite a few people questioned the novels’ veracity, pointing out they were riddled with flaws and claiming that they were written just to draw attention. But others thought the novels were true.","A few nosy people wanted to investigate the truth, but none dared to confront Yun Jianyue and Yan Xuehen for it. The former was notorious; only those with a death wish would dare ask her such a question. The latter had a reputation to uphold, so people couldn’t bear to ask her. Of course, some didn't care about her reputation, but they couldn’t find her.","So, people sought verification from Zu An instead.","Annoyed by the questions, Zu An escaped the mess under the pretext of paying a visit to the Fiend races. Neither confessing nor denying the matter would be right at this juncture anyway.","But that only made the crowd speculate more. Those who believed the novels to be fake were baffled that no one had stepped forward to suppress the rumors, be it the people in question, the imperial palace, or the academy.","The smarter ones slowly realized the truth. Could there be something among the three of them?","The bulk of the populace, however, didn’t have access to as much information, and most people would only believe such a matter to be true if they saw it with their own eyes.","Under Pei Mianman’s media manipulation, most people still believed the novels to be fake. Furthermore, there were so many discussions and conspiracies surrounding the trio that if the truth ever came to light, they would likely just shrug it off as another attempt to draw attention. Even if the truth eventually came to light, this three-sided relationship would be so over-discussed that there wouldn’t be any overly extreme criticisms directed at Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue anymore.","Zu An was awed. Manman is truly a prodigy. She found a solution to a problem that has confounded me for so long. All that’s left is to untangle the knots in Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue’s hearts.","But this won’t be easy either...","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue were extremely smart individuals. After the initial shock, humiliation, anger, fear, and all sorts of emotions, they slowly regained themselves and noticed something amiss.","Outsiders wouldn't know whether the novels’ content was real or not, but the two of them knew better. The initial books were 30% truth mixed with 70% falsehood, but the sequels became 10% truth and 90% falsehoods.","It must be an inside job—outsiders wouldn’t have known such details about us. Clearly, someone is plotting something. But who could be behind this?","Naturally, the first person who came to mind was Zu An. He was the most likely mastermind behind this mess! His motive was also clear. It was to first deliver a strong shock to numb the crowd, so they could stand together under broad daylight one day.","If the details about me are real, the details about the demoness (ice sculpture) must be real too, right?","They didn’t seek Zu An for confirmation as they were still reeling from embarrassment. Besides, they figured that Zu An would feign ignorance and not betray them to the other party, and vice-versa.","Since that was the case, it would be easier to just ask each other. So, they each headed out to confront each other, only to bump into the other midway. They were initially taken aback, but they quickly realized what was going on.","“Things have already gotten to this point, so I’ll get to the point. Are the details surrounding Zu An and you true?” Yan Xuehen asked directly.","Yun Jianyue hesitated. She normally wouldn’t have admitted to it, but it couldn’t be more obvious that Yan Xuehen was in the same plight as her—they were both just short of the final confirmation. There wasn't much point in denying it anymore. She had thought she could mock Yan Xuehen over this matter, but the world had already rained all kinds of criticisms on them. To make things worse, most people favored Yan Xuehen. There was no point in further mocking Yan Xuehen when both of them had heard it all.","So, she frankly admitted to it and said, “That’s right. What about you?”","There was a moment of silence before Yan Xuehen replied with a subtle “Mm”.","I knew it! Ah Zu has been with her for some time now, but he kept it from me! I must have looked like a fool in his eyes! Yun Jianyue narrowed her eyes.","Yan Xuehen sighed. “Demoness, we've been so busy fighting between us that we didn’t know someone else was watching us make a fool out of ourselves from the shadows.”","Yun Jianyue felt vexed too. “Was he behind the novels too?”","“Most likely so.” Yan Xuehen’s eyes turned cold.","The two women each felt anger surging in their chest. No wonder he escaped to the Fiend races' side! He’s avoiding us!","“What do you intend to do?” Yun Jianyue asked.","“I’ll be making a trip to the Fiend races to demand an explanation,” Yan Xuehen replied coldly.","“Yes, he owes us an explanation!” Yun Jianyue clenched her teeth. “Shall we head off now?”","Yan Xuehen nodded. She flashed into the sky and rushed to the northern Fiend races. Yun Jianyue kicked off the ground and flew alongside Yan Xuehen, not lagging behind in the slightest.","Both of them kept opening and closing their mouths hesitantly along the way. They had never felt so awkward before. After fighting for their entire lives, they would never have thought that they would end up with the same man!","Yun Jianyue was the one who broke the silence in the end. “When did you get with him?”","Yan Xuehen’s face reddened. She wasn’t fond of sharing such private details. “You ask him.”","Yun Jianyue’s eyebrows shot up. This woman is as hateful as ever.","“Fine. I’ll ask him in person. Let’s see who he chooses. This should draw the curtains on our many years of enmity,” Yun Jianyue sneered. You want me to share a husband and become sisters with this ice sculpture? Dream on!","She knew that men preferred Yan Xuehen’s type, so it was more likely for Zu An to choose Yan Xuehen over her. But so what? Even if I lose, I shall lose with my head held high.","Yan Xuehen was taken aback. She hadn't thought Yun Jianyue would go this far. Is she that confident that Zu An would choose her? After a brief silence, she said, “Don’t bother, I’ll back out. Things have never been possible between him and me.”","She didn’t want to just be a choice for someone, and she had never planned to openly be with Zu An either. Thus, she figured it would be best for her to quietly back out.","Yun Jianyue was infuriated. “What do you mean by this, ice sculpture? A win is a win; a loss is a loss. I don’t need your charity!”","Yan Xuehen calmly replied, “I don’t want to compete with you in this.”","Yun Jianyue suddenly fell silent. She felt the same way too. That bastard is at fault! “Aren’t you just afraid of losing to me?”","“I’m afraid of losing to you? What a joke.” Yan Xuehen could never remain calm when it came to her rivalry with Yun Jianyue. “You’re a proud person. Are you truly willing to become a choice for him?”","“That’s simple. We’ll let him determine the victor between us first before dumping him,” Yun Jianyue coldly replied.","Yan Xuehen was taken aback. As expected of the master of the Devil Sect! She considered it for a while before nodding. “Alright.”","The two women angrily flew toward the Fiend races’ imperial court to look for Zu An. Their hearts were heavier than ever.","Zu An was busy catching up with the little Fiend Empress when he sensed something and mentally prepared himself for what was about to come. Shortly after, two beautiful women appeared before him.","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue glanced at the little Fiend Empress. Their complexions alleviated a little when they saw she was properly dressed. They turned to Zu An and got to the point.","“Choose one.”"]},{"number":2749,"title":"Chapter 2749: Chapter 2701: Heart Turning Cold","paragraphs":["The little Fiend Empress was startled. The gossip had already spread to the Fiend races. She had intended to ask Zu An about this matter when the other two stars came knocking. There’s no need to ask anymore. This matter must be real.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Before he could say a word, another chirpy voice echoed from outside.","“Ah Zu, please tell me that the rumors about you, Sect Master Yan, and Sect Master Yun aren’t real...” A woman rushed into the room, only for her voice to abruptly stop when she saw the two women in the room. She froze up out of awkwardness.","Yan Xuehen recognized the woman. The latter had been Chu Chuyan’s personal maid, as well as a spy from the Shi clan—the elven princess Snow. Her appearance made the situation even more awkward.","Trailing behind Snow was a woman who was so beautiful that she mesmerized even Yun Jianyue and Yan Xuehen—the Medusa Queen, the woman who had once been the capital’s number one beauty, Yu Yanluo.","The two women hadn’t expected so many spectators for their confrontation with Zu An. They felt startled and incredibly awkward.","“Ah Zu~” Yu Yanluo’s beautiful face lit up in delight when she saw Zu An, but she quickly realized there were others in the room too. She bowed to the two women and said, “Paying respects to Sect Master Yan and Sect Master Yun.”","Her etiquette was so on point that it could have been a textbook example. No wonder the capital’s men were so enchanted by her back then.","“Madam Yu!” the two women returned the greeting.","The atmosphere became peculiar. They'd come to settle things with Zu An, only to be surrounded by his lovers. Yan Xuehen glared at Yun Jianyue, urging her to move things along.","Yun Jianyue felt vexed. Why do I have to do the talking? Don’t you have a mouth?","That said, she knew the reticent Yan Xuehen wouldn’t even be able to squeeze out a fart in such a setting, and the awkwardness would suffocate them to death before they got anything done. So, she turned around and walked out.","Yan Xuehen followed suit. This is the first time Yun Jianyue hasn’t looked so annoying to me.","Zu An was speechless as the other ladies looked at him with gossipy eyes.","He coughed lightly. “Give me a moment. I’ll be right back.”","After he left, the little Fiend Empress, Snow, and Yu Yanluo gathered to gossip. Despite their different personalities, it was human nature to gossip.","“I didn’t think the rumors were true.”","“I knew it. How could Ah Zu overlook those two gorgeous women around him?”","“But they are Chuyan’s and Honglei’s masters. Isn’t that weird?”","“I remember the two of them are mortal enemies. Ah Zu has quite the problem to settle here.”","The little Fiend Empress animatedly added, “Before you arrived, those two demanded for Ah Zu to choose between them!”","The eyes of the other two women lit up. “Woah! Things are getting heated up!”","Unable to withhold their curiosity, they quietly snuck to the doorway and pricked up their ears.","...","On the other side, Yun Jianyue dismissed the guards outside before taking in a deep breath. “Make your choice.”","Her voice was quivering. As the Devil Sect’s master, she had weathered countless storms, but she had never felt so nervous before. She already had an inkling that Zu An would choose the ice sculpture over her, and that thought pricked her heart.","I've fought with the ice sculpture my entire life. Who could have thought I’d lose to her on this?","She realized that Zu An not choosing her would hurt her far more than losing to the ice sculpture. She fully understood the risks of forcing Zu An with an ultimatum, but her pride wouldn’t allow her to be a coward and continue dragging things out.","Yan Xuehen felt nervous too. She was aware that her cold nature pushed others away from her, and that she was nowhere as passionate as the demoness.","He might be displeased with me for continuously pushing him away... but this works too. This relationship should never have come to be. I’ll find a quiet mountain valley and devote the rest of my life to my cultivation.","That was what she told herself, but there was an inexplicable pain in her heart that made her anxious. The fact that she felt such intense emotions despite having cultivated the Unshakable Daoist Manual spoke volumes.","As they awaited his answer, the two women looked at Zu An nervously.","Zu An felt his throat turning dry, but he answered, “You should also know that I don’t like to choose. If I have to, I’ll choose to take it all.”","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue were speechless.","You have successfully trolled Yan Xuehen for +666... +666... +666...","You have successfully trolled Yun Jianyue for +666... +666... +666...","This fellow is ridiculous!","Yan Xuehen coldly spat, “Impossible!”","Yun Jianyue scoffed out of sheer anger, “Dream on!”","How can I share a husband with that ice sculpture? And clearly, she feels the same way, too.","The spying crowd inside the main hall also spat in disdain.","“Ah Zu is shameless.”","“That ruffian-like personality is exactly like him.”","...","Zu An sighed. “We don’t have to make things so tense.”","“You knew how things are between us, but you still chose to withhold the truth and play us like fools.” Anger seethed in Yan Xuehen’s eyes.","“I was afraid of hurting you. You're Chuyan’s and Honglei’s masters. Unless the two of you allowed it, I couldn’t reveal our relationship to others.”","“Is it? How do you intend to explain the novels? Are you forcing us to accept this situation?”","“I wasn't the one behind those novels. It was Manman.”","The women in the main hall exchanged looks as if they had just learned something unbelievable. None of them could have guessed that Pei Mianman would be behind those novels!","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue were shocked too. They hadn't thought it would be her.","“She wouldn’t do something like that without your permission.”","“Actually, she received a request from Chuyan. On top of that, considering her ties with big sister Yun and Honglei, she also wanted to resolve your reservations.”","Yun Jianyue fell into deep thought. Manman was indeed her blood-related cousin, and she was on close terms with Yan Xuehen’s disciple as well. She did have the motive to pull off something like that.","Yan Xuehen was astounded. “It was Chuyan’s request? Why would she... make such a request...” Her voice quivered as she spoke.","Zu An sighed. “You remember the Great Snowy Mountain’s Snow Lady, right? That was Chuyan after being sent through spacetime. She recalled everything afterward...”","Yan Xuehen’s face paled after hearing his explanation. “Chuyan, I have wronged you...”","She turned around and left, not wanting to stay here any longer.","Zu An was startled. He quickly reached out to grab her.","Yun Jianyue’s face crumbled. She understood that Zu An had made his decision, and her heart felt chilled. She turned around and flew off in the opposite direction."]},{"number":2750,"title":"Chapter 2750: Chapter 2702: Confession","paragraphs":["But shortly after Yun Jianyue flew off, her surroundings suddenly retreated in the opposite direction. Before she knew it, she had returned to her original position. It went without saying that Zu An had dragged her back.","Yun Jianyue was speechless. Well, this is awkward.","She glanced at the ice sculpture, followed by the pairs of eyes hiding behind the door, and anger suddenly surged within her. “Bastard Zu, don’t think you can humiliate me like that just because you’re stronger than me!”","She raised her hand to end her own life.","Zu An hadn’t expected her to react so explosively. Horrified, he flashed to her side and grabbed her hand. “That’s not what I mean, but we should at least properly talk things out before you leave.”","“Didn’t you already choose the ice sculpture? I have no reason to remain here.” Yun Jianyue’s heart quivered as she spoke. Tears would have streamed down her face if not for her pride.","“That wasn't picking between you two.” Zu An was also at a loss. How was he supposed to know that consoling one side would only hurt the other side?","Yan Xuehen’s heart shook. She wasn't so dense as to think that Zu An was choosing her by grabbing her hand, but hearing him speak it aloud still hurt her.","The three women in the main hall were thoroughly immersed in the drama.","Snow uttered jealously, “He’s holding Sect Master Yan in one hand while embracing Sect Master Yun with the other. I reckon Ah Zu is the only one capable of that in the entire world.”","The little Fiend Empress snorted, “It doesn’t look like he’s going to get his way this time. Who knows? He might even lose the two of them for good!”","“Surely not?” Snow remarked. “Who do you think Ah Zu will choose?”","Even the usually quiet Yu Yanluo couldn’t resist the urge to speculate, “It could be Sect Master Yan. Her transcendent aura poses a fatal allure to men.”","“My bet is on Sect Master Yun. Not only is she the valiant master of the Devil Sect, but she’s also passionate beyond measure. No man can resist the immense satisfaction of conquering a woman like her.” The little Fiend Empress was more fond of Yun Jianyue, who walked the same path as her.","Snow frowned. “I don’t think Ah Zu is capable of choosing one at the other’s expense.”","...","“Then what’s your answer?” Neither Yan Xuehen nor Yun Jianyue wanted this ambiguous relationship to drag on. They wanted a conclusion and to settle things once and for all.","Zu An was frustrated. He'd been so focused on resolving the problem of public opinion that he'd neglected their own will. He'd thought that he could slowly coax them one by one, but little had he expected the two of them to confront him at once, and three more women were watching the drama on top of that. There was no way to resolve this privately.","Yan Xuehen sighed. “Since you’re incapable of making a decision, let's just end this. We should never have been together in the first place.”","Yun Jianyue shared the same thought. She also found it shameful to snatch her disciple’s man. Perhaps this was a good opportunity to take a step back and just remain friends.","Zu An was about to speak when he sensed something and looked at the sky.","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue initially thought he was trying to change the subject, but they quickly sensed something and looked up as well. They could sense a ship coming from outer space.","Zu An reached into his robe to retrieve Dreamland’s invitation letter. It was emitting a faint glow—a sign that it had been activated.","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue knew about Dreamland and were taken aback. Could that be...","A man who was dressed in a way reminiscent of a dignified Victorian butler appeared not too far away from Zu An. He was momentarily mesmerized by the two women beside Zu An, but shame soon flickered through his eyes. He bowed to Zu An and said, “Pardon my breach of etiquette, esteemed guest. Your female companions are so beautiful that I lost myself for a moment despite my strict training.”","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue’s faces heated up. It felt good to be complimented. They wanted to clarify that they weren’t Zu An’s companions, but they didn’t want to embarrass him in front of an outsider. In the end, they chose to hold their silence.","“You are?” Zu An asked despite having guessed the answer.","“I am Employee Number 9527 from the Universal Conglomerate. We have received a request from Dreamland to fetch invited guests, and I am responsible for fetching you.” The butler-like employee glanced at Zu An’s invitation letter with a smile.","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue’s hearts quivered. They hadn’t expected their day of separation to come so quickly. They were no longer in a mood to compete with each other.","The three women in the main hall also lost interest in the drama and ran out. “Ah Zu!”","They looked worried.","Yun Jianyue asked, “Can he bring others with him?”","Yan Xuehen’s eyes lit up too. She was worried about letting Zu An go alone.","Employee 9527 shook his head. “I’m sorry, but Dreamland strictly permits entry only to invitation holders.”","All the women looked disappointed.","Zu An asked, “Can you give me some time? There are some matters I still have to attend to.”","Employee 9527 looked troubled. “I’m afraid I can’t do that. I wouldn’t have minded waiting days or even half a month for you, but there are other esteemed guests onboard too.”","Zu An nodded. There are other guests onboard? This works too, since I can gather information about the myriad worlds from them. I’m practically venturing into the unknown now. “It won’t take that long. Just two hours or so.”","“That should be fine. I’ll inform the other esteemed guests. Please activate the invitation letter once you’re ready.” Employee 9527 bowed before disappearing into thin air.","“Ah Zu...” Snow couldn’t conceal her worry. She hugged Zu An tightly, fearing that he would disappear forever if she let go.","Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue were left in an awkward position. They released Zu An’s hands, thinking that it was inappropriate for the four of them to be hugging together.","“Don’t worry, this is a fortuitous encounter too. I’ll be careful.” Zu An gently patted Snow’s shoulder. He also felt reluctant to part ways with her.","“I’d rather you be safe here thanrisk your life outside,” Snow said with a hoarse voice.","Yu Yanluo and the little Fiend Empress nodded as well, agreeing with Snow’s words.","Zu An sighed. “We can’t hole ourselves up like ostriches. It’ll be too late for regrets if greater danger strikes in the future and we’re incapable of protecting ourselves. Besides, there are still people here who need saving. I might find solutions at Dreamland.”","Be it Mi Li’s body, Chu Chuyan, the Goddess of Wu Mountain, or Chang’e, there were too many things he needed to do.","The others knew he was determined to make the trip, so they didn’t try to further dissuade him. Instead, they reluctantly bade him farewell.","Zu An made his way up to Yun Jianyue and Yan Xuehen. Despite their imminent separation, he still didn’t know what to say.","Yan Xuehen quietly spoke up. “Now that we’re about to part ways, none of those things are important anymore...”","She was no longer in the mood to force him to choose between them. There were many words at the tip of her tongue, but she didn’t know how to voice them.","Yun Jianyue suddenly spoke up. “You little brat! Take care of yourself. If you return safely...”","She briefly paused here as she squirmed awkwardly, though her gaze remained firmly on Zu An. “As long as you return safely, I’ll even accept sharing a husband with this ice sculpture.”"]},{"number":2751,"title":"Chapter 2751: Chapter 2703: Raising Flags Everywhere","paragraphs":["Shock rippled through the crowd. No one had expected the domineering Devil Sect’s master to be willing to share a husband, but on second thought, this was to be expected. All of the women gathered here were extraordinary in their ways, but they'd still fallen for Zu An anyway.","But we didn’t expect her to be able to put down her enmity with Yan Xuehen for him. She must have truly fallen in love with Ah Zu. She must be trying to motivate him so he’ll grit his teeth and get through any danger he faces in Dreamland.","The ball had been thrown into Yan Xuehen’s court. All the gazes on her made her nervous. In truth, she didn’t think her concerns mattered now that Zu An’s safety was at stake. She might have said something similar to Yun Jianyue in the heat of the moment if they were alone, but how could she do so in front of so many people?","Amid her hesitation, her face turned pale. It suddenly occurred to her that she had lost.","The demoness has the guts to confess to Ah Zu in public, yet I’m unable to do the same. Everyone will think that my feelings for Ah Zu are less than hers. Even if Ah Zu understands my quandary, he might still feel uncomfortable about it.","Yan Xuehen felt bitter regret, but her pride wouldn’t allow her to change her tune. As a result, she just stood completely still on the spot. She felt so awkward that her fingernails were digging into her palm.","Zu An smiled. He grabbed both Yun Jianyue and Yan Xuehen’s hands and said, “Big sister Yun has said such words, and big sister Yan has implicitly acknowledged it. Looks like it’s a blessing in disguise for me.”","Yan Xuehen felt warmth in her heart. Ah Zu is as caring as ever. He resolved my regret and awkwardness with such ease. Now that I think about it, he was also involved in Manman’s actions. He's put a lot of thought into resolving my reservations.","Having thought things through, she didn’t shake off his hand. The warmth transmitted through his palm made her nervous heart slowly calm down.","Yun Jianyue eyed their hands in astonishment. Having been enemies for so many years, she could see through Yan Xuehen’s inner turmoil. I thought ice sculpture would shake off his hand. Tsk, I've already won here, but Ah Zu is taking such good care of her.","That made her heart boil with anger.","You have successfully trolled Yun Jianyue for +110... +110... +110...","“Hmph, we’ll talk about this when you return.”","The little Fiend Empress and the others secretly chuckled. Well well, you can’t expect maintaining a harem to be easy, right? Did I accept him too easily back then? I should have put him through a bit more, considering his philandering ways!","Having finally calmed down, Yan Xuehen worriedly said, “There’s no saying what you might face at Dreamland. You should bring some defensive artifacts with you.”","She regretted being so caught up in this matter that she'd forgotten to forge defensive artifacts for him. So, she took off her Flying Snow Sword and handed it over. “Ah Zu, your Blue Luan Sword Formation becomes stronger with more weapons. This Flying Snow Sword is a treasure passed down through the generations in our White Jade Sect. It should be of some help to you.”","The other women were shocked. The Flying Snow Sword had been with Yan Xuehen since she first entered the world of cultivation, yet she was giving it to a man now? Who was the one who said she practiced the Unshakable Daoist Manual?!","Yun Jianyue smiled. “I can’t be stingier than the ice sculpture. My Crescent Moon Blade won’t be of much use to you, so you can have my Empress Lantern instead. It can temporarily imprison an enemy.”","Seeing the other women reaching for their most prized treasures as well, Zu An hurriedly stopped them. “I appreciate your sentiments, but I've made ample preparations. I’ll feel more at ease if you keep these treasures with you.”","“But...”","Yan Xuehen wanted to argue, but Zu An interjected, “You've been gazed upon by a universal deity. There’s no saying when you might encounter danger. Your fighting prowess will be greatly reduced without your weapons, and that’ll only make me worry about your safety.”","Hearing those words, the others didn’t insist on it. “You must take care of yourself!”","All the women had countless words to say to him, but they were too embarrassed to speak up in front of everyone else.","Zu An smiled, and their surroundings suddenly changed. All the women realized that they were alone with their lover; they couldn’t see anyone else.","Snow’s heart thumped wildly. Did Ah Zu choose to bid me farewell first? Moved, she leaped into his arms, only to fall right through.","Zu An explained, “I'm currently in soul form. This way, I can bid all of you farewell at once.”","Snow pouted. I thought I was the special one. But with their separation imminent, she didn’t want to squander the precious time they had left on jealousy, so she spilled her heart out to him.","The same thing was happening in every corner in the world. All of Zu An’s lovers saw him, and their eyes reddened in sorrow. The more sentimental ones couldn’t stop their tears from flowing. Zu An could only console them over and over again.","Pei Mianman’s eyes were reddened too. “You don’t have a conscience! I've been working myself to the bone to settle those two women for you, but you’re dumping me now that the problem is almost resolved.”","“I didn’t expect Dreamland’s courier to arrive right now either,\" Zu An said.","Zu An was planning to update her about Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue, but Pei Mianman interjected, “I don’t want to spend the precious time we have left talking about other women.”","Zu An’s heart melted. He held her with his soul, and the two of them soaked in each other’s warmth.","In the imperial palace, Bi Linglong was worried. “Ah Zu, I’m worried that I can’t hold the fort when you’re gone. I won’t be able to face you if I lose your empire.”","Zu An smiled. “This is your empire, not mine. You've been doing a good job as the empress.”","“No, this empire belongs to you. I'm merely taking care of it on your behalf.” Bi Linglong regretted not having his child. If something happens to him... Touch wood! What am I thinking? Ah Zu will surmount all dangers!","In the Ocean races’ dragon palace, Shang Liuyu and Shang Hongyu gathered around Zu An. “We could have fought alongside you if we were stronger.”","“You shouldn’t rush your cultivation. With your talent and fortuitous encounters, I believe it shouldn’t take long before you make a breakthrough.” Zu An knew about their past lives and understood that they were destined for greatness.","Beneath the Bridge of Helplessness, Zu An said with a worried expression, “Chuyan, you're the one I worry about the most. There’ll be no one to talk to you once I leave.”","Only he had the power to bring others into this land of the dead. Once he was gone, Yan Xuehen, Pei Mianman, and the others wouldn’t be able to visit Chu Chuyan anymore.","A tear trickled down Chu Chuyan’s cheeks. Her eyes brimmed with concern and worry. “That’s why you have to return safely, or else I’ll be alone for a thousand years. I don’t know if I’ll have the courage to last that long without you.”","Zu An felt a sharp pain in his chest. His eyes hardened in determination. “Chuyan, I’ll be back. Wait for me!”"]},{"number":2752,"title":"Chapter 2752: Chapter 2704: Inauspicious Omen","paragraphs":["As a transmigrator who had watched plenty of movies in his previous life, Zu An was familiar with movie tropes. If a character took out a photograph and said that they had loved ones waiting for them at home, that they would return home to get married after this last operation, they were pretty much doomed to die later in the show. Those were all death flags.","Zu An thought about his earlier farewells with the ladies and shook his head with a bitter smile. It’s like I’m doing a speedrun for collecting death flags.","But now that he was going on a long journey, that was the least of his concerns at the moment.","He had also sent a sliver of his soul to gather the academy’s teachers to leave some final instructions. He entrusted the leadership of the academy to Yan Xiangu. The latter was the old libationer’s first disciple, and had the greatest strength and the highest prestige, so no one objected to the appointment.","The teachers gave their cherished treasures to Zu An for his self-protection. Even Ji Dengtu, who often scoffed at him, took out a bottle of pills and said, “Brat, these are pills that Xiaoxi and I came up with recently. They work much better than the other pills we've made. I didn’t want to give them to you, but Xiaoxi insisted on it. Now that I’ve done so, you better not die outside and waste my pills.”","Zu An knew Ji Dengtu had a sharp tongue but a soft heart. The latter was clearly worried about him but refused to admit it. Thus, he replied, “Don’t worry, I can’t bear to leave Xiaoxi behind. I’ll come back to look for her.”","Ji Dengtu was so angry that he threw a tantrum. It was almost as if he could already see his beloved daughter being taken away by Zu An.","You have successfully trolled Ji Dengtu for +119... +119... +119...","Amid the uproar, Qi Yaoguang said, “Libationer, I’d like to have a private word with you.”","The others were astounded. Has our little junior sister fallen in love with the libationer? Even Yan Xuehen and Yun Jianyue have fallen for him, so I guess it’s not that surprising for our junior sister to harbor feelings for him too.","Thus, they excused themselves with a smile to give them some privacy.","Ji Dengtu’s anger flared. Is this brat a walking aphrodisiac? Even our little junior sister has fallen for his tricks! This won’t do. I must knock some sense into Xiaoxi so she doesn’t get duped by this philanderer!","You have successfully trolled Ji Dengtu for +444... +444... +444...","Only Zu An sensed something was amiss. “Yaoguang, you seem a little frail.”","“I knew I couldn’t hide it from you.” Qi Yaoguang coughed. She gave up on her disguise, and her face immediately turned ghastly pale. “Don’t worry, libationer. I merely used my divination.”","Zu An quickly channeled a surge of pure ki into Qi Yaoguang’s body. Only then did her complexion finally recover a little. He was perplexed. “Someone of your cultivation shouldn’t become so weakened from a divination. Your earlier condition was so severe that it felt as if even your lifespan was affected.”","Qi Yaoguang smiled. “That would be the case for other matters, but when divining the libationer’s safety, the price was bound to be heavier.”","Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected her to go this far for him.","Instead of dwelling on this matter, Qi Yaoguang waved her sleeves and conjured an image of a massive vortex. There was a skeleton at its center. She said, “This is the result of my divination. I hesitated for a long time whether to tell you, but I thought I should at least give you a heads up so you could take precautions.”","“What does that mean?” Zu An looked at the image. The vortex induced a feeling of vertigo, and the skeleton inside looked jarring too. This looked terribly inauspicious.","“In the field of divination, bones represent death. I’m not too sure what that vortex means; it could represent water or some sort of danger.” Qi Yaoguang had a worried frown.","Zu An sighed. “Am I destined to die on this trip?”","Qi Yaoguang hurriedly shook her head. “Divination only shows the most likely flow of events. Your trip will be fraught with danger, but heaven’s will is fleeting. There will always be a sliver of hope. Fate isn't cast in stone. Libationer, you mustn’t give up hope.”","Zu An smiled. “I’m not the kind to surrender to fate. You may put your mind at ease, Yaoguang.”","Qi Yaoguang breathed a sigh of relief. “Libationer, will you harbor a grudge against me for sharing an inauspicious divination with you at this juncture?”","“Why would I harbor a grudge against you? I'm more than grateful to you for sacrificing your lifespan to warn me of danger,” Zu An replied gently. “I’ll be leaving soon, so I can’t help you any further. Seek Ji Dengtu and Xiaoxi’s help, and request some medicinal herbs from Bi Linglong. They can help you recover from your depletion.”","Qi Yaoguang smiled. “Don’t worry, libationer. It’s not my first time peering into heaven’s will and suffering such d backlash. May you have a smooth journey.”","...","Zu An bade farewell to his friends and lovers with his countless soul fragments. He had never felt time pass so quickly before. In a flash, it had already reached the time he had agreed on with Employee 9527. He returned his soul fragments into his main body and activated his invitation letter.","Soon, Employee 9527 appeared. “Esteemed guest, this way please!”","A cloud appeared beneath Zu An’s feet. He stepped onto it, and the two of them swiftly flew into space. He looked at the world beneath him with wistful eyes. There was no greater grief in the world than separation.","Soon, they arrived before a boat.","Zu An was surprised. He'd been expecting a high-tech spaceship, but it looked no different from an ancient wooden boat—and on top of that, it didn’t look big. As he boarded the boat, he asked in surprise, “I thought you said there were other guests. Where are they?”","He didn’t have to scan the area with his divine sense. The boat was small enough for him to see everything at a glance.","“This is a dispatch boat. The ship heading to Dreamland is docked at another world.” Sensing Zu An’s confusion, Employee 9527 elaborated, “All kinds of danger exist in the Myriad Worlds, so the coordinates of each world are kept secret. Most guests don’t want their world coordinates to be known to others, so we employ isolating measures to ensure client confidentiality.”","Zu An was taken aback. He had failed to consider this due to his lacking experience. It hadn’t been easy for him to eradicate the Monster World and restore peace. Should their coordinates be exposed, the annihilation worshipers or other dangerous entities could set their eyes here, and they would never have peace ever again.","That made him vigilant. “But you know the coordinates of all the guests.”","Employee 9527 smiled. “You can put your mind at ease, esteemed guest. Our Universal Conglomerate enjoys a stellar reputation across the Myriad Worlds. We have never leaked our guests’ secrets in the billions of years of our existence.”","“Billions of years...” Zu An was taken aback. “It looks like the Universal Conglomerate is extremely powerful.”","Employee 9527 smiled proudly. “Our conglomerate exists wherever civilization exists and the stars shine on.”"]},{"number":2753,"title":"Chapter 2753: Chapter 2705: Three Pieces of Information","paragraphs":["Zu An was taken aback. A single universe was already unimaginably huge as it was, and there were multiple universes on top of that. To think the Universal Conglomerate would have branches everywhere! This was proof of their strength.","“Doesn’t that mean that you’re highly respected within the conglomerate?”","9527 wasn't a small number, but it was nothing compared to the sheer number of planets out there in the Myriad Worlds. Having such a number showed that the employee was of considerable stature within the conglomerate.","Employee 9527’s face beamed with pride. “Esteemed guest, you’re flattering me.”","Zu An took this opportunity to shoot a question. “May I know which universal deity is protecting the Universal Conglomerate?”","The Universal Conglomerate couldn’t have grown so big without the aid of a universal deity.","Employee 9527 smiled. “This isn’t a secret in the Myriad Worlds. Our Universal Conglomerate worships the Deity of Order, and we maintain our principles to ensure fair trade. That’s also why different universes are willing to trade with us.”","Zu An nodded. I’ve learned about another universal deity. The Deity of Order... He didn’t ask about the Deity of Order’s name, knowing it could draw the latter’s gaze.","“Sit well, esteemed guest. We’ll be setting off.” Employee 9527 took out a formation disc and began controlling it.","Zu An studied the formation disc, curious to know how it worked. He quickly realized that the formation disc contained not just formations, but also some kind of technology. But even though the world he had transmigrated from, Earth, was a technological civilization, he wasn't a scientist. His high school-level scientific knowledge wasn't enough for him to comprehend the principles of the formation disc.","Soon, the boat set off. Zu An took one last look at the Cultivation World, wondering when he would return.","The boat initially moved slowly, but a light barrier soon formed around the boat, and it began moving at an incredible speed. The surroundings began glowing brightly as the boat seemed to travel through pockets of space.","Zu An would never have thought that this shabby-looking sailboat could travel at such fast speeds. Despite being on the boat, he felt no turbulence whatsoever. On top of that, he noticed that the boat wasn't just flying straight but traversing through ‘barriers’.","Top experts of the Cultivation World could also temporarily travel in space, but no matter how long they flew, all they saw was the bleak void and desolate planets. They wouldn’t see such a brilliant sight.","Sensing Zu An’s bewilderment, Employee 9527 explained with a smile, “This is spatial leap technology. It allows one to move at extreme speeds while traversing through normal world barriers.”","Zu An was awed. This technology is far superior to that of my previous world.","Employee 9527 soon stowed away the formation disc, and the boat automatically traveled toward the assigned coordinates.","“How much longer will it take for us to arrive at the temporary world?” Zu An asked.","“Using your world’s time calculation method, around two hours,” Employee 9527 replied politely.","“That’s long!” Zu An was surprised that it would take that long despite them traveling so quickly. The temporary world had to be extremely far away from the Cultivation World.","“This much precaution is required to ensure the safety of our guests.” Employee 9527 first verified that the boat was functioning properly before saying, “There’s still some time before reaching the temporary world, so why don’t we make a deal?”","Zu An was surprised. “What deal?”","Employee 9527 didn’t answer the question. Instead, he asked, “What do you think is the most important thing you need when exploring the Myriad Worlds?”","“Information,” Zu An replied without hesitation.","“Indeed.” Employee 9527’s eyes gleamed with approval. “Most people would answer 'strength', but there is bound to be someone stronger or possessing an ability that curbs you in the Myriad Worlds. That’s why it is important to collect intelligence beforehand to avert danger.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. “I presume you’re intending to sell information to me. Does the Universal Conglomerate know everything in the world?”","Employee 9527 shook his head. “The Myriad Worlds are vast. As formidable as our conglomerate is, we aren’t omniscient.”","He suddenly changed his tone and continued with a proud smile, “But we can answer most questions that people have.”","Zu An was awed. “May I know what currency the Universal Conglomerate uses?”","Employee 9527 replied with a smile, “There are many worlds across the universes, each one having their own currency. Unfortunately, what is valuable in one world can be commonplace in another. For instance, diamonds can be valuable gemstones in some worlds, but there are also worlds where diamonds rain from the sky.","“To deal with that issue, our Universal Conglomerate trades using credit points. All worlds trade with us using credit points, and we transport their resources to other worlds to sell and earn a profit.”","“That sounds fair.” Zu An wasn’t surprised. There were similar concepts in his previous world’s sci-fi novels.","“Of course it is. Our Universal Conglomerate will never take advantage of our customers!”","“What can I use to trade for credit points, and how many credit points would a piece of information cost?”","“Ores, weapons, armor, and cultivation methods can all be traded for credit points. However, your world isn’t particularly strong, so I fear you will struggle to earn enough credit points for even a piece of information. Secrets and intelligence are the most valuable assets in the Myriad Worlds.” Employee 9527 briefly paused before adding, “But if you’re willing to stake your World Law Beacon, you should be able to earn a decent amount of credit points.”","Zu An calmly replied, “You just mentioned that the Universal Conglomerate doesn’t take advantage of its customers. Do you think I don’t know how much a Wonderpoint World is worth?”","His friends and lovers resided in the Cultivation World. He wouldn’t sell it to anyone else even if it wasn’t a Wonderpoint World.","“This is a normal haggling method; it doesn’t defy our conglomerate’s principles.” Employee 9527 realized that his explanation wasn’t convincing, so he added, “But I was indeed a bit abrupt. Since this is our first meeting, in accordance with the Universal Conglomerate’s rules, I can provide you two free pieces of information. I’ll add an extra one in as a sign of my goodwill. I hope you will see our Universal Conglomerate in a positive light in the future.”","In the Myriad Worlds, those who possessed a Wonderpoint World were all formidable powerhouses. While the man before him appeared weak at the moment, his potential wasn't to be underestimated. It would be wise to befriend him while he’s still weak.","He'd thought he could exploit Zu An’s ignorance to buy the Wonderpoint World, but his recklessness had ended up piquing the other party’s displeasure. If the other party was vindictive, it could spell trouble for the Universal Conglomerate in the future. Resolving a future grudge with an additional piece of information was a worthwhile trade.","Zu An’s expression alleviated a little. “My gratitude to you and the Universal Conglomerate.”","He pondered for a while before asking his first question, “What universal deities are there in the Myriad Worlds?”"]},{"number":2754,"title":"Chapter 2754: Chapter 2706: Twelve Universal Deities","paragraphs":["That question had been on Zu An’s mind for a long time. The Cultivation World lacked information about the Myriad Worlds, and Mi Li had been ambiguous about it. I hope that the Universal Conglomerate won’t disappoint me.","Employee 9527 was startled, not expecting the question. He remarked, “Most people in the Myriad Worlds avoid discussing the universal deities, fearing it will bring disaster. However, our Universal Conglomerate deals with intelligence as well. We have the Deity of Order’s protection and the other universal deities’ tacit approval. We have permission to talk about them.”","Zu An was awed. The Universal Conglomerate was able to obtain the tacit approval of the universal deities? They're stronger than I thought.","“This piece of information should have been worth a huge fortune, far beyond what most people can afford. I feel like I’m taking a huge loss here.” Employee 9527 felt deflated.","Zu An smiled. “It’s my fortune to befriend you.”","Employee 9527’s awful complexion finally alleviated. This business could be worthwhile if he could earn the friendship of a future top expert. With this thought in mind, he began speaking, “There are thirteen universal deities logged in our records. It’s possible some universal deities might have passed away, and it’s also possible for there to be universal deities that we aren’t aware about. The Myriad Worlds are a huge place, after all.”","“I’d love to hear about them.” Zu An pricked up his ears.","Employee 9527’s expression turned solemn. He took out a small table and placed all kinds of offerings on it.","Zu An was surprised. This resembles some of the rituals recorded in the Baopu Sutra.","Employee 9527 took out an artifact and waved it around Zu An and himself. A peculiar melody played, and droplets of water began falling out of nowhere.","Zu An felt revitalized, as if he had been cleansed inside out. He was surprised. This must be some kind of sacred water or spirit spring water with the power to purge evil. It must have been worth a fortune.","Employee 9527 took out three incense sticks, which automatically lit up without him doing anything. He first prayed to the void before passing the incense to Zu An. “From my mouth to your ears, whatever I tell you today must never reach a third person’s ears, or else you’ll bring calamity upon yourself.”","“Of course!” By now, Zu An understood that secrets had value in the Myriad Worlds, and they could bring danger upon one too. He followed the other party’s instructions, taking the three incense sticks, praying to the void, and placing them on the table.","When he saw that the incense sticks didn’t go out, Employee 9527 breathed a sigh of relief. He began speaking, “First, there is the Deity of Memory, who records all information in the Myriad Worlds. There is a divergence among his worshipers. Some believe in only recording important figures, items, and events; anything else is a waste of time and effort. In any case, the Deity of Memory’s worshipers boast the widest span of knowledge and intelligence in the Myriad Worlds, with some of them knowing as much or even more than the Universal Conglomerate.”","Zu An nodded. The Mirror Scribe he'd met, Unblind Zuoqiu, worshiped the Deity of Memory, and had given him the invitation to Dreamland.","“There’s also the Deity of Chaos and Enigma. This deity...” Employee 9527 briefly paused to contemplate how to word his statement. “This deity’s jurisdiction appears to overlap with the Deity of Memory, but they are the opposite of each other.","“The Deity of Memory’s worshipers seek to record events happening in the Myriad Worlds, whereas the Deity of Chaos and Enigma’s worshipers seek to corrupt... Cough cough , I mean, alter events. There are many things now for which we don’t know whether they have truly happened or have been altered.”","The corners of Zu An’s lips slowly crept upward. Looks like my universal deity is quite the troublemaker. He had unintentionally carried out the duties of a Time Scribe, and he realized that his universal deity was very misunderstood.","Often, there wasn’t a clear distinction between truths and lies. Sometimes, beautiful lies were much better than harsh truths. Until the dust settled, it was possible to switch the truth with a lie.","“Naturally, the Deity of Memory’s worshipers and Deity of Chaos and Enigma’s worshipers are nemeses.” Employee 9527 appeared to be holding himself back. “The Deity of Chaos and Enigma’s worshipers are often madmen or lunatics. They act without rhyme or reason, so we, the Deity of Order’s worshipers, are on bad terms with them too.","“You should steer clear if you ever encounter one, or else it could lead to endless trouble. Fortunately, the Deity of Chaos and Enigma has very few worshipers, so it’s unlikely you’ll ever meet one.”","Zu An’s eyebrows shot up. He hadn’t expected his universal deity to have such poor reputation, such that even her worshipers were practically outcasts in the Myriad Worlds. It’ll be a huge mess if Employee 9527 ever learns about my identity.","Employee 9527 suddenly asked out of curiosity, “I’m guessing you’re curious about the universal deities because you have encountered their powers. May I know what deity you worship?”","Zu An was briefly stunned. But his brain whirred to action, and he quickly replied, “I am the Deity of Memory’s worshiper.”","That Time Scribe had been impersonating a Mirror Scribe. It must be pretty common for Time Scribes to disguise themselves as Mirror Scribes.","Employee 9527 was surprised. “I didn’t expect you to be the Deity of Memory’s worshiper. We might be able to trade information in the future.”","“Of course,” Zu An replied. I bet you’ll have the most interesting look on your face when you discover my identity in the future.","Employee 9527 continued, “Our conglomerate worships the Deity of Order. Order is necessary in the Myriad Worlds, or else there’ll only be slaughter and calamities.”","Zu An nodded in agreement.","“Speaking of calamities, there is the Deity of Annihilation. He believes that civilizations, people, and all living beings are the scourge of the Myriad Worlds, depleting its essence. His worshipers seek to bring annihilation upon everything. Needless to say, they are widely feared in the Myriad Worlds.”","“I have encountered his worshipers in the past,” Zu An replied grimly. “May I know the name of the Deity of Annihilation? What powerful entities are there under him?”","The more information he gathered, the more prepared he would be to deal with the Deity of Annihilation.","Employee 9527 shook his head. “The ritual grants us some level of immunity, but mentioning their names will still draw their gazes. That could spell the end of us.”","“I was too reckless.” Zu An was startled. So the Universal Conglomerate is fearful of this too.","“If you want information about the Deity of Annihilation, that will count as the second question,” Employee 9527 said with a smile.","“It’s fine. I’ll investigate it myself in the future.” Zu An had better questions to ask than to squander this precious opportunity. There was still time anyway.","Regret flickered through Employee 9527’s eyes. “Let’s resume our topic. Next is the Deity of Nebula. Little is known about him, for those who seek to understand him will be assimilated and lose all feelings, becoming one with the nebula.”","“In a way, he is more mysterious than the Deity of Chaos and Enigma, and he has very few worshipers. Some speculate that the Deity of Nebula is either the origin or the end of the Myriad Worlds. He is omnipresent, yet no one has ever seen him.”","Zu An heart shuddered. This resembled the universal deity whom Yan Xuehen had come into contact with.","“What if one becomes his worshiper?”","Employee 9527 grimly replied, “That’s not a good thing. His worshipers can gain tremendous power, but they lose everything in the end. That’s why no one wishes to embark on that path. Almost all worshipers of the Deity of Nebula stumble into that path by accident, but by then, it is already too late for them to back out. They are doomed.”"]},{"number":2755,"title":"Chapter 2755: Chapter 2707: The Death of Death","paragraphs":["Zu An’s heart sank into the abyss. When he first reunited with Yan Xuehen, the other party had appeared to be on the verge of ‘forgetting’ him. She'd mentioned coming into contact with a power that appeared to be even more advanced than Absolute Dispassion.","Absolute Dispassion already makes one forget many emotions; wouldn’t a higher level mean forgetting everything? That resembles the state of nebula that Employee 9527 described earlier.","“Is there no way for those who have already embarked on this path to avoid a tragic end?”","“Based on the current information we have collected, there is no solution.” Zu An’s agitation sparked a thought in Employee 9527’s head. “Esteemed guest, do you have a friend who is on that path too?”","Zu An nodded. Employee 9527 sighed.","As expected of an entity who possesses a Wonderpoint World. He might be weak now, but he already harnesses tremendous fortune. Even the people around him have such extraordinary experiences.","It’s extremely rare for anyone to step onto that path, whether knowingly or unknowingly.","The Deity of Nebula was feared, but his worshipers indeed wielded incredible fighting prowess. Becoming his worshiper was considered a fortuitous encounter that many envied in the Myriad Worlds.","“Please don’t be too worried, esteemed guest. Those who have embarked on this path will inevitably descend deeper into the abyss, but there is some time before they lose themselves,” Employee 9527 said in consolation.","Zu An was still worried. I'll have to tell Yan Xuehen about this when I return. She must stop practicing her Unshakable Daoist Manual. I should also warn Chuyan against following her master’s footsteps.","Employee 9527 proceeded to introduce another universal deity, “While the Deity of Nebula induces his worshipers to lose themselves and see no meaning in the world, it’s the opposite for the Deity of Bliss and Desire. He seeks ultimate bliss. He believes that all beings have desires, but these desires are inhibited by restrictions we impose on ourselves. Only by releasing our innermost desires can we enjoy the most fundamental bliss in the world.”","Zu An remarked, “The Deity of Bliss and Desire must have many believers.”","It resembled the Devil Sect’s creed, though this was at a much higher level.","Employee 9527 burst into laughter. “Indeed. No matter the world, it is difficult for one to resist bliss and pleasure. The Deity of Bliss and Desire has many worshipers. I’ll also offer you an additional piece of information—among his worshipers are special entities known as Bliss Demonesses. They are in another class. Even the greatest experts take pride in sharing a night with a Bliss Demoness. They say there’s no greater thrill in the world.”","Judging from the other party’s envious look, Zu An could tell that Employee 9527 had never tasted that kind of sensation before. He took this opportunity to ask, “May I know what the traits of a Bliss Demoness are?”","Since Employee 9527 was already volunteering information on his own accord, it would be foolish of Zu An not to probe deeper. More importantly, he was worried that Yun Jianyue would become a Bliss Demoness. What if it comes with side effects as well?","“A Bliss Demoness can bring bliss to others, but she also has a fundamental need for bliss. For that reason, renowned Bliss Demonesses tend to have a long list of lovers.” Employee 9527 revealed a look that all men understood. “If you ever encounter a Bliss Demoness, you might be able to snag her without taking the initiative.”","Zu An was speechless. He was at a loss for words. He'd thought it was already bad enough for Yan Xuehen to have caught the Deity of Nebula’s attention, but to think that Yun Jianyue was worse off! I have to stop her from venturing deeper into this path!","“Is it possible to veer onto another path after becoming a Bliss Demoness?” Zu An hurriedly asked.","“Similar to becoming a Deity of Nebula’s worshiper, once a person becomes a Bliss Demoness, they won’t be able to break free anymore. Besides, that is a blissful thing for them. They can’t bear to let go of that happiness, so why would they veer off?” Employee 9527 suddenly thought about something and asked in astonishment, “Do you, by any chance, know a Bliss Demoness too?”","Zu An replied with a sigh, “I have a lover who has received the Deity of Bliss and Desire’s gaze. I don’t know if she’ll become a Bliss Demoness.”","Employee 9527 was astounded. “Amazing! You have both a Deity of Nebula’s worshiper and a Bliss Demoness with you!”","He was glad that he had invested in Zu An. No wonder he became a Wonderpoint World’s master. He wields incredible luck and potential.","“But that doesn’t sound to be a good thing,” Zu An exclaimed with a frown.","Employee 9527 stared at Zu An. Well, I don’t think it’s necessarily a bad thing for her, though it is a bad thing for you. You’re going to be cuckolded real bad. Of course, he knew better than to say those words aloud.","“Don’t worry too much, esteemed guest. There are all kinds of peculiar abilities in the Myriad Worlds. There might be something out there that can suppress her desire.”","Zu An was speechless.","Employee 9527 quickly changed the subject. “Moving on, there is the Deity of Longevity. All civilizations in the Myriad Worlds, no matter how prosperous or prestigious, have an intrinsic desire for longevity, especially those in positions of power. Their strong desire for eternal life created the Deity of Longevity.”","Zu An was taken aback. “Are there beings in this world who can live forever?”","In human history, Qin Shihuang had sought the immortality medicine, and the other emperors had likely tried the same too. The greater their power and authority, the more they feared death.","“It’s possible to live for a very long time—the Deity of Longevity can greatly extend a person’s lifespan—but death remains inevitable. Death is a fundamental law that has existed since the creation of the Myriad Worlds.” Employee 9527 knew Zu An possessed exceptional luck, so he gave the latter a bonus piece of information. “The Deity of Longevity created different immortal medicines that can resurrect a person, allowing them to live a second life. Each one can send experts into a rampage vying over it.”","Zu An was surprised. He hadn’t expected the immortal medicines to be from the Deity of Longevity.","“With longevity naturally comes death, but there are rumors that the Deity of Death is dead. However, he still has some worshipers. Perhaps a new Deity of Death might be crowned in the near future,” Employee 9527 said.","“The Deity of Death can die too?” Zu An was baffled.","“Of course. Some say he was killed by the Deity of Annihilation. Some say he was devoured by the Deity of Nebula. There are also speculations that he died naturally. No one knows the truth.” Employee 9527 decided to sell Zu An a favor and provide him with more information.","A thought popped into Zu An’s mind. The Netherworld was emptied out. Could that be due to the demise of the Deity of Death?"]},{"number":2756,"title":"Chapter 2756: Chapter 2708: The Most Beautiful Woman in the Myriad Worlds","paragraphs":["Zu An had been wondering what had happened in the Netherworld to cause it to be emptied overnight. The Netherworld had been protected by the Shaman races, ghost deities, and the Six Paths of Reincarnation. It could even stand its ground against an invasion from the Celestial Court.","But the inscription on the Reincarnation Platform was so brief that it appeared that the Netherworld had been destroyed in a very short time, such that even Ox Head and Horse Face didn’t have time to leave complete information.","So, he asked Employee 9527 about it. He thought that it was worth a question.","“The Netherworld?” Employee 9527 frowned. “It sounds like it could be related to the Deity of Death, but my apologies, the Universal Conglomerate has no information about that. Perhaps you might have better luck with the Deity of Memory’s worshipers. Since I’m unable to answer this question, I’ll let you ask another one.”","Zu An was intrigued. “Have you memorized all the Universal Conglomerate’s information?”","It was amazing how Employee 9527 could answer his questions right away each time.","“Of course not.” Employee 9527 smiled. “Who knows how many civilizations there are in the Myriad Worlds? I can’t possibly remember everything. We’re implanted with a chip that grants us restricted access to the conglomerate’s database, depending on our access rights, so that we can strike deals.”","“Could your access rights be insufficient to access that piece of information?” Zu An asked, refusing to give up.","“That’s not the case here.” Employee 9527 shook his head. “The database will notify us as such if our access rights are too low to access a piece of information. In such cases, we can contact a colleague with higher access rights to handle the exchange. However, the database indicated that it doesn’t have the information you’re looking for.”","“I see.” Zu An was disappointed. At the same time, he was amazed by how the Universal Conglomerate had access to not only cultivation treasures but also sci-fi technology. No wonder their business got this big.","Employee 9527 continued, “All beings fear death. Some overcome it by pursuing longevity, maximizing their individual potential. Others go a different route, pursuing quantity over quality. They frantically reproduce to ensure the continuation of their race and bloodline.","“Naturally, there is also the Deity of Reproduction. As long as a single member of their race survives, they will be able to make a comeback. Such swiftly reproducing races are a huge headache for countless civilizations.”","Zu An was reminded of sunfishes and Antarctica krill from his previous life—those were animals who relied on mass reproduction to ensure the survival of their species. To think there would be such races in the Myriad Worlds too!","“Reproduction isn’t just limited to biological reproduction. For instance, the Deity of Reproduction’s worshipers from technological civilizations may also engage in actions such as cloning,” Employee 9527 explained.","Zu An was reminded of a famous anti-fan of a gaming company in his previous life. The gaming company had kept reporting the anti-fan’s social media account to stop him from spreading negative information, but a new one would just pop out right after. The gaming company couldn’t stop the anti-fan no matter what it tried.","I guess that anti-fan should count as a Deity of Reproduction worshiper.","“Next is the Deity of Love and Beauty. Her worshipers believe the meaning of life is beauty. They pursue everything beautiful, be it in appearance, buildings, sceneries, or the universe. In technological civilizations, it can even be applied to physics and mathematical equations. Often, they judge an equation by its aesthetics before it is proven to be true.”","Zu An was baffled. Huh? That works too?","“Unlike other universal deities, the Deity of Love and Beauty is the only confirmed female deity. It is also recorded in our database that she is the most beautiful woman in the Myriad Worlds. However, it has been a long time since anyone has seen her.” Employee 9527’s eyes shone as he spoke about the Deity of Love and Beauty. It seemed as if his greatest regret was having yet to see her.","“Are the other deities genderless?” Zu An asked out of curiosity.","“Of course. Universal deities can’t be judged in the same way as normal beings. Gender holds no meaning to them,” Employee 9527 replied.","I guess the Deity of Love and Beauty must be truly narcissistic to insist on existing as a woman.","“If you obtain news about the Deity of Love and Beauty, make sure to sell it to me. Such information will land me consecutive promotions in the Universal Conglomerate. You can trust me to compensate you handsomely for that,” Employee 9527 said with beaming eyes.","Zu An smiled. “You’re overestimating me. I doubt someone from a remote world like me will stumble upon the Deity of Love and Beauty when no one else in the vast Myriad Worlds knows about her whereabouts.”","“That’s hard to say. You are blessed with tremendous fortune.” Despite his words, Employee 9527 didn’t think Zu An would be lucky enough to stumble upon the Deity of Love and Beauty either. He continued his introduction, “Up next is the Deity of Knowledge. All civilized races hold knowledge in high regard and seek to understand the universes’ fundamental laws. The Deity of Knowledge’s worshipers are more common in technological civilizations.","“The Universal Conglomerate hires the Deity of Knowledge’s worshipers to resolve our problems. The chips in our heads that allow us to access the database were developed by them.”","Zu An figured the world he'd lived in prior to his transmigration could be considered a technological civilization too. In fact, most cultivators devoted their lives to comprehending dao. That was pursuit of knowledge, too.","“There’s also the Deity of Protection. From ants to higher entities, all beings have things they seek to protect. Naturally, there is bound to be a Deity of Protection as well.”","Zu An guessed that Mohism’s believers from his previous life would worship the Deity of Protection if they knew about his existence. Curious, he asked, “Then what does the Deity of Protection himself seek to protect?”","Employee 9527 was taken aback. “I don’t know. Some say he has devoted himself to protecting the Myriad Worlds to keep them from being destroyed, but who would have the ability to destroy the Myriad Worlds?”","Zu An nodded in agreement. Even if the sky collapsed, there were universal deities to shoulder the burden. These were problems for them to worry about, not him.","“I have already answered one of your questions. What else do you want to ask?” Employee 9527 felt as if he was taking a huge loss. The information he had just revealed far surpassed the value of a single question.","“I’d like information about Dreamland.” There was a lot of things Zu An wanted to know about, but his priority at hand was still learning about Dreamland. Qi Yaoguang’s prophecy had piqued his vigilance. This trip was likely to be fraught with danger. He should first overcome the crisis at hand before thinking about other matters.","Employee 9527 frowned. “The scope of your question is too big. I feel like I’m taking a huge loss here.”"]},{"number":2757,"title":"Chapter 2757: Chapter 2709: No Survivors","paragraphs":["Zu An clasped his fist and said, “It’s truly my fortune to have met you. I’ll etch in my mind the help you've provided me.”","He had indeed taken advantage of the other party by posing questions with wide scopes. Thus, he thought it was only right for him to provide the other party with some emotional value too.","It worked. Employee 9527’s frown was alleviated as he began explaining, “Dreamland is a highly elusive place with little ties to the outside world. There is a long interval between each opening, and the interval varies. A long time ago, it didn’t even open once every ten thousand years, but more recently, it has been opening once every millennium.”","“I heard that Dreamland can fulfill any wish. Is that true?” Zu An was curious.","“Not even universal deities can fulfill any wish,” Employee 9527 replied with a smile. “But Dreamland is indeed a mystical place. Our information indicates that it can fulfill wishes within a reasonable degree, especially since most people’s wishes aren’t that hard to fulfill. If one has the resources to deal with our Universal Conglomerate, we can fulfill most of their dreams, too.”","Zu An frowned. “But unlike the Universal Conglomerate, Dreamland isn’t an organization with connections and resources across universes. It can’t fulfill wishes the same way the Universal Conglomerate does.”","“Indeed. We have been investigating the methods employed by Dreamland to fulfill wishes, but we haven’t been able to figure it out,” Employee 9527 remarked.","“Not even the Universal Conglomerate has been able to figure it out?” Zu An was taken aback. To think there are things that even the most powerful conglomerate is unable to figure out!","“We have had employees who entered Dreamland, but most did not return. Those who returned struggled to explain Dreamland’s inner workings. Furthermore, the interval between each Dreamland opening is too long, and the place doesn’t seem too dangerous. In the end, we decided not to bother with it,” Employee 9527 explained.","“Did no one return with news from the previous Dreamland opening?” Zu An frowned. Dreamland was only sounding more and more baffling to him.","“No one returned from Dreamland during its last opening,” Employee 9527 replied grimly.","“Huh?!” Zu An was shocked. “Doesn’t that make Dreamland public enemy number one? Why did you mention it didn’t seem too dangerous earlier?”","“Those people chose to stay in Dreamland voluntarily.” Sensing Zu An’s doubtful gaze, Employee 9527 elaborated, “They contacted their friends and family beforehand to inform them of their decision to stay in Dreamland.”","“Could they have been coerced into it?”","Employee 9527 shook his head. “That can’t be. There are powerful experts among those who chose to stay in Dreamland. Putting aside whether Dreamland has the means to simultaneously coerce so many people, there should be no way for them to pull that off without any anomalies.”","“And this is not the first time something like that has happened. The last few times it opened, most people were reluctant to leave Dreamland. Think about it—it’s a place where dreams can be fulfilled. It’s only normal for one to not want to leave.”","“Based on what I have heard, a corresponding price has to be paid for a wish to be fulfilled. It’s not like Dreamland is operating a charity. I doubt Dreamland will continue to fulfill all their wishes just because they choose to stay there forever,” Zu An said.","Employee 9527 was awed. “There would be far fewer wars in the world if most people could be as rational as you. You are right, but you have to put yourself in their shoes. The temptation is not that easy to resist.”","Zu An was alarmed. I mustn’t fall for Dreamland’s temptation. There are too many people waiting for me back home. “Do you know which universal deity Dreamland falls under?”","“As I told you, we know very little about Dreamland,” Employee 9527 said. “Our staff has discussed this matter, and we are split into two main factions. One faction believes Dreamland belongs to the Deity of Bliss and Desire because it fulfills wishes. It’s hard to imagine anyone other than the Deity of Bliss and Desire accomplishing such a feat.”","Zu An nodded. Many people have refused to leave after setting foot in Dreamland. That fulfills the trait of losing oneself in desire.","“The other faction thinks they belong to the Deity of Memory,” Employee 9527 assessed Zu An’s reaction as he spoke.","“The Deity of Memory?” Zu An was taken aback.","“Indeed. Among the Deity of Memory’s worshipers is a branch that specializes in crafting dreamscapes. Some of our staff believe the easiest way to fulfill a person’s dream is within a dream,” Employee 9527 replied with a smile. “You are a Deity of Memory worshiper. I thought you would have heard about this.”","Zu An shook his head. “As you know, I've been living in a remote corner. It’s only in recent days that I learned more about the Myriad Worlds. This is the first time I’m hearing details about Dreamland, so there’s no way I could have known such information beforehand.”","“That’s true.” Employee 9527 didn’t doubt Zu An. “Since you’re a Deity of Memory worshiper, you might have a huge advantage in Dreamland if it is under the Deity of Memory’s jurisdiction.”","Zu An responded with a smile, but his heart swelled with bitterness. But I’m a Time Scribe instead of a Mirror Scribe. That puts me on the opposite side of the Deity of Memory! Who knows what fate will befall me if I get discovered?","“Please let me know if you ever find out which universal deity Dreamland worships. I’ll compensate you generously,” Employee 9527 said. “The same applies to any valuable information. All information about Dreamland is worth a lot.”","“Of course. It’s my fortune to have befriended you. But how should I contact you in the future? Should I visit one of the Universal Conglomerate’s branches?” Zu An asked.","“You can reach me by reporting my employee number at any branch, but that’s too troublesome.” Employee 9527 handed him a little cube. “You can use this to contact me instead.”","Zu An was intrigued. The cube resembled an antiquated Nokia phone, but it only had two buttons. One resembled the pick up button, and the other resembled a hang up button.","Employee 9527 taught him how to use it. “You might not be able to use this inside Dreamland. That place is too enigmatic. Our conglomerate sent employees in with this kind of communication tool. We were still able to reach them at the start, but we soon lost contact.”","Zu An’s heart shuddered. Looks like this trip is going to be fraught with danger. I need to be extremely careful. Seeing that there was no more useful information about Dreamland, he decided to pose his third question. “I have a friend who is trapped in a place for a thousand years...”","Upon learning Dreamland could potentially only be able to fulfill wishes within a dream, Zu An became worried it couldn’t resolve his problems, so he decided to pose his question to the Universal Conglomerate too. He could always find the solution for Mi Li’s body elsewhere.","As for the issues concerning the Goddess of Wu Mountain and Chang’e, he dearly hated the fact that he couldn’t ask more questions.","Employee 9527 quickly searched the database before replying, “Saving your friend is both easy and hard.”"]},{"number":2758,"title":"Chapter 2758: Chapter 2710: Spaceship","paragraphs":["“What do you mean by that?” Zu An asked.","“The situation you have described is the result of a special world law. Being the master of the world grants you control over its world laws, but you are unable to rewrite them. You can directly rewrite them once you become strong enough, thus saving your friend. Most people struggle to reach that level, however, which is where the difficulty lies,” Employee 9527 said.","“That said, the Myriad Worlds are a huge place. You don’t have to reach that level yourself. You don’t even require the help of a universal deity; there are experts beneath them capable of that feat as well. Otherwise, you can also achieve the same effect through the use of a treasure.","“Still, you’ll need luck to stumble upon an expert of that caliber, and even so, you’ll likely have to pay a hefty price to solicit their help. That’s why I said it can be both easy and hard.”","Zu An nodded, having understood what the other party was saying. He asked out of curiosity, “May I know how power levels are classified in the Myriad Worlds? How strong of an expert do I need to find to save my friend?”","“There are countless worlds and civilizations in the Myriad Worlds. Your world has its own standards for classifying cultivation levels, but the names and standards can be very different in another world. Besides, abilities can complement and curb one another—an expert in one world can be curbed by a weak ability in another world. Who’s to say who is stronger?”","Zu An frowned. This made things tricky.","“A simpler evaluation method gradually arose as civilizations interacted, such as planet level, star level, galaxy level, and universe level... It measures the rough extent of one's destructive prowess. Beneath planet level are the weaker cultivators in each civilization. In the context of the Myriad Worlds, they are all ants. You’re roughly at planet level right now.","“But these distinctions are vague and inaccurate. The Myriad Worlds is huge, as I have said before. Through the use of mystical artifacts or special abilities, a planet level can defeat a star level.”","Zu An knew Employee 9527 was consoling him, but he didn’t pay it much heed. His fighting style was indeed reliant on special abilities. He wondered where the celestials in the ancient era fell in this classification method.","“How strong would one have to be to rewrite the world laws trapping my friend?”","Employee 9527 pondered before replying, “That’s hard to say. Some people are strong but lack in their grasp of laws. Some people are weak but specialize in this field. I’m also not sure how strong the law is, as I have never been to the place you mentioned. However, I reckon star level should be enough...”","“Are there different strengths to world laws, too?” Zu An asked.","“Of course! Stronger worlds are bound to have stronger spatial laws than weaker worlds. The gap between planet levels can sometimes be larger than the gap between a planet level and a star level,” Employee 9527 explained.","Zu An recalled his understanding of the world from his previous life and nodded in realization. Many planets in the universe were as large as stars, but they didn’t metamorphose into stars because they lacked something critical or needed more time to build up. These planets could be thousands of times larger than other ordinary planets.","“I have answered your three questions. Just on time. We’re reaching our destination soon.” Employee 9527 got up and controlled the boat using his formation disc.","A white light flashed ahead of them, and an entrance appeared.","Zu An was surprised. He was certain there had been nothing ahead of him earlier. He probably wouldn’t have noticed anything amiss even if he flew past this area countless times.","As the boat entered the door, their surroundings suddenly lit up. They transited from pitch-black space into a vibrant world with a blue sky, white clouds, and warm sunlight. This world had no ground, or perhaps the clouds were the ground.","A massive ship floated above the clouds. It was so majestic that it made the boat they were riding appear like a little dinghy. What surprised Zu An was that the ship resembled the spaceships he had seen in his previous life’s sci-fi movies, just that it looked even more streamlined and high-tech. Its black metallic body gleamed with a brilliant luster, and there was a huge image on it that appeared to be the Universal Conglomerate’s logo.","Zu An’s instinct told him that the ship had terrifying offensive prowess, and that it wouldn’t be a good idea to make an enemy of it.","Employee 9527 tapped on the formation disc. A hole appeared beneath the massive spaceship, and a brilliant light shone on their boat.","Zu An’s surroundings blurred as the boat was sucked into the massive ship. The first thing he saw inside was a dock, with many boats in place. Uniformed staff members had their hands full inspecting the boats.","Zu An was perplexed. “Why are there such huge differences in the boats?”","Some looked to be built in the feudal era, whereas some were high-tech spaceships. It was bizarre seeing them side by side.","“Our Universal Conglomerate deals with all kinds of civilizations across the universes, including those specializing in technology and magic. To cope with different potential risks, we don’t limit our arsenals to just that of a single civilization, or else it would be disastrous if we encounter one that happens to curb it,” Employee 9527 replied smoothly. Clearly, Zu An wasn’t the first guest to have asked this question.","Zu An was surprised. “Are there civilizations that are completely immune to technology or magic?”","“The universe is huge. There will always be enemies beyond your imagination. For instance, your Cultivation World has ghosts and apparition entities that are immune to physical attacks,” Employee 9527 explained grimly. “Since we operate across universes, there is no harm in being more prepared.”","Even an organization as huge as the Universal Conglomerate had such great respect for the Myriad Worlds. Zu An’s expression turned even more severe as he prayed that his luck wouldn’t be too bad.","“Follow me.” Employee 9527 led Zu An into the spaceship. They first passed through an automatic door that verified their identity, followed by several lifts. Along the way, Employee 9527 asked out of curiosity, “Hm? Based on what I know, your Cultivation World has never come into contact with a technological civilization before. You seem rather nonchalant about all these things, as if you are already used to it.”"]},{"number":2759,"title":"Chapter 2759: Chapter 2711: Fatal Mistake","paragraphs":["Employee 9527 had fetched countless people before, and even the most composed person from a cultivation-esque world tended to ask questions about the spaceship and everything about it. And yet this man was so calm. This was at odds with the intelligence he had received.","Could he be a spy sent by other powers? That sparked Employee 9527’s vigilance.","Sensing the other party’s body tensing up, Zu An quickly explained, “I chanced upon a dungeon connected to a technological civilization, so automatic doors and elevators aren’t foreign to me.” He wouldn’t easily reveal that he was a transmigrator, so it was fortunate there was another convenient excuse here.","Employee 9527 breathed a sigh of relief. “I’d expect no less from a Wonderpoint World. It is linked to so many different dungeons. Most worlds hardly have dungeons at all.”","Zu An was surprised. Are dungeons that rare? I guess the Cultivation World is hiding many secrets. Worried the other party would continue probing, he quickly changed the topic. “How many guests are there on this ship?”","“There are four other guests. You’ll be able to meet them very soon.” Employee 9527 gestured to the facilities and began introducing them. “That is our practice room. It provides our guests with ki, spiritual energy, battle energy, mana, or anything they require for their training. You should cultivate several times faster in there than usual.","“Alternatively, you can also set the training room to ‘Combat Mode’. The system will randomly choose a battlefield and an enemy for you. You can fight to your heart’s desire without worrying about dying.”","“That’s incredible!” Zu An was amazed.","It would take an immortal-tier weapon or a top-notch dungeon to achieve these effects in the Cultivation World, yet this was merely an ordinary training room on this spaceship. This went to show just how powerful the Universal Conglomerate was.","“It is a long journey, after all. It’s our pleasure to provide our guests with the greatest degree of convenience possible. Most of our guests are disciplined and seek to constantly train to grow stronger. Forcing them to idle is worse than death to them. Moreover, they can also vent inside the training room, making it less likely for them to cause trouble on the ship,” Employee 9527 replied with a smile. “You can give it a try when you have time. Don’t worry; all of our facilities, including food, are free. Dreamland has already paid the tab on your behalf.”","Zu An nodded. I should give it a try, since I’ve reached a bottleneck in the Cultivation World. This is a chance for me to get a glimpse of other combat styles in the Myriad Worlds, too.","“Aside from training rooms, we also have beaches, hot springs, swimming pools, and other amenities. You can relax there when you’re fatigued,” Employee 9527 said as he gestured to the other amenities.","Zu An was surprised. Space should have been precious on the spaceship, yet there were so many indulgent entertainment facilities in it. The Universal Conglomerate sure is wealthy!","Employee 9527 suddenly lowered his voice and chuckled. “If you are seeking another kind of fun, you can try out our spa massage room. Our attendants are meticulously-selected beauties, coming in every style you can think of. Your imagination is the limit there! Of course, that will be charged separately.”","Zu An was speechless.","Out of curiosity, he asked, “Do you have that many attendants on standby on every ship?”","They had encountered some female staff members along the way, but they were far from being as diverse as Employee 9527 described.","Employee 9527 laughed. “There’s no way we would provide so many female attendants on every ship. Our protocol is to first confirm the guest list before summoning them over using our teleportation technology. It looks like you’re interested. I’ll send you a list later. You can browse their 3D holograms. You won’t be disappointed!”","Zu An smiled awkwardly. “I’ll pass today. I’m a little tired.”","You must be kidding! I have many lovers waiting for me at home. How can I go philandering around here?","Employe 9527 wasn’t surprised by his answer. “I understand. It’s your first time venturing beyond your world, so there must be a lot on your mind right now. If you do feel lonely at any point in time, feel free to tell me.”","Zu An responded with a sheepish smile.","“That’s the canteen. Right ahead of us is the bar. Our guests frequently drink and chat there while enjoying the scenery outside.”","Employee 9527 brought Zu An into an exquisite bar. It was graceful and quiet. There weren’t many seats, and they were scattered around to grant privacy among the guests. Its walls were floor-to-ceiling glass panels that allowed one to see the scenery outside clearly.","But Zu An was in no mood to admire the scenery outside; he was more interested in the guests at the bar.","Seated closest to the entrance was a peculiar youth with seemingly translucent skin and no mouth. His eyes were completely black, with no irises. Or rather, it was practically filled with irises; as upon careful examination, Zu An noticed specks of light inside the youth's eyes that were reminiscent of the night sky.","Despite looking young, his hair was sparse like that of a middle-aged man with a receding hair pattern. It felt as if a gust of wind could pull away his hair. Zu An wondered if the youth was a stressed-out programmer on the 996 schedule[1].","Seated by the glass panels was an old woman dressed in rags. A glance was enough to make Zu An’s stomach churn. He had never seen such an ugly woman. Her face was covered in meat lumps of all shapes and sizes; anyone with trypophobia[2] would convulse on the spot.","Zu An quickly averted his gaze and turned his attention toward the old man seated in the innermost area of the bar. The latter was also hideous with glaring scars on his face, but he could easily be considered dashing compared to the old woman. He seemed crippled as he was seated in a wheelchair.","But Zu An didn’t dare to underestimate the old man, as the latter was shrouded in a translucent flame that felt extremely intimidating even tens of meters away.","“%¥@*!#¥【、】+1...!” The old man harrumphed before taking his leave.","It was as if the wheelchair was part of his body, wheeling him out of the bar without being maneuvered.","Zu An was baffled. He couldn’t understand what the other party was saying. He turned to Employee 9527 with confused eyes, only to see the latter looking a little awkward. The old man must have uttered something unpleasant.","A voice echoed in Zu An’s mind. “He said ‘Here I was wondering how incredible a master of a Wonderpoint World must be, but he turned out to be a weakling.'”","Zu An was speechless. He tracked the voice and realized the one who had just spoken was the youth with transparent skin and sparse hair. He was baffled as the youth had no mouth.","Sensing his confusion, the youth replied, “I’m conversing with you through psychic waves.” He shook his head and turned around to continue enjoying the scenery, seemingly having lost his interest in Zu An.","The old woman covered in meat lumps cackled as she limped her way out of her seat with the aid of a walking stick.","Zu An realized he had made a fatal error. There could be many languages even within a single world, let alone across the Myriad Worlds, yet he'd overlooked this issue. This could make his trip to Dreamland far more dangerous.","1. An intense schedule first popularized in mainland China, known as “996” - or 9 am to 9 pm, six days a week. In other words, it's a 72-hour work wee.k ☜","2. Trypophobia is an aversion or strong disgust experienced when viewing clusters of small holes or bumps, not necessarily a fear of holes themselves. ☜"]},{"number":2760,"title":"Chapter 2760: Chapter 2712: A Deity of Love and Beauty Worshiper","paragraphs":["Employee 9527 had been talking to him in his world’s language, so Zu An had neglected the communication barrier. It was only when he failed to comprehend what the person in the wheelchair was saying that this occurred to him.","The most important thing on a battlefield was intelligence, but how was he to procure information when he couldn’t speak their language? If he couldn’t understand what anyone was saying, the only fate awaiting him was death. If only he had realized this problem beforehand, he could have consulted Employee 9527 about this. Who knew how much it would cost if he posed that question now?","Employee 9527 led him into an empty room next. Noticing Zu An’s bewilderment, Employee 9527 explained with a smile, “Our guests come from different worlds. It is difficult to come up with a standardized room design because of their different interests and lifestyle habits, so we decided to let our guests arrange their own rooms instead.”","“Arrange their rooms?” Zu An was taken aback.","Employee 9527 lightly tapped on a crystal ball on the table beside him, and the crystal ball lit up. “Place your hand on the crystal ball and imagine a room you feel comfortable in.”","Zu An placed his hand on the crystal ball, and the scenery abruptly changed. It first transformed into his room in Brightmoon City, then the residence on Mount Yuquan, and then his room in the imperial palace...","Taken aback, he hurriedly retracted his hand.","Employee 9527 chuckled. “You can design your room however you want to. I shan’t inconvenience you any further with my presence here. If you’re hungry, you may head to the canteen or call for room service. I wish you a pleasant journey with us.”","He was about to leave when Zu An stopped him and voiced out his concern. Then, he asked, “How do the other guests overcome the communication barrier?”","“There are mainstream languages that experts from each world use to converse with one another.” Employee 9527 was startled. “Doesn’t your world have such language books?”","Zu An shook his head. “Our world has never interacted with other civilizations except in dungeons.”","The Monster World was the only other civilization they had interacted with. Thinking back, he had learned the demon language back then for that purpose, though the demon language was unlikely to be a mainstream language in the Myriad Worlds.","“That complicates things. I was able to converse with you because we knew which world you were from through the invitation letter, and the conglomerate assigned me a translator for your language.” Employee 9527 retrieved a small chip from his throat. What he spoke next sounded guttural; Zu An couldn’t comprehend at all. He quickly pasted the chip back on his throat and continued, “My apologies; that was a demonstration.”","Then, he continued, “I have backup translators, and I can give one to you in view of our friendship. However, our translators only cover the languages of the other guests and the major powers. It can’t translate the languages of the other civilizations.”","Zu An was delighted. “I will surely repay this favor in the future!”","Employee 9527 was worried. “Don’t thank me yet. Our translators are connected to our spaceship’s database—that’s how it does its live translation. But Dreamland is a peculiar place where our signals are unable to reach. Our translators will not work in there.”","“Do you not have offline translators?” Zu An asked.","Employee 9527 was surprised that Zu An knew about that. “Our conglomerate has offline translators, but they are very expensive. Information is the most valuable commodity in the Myriad Worlds, and the number of civilizations and languages in the Myriad Worlds is as many as the stars in the sky. Offline translators can only cover some of the mainstream languages, and even so, the information they contain is already colossal.","“You’ll have to trade for one with resources, as you don’t have any credit points yet. What do you plan to use for the trade? I’ll apply for an offline translator for you right now, but the processing time for valuable commodities tends to take longer. It’ll be best if you can find something comparable for the exchange before my superiors process the request.”","He quickly took his leave afterward.","Zu An fell into deep thought. What do I have that can interest the Universal Conglomerate? They will be interested in the Wonderpoint World, but I can’t use that for the trade. They should be interested in an immortal medicine too, but...","While he was deep in thought, he heard knocks on his door.","“Who is it?”","“I heard there’s a new guest on the ship, so I came here to greet you.” It was a feminine voice that sounded sweet and energetic even through the door.","Zu An’s recent experiences left him in no mood to philander. He wanted to turn the other party down, when it suddenly occurred to him that the other party was speaking his world’s language. Thus, he opened the door and saw a beautiful woman dressed in red standing outside.","Even Zu An had to concede that the other party was truly gorgeous. Few in the Cultivation World could rival her looks.","The woman’s eyes lit up upon seeing Zu An. “You look dashing. Completely unlike the others.”","Zu An was speechless.","He couldn’t agree with her lest he unknowingly offend the other guests. “Miss, are you a passenger too? Why didn’t I see you at the bar earlier?”","The red-robed woman pouted. “A glance at those fellows is enough to make me lose my appetite for three days. There’s no way I would share a space with them.”","Zu An thought about the people he had met in the bar. The black-cloaked old woman was hideous, and the wheelchair-bound old man was disfigured. The only one who looked normal was the person with translucent skin but balding hair.","“I am Firework. What’s your name?” The red-robed woman suddenly looked at Zu An with widened eyes, her black, curly eyebrows fluttered in place.","“You’re indeed as beautiful as fireworks. I'm Zu An,” Zu An replied. It felt pleasant to talk to a beautiful woman.","“You’re good-looking and have a glib tongue. The only thing you’re lacking is a good name.” The red-robed woman harrumphed. “Do you intend to continue chatting with me here? Aren’t you going to invite me in for a seat?”","“That might not be appropriate.”","“What’s up with all these useless rules? I just want a place to sit down so that we can converse.”","It would be impolite for Zu An to turn her down when she had already said as much, so he invited her into his room while remaining vigilant. Someone who could board this spaceship was unlikely to be naive. She could be plotting something.","“Is this your world’s design aesthetic? I see beauty principles being applied everywhere. When do you plan to bring me over for a tour?” The red-robed woman looked at the room’s layout and nodded in approval.","Zu An was using his room in Mount Yuquan’s residence. He replied with a smile, “Could you be a worshiper of the Deity of Love and Beauty?”","The red-robed woman blinked. “Isn’t it rude to ask about a woman’s faith right away? But since you’re so good-looking, I shall make an exception and answer your question. Yes, I worship the Deity of Love and Beauty, and your appearance fulfills the requirement to be a worshiper, too. Would you like to join my faith?”","Zu An was speechless. He hadn’t expected the woman to ask him to change his faith right away.","He coughed softly. “I heard the Deity of Love and Beauty has already passed away.”","This was a good chance to fish for some information."]},{"number":2761,"title":"Chapter 2761: Chapter 2713: Doubtful Intent","paragraphs":["“Who says she’s dead? She just hasn’t shown herself for many years.” The red-robed woman harrumphed. “Besides, love and beauty will persist even if she passes away. It only means that there’s a chance for worshipers like us to become a universal deity.”","Zu An nodded. By now, he understood that every universal deity represented a different path. The daos had existed before the universal deities came into being; the latter merely represented the end of their respective paths.","A universal deity’s death merely meant that the highest entity on their respective path had vanished, but the path itself still existed. It was just a question of which worshiper would reach the endpoint first and become the new universal deity.","“So, which universal deity do you worship?” the red-robed woman asked out of curiosity.","“The Deity of Memory,” Zu An replied. The Deity of Chaos and Enigma sure is pitiful. Their worshipers have to pretend to be other universal deities’ worshipers lest they get pummeled.","The red-robed woman immediately became vigilant. “I forbid you from recording my ugly sides.”","“Didn’t you say we’re friends? I wouldn’t record a friend’s ugly sides,” Zu An replied with a smile.","The red-robed woman finally smiled. “You’re a decent lad. You’re much more interesting than those companions of yours.”","Zu An knew she was referring to other Deity of Memory worshipers. Worried that he would give himself away if this conversation persisted, he changed the topic and asked, “How do you know my world’s language?”","Employee 9527 had mentioned that only he had the translator because he was in charge of these guests. The guests were relying on their own methods to communicate. The wheelchair bound old man and the black-robed old woman didn’t understand his language, but after seeing how weak he was, they couldn't be bothered to learn.","“Fluttering Baldie taught me,” the red-robed woman replied with a grin. Her eyes were curved into crescents, making her look exceptionally beautiful.","Zu An was confused.","“You dumbo. It’s that translucent being.” Firework put her hands on her waist and harrumphed.","“Is that your nickname for him?”","“That’s his own name!”","Zu An nearly burst into laughter. He wouldn’t have expected that balding translucent fellow to have such a name. But again, it wasn't long ago that he'd met ‘Unblind Zuoqiu’ too. People in the Myriad Worlds weren’t particular about their names. Names like ‘Firework’ appeared to be the convention.","“Does he know a lot of languages?” Zu An remembered how the other party had conversed with him through telepathy, looking extremely enigmatic.","“Of course! He’s a Deity of Knowledge worshiper, pursuing all knowledge and wisdom. Fluttering Baldie specializes in languages. It’s not just limited to your world; there is practically no language he doesn’t know in the Myriad Worlds.” Firework assessed Zu An’s room layout as she replied.","Zu An was surprised. He hadn’t expected the balding middle-aged man to be so formidable. Employee 9527 had just told him that the Universal Conglomerate’s translator only supported the languages of mainstream civilizations, but the balding middle-aged man knew all kinds of remote languages!","He remarked, “Brother Baldie is incredible.”","“He’s not that amazing.” Firework casually sat on a table and shook her legs. “The hair of the Deity of Knowledge’s worshipers becomes sparser as they advance their cultivation. Knowledge and wisdom are highly demanding on brain power, so they need to channel every bit of their energy to support their brain. Hair follicles, which compete for nutrition, are useless to them.”","Zu An was speechless. No wonder he looks like those 996 programmers.","“You should have noticed the circle of hair around his head. He hasn’t reached the highest level. You have to tread carefully if you encounter a Deity of Knowledge worshiper with no hair. You won’t be a match for them,” Firework warned.","Zu An nodded as he took her reminder to heart. He remembered his earlier quandary and asked, “May I know how you convinced him to teach you our language? Do worshipers of the Deity of Knowledge seek to sow the seeds of wisdom and knowledge?”","“That’s impossible. Why don’t you get that cripple and old hag to ask him and see if he teaches them? The Deity of Knowledge’s worshipers are the stingiest people you’ll ever know. Whomever knows more gets to advance, so why would they go around spreading knowledge?” Firework puffed up her chest gleefully. “He taught me because I’m adorable and beautiful. No one across the universes doesn’t appreciate beauty. That’s why I’m advising you to embrace the Deity of Love and Beauty.”","Zu An was stunned. How am I supposed to learn that? Fluttering Baldie might have a peculiar appearance, but based on our previous encounter, he’s clearly a man. There’s no way he would be seduced by me. It doesn’t matter how handsome I am.","“Do you know the other two’s background? They don’t look easy to get along with.” Zu An recalled the animosity emanated by the other two, particularly the wheelchair-bound old man. He figured that he needed to be guarded against them.","Employee 9527 couldn’t go against his professionalism and privately reveal other guests’ personal information. It was fortunate that Zu An had bumped into this red-robed woman.","“That old hag is revolting . She is the very antithesis of our Love and Beauty Dao. I can’t be bothered to comprehend someone as disgusting as that. She probably specializes in poison, and those pustules are probably the side effects from dabbling with poisons.” Firework looked so disgusted that it looked as if she would puke if she said a single word more.","“As for that cripple, he’s probably Deity of Annihilation worshiper. He gives off an air of desolation as if he’s going to destroy the world. Those people are lunatics.” Firework shook her head. “There are so many beautiful things and people in the world, yet they want to destroy everything. Ridiculous!”","She turned to Zu An and said, “I heard you offended him. You’re dead meat. The Deity of Annihilation’s worshipers are vindictive. It might be inconvenient for him to make a move against you on the Universal Conglomerate’s spaceship, but he might go after you as soon as you move from here. But again, Annihilation worshipers don’t follow common sense. He might just find a chance to assault you on the spaceship. You should tread carefully.”","Zu An’s heart was chilled, but having weathered many storms, he didn’t fluster. He continued calmly, “This isn't my first time crossing paths with an Annihilation worshiper. He can come at me if he wants to.”","Firework clapped. Her eyes twinkled in glee. “Such manliness! I love it!”","Zu An was speechless.","Had it been another man, he would have been seduced by her beauty and incredible acting skills, but he'd dealt with his fair share of demonesses and temptresses. He could tell that she was putting on an act right now. Even if she was a Deity of Love and Beauty worshiper, there was no way she would treat him so well just because he was good-looking.","Firework suddenly added, “It’s too dangerous to make an enemy out of an Annihilation worshiper. It’d be best if you can resolve your grudge in advance. I heard that cripple is just jealous of your Wonderpoint World. Why don’t I talk to him on your behalf and tell him the way to obtain a Wonderpoint World, so he can give up on it?”","Zu An scoffed on the inside. So you’re after my Wonderpoint World. Thus, he feigned ignorance and asked, “Is a Wonderpoint World very special? Don’t the rest of you have one too?”","Awkwardness flickered across Firework’s face. “It is indeed special. Wonderpoint Worlds have many spatial rifts that allow them to swiftly connect to lost worlds. Every lost world is a fortuitous encounter. Aside from that, Wonderpoint Worlds are also absolutely safe. It is impossible to breach a Wonderpoint World without its master’s permission. That cripple wouldn’t have been able to get to you, but now that you have left your turf, it’s a different story.”"]},{"number":2762,"title":"Chapter 2762: Chapter 2714: Cross-dressing","paragraphs":["Zu An’s heart shuddered. This is indeed an underlying threat. “If a Wonderpoint World’s master is killed outside, can the murderer claim possession of the Wonderpoint World?”","Firework pondered about it before replying, “That will depend on where its master kept the World Law Beacon. If he carries it around with him, his enemy can steal and take over the Wonderpoint World. Most people wouldn’t dare target a Wonderpoint World’s master, as most of them are powerful experts, but your situation is peculiar...”","“Because I’m weak?” Zu An replied calmly as if he wasn’t speaking about himself.","“You are indeed weaker compared to other known Wonderpoint Worlds’ masters, but as a Wonderpoint World’s master, you are bound to harness tremendous luck and special abilities. That cripple won’t be able to get you that easily,” Firework consoled him.","“Aren’t you worried about offending him by divulging this information to me?” Zu An asked out of curiosity.","“You look better than him. As a Love and Beauty worshiper, it goes without saying that I ought to help you.” Firework smiled with twinkling eyes.","“Do you have more information on him?” Zu An figured Firework was after his Wonderpoint World as well.","“I heard he’s a renowned villain in one of the galaxies. He has committed many evil deeds, including theft, arson, and genocide. I abhor people who destroy beautiful things in the world.” Firework harrumphed. “He has three sworn siblings who are Annihilation worshipers too. You should be glad they failed to obtain Dreamland’s invitation letters, or else you wouldn’t have stood a chance against all four of them.”","“Do you know what abilities he has?” Zu An asked.","Firework shook her head. “I only know that he specializes in flames. Most Annihilation worshipers are such experts, as flame is the most optimal tool for destruction. I’m not sure about his other abilities. Most experts are extremely secretive about their abilities lest others curb them. Only those in the same galaxy might know a thing or two.”","Zu An nodded. Lucky it’s not my first time encountering an Annihilation worshiper, so I won’t be clueless if we come to blows.","“Why is Miss Firework going to Dreamland?”","“Because it’s fun. It only opens once in a thousand years. It’s interesting just thinking about it.”","Zu An hesitantly asked, “I heard most people who entered Dreamland in its last few openings never left it.”","“Who would make things difficult for an adorable beauty like me?” Firework put up a ‘V’ sign beside her face. She did look adorable. “Besides, won’t you protect me if something happens?”","Zu An smiled. “I’ll do my best to protect you since we’re friends, but I fear I might not be strong enough to help you when the moment comes.”","“Don’t be disheartened. I believe you’ll do fine. I have met many people, but few are able to remain composed in the face of danger like you. I believe you'll be able to deal with whatever comes your way.” Firework patted his shoulder.","“But I’m facing a quandary now...” Zu An summarized his communication issue.","“And here I was wondering what could have troubled you. That’s easy. I can just ask Fluttering Baldie to teach you,” Firework replied with a chuckle. She grabbed Zu An’s hand and led him outside. “He's much more useful than the Universal Conglomerate’s offline translators. Their translators don’t even cover remote languages.”","Zu An eyed the other party’s hand. It was very smooth, but it felt inappropriate for her to be holding his hand when they had only just met.","Firework brought him to Fluttering Baldie’s room and knocked on the door.","“Who is it?” Fluttering Baldie’s wary voice echoed from within.","“Open up, Baldie. It’s me,” Firework said.","Zu An was baffled. In our world, it would have been extremely rude to call someone a baldie, even if he is truly a baldie. But then again, Knowledge’s worshipers gradually lose their hair as they gain more knowledge. It could instead be flattering to call them that.","The door soon opened, and the balding middle-aged man excitedly rushed out. “Miss Firework, what brings you here so late at night...”","He swiftly noticed Zu An and their linked hands. His face twitched. “What’s he doing here?”","“We’re here to ask a favor. Can you teach him the languages of other worlds?” Firework asked with a smile. She emanated a youthful aura that made it hard to reject her.","Fluttering Baldie’s face flickered. A while later, he murmured, “I refuse.”","Firework was taken aback. “Why?”","Fluttering Baldie turned around and walked away from the door. “I’ll only teach you.”","The door slammed closed behind him.","Firework and Zu An were both speechless.","As Firework followed Zu An back to his room, she murmured in bewilderment, “This is weird. Fluttering Baldie was quite friendly when I talked to him earlier. Why is he suddenly so hostile?”","Zu An lifted their joined hands. “Could this be the reason?”","Firework was perplexed. “What’s wrong with me holding your hand? You’re beautiful; you conform to the standards of our Deity of Love and Beauty. I wouldn’t have held anyone else’s hand.”","“Could Fluttering Baldie be jealous?” Zu An couldn’t tell if Firework was just innocent, or if all Love and Beauty worshipers were so thick-headed.","“Jealous?” Firework was confused. “We aren’t lovers. Why is he getting jealous?”","Zu An retracted his hand, not knowing how to explain it to her.","Firework didn’t dwell on the matter. She settled down on a chair and rested her head on her hands. “This is troublesome. Let me see if there are other solutions.”","Zu An eyed her clothes. “Actually, I have an idea.”","“Oh?” Firework was surprised to hear that. Even I’m at a loss, but this fellow has an idea? Are masters of Wonderpoint Worlds that resourceful?","Zu An hesitantly asked, “Miss, can you lend me a set of your clothes?”","Firework was stunned. Her fair complexion swiftly reddened, and she exclaimed, “What are you trying to do?”","You have successfully trolled Firework for +110... +110... +110...","Zu An knew his request sounded perverted, so he hurriedly explained, “Please don’t misunderstand. Fluttering Baldie mentioned earlier that he’s only willing to teach you, so I was thinking of wearing your clothes to impersonate you.”","Firework rolled her eyes. “Are you taking me or Fluttering Baldie for a fool? Do you think you can impersonate me just by wearing my clothes?”","“I have an ability that allows me to disguise myself as women, but I need their clothes,” Zu An replied awkwardly.","Firework’s eyes lit up. “You have such an ability?”","She would have never been willing to give her clothes to a man whom she had just become acquainted with, but Zu An’s ability piqued her interest so much that she reached into her spatial storage and passed him a set of her clothes. She was curious to see how he would accomplish that feat.","“Don’t blame me for turning against you if you dare fool me!” As she passed her dress over, Firework’s face reddened.","Zu An nodded as he took out Pin Ru’s Wardrobe. To Firework’s bewilderment, he placed her dress into the wardrobe. He considered asking her to excuse herself for a while, but after some thought, he decided to just step into the wardrobe to change his clothes. “This wardrobe is made out of some special material...”","Firework was assessing the wardrobe when the doors suddenly opened. When she saw someone identical to her walking out, her eyes nearly popped out."]},{"number":2763,"title":"Chapter 2763: Chapter 2715: Warning","paragraphs":["“Who are you?” Firework was taken aback.","“I am Zu An,” Zu An replied with a smile.","Firework felt chills running down her spine. “Your voice...”","Zu An's voice remained the same despite having disguised himself as Firework using Pin Ru’s Wardrobe. But he took out the Kawaii Waifu Voice Changer and called a staff member over.","“Miss Firework, is there anything you need?” the attendant respectfully bowed.","Firework was baffled. She wasn’t the one who'd called the staff member over. After the staff member was dismissed, she examined the item in Zu An’s hand and asked, “Is this a voice changer?”","“You can say so,” Zu An replied sweetly.","Firework was baffled. It was the same voice as hers! She snatched the voice changer over and studied it. “But the voice isn’t coming from the machine.”","“It’s coming from my throat,” Zu An replied with a smile.","Firework walked over and placed a finger on his throat. “Huh? I don’t see a voice changer here.”","They were so close that Zu An could smell her fragrance. He instinctively took a step back before replying, “This is my voice now.”","Firework’s eyes flickered as she tried to make sense of the situation. “Your ability requires you to first fool a person with that voice changer before it can take effect, right?”","“You’re sharp-witted,” Zu An complimented her. He didn’t think there was a need to conceal this piece of information.","“That’s an interesting ability.” Firework scrutinized Zu An from head to toe, but she couldn’t find anything that could give him away. “I've seen similar abilities, but it’s usually not too difficult to see through them upon close inspection. But you look as if you were carved from the same mold as me!”","Curious, she first squeezed his chest before attempting to lift his skirt to inspect beneath.","Horrified, Zu An hurriedly backed off while holding his skirt down. “What are you doing?”","“I’m checking if you've turned into a woman.”","Zu An was speechless. This woman knows no shame.","Not wanting to dwell on this topic, he asked, “Do you think Fluttering Baldie will teach me if I ask him in my current state?”","“Of course. You’re sporting the look of an unrivaled cosmic beauty right there! How can he possibly reject you?” Firework gleefully harrumphed.","“Let me give it a try.” Zu An wanted to dive into it, since the journey wouldn’t take too long.","“Hold on,” Firework suddenly stopped him with a frown. “You aren’t planning to do anything weird with that baldie, are you?”","Zu An rolled his eyes in annoyance. “I'm not that perverted.”","“Tsk! I can tell from your demeanor that this is far from your first time cosplaying as a woman. If you aren’t a pervert, no one else is.” Firework clicked her tongue.","Zu An was stunned.","“This won’t do. Just thinking about it sends a shudder down my spine. I can’t let you sully my reputation.” Firework crossed her arms as if overwhelmed by goosebumps. She passed him a pendant. “Wear this.”","“What is it?” Zu An asked as he received the pendant.","“Think of it as a camera. Ah, it's similar to your world’s projection mirrors. It allows me to see what’s happening on your side, lest you use my appearance to do something perverted with that baldie.” Firework’s vibrant, subtle expressions fully showcased her youthful cuteness.","Zu An wanted to turn down her request, but he thought it would be ungrateful of him to do so. Besides, there was no way he would do anything with that baldie, so he had no qualms letting her watch their interactions. So, he wore the pendant around his neck.","The sharp-eyed Firework remarked, “Oh? You’re already wearing another pendant. Let me take it for you lest that baldie notice something.”","Without waiting for Zu An’s answer, her hand swiped for his pendant.","The vigilant Zu An dodged her hand by turning sideward. “Don’t worry about it. I’ll just put it in my clothes.”","He tucked the pendant under the dress. How can I entrust the pendant to someone else when the Jing Teng sisters are in there?","Firework was surprised. “You’re stronger than I thought.”","Even though she hadn’t gone all out earlier, her movements were so fluid that most people would have fallen for it. Yet Zu An had avoided her swipe with astounding ease. Such skills could only be honed by weathering many life-and-death encounters.","That made her smile deepen. Looks like I've put my bet on the right person this time. That cripple is going to suffer a huge setback.","“It’s only because you went easy on me.” Zu An smiled. “I’ll be heading over now.”","Firework waved her hand. “Go ahead. I’ll wait for you here.”","Zu An felt uncomfortable leaving a stranger alone in his room, but on second thought, even though this room was styled identically to Mount Yuquan’s residence, it didn’t contain any of his possessions. There were no secrets to be leaked in this room, so he decided to leave her be.","He soon arrived outside Fluttering Baldie’s room. He knocked on the door and was met with an impatient voice asking, “Who is it?”","“It’s me~” Zu An was amazed by how sweet Firework's voice was.","The door swiftly opened. The sight of Firework brought a smile to Fluttering Baldie’s face, but he quickly remembered something and scanned his surroundings.","“I didn’t bring that person with me.” Zu An knew what he was searching for.","“That’s good.” Fluttering Baldie’s smile deepened. “Miss, what brings you here?”","“You said you weren’t willing to teach that man, so I came back alone to learn by myself.” Firework’s voice was so sweet and cutesy that Zu An was getting goosebumps from hearing himself speak. Hmph! I’ll tolerate it for the sake of learning other languages!","Fluttering Baldie was perplexed. “I thought you weren’t interested, little sister Firework?”","“Can’t I change my mind? Are you going to teach me or not?” Zu An crossed his arms coyly.","Meanwhile, Firework watched everything through her screen. She was so amused that she rolled around on Zu An's bed. I must record this piece of dark history and use it against that fellow in the future. What fun!","Fluttering Baldie was mesmerized by the two massive volumes propped up by Zu An’s crossed arms. “I’ll teach you. I’ll teach you.” He led Zu An into his room and closed the door.","Zu An’s heart shuddered. I won’t let myself be humiliated if this fellow tries anything, even if I don’t learn any languages at all.","Firework lay on Zu An’s bed as she kicked her legs in midair. “Should I help Zu An if Fluttering Baldie tries to take advantage of him?”","She thought it would be interesting to see two men getting steamy, but at the same time, she would feel as if she was also being taken advantage of, since Zu An was disguised as her.","Zu An surveyed Fluttering Baldie’s room. It could hardly be called a room; it felt as if he was standing in the middle of space with brilliant stars around him. He could even clearly see several galaxies in the distance.","Fluttering Baldie noticed her expression and smirked in glee. “Knowledge worshipers have already explored most worlds. Only the boundless universes are worth further exploration.”","Zu An took this chance to shower him with compliments before requesting him to teach him other languages once more.","But Fluttering Baldie replied, “Miss Firework, I hope you won’t think I was being stingy earlier. Further association with that man could put me at risk of danger. I heard Fire Knight contacting his companions using a remote language. They will soon make a move. That lad isn’t even a match for Fire Knight alone; he won’t stand any chance when Fire Knight’s companions arrive. If you continue hanging out with him, you'll also be implicated.”"]},{"number":2764,"title":"Chapter 2764: Chapter 2716: Crash?","paragraphs":["That fellow is called some knight despite being wheelchair bound? That has to be a joke, right? Zu An retorted in his mind. Or is his wheelchair his mount?","“When do they plan to make a move?” Zu An asked.","“Tomorrow.” Fluttering Baldie puffed out his chest. He was proud that he could answer the beauty’s question.","Zu An was confused. “But I... Cough cough , that newcomer is still on the Universal Conglomerate’s spaceship. Does Flame Knight intend to make an enemy out of the Universal Conglomerate?”","“Who says they're going to attack the spaceship? Flame Knight is going to sneak his comrades in and quietly get rid of that fellow. The Universal Conglomerate won’t be able to do a thing without evidence,” Fluttering Baldie said. “Not to mention Dreamland implicitly allows others to steal their invitation letters. That Zu An or whatever only has his weakness to blame.”","Zu An frowned. He felt that something was amiss. There’s no need for Flame Knight to call his companions over just to deal with me. Could he be a surprisingly cowardly person despite his arrogant attitude?","Fluttering Baldie reined in his thoughts and said, “Let’s forget about that fellow and talk about languages. Miss, what languages do you know?”","The only language I know other than the Cultivation World’s language is the monster language...","He risked exposing his identity if he said that, but he, as Firework, couldn’t say that he didn’t know any languages at all. A thought suddenly popped into his mind and he said, “I know Chinese, English, Japanese, Korean...”","Fluttering Baldie was merely asking that question in passing, but Zu An’s answer shocked him. “Miss Firework, you’re well-learned! I've never heard about those languages before. Can you try speaking a sentence or two for me?”","Firework perked herself up. This fellow is more mysterious than I thought.","“(Chinese) Ni hao...”","“(English): Hello world...”","“(Japanese) Yamete kudasai...”","“(Korean) Shibal[1]...”","Fluttering Baldie’s eyes lit up. “Those are indeed new languages! May I know if those words all mean the same thing?”","“You could say so.” Zu An only knew those words from watching clips. He was worried his ignorance would show if Fluttering Baldie continued dwelling on the matter, so he grumbled, “Aren’t you supposed to be teaching me? Why am I teaching you instead?”","He was relieved that Fluttering Baldie, despite being known to be knowledgeable in all languages across the Myriad Worlds, happened not to know those few. It must have been either because Earth wasn't in the known Myriad Worlds, or that it had been countless years since Earth had gone extinct, so no one bothered to pick up their languages.","Both were depressing news to him, though.","When she saw how coyly Zu An was behaving, Firework’s hair stood on end. That crossdresser is faring too well. There’s no way it’s his first time doing this. However, her mind was swiftly drawn back to her face. “Aww, I’m so beautiful!”","Fluttering Baldie was mesmerized. He hurriedly apologized, “Pardon me, I got ahead of myself. Let me teach you first before further consulting you about those languages. So, what languages do you want to learn?”","“The more the better,” Zu An replied without hesitation.","Fluttering Baldie’s eyes lit up. “I’m sure Knowledge’s brilliance will shine on someone as studious as Miss Firework.”","“Are those languages easy to learn? How long will it take?”","“Of course they are! There’s nothing more interesting in the world than learning languages,” Fluttering Baldie replied with a smile. “For starters, we’ll start with the hundred mainstream languages, followed by the ten thousand common languages in powerful universes. Then, we’ll move on to the billions of languages used by the more famous galaxies...”","“Stop, stop! Why are there so many languages?” Zu An was horrified.","“That’s not a lot in the context of the Myriad Worlds. Every universe has many galaxies, and every galaxy has many planets. There are more civilizations in the Myriad Worlds than you can count. A billion languages isn’t that many.”","Zu An frowned. “That sounds fair. How long will it take for me to learn the hundred mainstream languages?”","Fluttering Baldie continued, “The hundred mainstream languages have been localized into countless more dialects. Our most talented Knowledge worshiper took 23 years to learn them. I’m embarrassed to say I’m lacking; it took me 26 years to learn them, putting me in third place in history. Miss Firework, I believe that you won’t fare any worse than me, given your wits.”","Zu An was stunned. “...You’re saying 26 years is already fast?”","“Of course it is! 26 years is nothing but a snap of the fingers to the universe,” Fluttering Baldie replied with a smile. “Besides, Miss Firework, when I’m with you, time can only pass too fast.”","Firework immediately sat up. “How disgusting!” She stared nervously at the video. If you dare let that baldie take advantage of you, I’ll immediately run over and expose you!","To her relief, Zu An stood up and said, “I’m feeling tired. I’ll learn another day.”","You must be joking with me! 26 years? I don’t have that much time! I guess I’ll have to strike a deal with Employee 9527.","Fluttering Baldie anxiously tried to stop him. “If it’s too much trouble, Miss Firework, there’s a simpler way you can learn the languages within a short time.”","“What is it?” Zu An was taken aback.","“We can resonate our brain waves. That’ll allow you to access my knowledge and learn the Myriad World’s languages,” Fluttering Baldie said.","“Forget it.” Zu An frowned. This kind of resonance was similar to mental sex. He still remembered the intense stimulation he'd felt when he joined his soul with Jiang Luofu’s and Yan Xuehen’s. Putting aside the fact that it would reveal his identity and secrets, there was no way he could tolerate having this kind of interaction with another man.","Fluttering Baldie looked at her departing silhouette as he took a deep whiff of her lingering fragrance. His eyes were downcast with melancholy. I was too anxious. I hope Miss Firework doesn’t mistake me for a pervert.","As soon as Zu An returned to his room, Firework harrumphed. “You should be glad you didn’t accept that fellow’s offer, or else you’d never hear the end of me!”","Zu An took off the dress and reverted to his original appearance. “No wonder you rejected his offer. There’s no easy way to learn those languages.”","Firework chuckled under her hand. “You’re stuck in a mental rut. Why do you think those are the only options? Do you think it took me that long to learn your language?”","“That’s right. How did you learn our language so quickly?” Zu An belatedly recalled this detail.","“Knowledge worshipers can fuse their knowledge into a page. You just have to burn that page with your spiritual energy or ki, and you can temporarily acquire the relevant knowledge. All you have to do to resolve your problem is convince him to give you a page about languages, right?” Firework rolled her eyes.","Zu An was overjoyed to hear that. “Why didn’t that baldie mention it?”","“Because you prattled on about learning those languages. To a Knowledge worshiper, such a shortcut isn’t considered learning. I didn’t expect the two of you to be so dumb as to cause such a huge misunderstanding,” Firework huffed impatiently.","Zu An laughed sheepishly. “I guess I’ll have to find another time to approach him.”","“You owe me one for using my identity.” Firework hurled her fist playfully.","“Of course. I’m grateful for your help.” Zu An bowed deeply.","Firework’s eyes curled into twinkling crescents. “That’s more like it. You'd better not turn me down when I ask you for help.”","Zu An was about to answer when their surroundings abruptly shook. Caught off guard, both of them lost their balance and fell together. A beautiful woman was in his arms, but Zu An wasn’t in the mood to enjoy it. “What happened?”","Firework’s expression looked grim as well. “Did the spaceship bump into something? This is bad! Are we going to crash?”","1. The joke here is that the latter two mean something completely different. 'Yamete kudasai' is formal Japanese for 'please stop', but in this context it probably refers to the phrase being used in a lewd context. Meanwhile, 'shibal' in Korean is a curse word roughly equivalent to 'fuck', so he's basically doing the joke of teaching someone the wrong word in a foreign language so they'll embarrass themselves. -Editor Felis ☜"]},{"number":2765,"title":"Chapter 2765: Chapter 2717: Assault","paragraphs":["Zu An and Firework dashed out of the room and saw the previously moving scenery outside come to a halt. The spaceship had stopped moving.","When Zu An first boarded the spaceship, Employee 9527 had triggered the self-destruction sequence for the temporary world before the spaceship drove off into a series of spatial leaps. Iridescent lights had colored the scenery outside the window along the way, looking as if countless shooting stars were passing by. There was no speed gauge, but Zu An could sense just how fast the spaceship was moving then.","But everything had now come to a halt. This was Zu An’s first inter-universe travel, but he could tell something huge had happened.","You have successfully trolled Fluttering Baldie for +444... +444... +444...","Zu An turned around and saw Fluttering Baldie had left his room too and was glaring at him. The latter must have witnessed him leaving the same room as Firework and gotten jealous.","A warning siren blared, as red lights flickered brightly in the corridors.","“Enemy attack! Enemy attack! All troops are to make their way to the warehouse!”","Firework was amused by the ongoing events. “Ha. Someone dares to touch the Universal Conglomerate’s spaceship. Interesting.”","Fluttering Baldie walked over and said, “Miss Firework, you should return to your room. It’s dangerous out here.”","Firework was unfazed. “It’s much more interesting out here. Why should I return to my room? You can return to your room if you’re afraid.”","Fluttering Baldie’s transparent face visibly reddened.","Zu An was speechless. Isn’t he a Knowledge worshiper? Why can’t he see past love? But on second thought, it could be because they had devoted themselves to academics that they were vulnerable to matters of the heart.","“Should we watch the commotion?” Firework asked Zu An with an excited gleam in her eyes.","“Sure.” This was a good opportunity for Zu An to see how others fought in the Myriad Worlds.","Firework smiled sweetly as she dragged Zu An toward the warehouse.","Fluttering Baldie looked like a pitiful dog abandoned by its owner. I know Love and Beauty worshipers are drawn to beautiful things, but I’m known to be dashing among Knowledge worshipers. Many of my peers are jealous of my fluttering hair.","You have successfully trolled Fluttering Baldie for +55... +55... +55...","Firework led Zu An to an elevated platform near the warehouse. In the distance, they saw a hole in the spaceship’s wall.","Although calling it a hole wasn't quite the most accurate, as it resembled a wormhole more. All sorts of monsters rushed out from the wormhole and charged at anyone in sight. Many staff members of the Universal Conglomerate were already collapsed in a pool of blood, while those who had just arrived were busy fighting against the monsters.","The monsters came in all shapes and sizes, but none of them surprised Zu An. All of them conformed to the traits of the countless monsters he had seen in Baopu’s tomb and the Monster World. What he was more interested in was the Universal Conglomerate’s fighting style.","Employee 9527 was clashing with the largest monster using a Star Wars-esque lightsaber.","The monster had the upper body of a beautiful, middle-aged woman. Her hair was tied into a graceful bun, and her makeup looked seductive. Her lower body, however, was that of a giant octopus with countless tentacles that flew toward Employee 9527.","Employee 9527, with his outstanding swordsmanship, could slice off a tentacle with each slash of his lightsaber, but the octopus lady would just regenerate them, rendering his efforts futile.","The spaceship’s staff members were also busy dealing with the other monsters. They wielded guns that shot out red beams. Any monsters struck by the red beams were left with a bloodied hole in their body.","Zu An figured the Universal Conglomerate was more inclined toward the technological side.","These laser beams are similar to sword ki but faster.","He noticed that some of the monsters moved astonishingly fast, evading the laser beams with all kinds of maneuvers before pouncing on the staff members and tearing them into shreds.","But then again, the laser beams lack the flexibility of sword ki and have a predictable trajectory.","“Aren’t we going to help them?” Zu An couldn’t bear seeing so many staff members dying.","“Isn’t it more fun to watch the show? Fighting and breaking out into a sweat isn’t beautiful,” Firework replied with a smile.","Zu An was stunned.","In the end, he still intervened when a young staff member was on the verge of being bitten to death by the monsters. He first exerted a suction force to drag the staff member away from the monster before unleashing sword ki to burst that monster’s head.","“T-t-thank... you...” The staff member was so gripped by fear that he stuttered.","“Take care of yourself.” Zu An dragged the staff member aside before engaging other monsters.","Firework stomped her feet in frustration. “Doesn’t that fellow know that he’s giving away his precious information?”","A black flash of lightning suddenly surged out of the wormhole and shot straight toward Zu An’s back.","“Be careful!” Firework shouted, but the enemy was so fast that her words failed to reach Zu An before the attack landed.","Years of dancing with danger had honed Zu An’s instincts. Despite not seeing anything, he performed a sideward instantaneous movement that allowed him to dodge that fatal attack.","Pah!","The black flash of lightning slowed down, revealing himself to be a bird-headed, human-bodied monster. His clothes appeared to be woven out of feathers, making him resemble an owl. He was wielding a silver hook that struck the spaceship’s floor after missing Zu An, ripping open a huge hole.","Zu An had noticed that the spaceship was made out of a special alloy comparable to the Cultivation World’s immortal-grade weapon materials. On top of that, it was inscribed with technological runes and layered with magic formations, granting it amazing defensive prowess. He himself would have struggled to breach it.","And yet, the birdman tore it apart as easily as ripping paper in half.","The birdman was enraged at having his attack foiled. He morphed back into a black surge of lightning to continue attacking Zu An.","Zu An didn’t dare let his guard down. He performed a series of instantaneous movements to dodge the birdman’s attacks. He did manage to avoid the attacks, but there were many close shaves where the slightest misstep would have cost him his life.","A resounding laugh echoed. A wall collapsed, and a fatty strutted in. “Number Three, you’re struggling with that brat? Let me do it if you can’t!” As he said those words, he snapped the necks of two staff members.","Meanwhile, the staff members were toppling over from the powerful suction force coming from the hole ripped into the spaceship. Some of them failed to stand their ground and were dragged out into space.","Employee 9527 was enraged. He sliced over a dozen tentacles in a single cut before hurling out a net from his sleeves to trap the octopus lady. Then, he flashed toward the spaceship’s hole, took out a light whip, and rescued his colleagues from the void of space. After that, he tossed a lump of paste at the hole. It swiftly enlarged and mended the hole.","Zu An, who was eyeing the situation with his peripheral vision, was awed by the Universal Conglomerate’s advanced technology.","Just then, the octopus lady screeched, “Stop wasting time, Number Four! I’m at my limit!”","It turned out that the net was contracting around her. It cut into her massive body, causing green blood to seep out.","“Hahaha! It’s all down to me in the end!” The fatty laughed. He sprinted forth, displaying agility that was at odds with his massive physique. He dashed to the octopus lady’s side, pulled out a pair of massive scissors, and cut open the net.","The octopus lady quickly ripped the net off herself. She inspected the lacerations on her body and roared in anger, “I’ll massacre everyone on this spaceship!” Her tentacles swiftly extended and randomly lashed out in all directions. Some of the tentacles flew toward Zu An, too.","Zu An was focused on his fight with the birdman when several tentacles suddenly flew over, while his instantaneous movement happened to be on cooldown."]},{"number":2766,"title":"Chapter 2766: Chapter 2718: We’ll Die Together","paragraphs":["Just as the tentacles were about to coil around Zu An, several red firecrackers suddenly descended upon them, blasting them apart into bloody mist.","Startled, Zu An looked up and saw a red-robed woman smiling brightly at him. He felt moved. Regardless of her motive, she has helped me a lot.","The octopus lady screeched as she hurriedly retracted her tentacles. Those firecrackers were fueled by Firework’s blood essence, so their flame couldn’t be easily put out. They spread toward the octopus lady’s body so quickly that she had to sever her tentacles. To make things worse, she realized she couldn’t regrow them anymore.","“You damned lass!” The octopus lady glared venomously at Firework. She shot a tentacle toward the ceiling and swung herself toward Firework as if she were Tarzan.","“Be careful!” Zu An wanted to help her, but he was stopped by the birdman’s silver claws.","The birdman burst into laughter. “Go easy on that little beauty, second sister. I’ll let her have a taste of my cannon later!”","The octopus lady scoffed, “I’ll laugh if you’re blown up by her firecrackers instead.”","The birdman laughed. “Doesn’t that make it more exciting?”","Firework’s gaze turned cold, though her smile persisted. “Why don’t I give them to you two since you like them so much?” She produced two lit firecrackers and tossed them over.","The birdman was unfazed. “Even your firecrackers look so beautiful.”","He swiped his silver claws at the two firecrackers, but to his shock, the firecracker behind suddenly accelerated and bumped into the one in front, causing an abrupt change in the latter’s trajectory and speed.","He couldn’t react in time, and the firecracker struck his thigh. He screamed in agony. Having seen what happened to the octopus lady, he quickly ripped off his pants and tore off a huge swathe of his flesh. Blood dripped from his leg.","Firework clapped her hand in amusement. “Is that exciting enough for you?”","The birdman’s face twisted in fury. “You bitch! I’ll make you suffer a fate worse than... AH!”","He screamed once more, as Zu An exploited his momentary lapse in judgment to launch an attack. He tried his best to protect his vitals, but he ended up losing an arm in the process.","“Incredible, big brother Zu!” Firework exclaimed with a smile. He has a conscience. At least he knows how to stand up for me.","The octopus lady was startled. This woman still has the energy to chat despite facing our combined onslaught. I can’t underestimate her. “Third brother, quickly subdue that brat so we can deal with this bitch together.”","“Alright.” The birdman clenched his jaw as he quickly regrew his arm.","Zu An was taken aback. These monsters are too tenacious!","In the Cultivation World, cultivators beyond a certain level could regrow their limbs too, but it usually took months of rest. It was inconceivable for anyone to regenerate that quickly there.","“Be careful, big brother Zu. These monsters only die when you destroy their energy cores. You can think of energy cores as the equivalent of your world’s demon cores, and their energy cores are located in different places,” Firework reminded Zu An.","The octopus lady was infuriated. “You talk too much!”","She thrashed her tentacles at Firework, but the latter was somehow able to weave between the gaps of the tentacles as if she were an agile bird. Despite the furious onslaught, none of the attacks were connecting.","This lass is still holding back. I wonder how strong she truly is. I’m lucky she’s still fooling around.","She gave up on capturing Firework, and instead focused on stalling the latter until her allies came over to reinforce her. By then, they could work together to capture the woman.","Number Four isn’t a match for 9527, but he should be able to stall him for the time being. Number Three should be stronger than that brat, but for some reason, not only is he struggling to bring that brat down, he’s even showing signs of losing.","Fortunately, my subordinates have the upper hand over the Universal Conglomerate’s employees. They don’t seem to have staffed this spaceship with many fighters.","Furthermore, our eldest brother hasn’t made a move either.","Employee 9527 angrily roared at the other staff members. “How did these fellows slip in here? Why didn’t our protection system work?”","The Universal Conglomerate’s spaceship was equipped with advanced technology that could detect and destroy enemies from a long distance away, but the defenses had never indicated an enemy presence. They'd only noticed the enemies when the latter were already aboard.","That spelled one possibility—there was a spy among them!","Who could it be? Did the enemy buy off one of our staff members...","Two more people appeared on the platform. It was the old woman with meat lumps on her face and the wheelchair-bound Fire Knight.","“Tsk tsk tsk. What a commotion!” The old woman’s voice sounded more jarring than a crow’s cawing.","“A commotion it is indeed.” Flames flickered eerily in Fire Knight’s eyes.","The old woman turned to Employee 9527 and said, “It seems you aren’t able to take care of this trouble. Should I help out?”","Employee 9527 had also realized that the situation was beyond his control. “The Universal Conglomerate will be grateful to you if you lend a helping hand.”","“I have no interest in the intangible. I’ll help you if you give me what I want,” the old woman coldly demanded.","Employee 9527 hesitated. That’s too valuable. But hearing his comrades’ screams of agony helped him make up his mind quickly. If the monsters get their way, and I lose the spaceship, it’ll be over for me even if I escape with my life. “Fine, I’ll give you what you want.”","“Smart. Heh! There are enough living entities here for me to create my new medicine.” The old woman opened her arms and murmured an incantation. Soon, a black fog gathered around her.","Psh!","Her body suddenly trembled. She looked down and saw a bloodied spear lodged in her chest. She turned her head around in disbelief. Holding the other end of the spear was the wheelchair-bound Fire Knight.","“Why?” the old woman asked in confusion.","“I can’t let you foil my plan, can I?” Fire Knight replied.","The old woman looked at the monsters below and widened her eyes in realization. “I see. They're your subordinates. Very well. Let’s all die together.”","Her body exploded into a thick black fog that swiftly spread into the surroundings."]},{"number":2767,"title":"Chapter 2767: Chapter 2719: Impervious to Poisons","paragraphs":["Zu An was startled. The black-robed old woman had only become terribly disfigured because she dabbled with poisons. A poison released by a dying poison specialist was bound to be extremely potent. Few aboard the spaceship would survive it.","He was about to shout out a reminder when flames suddenly enveloped the old woman, vaporizing the black fog while incinerating her body to ashes.","Fire Knight sneered, “I knew you specialized in poison. Did you think I wouldn’t be on guard against this move?”","Fire was the counter of most poisons, bacterias, and viruses; not to mention his was no ordinary fire.","“All hail our boss!” The fatty, the octopus lady, and the birdman cheered.","Employee 9527 finally understood how these monsters had slipped onto the spaceship. They had a partner onboard! He had treated Fire Knight as a VIP, but the latter trampled over his goodwill in such a manner. That made him incredibly angry. “Fire Knight, do you know the consequences of raiding a Universal Conglomerate spaceship? There will be no place for you in the Myriad Worlds!”","Those words were true. The Universal Conglomerate would obliterate Fire Knight even if he was ten times stronger than he currently was.","Fire Knight burst into laughter. “We Annihilation worshipers are always ready to return to our master’s embrace. Our accomplishments will be worthwhile even if it means we’ll eventually die under the Universal Conglomerate’s vengeance. I shall offer all living beings on this spaceship to our master, so he’ll know how sincere our faith is!”","Zu An’s heart sank. Such fellows are the most troublesome of all. They're so stuck in their beliefs that they don’t consider the pros and cons of their actions.","Firework laughed. “You speak as if you’re a devout believer, but you just covet Zu An’s Wonderpoint World and our invitation letters to Dreamland.”","The others widened their eyes in realization. It belatedly struck them that Fire Knight’s companions didn’t have invitation letters, but if they robbed the spaceship’s passengers, the four of them could head to Dreamland together.","After all, there was no name on Dreamland’s invitation letters.","Fire Knight glared at Firework with flames blazing in his eyes. “You damned lass! You’re the only one I struggle to see through on this spaceship. What’s your background?”","Firework weaved through the octopus lady’s tentacles like a butterfly. “What background could I have? I am merely the most adorable and beautiful lady in the universe.”","The crowd was speechless.","“Hmph! Conceal your identity all you like; it makes no difference to me!” Fire Knight harrumphed.","Fire blazed forth from his wheelchair’s handrest, converging into spears that shot toward Firework.","Firework was able to cope with the octopus lady’s attacks with ease, but Fire Knight’s interference put her in a dangerous position. The fire spears were precisely timed and aimed to seal off her escape. On top of that, she seemed to be fearful of the fire, causing her movement to slow. It seemed to be only a matter of time before she succumbed to the enemies’ onslaught.","A lightsaber suddenly appeared from the side and deflected some of the fire spears. Employee 9527 knocked back the fatty and swung his saber down on Fire Knight. At the same time, he conjured dozens more lightsabers that simultaneously assaulted Fire Knight.","Fire Knight continued to relax in his wheelchair as he spread a fan of fire with a casual wave of his hand. With a single strike, he melted over half of Employee 9527’s lightsabers.","“How’s that possible?” Employee 9527 was startled. He couldn’t believe what was happening.","Zu An frowned as well. Ranking in the top 10,000 of the Universal Conglomerate, Employee 9527 was no weakling. His assessment of Employee 9527 was that the former was no weaker than Fire Knight. It was baffling how one-sided the fight had turned out.","Fire Knight unleashed another wave of fire to knock down the remaining lightsabers. Even the one Employee 9527 held in his hand melted.","Employee 9527 collapsed to the floor, spewing a large mouthful of blood. He glared at Fire Knight with indignant eyes. “You despicable wretch!”","Fire Knight scoffed, “Don’t you think we’d have made thorough preparations before making a move against the Universal Conglomerate? Though I didn’t expect your antidote serum to be so strong as to delay my second sister’s poison for so long.”","The octopus lady snickered. “Do you think I’m so weak as to let you slice so many of my tentacles for free?”","It finally dawned upon Employee 9527 that the octopus lady had intentionally allowed him to hurt her because her poison needed to be catalyzed by her blood. Before he knew it, he had already fallen to her poison.","His complexion turned awful. She thrashed around the battlefield earlier, waving her tentacles everywhere. If I was inflicted with her poison, doesn’t it mean that...","Before he could finish that thought, he heard weapons falling to the ground. The Universal Conglomerate’s staff members collapsed one after another, moaning in pain. The poison had sapped their stamina, rendering them incapable of fighting.","Firework was also stunned. “Crap.” She fell from the sky before she could react.","“You wretch! Not that smug anymore now that the tables have turned, huh? I’ll make you suffer a fate worse than death!” The octopus lady stared at Firework’s beautiful face with jealous eyes as her tentacles shot for the latter. She was going to show Firework the true prowess of her tentacles.","There was suddenly a flash of black light. The birdman flitted over and swiped Firework away. “Big sister, we agreed that this beauty is mine. I can’t let you ruin her before I have a taste.”","But his expression quickly darkened as he realized there was no one in his arms. Firework had been pulled away by a weird suction force coming from Zu An!","Zu An used the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra to pull Firework into his arms, saving her from those two monsters’ demonic claws.","Firework’s face briefly turned red, but she quickly snapped out of it and asked, “Why aren’t you affected by the poison?”","Even experts of her and Employee 9527’s caliber had fallen for the poison, let alone others on the spaceship. It was baffling how this fellow was unfazed.","Zu An was perplexed as well. His unique constitution and the Primordial Origin Sutra made him impervious to poison, but he hadn’t expected this trait to work against the poisons from the experts of the Myriad Worlds, too. The Primordial Origin Sutra is stronger than I thought.","The others on the spaceship were also astounded.","“Boss, that fellow is unfazed by my poison!” the octopus lady exclaimed.","“He has an instantaneous movement ability that allows him to dodge Number Three’s attacks,” the fatty said while waving his scissors.","“He has a skill that allows him to absorb energy and generate a powerful suction force. You must tread carefully around him,” the birdman added.","The trio were slowly forming an encirclement around Zu An. Fire Knight stared at Zu An before he remarked, “I’ve underestimated you, brat.”"]},{"number":2768,"title":"Chapter 2768: Chapter 2720: The Kill","paragraphs":["Thanks to Employee 9527’s translator, Zu An could now understand Fire Knight’s words.","Firework whispered, “Take me away with your instantaneous movement. You aren’t a match for them alone.”","They needed to get to somewhere safe where she could neutralize the poison before they would stand a fighting chance.","Zu An didn’t respond to her. Instead, he eyed the monsters attacking the poisoned staff members. All of the Conglomerate’s staff members had lost their fighting ability, rendering them helpless to the monsters’ assault. It didn’t take long for a couple of them to be torn to shreds.","Zu An’s expression darkened. These staff members had treated him kindly on the journey. He couldn’t just turn a blind eye to their plight.","Golden sword ki suddenly appeared in mid air and impaled the closest monster. The remaining monsters screeched as they fled from the Conglomerate’s staff members to dodge the barrage of sword ki.","Firework was frustrated. “Are you stupid? You can’t save them even if you stay behind! Ugh, it’s too late to escape now!”","There was a good chance they could have escaped from the encirclement if Zu An had employed his instantaneous movement earlier. But now that the four had completed their encirclement, there was no way they could escape anymore!","Zu An calmly replied, “I can’t turn a blind eye to their plight.”","It wasn't out of sheer recklessness that he chose to stay behind. He knew that even if he broke free of the encirclement, he would still be trapped on this spaceship. If they got stranded in bleak space, not only would he be unable to get to Dreamland, but even survival would be an issue.","It would thus be wiser to stay behind and fight back. If he rescued the Conglomerate’s staff members, he could resume his journey to Dreamland.","The Conglomerate’s staff members looked at Zu An with grateful eyes. Had they been in Zu An’s place, they didn’t think they would be able to make the same decision.","Employee 9527 sent a telepathic message over. “I appreciate your goodwill, but you aren’t a match for them. Find an opening to escape to the spaceship’s tail. You’ll find a few escape pods there. Should you escape safely, please report this matter to the Universal Conglomerate. We’ll be thankful to you.” He was strong enough to withstand the poison to relay the message.","Zu An was surprised. He hadn’t expected his kindness to secure him an escape route, though the odds of him being able to take said route were now extremely slim...","Fire Knight harrumphed coldly. “I didn’t expect you to have such useless compassion. You might have obtained a Wonderpoint World by chance, but it’ll just become a stepping stone for me.”","“What does a hideous thing like you know? Our big brother Zu is a great man, unlike despicable scums like you!” Firework argued back despite her earlier grumbling about Zu An’s decision.","Fire Knight’s flames quivered. “You little bitch! I shall show you what true agony is!”","Birdman anxiously interjected, “Boss, you agreed to give her to me.”","The octopus lady harrumphed. “Get lost! I want her as well. I shall stuff her full of my tentacles!” Her tentacles flailed nonstop out of excitement, as if she was imagining something in her mind.","Zu An felt the lady in his arms trembling. I didn’t expect her to get frightened by that.","Birdman roared in anger, “Second sister, the people you've toyed with become big enough to stuff a train in! How am I supposed to play with them after that?”","The octopus lady rolled her eyes. “It’s not my problem that you’re small.”","The birdman was speechless.","Fire Knight angrily smacked the wheelchair and said, “Shut up! Why are you fighting among yourselves when we haven’t dealt with the enemy yet? Capture them first. Second sister, you can have the guy. Third brother, you can have the woman.”","The octopus lady’s eyes lit up. She turned to Zu An and licked her lips with her crimson tongue. “This lad doesn't look too bad either. Deal!”","Zu An was stunned. The birdman was a pervert, but the octopus lady was even worse, preying on both men and women alike. Who knew how many people had been stuffed to death by her? And she’s eyeing me now.","Zu An’s expression turned severe. He was in a grim situation; the four of them were extremely strong. He had no intention of letting anyone pop his ass cherry.","The octopus lady was the first to make a move. She weaved dozens of her tentacles into a net and cast it over Zu An.","“Quick, dodge to the back left, then head toward the back right...” Despite being poisoned, Firework’s combat sense remained. She quickly gave out orders in hopes of creating an escape chance.","But Zu An remained still as the tentacles loomed over him.","Firework was flustered. Is this fellow scared stiff? Why isn’t he dodging? The thought of the miserable plight that would befall her made her face turn cold. If it comes to that, I’ll bring them down with me.","Since she used firecrackers as her weapon, it went without saying that she had some powerful explosives on her for defensive purposes. If those monsters dared to touch her body, she would immediately ignite them.","The only regret she had was that she would be blown apart. Having her body scattered around didn’t align with her sense of aesthetics.","The octopus lady revealed a perverted grin. They're now both in my grasp! To avoid any mishaps, she sprayed a pink venom at the duo.","Fire Knight was baffled. That fellow might not be strong, but there’s no reason for him to surrender without putting up a fight. Why isn’t he fighting back?","His vision suddenly blurred, then pink venom suddenly sprayed all over him. Countless tentacles tightly wrapped around his body as their suction pads relentlessly suckered onto every inch of his skin. Despite his mental fortitude, his mind was shaken up.","Fire Knight was stunned. I've seen how my second sister toys with her prey, but I never thought a day would come when I’d be a victim of that. As he unleashed flames from his body, his anger flared.","The octopus lady screeched in agony as she hurriedly retracted her tentacles, but most of them still ended up charred. Sensing Fire Knight’s rage, she anxiously explained, “Boss, I don’t know what happened. My attacks were aimed at that fellow...”","“Be careful, second sister!” the fatty shouted from some distance away.","He'd seen the brat switching places with their boss at the very last moment, but that wasn't all. The brat proceeded to charge at the octopus lady, but his second sister was too caught up in having attacked their boss to notice that. So, he had to quickly shout a warning.","By the time the octopus lady registered the warning, Zu An was already at her flank. It was too late for her to dodge his subsequent attack. Even so, she wasn’t worried. She would only lose a few tentacles at worst. With her strong regenerative prowess, she would recover right away.","“You rascal! You made me offend our boss! I’m going to stuff you...”","Her body suddenly jolted. All her tentacles fell limp, and she plummeted to the ground.","She was dead."]},{"number":2769,"title":"Chapter 2769: Chapter 2721: Target the Weakness","paragraphs":["Everyone present was baffled by that sight. Just a second ago, the octopus lady had still been extremely smug, only to drop dead right after.","Even Employee 9527 was baffled. He had fought the octopus lady earlier, and even though she wasn’t a match for him, her powerful regeneration made her a troublesome foe to deal with. In the end, he'd even fallen to her poison.","Zu An was clearly weaker than the octopus lady, so how could he instant-kill her?","Did Miss Firework secretly make a move? Did she pretend to fall for the poison?","“Second sister!” the scissors-wielding fatty exclaimed in shock. He rubbed his eyes in disbelief.","The birdman was bewildered. He wasn't on good terms with the octopus lady as the latter often snatched his women, and he had been coveting her position as number two for a while now, but seeing her drop dead all of a sudden still filled him with melancholy.","Only Fire Knight had seen what happened. Zu An had whipped out a pitch-black knife to cut one of the octopus lady’s tentacles. Black runes immediately appeared all over her body, and she died right away despite her tremendous regeneration.","He yelled, “His knife has an instant-kill effect. Avoid it at all costs!”","The other monsters were shocked. They finally understood what had happened.","Zu An sighed. He'd been planning to assassinate the other monsters with the Poisonous Prick, but little had he expected to be seen through right away.","Earlier, he'd swapped positions with Fire Knight right before the octopus lady’s tentacles connected, causing the attacks to fall on Fire Knight instead. At the same time, he'd exploited the octopus lady’s lapse in attention to charge up to her and wound her with the Poisonous Prick.","He had witnessed Employee 9527’s earlier fight with the octopus lady, so he'd known about her tremendous regenerative prowess and that it would be difficult to kill her with ordinary means. Fortunately, his Poisonous Prick happened to curb that.","Let’s see how you regenerate when Poisonous Prick kills you in an instant!","In truth, he hadn’t been certain if it would work out. Perhaps these skills had worked on enemies in the Cultivation World and the Monster World, but they could have fallen short when dealing with even stronger enemies in the Myriad Worlds.","And yet, everything had still turned out fine.","Ideally, Zu An would have assassinated the strongest Fire Knight with the Poisonous Prick, but the latter had unfathomable strength and was enveloped in flames. He doubted he would be able to hurt the latter.","Rather than risk revealing his trump card but failing to achieve anything, he'd decided to take the safer route and eliminate an enemy first.","The octopus lady was the second strongest in the group, and her tentacles were simply too disgusting. Even he was intimidated by them, let alone Firework. The last thing he wanted was for those tentacles to touch his body. It also helped that the octopus lady’s flailing tentacles had been spread throughout the warehouse, making it easier for him to stab her.","Firework stared at the man holding her in astonishment. A smile emerged on her lips, and she remarked, “Big brother, you’re incredible.”","Fire Knight asked with a coarse voice, “How could you have moved me? That’s a skill at the level of a world law! And that sure-kill dagger too! How can someone as weak as you possess so many overpowered skills and treasures? I get it now. I should have expected this much from the master of a Wonderpoint World. No wonder Wonderpoint World masters across the Myriad Worlds are so powerful. Those places are indeed littered with treasures.”","The birdman’s eyes lit up. “Boss, have we struck it rich this time?”","Other Wonderpoint World masters were top-tier powerhouses, whereas this fellow was pathetically weak. While he did have some troublesome skills, those wouldn’t pose a threat once they learned about and guarded against them.","It’s me, not we. If I monopolize his Wonderpoint World, skills, treasures, and weapons, it will only be a matter of time before I reach a level on par with the other powerhouses of the Myriad Worlds! Although Fire Knight would never say those words aloud.","He twisted his wheelchair handle. The sharp spikes at the back of his chair unleashed intense flames, making him look like a blazing sun. The flames first enveloped the warehouse before morphing into floating flowers.","He smiled in satisfaction as he said, “I've sealed off the area. There’s no way he can escape now.”","That was indeed the case, as the surrounding spatial ki had turned viscous. It would be impossible to overcome this seal unless one was stronger than Fire Knight or adept at spatial formations.","“Be careful, big brother. This is a very powerful spatial seal. It’ll greatly diminish the effectiveness of your movement skills and instantaneous movement. You have to take that into account when you fight them,” Firework reminded Zu An.","Zu An nodded. It wasn't his first time encountering such spatial seals, so he wouldn’t make such an elementary mistake.","There was no question these monsters were stronger than him, but strength wasn't the sole determining factor in the outcome of a fight. For instance, oxen were much stronger than lions and tigers, but they were often still hunted down by the latter.","Combat experience, artifacts, abilities, and skills could easily affect the outcome of a battle.","Judging from the earlier clash, Zu An could tell that he wasn't as weak as he thought at first, and the experts of the Myriad Worlds weren’t as strong as he imagined, either. He would struggle against them, but he still had a shot at victory.","“Number Three, Number Four, you two strike together. I’ll control the formation from the side. The battle will be over as soon as he reveals an opening!” Fire Knight ordered the others.","He was a wary person, and he didn’t dare to let his guard down despite being the stronger one here. Despite the storms he had weathered, he'd still been startled by Zu An’s position swap ability and sure-kill dagger. If the latter had more of such artifacts, there was a chance that he would be defeated. It was safer for him to dispatch his underlings first to probe Zu An’s trump cards.","The birdman could tell what their boss was thinking, and the truth was that he was also intimidated by Zu An after witnessing how his second sister had died earlier. However, he didn’t dare to refute his boss in public. So, he racked his brain and sent a telepathic message, “Number Four, our boss’ seal has limited the effectiveness of my movement skills. You’ll take the front later, and I’ll support you from the flank.”","“Okay! Let’s avenge second sister!” The fatty flailed his big scissors as he snipped at Zu An from afar.","Alarmed, Zu An hurriedly dodged to the side. A huge gorge appeared where he'd been standing before, as if invisible scissors had snipped it open.","“Eat my scissors!”","The fatty displayed agility that contrasted with his massive physique, releasing snip after snip at Zu An. The birdman also launched a barrage of claw swipes at Zu An from all directions.","With a flick of his wrist, Zu An whipped out the Tai’e Sword to deflect the attacks. My movement speed has been reduced by around 30%. That makes it much harder to cope with their attacks.","Fire Knight frowned. Even though Zu An looked flustered, he still dodged all of the attacks with his delicate footwork. How does he wield such formidable combat ability when he’s so weak? Only someone who often treads along the boundary of life and death could hone such combat sense. I can’t drag this on anymore!","So, he shouted, “Aim for the weaker one!”","The birdman and fatty caught his drift and directed their attacks at Firework.","This immediately put Zu An at a critical disadvantage. He was already barely holding on, and having his weakness targeted broke the delicate balance. Gashes appeared on his body. If not for his sharp combat sense, he would have been crippled by now.","His blood splattered on Firework’s face. She shouted angrily, “You’re renowned figures in the Myriad Worlds! Have a sense of shame!”"]},{"number":2770,"title":"Chapter 2770: Chapter 2722: Verge of Death","paragraphs":["The birdman laughed. “What nonsense! Fighting is all about winning. Only fools would insist on fighting against their enemy’s strengths instead of exploiting their weaknesses.”","Firework was rendered speechless. There were many places in the Myriad Worlds that practiced the law of the jungle, where the winner took all. There was nothing wrong with what the birdman had said.","Nevertheless, she was still angry because these bastards were using her to threaten Zu An.","The birdman snorted, “Yes, continue watching me with that look of disdain. I want those eyes on me when I’m playing with you later.”","Firework and the onlookers were stunned.","Even the fatty was vexed. “Stop rambling, or else I’ll snip off your dick!”","The birdman felt a chill between his legs, knowing his thick-headed fourth brother wouldn’t hesitate to do what he said.","Zu An keenly sensed his lapse in attention and exploited the opportunity to charge out of their encirclement. He circled behind the birdman and used Hundredwarble’s mental attack.","Piercing pain assaulted the birdman’s head. He screeched in agony as he tried to escape in a fluster, knowing a follow-up attack was coming, but he was still a step too late. Zu An was already swinging the Tai’e Sword at his neck.","“Audacious!” The Fire Knight had been keenly watching the battle from the side. There was no way he would give Zu An the chance to kill another one of his companions. He quickly conjured a fire lance and hurled it out.","He intentionally avoided the vitals as he was worried Zu An would use the position swap skill, but the fire lance was still strong enough to stop Zu An’s sword. That would no doubtbuy enough time for them to launch a decisive attack to kill Zu An off.","“What you lookin’ at?”","“I’m looking at you, shithead!”","The exchange left everyone in the warehouse baffled. It was beyond their imagination why those two would suddenly exchange jabs.","Fire Knight was dumbfounded, too. He had no idea why he had blurted out a response at this critical moment, causing him to be a split second late in rescuing his third brother.","“Shit!”","But he quickly noticed Number Four charging at Zu An with his giant scissors, and that made him heave a sigh of relief. He might have stopped me for an instant, but he won’t be able to stop Number Four.","“Be careful of his soulspeak!” Fearing his words would be relayed too slowly, Fire Knight chose to inform his companions via telepathy instead.","The fatty nodded in response. As long as he rescued Number Three, they would be able to overcome this crisis and slowly turn the tides on Zu An. But the next moment, he suddenly lost track of Zu An’s whereabouts.","Fire Knight’s anxious voice echoed in his head, “Be careful!”","Alarmed, the fatty quickly pulled back his scissors to protect himself. He figured that Zu An would resort to the sure-kill dagger to bring him down.","His armor was crafted out of 81 layers of his shed skin; its thickness wasn't to be scoffed at. Even if Zu An plunged his dagger into the armor, it wouldn’t reach his flesh. Instead, that would be an opportunity for him to snip off Zu An’s head, or at least cripple him.","But what happened next threw him off guard. Zu An didn’t switch to his sure-kill dagger, but instead continued attacking with his sword.","The fatty's abrupt switch from offense to defense and his lapse in judgment ultimately created an opening. Right before he could close his scissors, the Tai’e Sword slipped in and stabbed him.","Pu!","Blood spurted out, but it immediately froze into a flower. It was the Snowflake Sword, paired with the Snow Phoenix’s ability! Zu An’s recent exchanges with Yan Xuehen had helped him fully comprehend the essence of frost, allowing him to completely encase the fatty in ice in an instant.","In the next second, intense flames gushed. The Fire Knight’s intervention was on time, unlike before. He carefully controlled his fire to thaw his companion while avoiding further damage.","The fatty gasped for air, his body drenched in sweat. He knew how much of a close shave that had been. Despite his boss’ timely intervention, Zu An’s sword ki had still seeped into his body and suffused it with bone-piercing frost. Perhaps he'd survived that attack thanks to his thick layers of skin armor, but he'd lost his combat ability.","Meanwhile, Zu An quickly flitted out of the warehouse with Firework in hand. He'd chosen to wound the fatty instead of killing him to bait Fire Knight into intervening, thus gaining a chance to break free of the encirclement.","Fire Knight blazed with anger—literally. They'd had the decisive advantage, but somehow, Zu An had managed to kill one, wound one, and slip away.","“Big brother, that lad broke free of your spatial seal. He must be adept in spatial formations!” the birdman exclaimed.","“Shut up! I can see that.” Fire Knight’s eyes flickered in rage, but moments later, he chuckled. “Very well. This only makes the hunt more meaningful. The more secrets he holds, the greater the rewards we’ll reap from him. We’re in the middle of nowhere, and he isn’t strong enough to traverse space yet. He might be able to escape from the warehouses, but where can he go?”","“Our boss is wise!” The birdman fawned on Fire Knight.","Fire Knight ordered him, “Take care of Number Four and tie the others up. I’ll chase him.”","The birdman was taken aback. “Boss, that fellow is extremely sly...”","Fire Knight’s eyes turned cold. “Do you think I’d lose to him?”","“Of course not! Boss, I’m sure you’ll catch him without a hitch,” the birdman hurriedly changed his tone.","Fire Knight harrumphed. His wheelchair burst forth like a valiant steed to chase Zu An.","The earlier clashes had revealed that Zu An’s foundation was beneath his; it was just that the latter possessed bizarre skills that made him a tricky opponent. Not only had his comrades failed to be of help, but under the influence of those bizarre skills, they were even a hindrance.","That was why he chose to pursue Zu An alone.","Zu An flitted through the spaceship with Firework in his arm while searching for the escape pods Employee 9527 mentioned.","Firework stared at him with glowing eyes. “Big brother, you’re incredible. With your cunning schemes, you played those monsters like fools.”","It would take sharp combat sense and great intelligence to come up with such an intricate ploy in the middle of a battle.","“I was lucky they fell for my tricks twice. From this point on, things will only get harder,” Zu An replied.","Just then, he heard a whimper. He rammed down a door and saw Fluttering Baldie lying in the corner of the room, breathing shallowly. There was a gaping hole in the latter's chest, and blue blood covered his translucent body.","“What happened to you, Brother Baldie?” Zu An was taken aback. No wonder I didn’t see him despite the huge commotion earlier."]},{"number":2771,"title":"Chapter 2771: Chapter 2723: Possession","paragraphs":["“It’s you?” Fluttering Baldie noticed Firework in Zu An’s arm and stiffened up.","“What happened to you, baldie?” Firework eyed the gaping hole in Fluttering Baldie’s chest.","“Fire Knight assaulted me.” Fluttering Baldie sighed. “I was dumb. I gloated when I heard Fire Knight was assembling his comrades to deal with this fellow over here. Little did I know he said those words aloud to make me lower my guard. His goal was the spaceship and all of us from the start. I realized that too late.”","Zu An sighed. Had the guests on the spaceship cooperated with the Universal Conglomerate, Fire Knight and his comrades wouldn’t have stood a chance. It was a pity they'd been divided, so Fire Knight took them down one by one.","“What happened, Miss Firework?” Fluttering Baldie finally noticed something was amiss with Firework. It doesn’t look like they're embracing to flaunt their love.","“I fell for an octopus demoness’ poison.” Firework’s eyes blazed with animosity. I wouldn’t have ended up in this embarrassing situation if not for that!","“Ah. Their poison is colorless and odorless; it’s hard to guard against it. It robs you of your strength and renders you incapable of circulating your ki. However, there’s nothing to worry, as the poison clears within a day,” Fluttering Baldie said, tapping into his vast knowledge reserve.","“What’s the point of saying that now? We’ll all be dead by then!” Firework rolled her eyes. He was aware of Fire Knight’s movements but didn’t warn us about the octopus demoness’ poison. He probably doesn’t have good intentions in mind.","Zu An interjected, “Fire Knight is still chasing us. Brother Baldie, I’ll take you with me.”","He held Firework with one hand and lifted Fluttering Baldie with the other.","Firework pouted. It’s doubtful whether we’ll be able to outrun Fire Knight by ourselves, so why are we picking up more baggage? That said, given how he had wanted to save the Conglomerate’s staff members earlier, she knew it was unlikely Zu An would give up on the baldie.","Zu An flitted across the spaceship following Employee 9527’s directions. He even found a hidden passageway, to the others' surprise.","Soon, they arrived at the dock where the escape pods were kept. Zu An first placed Firework into an escape pod before proceeding to move Fluttering Baldie.","But Fluttering Baldie shook his head and said, “I won’t be able to make it. You go ahead...”","Firework retorted, “You should have said so earlier then! Why are you only saying that now?”","“All beings are primed with survival instincts, and I’m no exception,” Fluttering Baldie replied with a bitter smile. “I was clutching onto a sliver of hope earlier, trying my best to recover, but my life force has been severed. Unless I can get a legendary immortal medicine, there’s no hope for me.”","Zu An fell silent. He didn’t have any immortal medicine on him, and he wasn’t so naively compassionate as to use it on a mere acquaintance.","Fluttering Baldie bowed to Zu An and said, “I’m in awe of your magnanimity in putting aside our misgivings to save me.”","He retrieved a cluster of blue light from his head. Despite not having a corporeal form, it looked as beautiful as a gemstone.","“I've devoted myself to studying languages across the Myriad Worlds, and I have accomplished a fair bit.” Fluttering Baldie smiled in glee, proud of his work. “You disguised yourself as Miss Firework to learn the languages of the Myriad Worlds. I have no other way of repaying you, so I’ll give you everything I've learned lest my many years of research go to waste.”","Zu An was astonished. “You know about that?”","Fluttering Baldie sighed. “I am a Deity of Knowledge worshiper. I would be a fool if I couldn’t even see through that afterward.”","That Firework he had met in his room had been overly friendly, and there were some differences in their speech patterns and gestures, too. It was just that lust had gotten the better of him, so he hadn't thought too much into it.","Now that he met the real Firework once more and saw how cold the latter was, he'd connected the dots and realized that the Firework he had met in his room was fake.","“My apologies...”","Fluttering Baldie interjected, “You don’t need to apologize. It was a good move to deal with Deity of Knowledge worshipers like me. I admire your street smarts. If you truly want to do something for me, please complete my thesis, place my name on it, and present it before the academics of the Myriad Worlds...”","His voice grew increasingly weaker before finally fading away entirely.","The blue light floated up to Zu An.","“That’s a valuable treasure. It’s the crystallization of the knowledge he's accrued in his lifetime. He devoted his life to studying the Myriad Worlds’ languages; there’s no one who knows languages better than him. With that, you can become proficient in countless languages right away,” Firework said.","“How do I use it?” Zu An asked.","“Place it on your forehead, and it’ll fuse into your mind,” Firework explained. “You have to do it quickly. Once it’s out of the body, it’ll dissipate quickly. It’ll be a huge pity if that happens.”","It would help Zu An tremendously if he grasped more languages before arriving at Dreamland, so he placed the blue light on his forehead. A cooling sensation seeped into his forehead, and he felt a trove of knowledge flowing into his mind.","“AH!”","Zu An clutched his head in pain. The sheer amount of knowledge appeared to have dealt a heavy blow to his consciousness, putting him in a groggy state. The next second, he found himself standing in the middle of a vast space, with knowledge of different languages surging around like a rapid river.","He felt as if needles were pricking his head. He had no choice but to calm his mind and quietly accept the inflow of knowledge.","All of a sudden, however, the river parted, and a transparent light figure emerged.","Sensing the foreign presence, Zu An opened his eyes and called out, “Fluttering Baldie?”","It was indeed Fluttering Baldie, but his body was even fainter, as if he was just a soul entity.","“It’s been a long time since I felt this young. Your cultivation might be weak, but your body is astoundingly powerful. It harnesses untold potential. More importantly, Miss Firework fancies you,” Fluttering Baldie said with a smile.","Zu An was alarmed. Fluttering Baldie had turned from a weak, dying victim into a sinister, triumphant villain. He swiftly figured out what was going on and asked, “You’re trying to possess me?”","“You aren’t too dumb. It’s too bad you let your greed get the better of you. You wouldn’t have fallen for such a simple trick if you didn’t covet my knowledge,” Fluttering Baldie replied gleefully. He'd thought he would die, but the tides had turned faster than he thought."]},{"number":2772,"title":"Chapter 2772: Chapter 2724: Unexpected Reunion","paragraphs":["“I made you lower your guard by exploiting my dying state.” Fluttering Baldie was proud of his deception. “You can be glad you haven’t lived in vain. It’s your honor to have a soul as intelligent as mine occupying your body.”","Zu An sighed. “You should be the one feeling flattered. You’re going to use my body to approach Miss Firework, aren’t you?”","Fluttering Baldie’s face reddened at having his thoughts exposed. “Miss Firework is fond of you. It’ll be easier for me to get close to her with your body.”","Zu An scoffed, “Do you think Miss Firework truly likes me?”","“Is that not the case?”","“You clearly don’t know women.”","Those words enraged Fluttering Baldie. “Hmph, the barks of a loser! Once I take over your body, I’ll be able to hold her openly.” He morphed into a shadow and lurched toward Zu An.","Clang!","The deep reverberation of a bell echoed. A purple-gold alms bowl appeared above Zu An, emitting a golden dharmic note that cleansed the dark shadow.","Fluttering Baldie snorted, “Using such a mediocre trick against me?”","The shadow rapidly expanded until it covered the alms bowl. The golden light dimmed as if corrupted, and the reverberating dharmic note gradually faded into silence.","Crk crk crk...","Cracks appeared on the alms bowl until it shattered into dust. Zu An’s treasure was nowhere enough to withstand Fluttering Baldie’s powerful soul energy.","The shadow morphed into a fearsome storm cloud that seemed to herald a devastating tornado. Zu An looked small and insignificant before the storm, and it felt as if it would only take a whiff for him to be devoured whole.","Just then, a woman in a red dress manifested beside Zu An.","“Huh. How did you get involved with such a powerful enemy?” The woman was none other than Mi Li. She'd been awoken by Fluttering Baldie’s powerful soul pulsations.","Zu An smiled. “You appeared at a good time. That fellow wants to possess me.”","“He wants to possess you?” Mi Li’s gaze turned cold. Her soul was bound to Zu An’s, which meant that she would die if Zu An’s soul was possessed.","“Oh? It’s a rare twin soul—a man and a woman on top of that! That explains how you were able to disguise as Miss Firework so convincingly. It’s going to be a feast for me!” The wind transformed into a demonic face that greedily lunged at the duo.","Mi Li stood still before the approaching demonic face. Meanwhile, Zu An sweated profusely, to the point where he couldn’t hold himself back from making a move anymore.","Just then, Mi Li pursed her lips and made the gentlest suction sound, as if taking a sip of tea.","The ferocious demonic face warped in fright. “This stature! It can’t be...”","He desperately retreated, but where could he escape to? The shadow swiftly flew into Mi Li’s mouth, and even the demonic face began trembling intensely.","A pair of hands grew out of the face and attempted to claw forward as if to grab onto something. But no matter what he did, he couldn’t escape the fate of being devoured by Mi Li.","In the blink of an eye, Mi Li had already consumed everything. She let out a burp. “Not too bad.”","Zu An was stunned.","This was beyond his imagination. He'd thought there would be an intense battle, but Mi Li had easily devoured Fluttering Baldie’s soul as if it were nothing at all. “My beautiful master, shouldn’t you explain things to me?”","“It would have been hard for me to deal with him if he was in his normal state, but he happened to be a soul entity. Whether a possession succeeds or not depends on the rank and not the volume of the soul. He was weaker than me, so his only fate was to be consumed,” Mi Li replied.","Zu An asked, “What does the ‘stature’ he mentioned earlier mean?”","“It refers to how high one stands. To explain it in your words, it's similar to the concept of dimensions. A higher dimension being is bound to crush a lower dimension being. His stature was lower than mine, so he was unable to hurt me, but I could easily hurt him.” Mi Li yawned. “I’m going to take a nap and digest his soul energy.”","She went back to sleep.","Zu An was speechless. I feel as if she’s hiding something from me, but I can’t force her if she doesn’t want to speak.","When he opened his eyes once more, he was faced with Firework’s anxious expression. She asked, “Big brother, are you okay?”","“I’m fine,” Zu An replied.","He immediately noticed the massive trove of knowledge in his mind, containing information about languages across the Myriad Worlds. He now grasped all the languages Fluttering Baldie had devoted his life to studying.","“It’s all my fault. I didn’t expect that damned baldie to be this cunning!” All of a sudden, Firework coldly eyed Zu An. “Hold on. Are you that damned baldie?”","Zu An laughed. “Don’t worry. He did try to possess my body, but failed.”","“Are you sure?” Firework remained skeptical.","“Of course I am.”","Firework pondered for a while before finally smiling once more. “Your eyes are still as pure and innocent as before. Alright, I believe you aren’t that damned baldie.”","Zu An was stunned, but he wasn’t in the mood to bicker with Firework. Perhaps it was due to the earlier possession attempt or the flood of information in his mind, but he was feeling incredibly weak. What the hell? Mi Li was nourished by Fluttering Baldie’s soul, but somehow I’m feeling exhausted.","Even so, there was no time for him to dwell on that. There was an abrupt spatial warp, and Fire Knight appeared at the entrance on his wheelchair, saying, “I’ve finally found you two.”","With a wave of his hand, he unleashed fire arrows, destroying all the escape pods.","Zu An used his final sliver of strength to pull Firework out of her escape pod, lest she get taken out in an explosion.","“It’s all that baldie’s fault!” Firework cursed. If not for him, we would have been gone by now! She whispered to Zu An. “Reach into my clothes. I have two larger firecrackers in there. Find a chance to hurl them at that bastard. We’ll drag him down to hell with us!”","Zu An was speechless.","“You want to drag me down? Don’t even think about it!” Fire Knight harrumphed as he hurled two fire chains at the duo. Zu An and Firework felt their bodies being weighed down, preventing them from making the slightest move.","Firework’s expression collapsed into despair. Zu An frowned contemplatively.","Fire Knight was about to drag his two captives back when he suddenly turned around and shouted, “Who is it?”","Zu An and Firework looked over. Another wormhole-like entrance appeared on the wall, and a woman dressed in white walked out.","Zu An was stunned. “Xuehen?”"]},{"number":2773,"title":"Chapter 2773: Chapter 2725: More Terrifying Than the Deity of Death","paragraphs":["It was as if the woman had just walked out of a painting. Her robes were as white as snow, and her hair fluttered gracefully. She commanded an ethereal air.","Firework’s eyes lit up. “She was practically born to be a Love and Beauty worshiper!”","The woman was so beautiful that even other women were drawn to her.","Upon hearing Zu An’s voice, the white-robed woman looked over with impassive eyes devoid of the slightest emotion.","Xuehen was as cold as frost, but the time she had spent with Zu An breathed some life into her. In contrast, this woman felt empty like the void. Even a glance at her induced nihilism. It felt as if there were no meaning to life, death, and conflict.","“Who are you?” Fire Knight asked grimly. He couldn’t read the woman who had just appeared, and that placed great pressure on him.","The woman stretched her hand out. “Hand over Dreamland’s invitation letter.”","Her words came out awkwardly, as if it had been a long time since she last spoke, but her voice was still very pleasant-sounding.","Fire Knight sneered. They had come here to steal the other passengers’ invitation letters, yet someone else dared to rob him? This was ridiculous.","“What if I refuse?” Fire Knight snorted. If not for him struggling to get a read on the woman’s strength, he would have already made a move.","“Then I’ll have to make a move.” The white-robed woman sighed. She took a step forward, and her aura abruptly surged.","Fire Knight was taken aback. The woman was stronger than he had expected. His eyes flickered as he said, “Hold on. Those two have invitation letters too, and they’re powerless to resist now. You can have their invitation letters.”","With his second sister dead, the old woman’s and Fluttering Baldie’s invitation letters were enough for his other two brothers to use. It didn’t matter whether he had Zu An’s and Firework’s invitation letters or not.","He had a fearsome reputation as an Annihilation worshiper, but that didn’t mean he sought to resolve everything through violence. He saw no point in confronting a powerful expert over a matter that was easily resolved.","The white-robed woman glanced at Zu An and Firework.","Zu An felt a little awkward as he was still carrying Firework. Despite knowing the other party wasn’t Yan Xuehen, he couldn’t help but feel that he was caught in the act of adultery.","Firework felt nervous as well. Even Fire Knight was too much for them to deal with, and this mysterious woman just had to appear out of nowhere. It was like the saying ‘trouble comes in pairs’.","The white-robed woman eyed them impassively before turning back to Fire Knight. “I don’t want theirs.”","“...So you’re just after me!” Fire Knight roared in anger.","He was reluctant to pick meaningless fights with experts, but that didn’t mean he was afraid of trouble. Dozens of fire chains shot forth from his wheelchair, sealing off all of the white-robed woman’s escape paths.","“Be careful!” Zu An exclaimed. Despite knowing the woman wasn’t Yan Xuehen, he was still concerned because of their resemblance.","Firework grumbled coyly, “Big brother, you can’t just fall for her just because she’s gorgeous. Have you forgotten you’re still holding me?”","Zu An was speechless.","The white-haired woman stood still as if she couldn’t see the fire chains flying toward her. Soon, the chains shackled her body.","Fire Knight smiled triumphantly. I thought she was some powerful expert, but that’s all she amounts to...","Yet his smile quickly faded. After shackling the woman’s body, his fire chains didn’t stop; they passed right through her! It was as if her body was incorporeal.","Unwilling to accept the result, Fire Knight shot out more chains, but the other party stood still and allowed the chains to pass through her. She wasn’t hurt whatsoever.","“How is this possible?!” Fire Knight was flabbergasted, as if he had witnessed the inconceivable.","The white-robed woman took a step forward and the surrounding fire chains all shattered, including the ones shackling Zu An and Firework. She lifted her sheathed sword, and an incomparably sharp wave of sword ki surged toward Fire Knight.","Fire Knight was horrified. Not daring to hold back, he unleashed all his flames to manifest a humongous fire skeleton head to rip the sword ki apart.","Faced with the fire skeleton head, the sword ki resembled an ant confronting a whale. It felt as if even a blow from the whale could cause the ant to disintegrate. And yet, when both sides clashed, the more intimidating fire skeleton head was sliced in half like butter coming into contact with a red-hot knife.","The sword ki surged forth with unstoppable momentum, slicing Fire Knight and his wheelchair in half. The corpse swiftly disintegrated into flames.","The white-haired woman frowned. She sensed that Fire Knight wasn’t dead yet. Thus, she turned around and walked away.","Zu An hurriedly shouted, “Miss, what’s your name?”","His encounters with the Goddess of Wu Mountain and the Mermaid Queen made him wonder if there was any connection between Yan Xuehen and the woman before him. Not only did they look identical, but they had strikingly similar dispositions, too. On top of that, they wielded the same void divine power.","The white-robed woman glanced at him with a frown before walking away to pursue Fire Knight.","Noticing Zu An’s daze, Firework remarked, “Hey! She might be beautiful, but you don’t have to fawn on her that much. I’m not bad myself, but I don’t see you being that proactive!”","There was no reason for Zu An to tell her about Yan Xuehen. Now that he was freed from the fire chains, he took a brief moment to recuperate before chasing after the white-robed woman with Firework in his arm.","Firework was taken aback. “Wait wait wait! This is our chance to escape! Are you squandering this opportunity to head back and look for her?”","Zu An hurriedly replied, “She resembles a friend of mine. I have questions to ask her.”","“Tsk!” Firework rolled her eyes. “That’s what all men claim when they see a beautiful woman. Can’t you come up with a better excuse?”","Zu An ignored her. “I shouldn’t implicate you in this. Do you want to stay here?”","“I’m coming with you.” Firework hurriedly explained herself. “I’m still under the effects of the octopus demoness’ poison. I’d be dead meat if even a small fry stumbled in here.”","Zu An thought her answer made sense, so he continued giving chase while carrying her.","When they arrived at the warehouse, they were shocked by what they saw. The noisy warehouse had turned eerily quiet, and the army of monsters had collapsed in puddles of blood.","Employee 9527 and a few other Conglomerate’s staff members were still alive, but they were frozen stiff in shock, as if they had just witnessed something unbelievable.","Fire Knight and the birdman were standing in two corners of the warehouse. Fire Knight, having lost his wheelchair, was now using two spears as crutches for support. The birdman was backed against the warehouse wall while holding his silver claws tightly.","They were covered in so many wounds that fresh blood flowed profusely from them, but they didn’t have the energy to tend to their injuries. They stared nervously at the white-robed woman standing at the center of the warehouse.","As beautiful as the woman was, to them, she was even more terrifying than the Deity of Death."]},{"number":2774,"title":"Chapter 2774: Chapter 2726: Golden Emblem","paragraphs":["An intense battle had broken out in the short time Zu An and Firework were making their way here. Fire Knight’s group had suffered heavy losses.","The white-robed woman sensed the pair’s arrival and glanced backward. Her gaze mainly fell on Zu An, as she sensed something peculiar about him.","Noticing her lapse in attention, the birdman quickly charged toward the wormhole in the distant wall. He specialized in speed, and he was giving it 120% out of desperation to escape.","Half of his body managed to slip into the wormhole when a sharp wave of sword ki sliced through him. The other half failed to enter the wormhole and squirmed ceaselessly on the spot.","Those in the warehouse gasped.","The half body tried to regenerate, but the sword ki was imbued with peculiar energy that hindered regeneration. Instead, a tinge of gray began spreading from the wound and swiftly enveloped the entire half.","Then, the half disintegrated into dust, not leaving any traces behind.","The remaining people in the warehouse were speechless. The white-robed woman’s blade is terrifying! Wait a moment, she didn’t even draw her sword!","Fire Knight remained on the spot. My foolish third brother. Do you think I would have stayed still if it was possible to escape?","He picked up his crutches and put them together to form a fire lance. Intense flames shrouded his body. They formed new legs that allowed him to stand up and clothed him in fire armor that made him resemble a general on the battlefield. The terrifying pressure he emanated suffocated most of the people in the warehouse.","“It’s been a while since I felt such pressure. Miss, I have you thank you for sparking such excitement in me.” Fire Knight pointed his fire lance at the white-robed woman. “I am Fire Knight. Draw your sword!”","The white-robed woman calmly replied, “You aren’t worthy.”","Fire Knight and the onlookers were speechless.","Big sister Yan is so domineering! Zu An thought.","Firework looked at the white-robed woman in awe and admiration.","Fire Knight sneered in anger, “Very well. Let’s see how much longer you can keep your sword sheathed!”","As he charged at the white-robed woman with his lance, he manifested a giant avatar of a fire-armored general. Together, they thrust their lances toward her.","Employee 9527 was horrified. This isn’t good! He knows he’s doomed, so he’s planning to bring all of us down with him! No matter the outcome of the battle, the spaceship won’t be able to take the brunt of his attack. If the spaceship explodes, no more than a handful of us can survive.","Zu An anxiously placed Firework down by the side and channeled his Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra. He was trying to absorb the shockwaves of their clash, lest the spaceship be destroyed.","The white-robed woman frowned. She could see through Fire Knight’s intention. She raised her sheath and gently flicked it; her sword popped out by an inch. A cold glint of light shot out.","Much to Fire Knight’s shock, the massive fire avatar imbued with annihilation power was sliced in half. He had no time to react before he was obliterated by the cold glint of light, too. The light harnessed a peculiar power that was able to extinguish the flames, so the disaster was averted.","Those from the Universal Conglomerate cheered in delight, but they soon felt worried, as it struck them that they still didn’t know whether the white-robed woman was friend or foe. Even though she had killed Fire Knight, there was no telling whether she would go after the rest of them, too.","Even Zu An was nervous. He knew he wouldn’t stand much of a chance against the white-robed woman.","Just then, the white-robed woman walked over and carefully assessed him.","Firework nervously spoke up. “Miss, we aren’t from the same group as Fire Knight.”","The white-robed woman ignored her and asked, “Why do you carry nebula power?”","Zu An was stunned. Nebula power? Is she referring to the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra? Or was I afflicted with Yan Xuehen’s nebula power due to our frequent bonding?","The white-robed woman carefully examined him before shaking her head. “Perhaps I was seeing things.”","She walked over to Fire Knight’s corpse, picked up the invitation letter that had fallen to the ground, and asked, “This spaceship is heading to Dreamland, right? May I have a room, too?”","Employee 9527 hurriedly nodded. “Of course!”","He’d been worried that the white-robed woman would deal with the rest of them as well, so it was a huge relief to hear her making such a simple request. Did she cause such a huge commotion just to steal Fire Knight’s invitation letter? Wow, Fire Knight is a pitiful one. He wanted to steal the other guests’ invitation letters, only to get robbed himself.","Employee 9527 requested for Zu An to get some antidotes for them from the medical bay. He wouldn’t dare ask the white-robed woman to run an errand for him.","The Universal Conglomerate had prepared antidotes for common poisons. These antidotes weren’t specifically tailored for the octopus demoness’ poison, but at least it would restore their mobility.","Soon, Employee 9527 settled the white-robed woman in the most luxurious guest room. He considered asking the latter about her background, but she showed little interest in conversing with him, so he decided to keep his questions to himself. He stationed staff members near her room to attend to her every need.","Only then did he rush out to meet Zu An. He said amicably, “Pardon me for only attending to you now, Brother Zu.”","Zu An replied with a smile, “Don’t worry about it. It’s important to attend to that lady first, or else she might destroy the spaceship with a slash.”","Employee 9527 smiled sheepishly. “I’m glad you’re so understanding, Brother Zu. I’m truly grateful for your help. We would have all been dead if not for you.”","Zu An clasped his fist and said, “The one who saved you was the white-robed woman.”","Employee 9527 shook his head. “That’s not true. My colleagues and I would have been massacred by those monsters if you hadn’t put your life on the line to protect us before the white-robed woman arrived. Ah, you asked about a mainstream language offline translator earlier. That’s usually worth an exorbitant sum, but I’ll request for one to be given to you for free as compensation.”","Zu An smiled. “There’s no need for it. I’m well-versed in most languages now.”","“Oh? What do you mean by that?” Employee 9527 was confused.","Zu An told Employee 9527 about how Fluttering Baldie had intended to possess him, but it ended with him inheriting Fluttering Baldie’s knowledge about languages instead.","Employee 9527 was appalled to hear that. “That baldie is despicable! He’s a disgrace to all Deity of Knowledge worshipers!”","Zu An wasn’t bothered by it. “There are good and bad people among each universal deity’s worshipers. It would be unwise to stereotype them based on the black sheep.”","“Brother Zu is magnanimous. No wonder you have a Wonderpoint World despite your young age.” Employee 9527 pondered for a moment before taking out and passing over a golden emblem. “Please take this instead. It represents our Universal Conglomerate’s friendship. We only give it to people whom we owe a huge debt to. With this golden emblem, all Universal Conglomerate branches across the Myriad Worlds will treat you as a VIP.”"]},{"number":2775,"title":"Chapter 2775: Chapter 2727: Forgetting Everything","paragraphs":["The golden emblem was made from a special alloy, inscribed with the Universal Conglomerate’s logo. Light flowed on its surface, and it felt cool to the touch. It seemed to have a calming effect as well.","“Our emblems are exclusively forged in our headquarters, and only a small number of employees are authorized to inscribe the relevant details. Outsiders can’t hope to recreate it,” Employee 9527 explained with a smile.","Unless he did it willingly, Fire Knight and the others could only obtain the emblem mold from him, which wouldn’t be sufficient to be recognized by the Conglomerate.","Zu An was surprised. It sounded as if very few people had the right to forge the emblem, and someone ranked 9527 shouldn’t have had that opportunity. It suggested that Employee 9527 could be of surprisingly high standing in the Conglomerate.","But since Employee 9527 wasn’t saying a thing, Zu An couldn’t probe either.","It was a close encounter, but Zu An had gotten a lot out of it. He had become proficient in countless languages in the Myriad Worlds, and that was a huge advantage when it came to collecting intelligence.","The golden emblem was a huge bonus, too. Having witnessed firsthand how affluent the Universal Conglomerate was, he knew it would be tremendously beneficial to forge close ties with them. Not to mention this wasn’t just an informal relationship, but a formal one affirmed by the emblem.","“Thank you.” Zu An accepted the emblem with a smile.","Employee 9527 bowed to Zu An and said, “Have a good rest, Brother Zu. I’ll have to clean up the mess on the spaceship, so pardon me for not being able to accompany you.”","Zu An bade Employee 9527 farewell. He pondered for a moment before deciding to visit the white-robed woman’s room.","The maids outside the room greeted him warmly; they were grateful to him for saving them. One asked, “Benefactor, are you here to pay a visit to the miss? Shall we inform her of your arrival?”","Zu An was still hesitating over how to approach this matter when the white-robed woman called out, “Who is it?”","Since she had discovered him, Zu An replied, “I am Zu An. I have something I’d like to ask.”","There was a brief silence before the door opened. A cold voice echoed, “Come in.”","The maids stepped aside to let Zu An in.","Zu An was surprised when he saw the room’s layout. Employee 9527 had assigned the white-robed woman the best room out of gratitude for her help and fearfulness of her strength, but the arrangement was surprisingly humble.","It was an empty room with a bed. Even from afar, Zu An could feel a chill emanating from the bed, as if it were the Cold Jade Bed from Return of the Condor Heroes.","Zu An stared at the bed after entering the room, not saying a word despite claiming to have something to ask. That brought a frown to the white-robed woman’s face, and she asked, “What do you want to ask?”","Awkwardness flashed across Zu An’s face. “I’d like to ask your name.”","The white-robed woman was speechless.","Zu An also realized his question was abrupt, so he hurriedly clarified, “Please don’t misunderstand. I happen to have a friend who resembles you greatly, so I came here to ask out of curiosity.”","“Your flirting methods are outdated,” the white-robed woman replied calmly as if nothing in the world could faze her.","“I’m speaking the truth.” Zu An knew his words didn’t sound credible, so he paced around the room before asking, “Miss, are you a Nebula worshiper?”","The white-robed woman stared at him quietly, looking as if she would evict him at any moment.","Zu An hurriedly added, “That friend of mine unintentionally caught the Deity of Nebula’s gaze. She emanates an aura very similar to yours, though she’s nowhere as strong as you.”","The white-robed woman’s interest was finally piqued. “Oh? What’s your friend’s name?”","“Her name is Yan Xuehen.”","When he answered the question, Zu An felt both expectant and nervous. It could be a similar case as the Goddess of Wu Mountain and the Mermaid Queen, where the white-robed woman was related to Yan Xuehen, but it could also be that the white-robed woman was another form of Yan Xuehen, similar to Chu Chuyan and the Snow Lady.","Even though it hadn’t been long since he left the Cultivation World, something could have still happened to Yan Xuehen in the meantime. That had been the case with Chu Chuyan back then.","“Yan Xuehen...” the white-robed woman murmured the name before shaking her head. “I’ve never heard of her.”","Zu An exhaled in relief, though he also felt a tinge of disappointment.","“I am Tingxue,” the white-robed woman added.","Zu An was surprised. He hadn’t expected her to reveal her name. She has a ‘Xue’ in her name, too. Is she really not related to Yan Xuehen?","“Are you on close terms with that woman?” The white-robed woman quietly looked at him.","“We are extremely close. She’s my lover, and we are mutually in love...” Zu An replied with a heavy heart. He regretted that he couldn’t spend more time with his lovers before leaving.","“I can tell. I sense nebula energy from you. You must have gotten it from her,” the white-robed woman said.","Zu An smiled awkwardly.","“What a rare case.” The white-robed woman paused. She struggled to speak fluently as she rarely spoke. “Unlike other universal deities, the Deity of Nebula rarely gazes upon anyone or bestows their power. I was the only one for many years. I never expected there to be someone else.”","Zu An replied bitterly, “But this isn’t a good thing. I heard those treading down this path are doomed to become one with the nebula. The deeper they comprehend this dao, the more they lose their emotions and forget about everyone around them.”","The white-robed woman was speechless.","Zu An belatedly realized he was disparaging the other party. “My apologies, I wasn’t talking about you...”","But the white-robed woman interjected, “You’re right. I have forgotten about many things and many people.”","This was the first time she’d shown a hint of emotion.","“...” Zu An tried probing, “Did you want to forget about those things?”","The white-robed woman shook her head. “I have already forgotten. I don’t know if those memories were happy or sad, though those emotions mean nothing to me now, so there is no meaning in feeling conflicted over this. I just feel a tinge of regret now and then.”","Zu An saw Yan Xuehen’s future in her, and that made his heart ache. “Miss, how long did it take for you to begin losing your emotions and memories after catching the Deity of Nebula’s gaze?” He wanted to gather more details so he could help Yan Xuehen.","“I’ve forgotten about that, too.” The white-robed woman looked at him as if she was talking about something unrelated to her.","“...” Ugh, she doesn’t know anything at all. Since they were having a pleasant conversation, Zu An decided to probe further. “Miss, why did you go after Fire Knight?”","“They destroyed a world. A girl from that world gave me a flower not long ago. She was dead by the time I arrived,” the white-robed woman lowered her gaze as she replied.","Zu An widened his eyes. For a moment there, he felt a sliver of rage from the white-robed woman. She hadn’t completely lost her emotions; they had just become very faint.","“Such lowlives ought to be ripped into pieces!” Zu An had witnessed the miserable plight that befell destroyed worlds, and he thought people who committed such massacres should suffer even after death.","Unfortunately, he’d been so shocked to see ‘Yan Xuehen’ that he forgot to imprison the souls of Fire Knight and the others in the eighteenth level of the Netherworld. Come to think of it, I don’t think I sensed their souls earlier. It’s as if the white-robed woman destroyed even their souls.","“I thought your goal was their invitation letter,” he eventually continued.","“It was indeed one of my goals.”","“...Why do you want to head to Dreamland?”","—","Translator’s Thoughts:","Nebula, in this case, is often translated as Primordial Chaos in most Chinese novels. It refers to the state of the world, before worlds were formed, before heaven and earth are separated, and everything is just a huge mess of dust and energy lingering around.","There is no good translation for this term that accurately captures the connotations - so take Nebula in this case with a pinch of salt, that it’s not an entirely scientific term but also comes with fantasy/folklore connotation as well."]},{"number":2776,"title":"Chapter 2776: Chapter 2728: Dreamland","paragraphs":["The white-robed woman looked at him. Her eyes were as deep and mesmerizing as deep space, but they carried an air of serenity even as she replied, “None of your business.”","Zu An was speechless. Considering the woman's nature and that they weren’t on close terms, her answer wasn’t surprising, but being rejected by someone who resembled Yan Xuehen still felt terrible.","The white-robed woman turned around to look out the window, seemingly deep in thought.","The atmosphere became awkward. Zu An didn’t think it was appropriate for him to continue lingering in the room, so he bade his farewell and took his leave. The woman didn’t say anything else, as if nothing piqued her interest.","While Zu An was returning to his room with a melancholic heart, he stumbled upon a beautiful, red figure leaning against the wall along the corridor. Firework looked at him with an unreadable smile as she asked, “She didn’t let you in?”","Zu An harrumphed. “I got into her room.”","“And yet you’re out so quickly. You must have failed to satisfy her,” Firework teased.","“...” That’s an innuendo, right? Zu An opened his room door as he asked, “Do you need something from me?”","“Can’t I spend time with you?” Firework naturally followed him into the room. She continued with a dissatisfied pout, “Don’t you think it’s too much to forget about your old lover as soon as you find someone new? Just a while ago, I was still your little sister, but look at how distant you are now.”","Zu An was speechless. “When did I call you little sister?”","“I called you big brother. Doesn’t that make me your little sister?” Firework replied matter-of-factly.","Zu An was speechless.","“Fine, I’ll stop teasing you.” Firework took a seat on a chair behind him and massaged his back with her little hands. “Did you manage to gather any information about the white-robed woman?”","“You’re interested in her?” Zu An closed his eyes and enjoyed the massage. He knew that Firework harbored an ulterior motive, but it was hard to turn down an understanding little sister like her.","“Of course. Someone as beautiful as her ought to worship our great Deity of Love and Beauty,.” Firework’s eyes gleamed with excitement. She was already imagining the immense contribution she would accrue by leading the beauty into the universal deity’s embrace.","“You’re going to be disappointed. Tingxue is a Nebula worshiper,” Zu An replied with a sigh.","“You’ve gotten her name, too? You’re quite the charmer, aren’t you?” Firework whistled before sighing as well. “I expected as much. Her cold attitude reeks too much of Nebula. What a pity I failed to get to her before Nebula.”","Zu An asked, “Is there no way to lead a Nebula worshiper onto another path?”","Based on the intelligence he had gathered thus far, most universal deity worshipers had a chance to switch their faith after paying a price.","Firework shook her head. “It’s impossible. All Nebula worshipers are doomed to lose their emotions and forget everything, until they return to Nebula’s embrace.”","Zu An was stunned. Tingxue’s fate sounded like an omen of Yan Xuehen’s future, and that left him with a heavy heart.","“Did you find out why she’s heading to Dreamland?” Firework asked.","Zu An shook his head. “I don’t know.” He still felt a little stifled thinking about Tingxue’s cold tone.","Firework burst into laughter. “Heh. Looks like she doesn’t like you that much either. You should know who's a true friend, who's been through thick and thin with you.”","“Oh? But I don’t know why you’re heading to Dreamland either.”","“I’ll tell you my reason if you tell me yours.”","Zu An didn’t mind revealing his reason. “I heard Dreamland can fulfill all wishes. I’m looking for some special materials and ways to save my friends.”","“I bet they're all women,” Firework scoffed. “Despite your honest front, you’re quite the philanderer.”","Zu An just responded, “...I’ve told you my reason. What about you?”","Firework replied, “Well, I think it’ll be fun there.”","Zu An’s resulting stare left her embarrassed, so she quickly added, “Eesh, I knew you wouldn’t believe me. Fine, fine, I’m heading there to uncover Dreamland’s secrets.”","“Secrets? What secrets?” Zu An was perplexed.","“Have you wondered what kind of entity has the power to fulfill all wishes?” Firework asked.","“Universal deities?”","“Not even universal deities possess such power.”","Zu An took that information to mind. I guess even universal deities have limits. “Does this mean the rumor that Dreamland is capable of fulfilling all wishes is a lie?” He had been skeptical about this, but he was still disappointed by the news, as there were questions he needed answers to.","“It’s not necessarily a lie. Dreamland opens once every thousand years, but no one has ever accused its wish-granting ability of being a lie before,” Firework said. “That’s what bewilders me. On top of that, no one returned from the last entry. Everyone is curious about what happened. I’m not the only one who wants to investigate the matter.”","“Wouldn’t it be wiser for Dreamland to lie low if it did something unforgivable to the previous batch of invitees?” Zu An was intrigued.","“Perhaps they're simply confident, or there's a compelling reason why they have to do it. We’ll know once we get there,” Firework said. “Once you get there, don’t trust anyone’s words.”","“Not even yours?”","“You’re terrible~”","The spaceship arrived at the galaxy where Dreamland was located. Even Tingxue couldn’t resist the urge to head to the front of the spaceship to take a look at the famous Dreamland. However, the galaxy was enveloped in iridescent lights, making it impossible to see within.","“This is why Dreamland remains a mystery despite having opened many times in the past,” Firework explained.","“Since guests have to be transported to Dreamland each time it opens, the major powers should already know Dreamland’s location and attempt to investigate it, no?”","“Did you think that Dreamland stays in one place? The Universal Conglomerate once tried recording Dreamland’s coordinates, but when they returned later, the area was empty. Many theorize that Dreamland doesn’t stay in a single location; it’s constantly moving, and it only reveals its coordinates whenever it opens.”","Zu An frowned. “But Dreamland has opened many times before. Can’t we calculate the trajectory of its movements by recording its coordinates each time it opens?”","“Major powers have tried that, but they can’t find a pattern in the trajectory of its movements. They eventually concluded that Dreamland is no ordinary planet. The movements of planets and even entire galaxies can be calculated, but somehow, they couldn’t do the calculation for Dreamland.” Firework looked at the iridescent lights in excitement. I can finally get to the bottom of this.","“It truly is a mysterious place!” Zu An recalled Qi Yaoguang’s divination, and his heart clenched up."]},{"number":2777,"title":"Chapter 2777: Chapter 2729: Space Elevator","paragraphs":["The Universal Conglomerate’s staff members matched Dreamland’s radio frequency and requested entry. Moments later, Dreamland’s staff members granted them permission.","The iridescent lights parted, revealing a passageway. The spaceship flew inside as instructed. Everyone on the spaceship examined their surroundings, but they couldn’t make out much through the thick layer of light.","Some time later, the area in front of them opened up, and a planet came into sight. A massive spaceport was present at the outer perimeter of the planet, and the spaceship was directed to stop there.","Employee 9527 walked up to Zu An and the others and said, “Esteemed guests, we’ll have to bid you farewell here as we aren’t allowed to enter Dreamland. Dreamland’s staff members will be leading you in. Be assured that we’ll be here to transport you back to your planets once you're done, provided you’re willing to leave.”","Zu An’s heart quivered. Many people had become reluctant to leave Dreamland after entering it, so he needed to be vigilant in case the same happened to him as well. There were many important people waiting for him at home.","After the spaceship docked, the doors opened, and the Conglomerate’s staff members guided the guests out.","Employee 9527 snuck over to Zu An’s side and said, “Brother Zu, take care of yourself!” He was also worried that Zu An wouldn’t return.","Zu An nodded. “Thank you. I’ll surely return, and I’ll be troubling you to send me back.”","“Haha, leave it to me!” Employee 9527 patted Zu An’s arms before waving him farewell.","Zu An alighted from the spaceship and gazed at the extravagant spaceport before him. I wonder what kind of technology they've employed here. Somehow, we’re able to walk normally here even though the port isn’t enclosed.","The different types of spaceships docked in the spaceport hinted at the diverse civilizations spread across the Myriad Worlds. It was weirdly beautiful. He even spotted a worm spaceship, something he had only seen in a sci-fi movie before.","He had to concede that the people in his previous world were very creative, to have created content that so strikingly resembled real life. Bizarre entities alighted from different spaceships, and they were quickly welcomed by the spaceport’s staff members.","Interestingly, the spaceport was able to dispatch staff members who corresponded to the guests’ races, and they could always converse fluently in the other party’s native language. This amazed the guests. No wonder people say it’s a place that can fulfill miracles.","The staff member who welcomed Zu An’s group was a human man. He flipped through his notebook and remarked in surprise, “Hm? There should be two more guests, right?”","“A mishap befell them. They won’t be able to make it in,” Firework replied with a smile.","“I see. Please follow me.” The staff member was already accustomed to such situations. Along the way, he politely asked, “Would you prefer to first have some afternoon tea at our spaceport, or would you like to head straight to Dreamland Hotel?”","“Of course we’ll head straight to Dreamland Hotel. I can’t wait to see the legendary Dreamland.” Firework’s voice quivered in excitement.","“You won’t be disappointed with Dreamland,” the staff member puffed up his chest and replied. He then turned to Zu An and Tingxue. “What about you two?”","“I’ll head straight to Dreamland Hotel, too,” Zu An replied. The spaceport was extravagant, but how could it compete with the true Dreamland?","Tingxue stood coolly without saying a word, but she appeared to implicitly agree with Zu An.","“Please follow me.” The staff member led the way.","Zu An examined the surroundings, though his focus was more on the other guests. Those bizarrely-dressed guests vocalized weird sounds that he wouldn’t have been able to understand before, but to his delight, he could understand everything that was being said.","Fluttering Baldie’s knowledge of languages is indeed amazing.","Some guests carried both curiosity and respect for Dreamland, and they couldn’t wait to explore the place. They discussed where to head next.","Meanwhile, others grimly warned their companions to remain vigilant. Unlike the ignorant newbies, they understood the dangers that lurked within Dreamland.","A small group of people looked relaxed and self-assured. Zu An couldn’t overhear their conversation, which suggested that they were all powerful experts. They were aware of the dangers surrounding Dreamland, but they were confident in their strength.","Soon, Zu An arrived before a giant building. Confused, he asked, “I thought we’d be riding on a flying ship or something?”","The staff member replied with a smile, “To elevate our guest experience, Dreamland has chosen to employ space elevators instead of using flying ships as a transportation medium.”","He ushered the guests toward the elevator lobby and pressed the down button. Soon, the elevator door opened. “Please enter.”","Firework looked at the elevator’s transparent glass walls, followed by the thick wires extending beneath the spaceport into the planet. She hesitantly asked, “Are you sure your elevator is reliable?”","The staff member replied, “Esteemed guest, please put your mind at ease. Our space elevator has never malfunctioned to date. Our space elevator also functions as a mini flying machine if anything happens, so you’ll land safely no matter what happens.”","Tingxue walked into the space elevator first without saying a word. She sat by the window to admire the scenery outside. It wouldn’t hurt her even if the space elevator suddenly exploded anyway.","Firework stuck out her tongue before dragging Zu An in with her.","Tingxue suddenly turned over, eyed their connected hands, and asked, “Are you two a couple?”","“None of your business.” Firework harrumphed. She'd wanted to convince Tingxue to worship Love and Beauty alongside her, but when she learned that the other party was a Nebula worshiper, she lost her interest.","Once a Nebula worshiper, always a Nebula worshiper.","“I’m merely curious. He mentioned that he has a wife.” Tingxue turned her head back and reverted to being an ice sculpture.","Zu An was speechless.","Firework was baffled too. She tugged Zu An’s arm, tiptoed, and whispered to him, “Is that woman jealous?”","“That’s impossible!” Zu An huffed. A Nebula worshiper wouldn’t harbor such feelings.","Firework thought that made sense.","Just then, the space elevator began moving. Her attention was immediately drawn to the scenery, her curious gaze flickering all around.","The spaceship traveled so smoothly that Zu An didn’t feel the slightest shake.","A sweet AI voice played to inform them about things they ought to take note of. At the same time, a massive screen appeared on the elevator door, playing Dreamland advertisements."]},{"number":2778,"title":"Chapter 2778: Chapter 2730: Big Miss","paragraphs":["Firework looked at the advertisements and laughed. “I hadn’t expected Dreamland to hire her for their promotional videos. She’s the Fairy Galaxy’s hottest female celebrity, though I think big sister Tingxue is much more beautiful than her.”","Tingxue turned to her and said, “You’re beautiful too.”","Firework’s eyes lit up. “It’s my greatest honor to receive big sister Tingxue’s compliment.”","Zu An couldn’t be bothered to join their conversation, so he made his way to the window and saw many similar elevators descending at the same time. The journey was so smooth that he wouldn’t have known that they were descending if he hadn’t looked outside.","Dreamland must be a technological civilization. It would take advanced technology to construct such amazing systems. They might even be ahead of those advanced civilizations I saw in sci-fi films from my previous life.","It would have been great if he could have scrutinized Dreamland in its entirety from above, but the iridescent lights and clouds hindered him from doing so. No wonder so little is known about Dreamland. They're truly secretive.","The further they descended, the thicker the fog became. It came to a point where they couldn’t see the scenery outside anymore. Zu An decided to sit down on a chair.","Firework continued chatting with Tingxue, though she did most of the talking. Zu An wondered how she could hold so many words in that little mouth of hers.","There was a slight shake, and the elevator door opened.","“Esteemed guests, welcome to Dreamland!”","Staff members were already waiting outside.","Zu An and the others stepped out of the elevator. They were probably at a transport hub to receive guests from the space elevator and transport them to their final destination.","“Esteemed guests, we have three hotel styles for you to choose from—the fiery beach, the serene mountain, and the fleeting clouds. May I know which one you prefer?” the staff member said with a smile.","Zu An frowned. “Don’t all guests stay together?”","“We understand every guest has their individual preferences, so we’re doing our best to fulfill our guests’ needs within the scope of our abilities,” the staff member replied. “Be assured that the hotel style only determines the location and environment of your stay. You’ll receive the same service and information.”","They understood what the guests were worried about.","“It has to be the fiery beach for me,” Firework said with glowing eyes.","“Alright.” The staff member turned to Tingxue and Zu An. “What about you two?”","“I choose...”","Firework interjected before Tingxue could finish her sentence. “Big sister Tingxue is with us. She’ll be taking the beach too.”","Tingxue opened her mouth, but she didn’t refute Firework’s words in the end. Someone of her nature would have preferred the mountain or the clouds, but for some reason, she instinctively didn’t want to pick the clouds. She'd been about to pick the mountain when Firework chose on her behalf.","It was all the same for her, so she couldn’t be bothered to argue.","Zu An chuckled. “I’ll pick the beach too.”","Firework grinned brightly.","“This way, please.”","The staff member led them out of the building and onto a convertible jeep. Looking at the brilliant sun and the tropical forest, Zu An had a bizarre sensation of having returned to his previous life.","Firework stood up, raised her arms, and cheered in excitement.","The staff member driving the jeep didn’t stop her despite her seemingly dangerous actions. These guests were all experts from all over the Myriad Worlds. They would emerge unfazed even if a massive truck crashed into them.","Unaccustomed to Firework’s rowdiness, Tingxue shifted to the side, which brought her closer to Zu An. Her cold aura cooled the scorching weather for him.","Zu An sighed. He had experienced something similar from Yan Xuehen and Chu Chuyan, and he couldn’t help but wonder when they would be reunited. He turned to the staff member driving the jeep and asked, “I heard Dreamland has the power to fulfill wishes. May I know where I can gather more information about this?”","He wanted to know if he could save Chu Chuyan, and if so, what price he would have to pay.","“There’s no rush. Please have a rest at the hotel first. We’ll make arrangements accordingly once our big miss’ coming-of-age ceremony concludes,” the staff member replied with a smile.","“Big miss?” Zu An was surprised.","“Yes, she’s the doted-on daughter of the incumbent master of Dreamland. She’ll be reaching adulthood in a few days. It coincides with your arrival, so you can attend her coming-of-age ceremony, too.”","Zu An frowned. He had no interest in Dreamland’s big miss. If anything, he was unhappy that he was getting delayed over this matter.","Firework, on the other hand, was hyped. “Is your big miss beautiful?”","The staff member was stoked to receive that question. “Our big miss is the most beautiful woman in Dreamland!”","“Oh? Is she as beautiful as our big sister?” Firework hugged Tingxue’s arm as she asked.","The staff member glanced at Tingxue via her rearview mirror and was enchanted. “She’s as beautiful as this esteemed guest.”","“Tsk. You’re just giving me the politically correct answer.” Firework harrumphed in disbelief.","The staff member quickly changed the topic to not offend her. “Our big miss will be conducting Dreamland’s rite after her coming-of-age ceremony. She’ll answer your questions then.”","Zu An could tell that Dreamland had planned it as such, as there was no point in probing now. I’ll have to wait for that rite or something.","The jeep soon arrived at the seaside. Dashing men and beautiful ladies sunbathed on the beach. It was a beautiful sight.","Firework whistled. “I made the right choice. Let’s play at the beach once we settle into our rooms.”","Zu An’s eyebrows shot up when he thought about Firework and Tingxue wearing bikinis. That made his heart pump vigorously. No wonder they say all men are pig trotters.","Tingxue frowned, but she didn’t respond either. She wasn’t too interested in this matter.","The jeep stopped before a hotel. Looking at the extravagant hotel, Firework murmured, “It’s a bit tacky, but I like how bling-blingy it is.”","Zu An was awed by the hotel’s size. Even with his divine sense, he couldn’t perceive its entirety. It was almost as if this hotel were a world of its own.","“This way, please.” The staff member stepped forward to lead the way. “Please take your invitation letter to the receptionist to register.”","Right as they entered the hotel, a commotion broke out in front of them. A guest was fumbling around while exclaiming, “Someone stole my invitation letter!”"]},{"number":2779,"title":"Chapter 2779: Chapter 2731: One Punch Man","paragraphs":["A hulking man with goat horns was patting down his body while glaring at those around him, as if trying to determine who stole his invitation letter.","The female receptionist was put on the spot. “Esteemed guest, we need your invitation letter to register you.”","“You sent the invitation letter over. Surely you must have a record of it? You would know whether I have the invitation letter or not if you just look it up,” the hulking man said with a harrumph.","“My apologies. Our invitation letters are unnamed,” the female receptionist explained.","“The Universal Conglomerate’s staff members who drove me here can testify for me. So can your staff members who escorted me from the spaceport to the space elevator,” the hulking man said in displeasure.","“My apologies, but our staff members won’t vet your invitation letters. You have to register with your invitation letter here,” the female receptionist gave a formal response.","“Apologies, apologies! All you can do is apologize. How do you intend to resolve this matter?” The hulking man lost his patience. “I still had the invitation letter with me when I alighted from the spaceship, but it suddenly disappeared when I passed through your spaceport and space elevator. I suspect your staff members stole my invitation letter!”","The female receptionist’s expression turned cold. “Please do not malign our staff members. They would never steal our guests' possessions. We only recognize our guests by their invitation letters and not by their faces. If you do not have an invitation letter, I’ll have my colleague send you back to the spaceport. In the meantime, please wait by the side so that you don’t hinder the guests behind you from registering.”","The hulking man was enraged. “Do you know who I am? How dare you speak to me like that!”","Four Dreamland guards walked over. “Guest, please calm down!”","The guards tried to move the hulking man aside, but the latter unleashed a terrifying aura and shook them off. “Scram! Who do you think you are, to dare lay your hands on me?!”","Zu An was astounded. The four guards were extremely powerful—personnel dispatched by Dreamland to maintain order here were bound to be anything but weak. Yet the four of them combined were still no match for the hulking man. The aura he'd unleashed was even stronger than Fire Knight’s.","The other guests watched the conflict with interest. This was a chance to gauge how strong Dreamland was.","The hulking man proudly declared, “I am the master of nine stellar systems. How dare you lackeys attempt to manhandle me? I’ll spare you out of respect for Dreamland. Hurry up and register me!”","He cast a sweeping gaze at the surrounding crowd and continued, “Pray that I don’t find out who stole my invitation letter, or else I’m going to rip that person to shreds!”","Some guests were intimidated by his threat, but others remained calm, and yet others responded with disdain.","It was then that a lazy voice echoed, “What happened here?”","The crowd parted to allow a tall, beautiful figure to enter. There were two things about her that immediately caught people’s attention.","One was her impeccable thighs—they were long, but they perfectly filled out her tight jeans. The other was her tight shirt that resembled that of an office lady, though it looked more casual.","Dreamland should give fitting uniforms to their employees. Her clothes are too small for her! Look at those buttons! They're on the verge of popping out. Ugh, it’s hard not to imagine just how huge she must be. It’s both annoying and amazing how the shirt doesn’t give us a peek of what’s beneath.","Her sexy yet conservative clothes made it hard to get a grasp of her personality. She had a beautiful face, too, but it was nowhere as eye-catching as her incredible figure and tight clothes.","She had a lollipop in her mouth, and she exuded an air of laziness, discipline, seductiveness, and innocence... It was hard to imagine how all these traits could appear in a person simultaneously.","Firework nudged Tingxue. “Big sister Xue, I knew there were no good men in the world. Look at how they're gaping at that woman.”","Tingxue maintained a look of impassiveness, not replying to that remark.","Zu An’s face heated up, knowing Firework was talking about him. “I’m trying to assess how strong she is.”","“So what’s your verdict? E or G?” Firework rolled her eyes.","Zu An was speechless.","“Captain Yani, someone is causing trouble here.” The female receptionist quickly filled the woman in about the chain of events.","The hulking man was enraged. “Don’t talk nonsense, lass! Who’s causing trouble? You’re the ones intentionally making things difficult for me.”","“I am the guard captain, Yani. Guest, you may direct your problems to me.” Yani stepped in front of the female receptionist to protect her.","The hulking man looked at Yani’s voluptuous figure and coughed softly. “Fine, I’ll drop this matter on Captain Yani’s account. Hurry up and register me. I want to rest now. Captain Yani, may I have the honor of sharing dinner with you?”","Yani waved her hand. “Guest, please register with your invitation letter first. I’ll consider whether to share dinner with you afterward.”","The hulking man’s expression darkened. “Are you toying with me now? You already know that someone has stolen my invitation letter.”","Yani’s expression turned cold. “If you don’t have an invitation letter, you aren’t a guest of Dreamland. Are you going to leave by yourself, or do I have to send someone to escort you out?”","“You bitch!” No one dared to challenge the hulking man in the stellar systems he ruled over. He had never suffered such grievances before. Unable to take it, he swiped his hand at Yani.","Since they refuse to listen to logic, you shouldn’t blame me for resorting to violence! I bet this voluptuous lass will be fun to play with.","None of the guests tried to play the hero. They wanted to see how strong the guard captain was, so that they could gauge Dreamland’s strength.","Yani responded by hurling out a simple fist.","The hulking man narrowed his eyes in astonishment. He realized he had made a grievous mistake, but it was too late for regret. Yani’s fist collided with his, causing his fist to burst into a bloody mist.","But the attack didn’t stop there. Yani’s fist continued advancing toward his head and popped it like a watermelon.","The powerful shockwave from her fist smashed a hole through the clouds and the atmosphere, revealing vast space and the worlds beyond. It took a while before the worlds faded from sight, and the clouds converged to cover the hole.","The noisy hotel lobby plunged into silence."]},{"number":2780,"title":"Chapter 2780: Chapter 2732: Dreamland’s Service","paragraphs":["The crowd was stunned.","Despite knowing that Dreamland had to possess formidable military might to have survived so many years, they hadn’t expected this curvaceous woman who looked like a trophy wife to be this powerful.","She'd shattered the atmosphere with a single punch, revealing countless worlds in the universe. Her strength was top-notch even in the Myriad Worlds. Most experts of this caliber were famous kings in the Myriad Worlds, but who could this woman be?","The previously amused spectators were now horrified and grim. They wondered if they would meet the same fate as the hulking goat-horned man if they were faced with that punch, and their answer wasn't optimistic. Only a handful could remain composed.","Yani lazily eyed the crowd. “You’re welcome in Dreamland, but please don’t cause any trouble. We have fine wine for friends, but fists for enemies.”","She waved her fists intimidatingly, prompting many guests to retreat several steps for fear of ending up in the same plight as the hulking man.","Her threat worked, as the previously chaotic scene immediately became orderly. No one else dared to cause trouble.","Firework murmured in awe, “That woman is incredible. Big sister Xue, can she beat you?”","Tingxue didn’t respond, though her expression remained calm.","Firework had expected such a response, so she turned to Zu An and asked, “How many strikes of hers do you think you could withstand?”","Zu An shook his head. “I wouldn’t last even a single strike.”","“No, I’m sure you can handle her.” Firework enjoyed Zu An’s look of confusion as she gleefully continued, “Someone with as many wives as you is bound to be good at humoring women. Yani, as formidable as she is, is ultimately a woman. We’re counting on you to settle her, so we can have a smooth-sailing journey in Dreamland.”","Zu An was speechless.","“Why are you staring at me? If Yani were a dashing man, I’d have made a move.” Firework harrumphed.","Even Tingxue looked over. Zu An couldn’t be bothered to respond to Firework's nonsense, though.","Soon, it was their turn to register. As they handed their invitation letters over, they couldn’t help but be more awed by Yani’s incredible figure now that they were looking at her up close. She was very tall, standing at least at 1.9 meters, if not two meters.","Standing next to her, Firework looked like a potato. She was more beautiful, but height was a powerful weapon when two people were put in the same frame. Seemingly oblivious to this, she leaned over to Yani and asked, “Miss, do you have a boyfriend?”","“I don’t. Do you plan to introduce one to me?” After confirming their invitation letter, Yani dropped her frosty demeanor and responded to Firework’s question with a smile.","“What do you think about him? His heart fluttered earlier when he saw your earlier punch.” Firework dragged Zu An forward.","Zu An was speechless. What’s wrong with this woman?","Yani assessed Zu An. “He’s indeed dashing, but I’ll be too busy maintaining Dreamland’s order to date anyone.”","That was a subtle rejection, but Firework acted as if she didn’t get it. “Does that mean you’ll be keeping all of us safe?”","“Of course. We are obliged to ensure the safety of our guests,” Yani replied.","“That works! Look at how weak he is compared to the experts around us. It’s as if he'll disappear with a poof if someone tries to harm him. You should protect him at close range lest that happens,” Firework said.","The weird looks cast by the other guests made Zu An feel incredibly awkward. He quickly dragged Firework back and said, “Miss, please don’t mind her. My little sister is joking.”","But Yani chuckled. “I’m afraid that with the responsibilities I shoulder, I can’t protect you at close range, but you can take this. Press it if you’re in danger, and I’ll rush over right away.”","She handed a coinlike item into Zu An’s hand. It was a signal transmitter, and she would sense it if he pressed it.","Zu An wanted to say more, but Firework shoved him back and said, “Thank you, big sister Yani. My big brother will send you an invitation when you have more time.”","Zu An was speechless.","After they left, another bold customer tried the same method on Yani. Despite her ferocity, her figure was nothing short of incredible. Winning over an expert like her would be quite the thrill.","But Yani roared with a darkened expression, “Scram!”","“Right away!”","The other guests burst into laughter.","“Do you think anyone can pull off that move?”","“You should take a look in the mirror!”","A hotel staff member led Zu An’s group to their rooms. Firework had requested for them to be placed next to one another. Zu An’s room was in the middle, Tingxue's was on the left, and Firework's was to the right.","“Let’s head to the beach together after changing our clothes!” Firework told the other two before closing her door.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. He was indeed tempted.","Unfortunately, Tingxue responded by slamming her door shut. Zu An shrugged before closing his door too.","Despite being located next to one another, their rooms were 200-square-meter luxury villas. The floor-to-ceiling glass walls ensured that the room was well-lit while granting a good view of the scenery outside.","Profound spatial technology had been used to expand the rooms. They could have been bigger, but they were kept at their current size for maximum comfort, lest the emptiness feel jarring.","Zu An opened the cupboard and found all kinds of clothes inside. They were automatically adjusted to suit the guest’s size. It was also then that a voice recording played, informing him that he could request clothing of any style, and the hotel would tailor them on the spot and deliver them right away.","“As expected of Dreamland.” Zu An had no interest in clothes, but he could already imagine the neighboring Firework squealing in delight. He took some time exploring his room before lying on the bed, picking up an introduction booklet, and browsing through it.","A hologram was projected from the booklet, and it prompted him to select a language before introducing the room facilities to him. Zu An thought to himself that even imperial palaces weren’t as comfortable as this.","However, his attention was soon drawn to a specific function. The hotel provided a list of portraits of beauties to choose from if the guests were feeling lonely.","“These beauties are renowned celebrities in their respective worlds. They are contracted by Dreamland to fulfill your demands. You may view their holographic information and introduction by tapping their portrait.","“Once a beauty is chosen, we will send them to your room in the shortest time possible. There is no need to worry about a breach in privacy; they will not remember what happens in the room.","“Also, all expenses incurred within the hotel will be shouldered by Dreamland.”"]},{"number":2781,"title":"Chapter 2781: Chapter 2733: Missing","paragraphs":["Zu An was amazed.","No wonder this place is called Dreamland. It is indeed a dream to men. Hold on, what about female guests? Are their lists filled with all kinds of hot male stars? How can a gentleman like me read this kind of nonsensical content?","He tossed the list aside and continued observing the other guests on the beach outside his windows. It broadened his horizons—there were people of all shapes and sizes.","There was a four-legged shark wearing sneakers and holding a wooden bat, a wooden puppet with a massive head, a flying crocodile, an elephant covered in thorns... There were all kinds of civilizations in the Myriad Worlds, so much so that they stretched the limits of the imagination.","A while later, he started getting distracted. He eventually returned to his bed and picked up the list. I’m not being lustful. It’s just a way to investigate other civilizations in the Myriad Worlds.","He took a casual flip and was awed by the variety before him. They boasted different charms, be it innocent or seductive, slim or curvaceous... It helped that the list was neatly categorized, so he could easily pick based on his preferences.","There were also different lists such as ‘Trending’, ‘High Reviews’, ‘Popular’, ‘Most Clicks’, ‘Monthly Board’, ‘Daily Board’, etc.","Zu An’s eyes were opened. He clicked on the ‘Overall’ ranking, and those on the list were indeed gorgeous. It wasn’t a surprise, since they had survived harsh market testing.","Huh? Why don’t I see that female celebrity from the space elevator?","He tapped on the celebrities’ profiles and soon noticed a pattern.","In the Myriad Worlds, the primary factions were the Starcloud Empire and Freedom Confederation. Both powers controlled many universes, and the sheer number of planets under their control was uncountable. They were hostile to each other, but they were also equally matched.","Other than these two major powers, there were also many influential powers, such as the Universal Conglomerate.","There were also many different types of civilizations, such as pure cybernetic civilizations made up entirely of robots. They boasted high learning ability and had their consciousness linked to the internet, making them terrifying.","There were also reptilian, arthropod, and fungal civilizations. In particular, planets populated by the latter were to be feared.","...","The celebrities on the list could satisfy every racial fetish a person had. Zu An was, once again, awed by how lust was a strong motivator for progress.","In my previous life, many guys self-learned Japanese through adult films. To think I’d be learning about different civilizations across the Myriad Worlds via this.","A thought soon occurred to him as he flipped through the list of female celebrities. While some of them carried unique racial traits, he couldn’t help noticing most of them were humanoid, but why would that be the case?","Is it a coincidence or an inevitability...","While Zu An was pondering that question, someone knocked on his door. Firework called out, and Zu An instinctively rushed over to open the door.","When he saw what was on the other side, he was stunned.","Firework was wearing an adorable yet sexy bikini. Her slender waist, fair belly, and long, slender legs perfectly encapsulated the concept of youthful vibrance.","“Does your room have...” Firework was about to ask a question when she noticed the list in his hand. Her eyes widened into a glare. “Shame on you! What nonsense are you reading...”","“I was doing research...”","Firework interjected before he could finish his piece. “Of all things you could research, why are you researching that! I noticed that too when I was changing my clothes. I wondered if you’d be ensnared by that, so I came over to take a look. I knew it! Big brother, you’re a disappointment!”","“...” I really am doing research. Knowing she wouldn’t believe him either way, Zu An asked, “Is it also female celebrities on your side?”","“Of course not. It’s a bunch of pale-faced moochlords. Ugh, how disgusting. None can match you, big brother.” Firework harrumphed. She snatched his list, stuffed a firecracker into it, and tossed it onto the ground.","With a loud explosion, the list was blasted to bits.","Zu An was speechless. My research material!","“Stop looking at that. Big sister Xue and I look much better. Let’s go to the beach. Hurry up and change your clothes. I’ll go call big sister Xue.” Firework pushed him before the wardrobe before running over to knock on the next door.","Zu An was stunned. This woman just makes herself comfortable with anyone.","There was no way to continue his research after his list had been destroyed. Maybe I can gather more information by interacting with other guests on the beach. He changed into leisurely beach shorts and headed to the neighboring room.","Firework eyed his perfect abs, and her face reddened. “You’re surprisingly ripped.”","Zu An ignored her remark and asked, “Is Miss Tingxue not in her room?”","“She isn’t opening her door.” Firework pouted. An idea popped into her mind, and she said aloud, “Big sister Xue, big brother Zu has changed his clothes and is waiting for you too.”","The door soon opened. “I told you I’m not going...”","Tingxue noticed their revealing beachwear and blushed.","Firework chuckled. “I guess big brother Zu’s name works the best.”","Zu An eyed Tingxue. She has already lost her emotions. Surely not.","Tingxue coldly replied, “I don’t like that kind of clothing. Don’t bother calling me anymore.” She slammed her door shut afterward.","Zu An felt a mixture of disappointment and relief. He was disappointed at not getting to see her in a swimsuit, but he was also relieved that no one else could see someone who resembled Yan Xuehen wearing that.","Firework shrugged. She stuck out her tongue adorably and said, “Since she isn’t going, let’s go by ourselves.”","Zu An let her drag him to the beach. He took out the towel he had prepared beforehand and draped it on her.","Firework laughed. “What’s wrong? You can’t bear others seeing my skin?”","Zu An was surprised by his own actions as well. As a transmigrator, he had been to swimming pools, beaches, and saunas many times before. He was more than accustomed to such skimpy wear. Why would I subconsciously try to cover her?","Firework was delighted to see him stumped. Just then, she noticed his pendant and reached out to grab it. “Ooh, this pendant is gorgeous.”","Zu An instinctively guarded the pendant, which made Firework harrumph. “How stingy! Why are you so nervous about the pendant? Did your girlfriend give it to you?”","Zu An answered with a nod. The Jing Teng sisters were still residing in the pendant.","Only guests carrying invitation letters were allowed in Dreamland. It was forbidden to bring anyone else along. Fortunately, their true body was a talisman paper, so there was no need to worry about anyone finding them.","Upon hearing his answer, Firework’s mood plummeted.","The two of them made their way to the beach amid silence. Whistles could be heard now and then from their surroundings—many men were mesmerized by Firework’s beauty.","Firework walked straight toward the sea, tossing her towel onto the beach before diving into the water, swimming around energetically like a dolphin. This reminded Zu An of Shang Liuyu and Shang Hongyu. The sight of them frolicking in the water was enchanting.","A while later, however, Zu An’s eyes narrowed. It had been a while since Firework surfaced from the water, and he couldn’t see her silhouette in the sea either!"]},{"number":2782,"title":"Chapter 2782: Chapter 2734: Rescue","paragraphs":["Zu An rushed to the seaside. “Firework, where are you?”","He infused ki into his voice, such that even people fifty kilometers away would be able to hear him. Unfortunately, there was no response.","He leaped into the sea and spread his divine sense outward. When he detected a massive shadow several kilometers away, his expression darkened. The shadow couldn’t have been a hotel guest, and there wasn't supposed to be such a behemoth loitering on the beach near the hotel. Thus, he anxiously flew over.","Just then, there was an explosion. Tsunamis over fifty meters tall gushed from the sea. Guests on the beach exclaimed in astonishment, having noticed that something was amiss.","Zu An was startled. The explosion had come from Firework’s firecrackers. She must have met with danger! Knowing this wasn’t the time to be wondering where she hid her firecrackers in her skimpy bikini, he rushed over.","He spotted Firework’s silhouette amid the waves. She was desperately swimming toward the shore, but a massive shadow flickered behind her, and she was dragged backward.","Zu An quickly drew his sword and slashed at the shadow, his sword ki slicing the sea in two.","The crowd could finally see what the shadow was. It was a mountain-like sea monster emanating such a terrifying aura that the guests escaped to the hotel in a fluster. There were hardly any weaklings in Dreamland, but no one wanted to fight this behemoth from the sea.","A few people watched Zu An with curiosity. That fellow doesn’t seem strong, so how is he able to unleash such tremendous force with his sword as to slice the sea in half?","Pu!","Zu An’s sword ki landed on the sea monster, causing it to bleed profusely. However, the creature was so huge that it was unfazed by wounds that would usually be fatal. It wriggled and dove into the deeper sea, displaying speed that was at odds with its massive size.","Zu An activated the Crown of the Ocean Deity’s ability. Wherever the sea monster dove, the seawater automatically parted.","Boom!","With no seawater to support it, the monster crashed right into the seabed. Fresh blood oozed from its mouth, nose, and various parts of its body. If they had been further away from the shore, where the seabed was deeper, this maneuver could have taken the monster’s life.","Zu An flitted over and was about to grab Firework’s hand when the sea monster suddenly emanated a peculiar light, and in the next instant, it disappeared with Firework.","Zu An was shocked. That appeared to be teleportation. The sea monster had to have set a safe teleportation point somewhere in the sea, so it could teleport there whenever its life was in danger.","Zu An combed the sea, but despite searching tens of thousands of kilometers, he found no traces of the sea monster and Firework. He knew what he was doing was the equivalent of searching for a needle in the haystack, but he couldn’t sit still when his companion was in danger.","He used the Sea God Crown’s ability to commune with nearby sea creatures, and he soon found a lead.","He advanced another twenty kilometers and stumbled upon an area of the sea that was bombarded by intense lightning. There was some kind of formation there. This left him with no choice but to return to the hotel first.","The only silver lining was that the sea monster didn’t intend to hurt Firework, or else she would have been gone in a chomp.","On the way, Zu An bumped into a white silhouette—Tingxue. She said, “I just arrived. I lost your trail.”","“Thanks for coming!” Zu An had been searching the sea, so it was normal for her to be unable to find him. “Let’s head back and talk.”","When they returned to the hotel, they saw infuriated guests questioning the hotel staff, asking how there could be such dangerous sea monsters lurking in the vicinity of the beach. It was an unfamiliar lady this time, but it could be them next time!","Guard Captain Yani tried her best to maintain order while placating the guests. “Please be assured that the area around our beach has always been safe. We implemented anti-shark nets and defensive formations within a ten-kilometer radius...”","Unfortunately, the crowd wasn’t going to let things slip. They furiously questioned her about the sea monster. They had seen it with their own eyes, after all.","Yani was also at a loss. “We’re investigating the incident. Please calm down...”","But such words were insufficient to placate the crowd.","Just then, Zu An returned and loudly asked, “What’s going on out at sea? Why is there violent lightning in the deeper parts of the sea? There seems to be some kind of mysterious formation there. Is it from Dreamland?”","Yani was taken aback. “It’s not from Dreamland. The sea has gotten more violent in recent years, and sea monsters have occasionally appeared in the vicinity. However, we have never had a sea monster approach the beach before...”","Those words further stoked the guests’ anger. They angrily said that Dreamland wasn’t taking care of their guests’ safety.","Just then, a gentle voice called out, “The safety of our guests is our utmost priority. Put your mind at ease. There has never been a security incident in the many times we have hosted the Dream Gathering. I’ll offer you a satisfactory explanation once we get to the bottom of the matter.”","The crowd looked over and saw a seductive woman sashaying her way down the stairs. She had naturally curly hair, and her body swayed as she moved. Many guests looked at her with heated gazes.","“Paying respect to the Ninth Elder!” Yani and the other staff members bowed.","The crowd was taken aback. This woman is of even higher standing than Yani?","“It’s my pleasure to meet all of you. I am Diodora from the Dreamland Elder Council.” The seductive woman did a simple introduction. “I have been made aware of the incident at the beach, but there is something amiss about it. It should have been impossible for the sea monster to appear in the vicinity of the beach...”","Zu An sneered, “Are you saying that I put my friend’s life at risk to slander you?”","Several guests supported him. They had witnessed the incident, and this female elder was trying to shirk responsibility for it.","“We’ll get to the bottom of this...”","Before she could finish speaking, Zu An interjected, “I don’t need you to investigate this incident. I need you to help me save my friend!”","It would be difficult for him to single-handedly breach that mysterious sea region, and who knew if the sea monster had any helpers?","“I was about to get to that.” Diodora turned to the guard captain and said, “Yani, take your guards on board our combat ship and journey into the sea to rescue that guest.”","Yani was hesitant. “But the security here...”","“Don’t worry. I’ll take charge,” Diodora replied with a smile.","Yani breathed a sigh of relief. “With the Ninth Elder present, I’m sure everything will be fine.”","The guests assessed Diodora as they wondered if this seductive female elder was even stronger than Yani.","Yani went up to Zu An and said, “Guest, please come with me.”","Zu An was about to leave when Tingxue spoke up. “I’ll go with you.”","Another person in the crowd chimed in. “I’m coming as well.”"]},{"number":2783,"title":"Chapter 2783: Chapter 2735: The Brightest Pearl in Space","paragraphs":["The crowd looked over.","The voice came from a sprightly young lady with golden hair that glowed brilliantly under the hotel’s light. She had blue eyes that resembled the deep ocean. Her graceful dress suggested that she was from a powerful family.","Zu An was perplexed. Why was the other party offering to tag along when he didn’t know her?","Could she be Firework’s friend? But Firework has never mentioned her, and I don’t think I’ve ever seen the two of them together.","While he was feeling confused, someone had already recognized her. “Isn’t she the granddaughter of the Acadia House’s patriarch, the first in line to inherit the house?”","“The Acadias, who are ranked top three in the Round Table Council?”","“You’re talking about the Universal Conglomerate’s brightest pearl?”","“Who else other than her?”","“Wow. Isn’t it often said that the Acadias possess wealth that can match a nation?”","...","Zu An was surprised.","Employee 9527 had told him that the Universal Conglomerate’s highest leadership was the Round Table Council, which consisted of seven people. Of the seven people, there were three that wielded considerably greater influence and authority.","Those three were of equal stature. They were the founders of the Universal Conglomerate, and it wouldn’t be far-fetched to say that they were its true owners.","The Acadia House was one of the three founding houses. If that lady was the Acadia House’s first miss, it would be a gross understatement to say that her family wealth matched a nation's.","A white-haired butler anxiously stepped forward to dissuade the golden-haired miss. “Miss, you mustn’t put yourself in danger for a stranger.”","The golden-haired miss shook her head. She walked straight up to Zu An and curtsied. “Pleased to meet you. I am Isabella Acadia.”","Zu An returned the greeting. After a quick self-introduction, he asked, “Miss Acadia, may I ask why...”","“Please, call me Isabella,” the golden-haired lady said with a sweet smile. “I sense the aura of our Universal Conglomerate’s golden friendship emblem from you. It shows that we’re indebted to you. As a member of the Acadia House, I can’t turn a blind eye when you’re in need of help.”","Upon hearing those words, the other guests looked at Zu An in a different light.","They hadn’t expected this humble-looking chap to have the Universal Conglomerate’s legendary golden friendship emblem. As long as he had this emblem in hand, he would be taken care of wherever the Universal Conglomerate’s influence extended.","And now that he had struck a connection with the Acadia’s first miss, he was practically on a rocketship bound for greatness!","Zu An was grateful. “Thank you, Isabella!”","The old butler stepped back with a sigh, though he continued to look worried.","With Isabella joining the crew, other guests began enthusiastically offering their help, hoping to forge a connection with the Acadias’ first miss. It helped that Isabella was beautiful and adorable as well.","Seeing that, Diodora said with a smile, “Our big miss will be holding her coming-of-age ceremony two days later. She’ll be hosting the Dream Gathering this time. If you have any wish, you can relay it to our big miss there. If you can pay the price, Dreamland will fulfill your wish.","“Unfortunately, you won’t be able to participate in the Dream Gathering if you miss the timing. There are too many variables to this rescue operation. Captain Yani, you’re more experienced in this field. Do you think two days will be enough to make a return trip?”","Yani leaned against the pillar as she lazily replied, “Dreamland has always had a hostile relationship with the ocean races. We’re venturing into their turf this time. It’s unlikely we’ll be able to make it back within two days.”","Those words prompted many guests to retract their offer to help.","“Ah, I just remembered I have other matters to attend to. I’m afraid I won’t be able to join you for the rescue operation.”","The others gave similar excuses too. The volunteer count for the rescue operation plummeted.","Zu An frowned. He had traveled to Dreamland to find a way to save Chu Chuyan and reunite with the Goddess of Wu Mountain and the ancient Mermaid Queen. There was no saying when a second opportunity would arise if he missed this one.","I’m not as close to Firework, and there’s no guarantee she’s still alive after being captured by the sea monster...","In the end, his gaze hardened in determination. Firework had helped him a lot along the way. How could he turn a blind eye to her when she was in need of help?","I’ll find another way to save Chu Chuyan and the others...","Having made up his mind, he stepped forward and said, “Captain Yani, let’s set off quickly.”","The longer they waited, the more danger Firework would be in.","Yani was surprised. She hadn’t expected him to give up this opportunity for a woman. A mischievous smile crept onto her face as she said, “I didn’t think you’d be the sentimental type. Let’s go.”","Tingxue calmly said, “I’ll go with you.”","Zu An was surprised. “But you might miss the Dream Gathering.”","“Firework is my friend as well,” Tingxue said flatly. “I already don’t have many friends. I don’t want to lose another one.”","Zu An felt a warm surge in his heart. Tingxue had appeared nonchalant or even impatient to Firework’s incessant chatter. He hadn’t expected Tingxue to already consider Firework a friend.","Isabella stepped forward and said, “Don’t forget about me.”","The old butler was startled. “Big miss, the Dream Gathering is of utmost importance...”","Isabella interjected, “What dreams do you think I could have that requires Dreamland to fulfill?”","The old butler was rendered speechless. With the Acadias’ immense fortune, Isabella could even get someone to pluck the stars in the sky for her. In the many years he had served her, nothing had been beyond her reach.","A few other guests joined the rescue operation. To them, Dreamland’s promise felt unrealistic, not to mention they wouldn't necessarily be able to afford their wish. In contrast, the Universal Conglomerate’s Isabella Acadia was very real, and forging close ties with her could bring about great benefits in the future.","Even better, if one could win Isabella’s heart, they could soar through the skies like a phoenix.","“Feel free to follow us if you aren’t afraid of death.” Yani grabbed a coat, flung it on her shoulders, and made her way to the harbor.","A combat ship was waiting there. It resembled a modern military frigate, equipped with cannons, missile launchers, and radar. There were older-looking weapons inscribed with runes too, possibly weapons from magic civilizations.","This bolstered Zu An’s confidence. With the aid of this powerful ship, Yani, Tingxue, and other experts onboard, his chances of rescuing Firework were much higher now."]},{"number":2784,"title":"Chapter 2784: Chapter 2736: Doubt","paragraphs":["Since they were setting off to rescue someone, there was no excessive bureaucratic paperwork. It didn’t take long for the military frigate to set off.","The vessel traveled at an incredible speed. Some kind of force at the frigate’s bow parted the seawater in half, allowing it to sail with minimal resistance. On top of that, there were waves alongside the frigate that pushed it ahead. This was likely the result of a powerful formation.","Most of the guests gathered around Isabella, wanting to get close to her. They weren’t interested in rescuing Firework; they just wanted to capitalize on this rare opportunity to socialize with the Acadias’ successor.","The white-haired butler stepped in front of Isabella to ensure the guests maintained their distance from her.","Isabella maintained a dignified front, showing no impatience whatsoever. She took care of everyone’s emotions, leaving them with a sense of accomplishment, as if she were granting them each special treatment.","Zu An was impressed. As expected of a powerful house’s successor. Her socializing skill is incredible.","But he wasn’t in the mood to fawn on her. He stood at the frigate’s bow and observed the ocean. It's been a while since Firework was captured. I wonder if she’s still safe.","Dark clouds gathered in the distance, and the waves grew choppier.","Looking at the darkened sky, Zu An had an ominous premonition. The book in his mind flipped open, revealing a white skeleton image. He was reminded of the divination Qi Yaoguang had made before he left the Cultivation World. Could the danger she divined be related to this trip?","He had crossed blows with that sea monster. It was powerful, but not impossible to overcome. Additionally, he was accompanied by top experts, including Tingxue and Yani. Isabella and her butler were also no doubt formidable in their own right, or else they wouldn’t dare to join the trip.","The other guests are experts as well, and Dreamland has provided us with a good frigate. We should have the advantage here.","Even so, Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. His unease intensified.","Just then, Yani emerged from the cabin. She spotted Tingxue standing by the railing and was immediately enchanted. Tingxue’s hair and white dress fluttered in the sea breeze, making her look like a beautiful portrait.","Yani retracted her gaze and walked up to Zu An. “Are you sure this is the right direction?”","Zu An instinctively took a step back. He wasn't short by any means, but this woman was towering. When she was standing in front of him, he could only see her strained shirt button, and that put some pressure on him.","“Indeed. The ocean creatures told me this was the way.”","He had communicated with ocean beings through the Crown of the Ocean Deity to obtain a rough direction.","Yani’s eyebrows shot up. “Oh? It seems you have the ability to commune with the ocean.”","It wasn't hard to figure that out when she had seen him part the ocean water when battling the sea monster by the beach.","Zu An didn’t deny it. “What lies in the depths of the ocean?”","Yani shook her head. “We don’t know.”","Zu An was bewildered. “Aren’t you the masters of Dreamland? Surely you should know the situation on this planet, no?”","Yani sighed. “As you said, it’s ‘Dreamland’ and not ‘Dreamocean’. We govern the land. Anything else is beyond our jurisdiction.”","Zu An was speechless. I don’t even know how to refute that.","Yani looked into the distance and said, “All we know is that the ocean is a forbidden zone. We have sent experts in to explore the area, but none returned alive.”","Zu An’s heart shuddered. If even she's saying that, the Dreamocean must indeed be dangerous.","“If it’s that dangerous, why did you open a hotel next to the beach?” Zu An asked angrily. Firework wouldn’t have met with danger if not for that.","“Only the forbidden zones in Dreamland are dangerous. The other places are very safe. We have always maintained a non-interference policy with the sea monsters. It’s only in recent days that ferocious sea monsters started appearing in the vicinity. Even so, we never expected one to invade our beach,” Yani said with a frown, as if she couldn’t make sense of the situation either.","Anger surged into Zu An’s mind, but he forced himself to calm down. There was no point assigning blame right now, especially when he was relying on Yani’s help to rescue Firework.","“Do you have a way to pass through the lightning sea?”","“This frigate can withstand the lightning at the outer perimeter, but the lightning grows stronger the further we venture in. We don’t have the means to reach the inner area. If we can’t find your friend in the outer perimeter, I’m afraid...” Yani didn’t finish her sentence, but her intent was relayed loud and clear.","Zu An’s heart sank. I reckon Firework won’t be able to withstand the terrifying lightning either.","“Don’t you think there’s something weird about this matter?” Yani suddenly asked.","“How so?” Zu An replied.","“We haven’t had any conflict with the sea monsters for thousands of years, but they suddenly appeared on our beach.”","“Hah. You already mentioned that ferocious sea monsters have recently appeared in the vicinity, but you didn’t take any preventive measures. That’s just an accident waiting to happen.”","“Contrary to what you may believe, we did take thorough protective measures. We installed anti-shark nets and protective formations. It shouldn’t have been possible for a sea monster to enter our beach.”","“But it just happened.”","“What you see may not be the whole truth.”","“What do you mean?”","“I understand how you feel, but don’t you find it weird? Sea monsters crave flesh and blood. They don’t hesitate to devour a person if a chance arises. And yet, that sea monster kidnapped your friend instead of eating her.” Yani paused. “Do you think it’s normal for sea monsters to kidnap a person?”","Zu An frowned. “Sea monsters have sentience. They might be up to something.”","Yani chuckled. “Do you truly understand that friend of yours?”","Zu An stiffened up. He did have an inkling of suspicion, but he hadn't thought deeper into it. Perhaps others would think they were a couple in love, but he had only met Firework not long ago on the Universal Conglomerate’s spaceship. Other than her name and her faith, he knew nothing about her. Even those things could be fake.","He thought about how friendly Firework had been to him from their first meeting. Could she have other motives?","Judging from his expression, Yani could tell that her words were getting through, so she continued, “We’ll do our best to rescue the guest, but I am responsible for the safety of the other guests onboard, too. I seek your understanding in this.”","Shortly after Yani left, Zu An suddenly felt the temperature plummet. He turned around and saw Tingxue walking to his side.","“I overheard your conversation.”","“What’s your take?”","“I can’t say much, but I sense Firework bears no malice.”","Her words cleared the fog in Zu An’s mind. That’s true. Firework might have been keeping secrets from me, but it doesn’t mean she’s hostile. There’s no need to overthink.","Just then, the frigate’s siren blared. A shadow appeared on the distant ocean surface."]},{"number":2785,"title":"Chapter 2785: Chapter 2737: A Bizarre Dragon","paragraphs":["There was no lack of experts on the frigate, and they quickly identified the shadow to be a massive iceberg in the ocean. Unlike other clear and pristine icebergs, this one was grayish and dull.","“Careful! There’s an iceberg ahead,” one of the crew members shouted.","“Shatter it,” Yani commanded.","Their frigate was big enough to crash through most icebergs without taking any damage, but she sensed something amiss about the iceberg and thus decided to play it safe.","The crew members shot beams at the iceberg.","The white-haired butler pulled Isabella behind him for protection, whereas the other guests quickly gathered around Isabella while uttering cheesy lines like “Don’t worry, I’ll protect you.”","Zu An watched as the destructive beam struck the iceberg.","Boom!","A third of the iceberg was shaved away, and cracks appeared in other areas. It looked as if it was going to shatter very soon.","But the crowd on the frigate looked grim. Normal icebergs would have completely shattered upon being struck by that beam, yet only a portion of it had shattered after so many attacks. Something was off about it.","The relatively calm ocean suddenly became tumultuous, as if the surrounding water had begun to boil. Huge waves raged, undermining even the frigate’s stability formation. As a result, those standing on the deck began sliding from side to side.","“Be careful, big miss!”","“Guests, please make sure to hold onto something.”","“Prepare for battle!”","...","The ocean ahead of them slowly parted, and an enormous dragon raised its head.","The crowd finally understood what that iceberg was. It was a tumor growing on the dragon’s head; it was only encased in thick ice because it was on an ice dragon.","And now, the ice dragon was fuming after having its tumor struck.","Zu An was stunned. It wasn't his first time fighting a dragon, but compared to what stood before him, the ones he'd fought were nothing more than snakes. The pressure he felt was on a completely different level.","He had also never seen a dragon with such a color—it was an unnerving grayish-white.","Dragons weren’t rare entities in the Myriad Worlds. There were even worlds where they were considered a delicacy. For that reason, the guests didn’t show much fear upon seeing this one.","One even flew over and laughed heartily. “Miss Isabella, please watch as I vanquish the beast blocking your way!”","Two more guests joined him to flaunt their valor to Isabella.","Zu An was flabbergasted. I should have known there are bootlickers in every world... But still, are these fellows out of their minds to challenge that dragon? Or are the experts of the Myriad Worlds that strong?","The one who came forward first was worried others would steal his limelight, so he roared, “I’ll be taking the life of this beast!”","He whipped out a spear and charged at the grayish-white dragon with a revolving motion that quickly brewed a tornado. Due to the wind from his movements, a fifty-meter-wide gap formed in the waters, and any fish or sea monsters that came close to the tornado exploded into a bloody mist.","Zu An could tell that it wasn't really a tornado, though. Every gust of wind was a spear sweep. That man’s spearmanship is impressive.","The spearman looked at the grayish-white dragon in front of him and smirked.","This big oaf isn’t reacting even though I’m already this close to it. Hmph! Does it intend to take my ultimate move head-on? It’s courting death!","If I can kill this dragon in a single blow, I might win Miss Isabella’s heart with my valor and rise to the top of the world...","All of a sudden, he narrowed his eyes and exclaimed, “No, this is...”","His words were cut short. The grayish-white dragon opened its mouth and devoured him together with the tornado.","Urp~","As if it was showing respect for the spearman’s all-out attack, the dragon burped.","Zu An was stunned. You were still looking incredible a second ago, so why did you get gobbled up in the next second?","Cold sweat trickled down his back. Had he been up against that spearman, he would have had to resort to his many skills to create a window for victory.","And yet, that spearman hadn’t lasted a second against the dragon. The incredible tornado of spears he'd brewed with his spearmanship had failed to pierce the dragon’s scales.","Mocking laughter echoed from the sky. “Useless. Someone with mediocre skills shouldn’t be sullying Miss Isabella’s eyes. Watch me instead!”","That person murmured an incantation and morphed into a massive avatar that towered even over the dragon. “Miss Isabella, I’ll scale that lizard for you to make a belt.”","The avatar reached out to grab the dragon by the neck. In his eyes, the dragon was merely a massive snake, so it should share the same weakness as well. His hands moved at a speed at odds with his massive size, grabbing the dragon almost instantaneously.","He was about to twist the dragon’s head off when he saw disdain flash through the dragon’s eyes. He exclaimed in horror, “H-how is this possible...”","The dragon’s grayish-white aura crept onto the avatar’s hand, causing it to swiftly deflate like a punctured ball. The aura continued to encroach toward the guest until it finally touched him.","The arrogant man froze up. He plummeted onto the ocean surface, shattering into countless pieces.","The crowd on the frigate was stunned.","The third man in the sky was dressed like a cowboy in a Western movie. He harrumphed. “Only fools would engage an ice dragon in close-quarters combat.”","Zu An frowned. He realized the grayish-white aura wasn't ice, but something he was very familiar with—death energy!","The cowboy made a move before he could be warned, though. He whipped out a gun from his waist. The gun’s barrel extended then continued rapidly transforming as if it had come out of a Transformers movie, until it was a huge cannon barrel.","“Eat my lightning cannon!” The cowboy roared in laughter as he pulled the trigger.","A blue light burst out of the barrel and instantly struck the dragon’s forehead.","Pah!","The dragon’s head exploded, blasting flesh bits into the surroundings. Its body plummeted into the ocean, raising huge waves.","The cowboy descended slightly so that the huge waves could serve as his backdrop. He performed a bow toward the frigate and said, “My dear Miss Isabella, this is my gift to you. Are you satisfied?”","But what he thought was a cool action didn’t spur any reactions. Confused, he raised his head and saw the crowd staring past him with fearful eyes."]},{"number":2786,"title":"Chapter 2786: Chapter 2738: War Goddess","paragraphs":["Taken aback, the cowboy hurriedly turned around.","The dragon who had plummeted into the ocean not long ago had at some point already risen back up. Flesh had fallen off its massive head, revealing the white bones inside.","“How’s that possible?!”","It shouldn’t have been possible for anything to survive after sustaining such injuries, so why was this dragon unfazed?","Unfortunately, the cowboy would never get his answer, as the dragon unleashed a breath that swiftly enveloped him.","A miserable scream could be heard from within the grayish-white breath before abruptly being cut off. When the breath finally dissipated, a white skeleton wearing a cowboy hat and holding onto a gun fell from the sky.","A commotion broke out on the frigate.","Even though those three had been buffoons trying to impress Isabella, they weren’t weak. And yet, they were all killed in a single blow. The dragon was truly dangerous.","Isabella’s eyes reddened. “It’s because of me that they...”","The butler quickly consoled her. “Big miss, this has nothing to do with you.”","The other guests consoled her as well, thinking that her heart was as beautiful as her face. However, after witnessing the trio’s fate, none of them dared to confront the dragon anymore.","Yani shouted from a higher vantage, “Be careful, everyone. That dragon boasts exceptional defensive prowess.”","The crowd could tell as much without her pointing that out. The trio’s attacks were formidable, but they'd failed to deal any concrete damage to the dragon.","The dragon’s head had begun regenerating, and it didn’t take long for it to revert to its original appearance. It was as if the earlier attack had never happened.","“Be careful! It has incredible regeneration, too!”","“Holy shit! Is that dragon a Longevity worshiper?”","...","Upon hearing the discussions on the deck, Zu An frowned.","Isabella walked over and asked, “Mister Zu, are you sure it's death energy?”","“You can’t tell?” Zu An was perplexed. Surely these experts from the Myriad Worlds can recognize death energy, right?","Isabella replied, “Ever since the Deity of Death’s demise, it has been a long time since anyone last saw death energy.”","Zu An was speechless. But the Netherworld is filled with it. As the master of the Netherworld, maybe I have a higher affinity with death energy.","The frigate suddenly shook violently. Isabella screamed as she fell to the side. Due to her walking toward Zu An earlier, the white-haired butler was some distance away and couldn’t reach her in time.","Fortunately, Zu An instinctively reached out to grab her hand with one hand and her waist with the other to stop her from falling. “Are you all right?”","Isabella shook her head. Her cheeks were slightly reddened. “Thank you.”","The white-haired butler was taken aback.","The other guests were anguished. We've been fawning on Miss Isabella, but we never got within a meter of her. But that fellow went ahead to grab her hand and waist! Goddamnit!","Zu An didn’t have time to check on the influx of Rage points in his system, as an enormous tsunami over three hundred meters tall was about to crash into the frigate.","The dragon, enraged by the earlier attack, had begun its counterattack.","The frigate fired its cannons at the tsunami. Amazingly, they managed to blast it away.","The crew members and guests cheered, but that only lasted a second. To their horror, when they spread their divine sense outward, they discovered more tsunamis awaiting them—several hundred, in fact.","The frigate’s weapons were powerful enough to disperse a couple of tsunamis, but the remaining ones would still crash into them nonetheless.","Being struck by a tsunami of such a size would be equivalent to having an entire sea crushing them in an instant. No matter how sturdy the frigate was, it wouldn’t be able to take it.","Yani narrowed her eyes. Her fingers cracked as she clenched her fist. She was about to hurl out a punch when Zu An, standing at the bow of the frigate, suddenly raised his hand.","The raging tsunamis suddenly stopped.","The crowd was stunned.","There were many experts on the frigate, and some wielded the strength to disperse the tsunamis, though they couldn’t ensure that others wouldn’t be hurt by the ocean waves in the wake of their attack.","And if one thing was for certain, none of them had the power to stop all the tsunamis in place the way Zu An had.","Zu An was one of the weaker ones on the frigate. Many of those onboard believed that they could defeat him in a fight. However, they didn’t think they could perform the same feat he had just pulled off, even if they were ten times stronger.","Isabella’s eyes lit up. She couldn’t help but stare at Zu An.","Her suitors clenched their teeth in anger. Damn it! He stole the limelight!","Zu An pressed his palm downward, and the tsunamis returned to the ocean. Such huge movements should have raised gigantic waves and terrifying winds, but that didn’t happen.","The swimming dragon suddenly realized it couldn’t stir the surrounding water anymore, so it raised its head in bewilderment. When it realized the culprit was Zu An, it opened its mouth and roared.","A figure flew out of its mouth, while two other figures rose from the ocean.","It was the trio who had confronted the dragon earlier. Even the cowboy, who'd been reduced to a skeleton earlier, had regrown his flesh, though his skin was eerily pale.","The dragon uttered a bizarre note, and the deceased trio suddenly opened their eyes. Then, their silhouettes flickered as they flashed toward Zu An.","One brandished his spear and morphed into a sharp tornado. Another manifested a massive avatar and hurled a gigantic fist down on the frigate. The third transformed his gun into a cannon and fired it.","The crowd on the frigate was horrified. Death was frightening, but something even more frightening than that was being controlled like a puppet after dying.","Zu An was about to dodge the attacks when Yani suddenly flashed to his side. With a cold harrumph, she first raised her palm and grabbed the incoming cannonball, extinguishing it. Then, she tossed it back at the cowboy with even greater speed.","Kaboom!","The cowboy was blown to bits.","At the same time, Yani used her other hand to grab the incoming speartip between her fingers. With a twist, it broke off. She flicked her fingers, sending the speartip flying into its owner’s forehead.","The spearman burst apart at the same time as the cowboy.","Following that, the massive avatar’s punch arrived, but Yani casually hurled a punch of her own in response. The thick black clouds in the sky dispersed, revealing the blue sky. As for the unlucky man behind the avatar, he had long disintegrated under the sheer force of Yani’s punch.","Even the dragon’s lower jaw nearly dropped to the ocean floor, let alone those on the frigate."]},{"number":2787,"title":"Chapter 2787: Chapter 2739: An Undying Body","paragraphs":["“This woman is insane!”","That was the thought on everyone’s mind. Even Tingxue raised her eyebrows, surprised by Yani’s strength.","The grayish-white dragon opened its mouth and roared furiously, unleashing an invisible sonic boom that caused the surrounding ocean water to bubble.","The crew members activated the frigate’s defensive formation, forming a transparent barrier around the vessel. It blocked the sonic boom.","However, the grayish-white dragon followed with a breath. Those on the frigate shuddered in fear as they remembered how an unlucky person had been killed and enslaved by this breath. Many guests were prepared to leap off the frigate to avoid the attack.","Yani harrumphed as she hurled a punch over.","It was a simple move, but her punch easily smashed through the dragon breath and charged toward the dragon’s head. Upon contact, its head exploded into a rain of flesh and blood, and its body plummeted into the ocean as a carcass.","Many on the frigate gulped. Good thing we didn’t cause trouble at the hotel, or else we could have been the recipients of that punch.","Zu An was dumbstruck, too. Is she One-Punch Woman?","But Yani didn’t look relieved in the least. She eyed the area where the dragon had just plummeted with a frown. The water bubbled, and a massive bone dragon flew out from within. It opened its mouth and unleashed a soundless roar.","The dragon was truly enraged this time. Despite losing its flesh, it felt more intimidating than before.","“This appears to be its true form,” the white-haired butler said grimly as he stood in front to shield Isabella. “Big miss, it looks like we have encountered a Deity of Death worshiper, and I suspect that is the legendary envoy, Alati.”","The word ‘envoy’ shocked the nearby guests. Many showed looks of despair.","In terms of strength, envoys were second only to the universal deity of their respective daos. They wielded power bestowed by their universal deity, and ordinary worshipers wouldn’t stand a chance against them.","Furthermore, Alati was an extremely famous envoy in the Myriad Worlds. Death followed wherever he appeared. Countless famous and legendary experts had fallen to him.","He'd disappeared when the Deity of Death passed away. Some said he'd been protecting the Deity of Death when the Deity of Annihilation personally vanquished him. Some said he'd betrayed the Deity of Death at a critical juncture and gone into hiding.","No one on the frigate had expected to encounter the legendary Death envoy here.","The talk about the almighty Death envoy brought a frown to Zu An’s face.","It was then Isabella who voiced the doubt that was lingering in his mind. “Hm? Somehow, it doesn’t feel as powerful as the legendary Alati.”","The white-haired butler replied, “The demise of the Deity of Death was bound to weaken all Death worshipers, especially Alati, who used to be a Death envoy. It’s struggling to maintain its sanity. It’s more like a corpse that is battling by instinct.”","“I see.” Isabella nodded. The other guests breathed a sigh of relief.","Zu An was awed. As expected of someone tasked to protect the Universal Conglomerate’s princess. That old butler is highly knowledgeable.","It was then that there was a twist in the battle.","Yani fearlessly charged at the bone dragon and hurled a fist. The dragon fought back ferociously. The terrifying shockwaves rising from their clashes produced a massive whirlpool under them.","The crew members quickly steered the frigate away from the whirlpool, while the other guests watched the battle.","Yani clearly wielded the upper hand, with every punch she hurled shattering multiple of her enemy’s bones.","A few guests whistled. Yani’s beautiful appearance and explosive figure made her quite a spectacle to behold when fighting.","“She’s ferocious. I wonder if she’d be as ferocious in bed.”","“Pft. Her legs would crush that scrawny body of yours.”","...","Of course, the guests dared not say those words aloud, fearing that Yani would murder them on the spot.","Yani suddenly roared and punched the bone dragon in half. The crowd gasped.","Forget it. It’s safer to pursue the adorable Isabella.","“Big sister Yani has won!” Isabella cheered.","“Not yet,” Tingxue said.","Confused, Isabella glanced at the old butler for confirmation.","The old butler nodded. “Alati was a Death envoy, after all. It wouldn’t be that easy to kill it, even if it is far weaker than before.”","Shortly after those words were spoken, the bone dragon emerged from the ocean with its shattered bones and torn flesh regenerated.","Yani frowned. She charged at the bone dragon once more and engaged it in an intense fight.","Some time later, the dragon plummeted into the ocean once more. However, it didn’t take long before emerging yet again.","This time, Yani learned from her lesson and sought to shatter the bones into powder, thinking there was no way Alati could regenerate from that.","However, the dragon still emerged again shortly after, with the shattered bones reassembled as good as new.","“How is that possible?!” the guests exclaimed in disbelief. Yani had already killed the bone dragon multiple times now, but the latter kept returning to full health.","Yani’s breathing had become ragged, and her chest puffed up and down, threatening to pop her buttons and break free of her shirt. At this rate, she was going to be at a disadvantage. Despite being the stronger one here, it felt inevitable that she would be defeated.","“Uncle Alfred, are Death envoys immune to death?” Isabella was intrigued.","The old butler frowned. “That’s impossible. If that was the case, Death worshipers would be invincible. Even the Deity of Death can die, so how can a fallen envoy be immune to death?”","A groan suddenly echoed.","As the battle dragged on, Yani was eventually struck by the dragon’s attack and knocked back. The dragon pursued her relentlessly, not giving her time to rest, determined to exact vengeance for the earlier insult."]},{"number":2788,"title":"Chapter 2788: Chapter 2740: Descent","paragraphs":["The guests on deck stirred when they saw Yani in danger, but none of them made a move. Having witnessed the fate that had befallen those three unlucky fools, no one wanted to be afflicted by Alati’s death energy and enslaved after death.","“Uncle Alfred, please save big sister Yani!” the kind-hearted Isabella urged the old butler.","“Big miss, the old master has entrusted me with your safety. I’m afraid I can’t help you with this.” The old butler refused to leave Isabella’s side. An earlier moment of carelessness had resulted in Isabella being held by a young man. That nearly made him break out in cold sweat.","It’s a relief that the man meant no harm, or else big miss would have been in danger. I can’t let the same mistake happen again.","Zu An was about to make a move when Tingxue said, “I’ll deal with that dragon. You save her.”","She charged forth without unsheathing her sword, unleashing a huge wave of sword ki.","Boom!","The bone dragon was torn apart by the sharp sword ki and plummeted into the ocean.","The ensuing powerful shockwave knocked Yani back. She was so weakened from being exposed to death energy that the shockwave made her spurt blood, and she also fell toward the ocean.","Alarmed, Zu An controlled the water to slow Yani’s rate of descent as he rushed over to grab her. Each time he came into close contact with her, he was awed by the vastness she carried in her bosom.","“Thank you...” Yani said weakly, looking unlike her earlier imposing war goddess image.","Zu An expelled the irrelevant thoughts from his head and asked, “How are you feeling?”","“Not too well.” Yani raised her hands, revealing the grayish-white energy covering them. The energy tried to creep up her arm, but she suppressed it from spreading further with her own ki. “The death energy assimilates my own energy. The more I try to expel it, the more it fuels its growth.”","Stopping the death energy only fueled its strength further, and not stopping it spelled immediate death. It was hopeless either way.","Just then, the ocean surface began to swirl. Zu An could feel the bone dragon regenerating, so he said, “Let’s return to the frigate first. Can you fly?”","Yani frowned. “It should be possible.”","Knowing she was putting on a strong front, Zu An said with a smile, “I’ll carry you.” He lifted her in a princess carry and brought her back to the frigate.","Startled, Yani stared at Zu An’s face, and slowly, she started feeling a little uncomfortable.","The others on deck also stared at them in bewilderment. Even Tingxue glanced over, as if questioning why they were flirting when they were fighting for their lives here.","However, it all made sense when they noticed the death energy afflicting Yani’s body. Her condition was poor enough to warrant such treatment.","“Big sister Yani, I have some medicine...” Isabella reached into her waistbag and fumbled around.","“Big miss, that’s indeed the legendary death energy. You mustn’t get close to them. No living being can get rid of death energy after being afflicted with it; it will continuously sap its host’s life energy until the host returns to death’s embrace.” Alfred stopped Isabella from heading to Yani’s side.","The guests who wanted to check the situation also retreated in fear. What the hell! That weird energy can spread?!","Alfred’s words were credible, especially after they'd witnessed the plight of those three fools.","“Is there no way to save big sister Yani?” Isabella asked anxiously.","“Only Longevity’s life priests or Reproduction’s offspring priests have the power to curb death energy with their tremendous life force, but this is death energy from Death’s envoy. Normal priests wouldn’t be able to deal with it.” Alfred looked around and confirmed there were no such priests onboard the frigate.","“Should we toss her into the ocean...” someone proposed. The crowd looked at him with weird eyes, so he stiffened his neck and continued, “I bet you had the same thought, too. If we keep her on the ship, the death energy on her will just grow stronger. When it finally blows up, all of us will be infected by it!”","The crowd stirred. As beautiful and powerful as Yani was, that was already a thing of the past. She was now a walking poison that could bring everyone down with her.","“We can’t do that! Big sister Yani is our comrade. How can we abandon her? What if your comrades abandon you when you’re injured?” Isabella raised her arms to guard Yani.","The crowd couldn’t do anything to Isabella, so they could only try to convince her.","“Miss Isabella, we know that you’re kind, but there is no other choice. We’ll die otherwise.”","“The death energy is still suppressed in her arms. She might still survive if we chop off her arms. Due to the death energy’s contamination, it’s unlikely she’ll be able to regrow her arms, but she should still be able to live a normal life with prosthetics.”","...","Hearing the discussions, Zu An said, “Let me give it a try.” He didn’t think the death energy was as terrifying as they put it.","“Don’t get infected yourself. You’ll only make things worse.” Many guests were alarmed. Yani was strong enough to temporarily suppress the death energy, but Zu An was far weaker. If he were to get afflicted by the death energy, it could act up right away, and that would put everyone on the deck in danger.","“Don’t worry. You can toss me overboard if I get infected,” Zu An replied coldly. He pushed aside the others and walked up to Yani.","The ocean billowed. Alati regenerated once more and let out a miserable howl.","“You’re too noisy!” Tingxue harrumphed. She unleashed another wave of sword ki at the bone dragon, causing it to scatter yet again. Then, she quickly turned her gaze back to Zu An with a tinge of concern in her eyes.","The crowd on the deck gulped. How is this loner that strong? She’s as powerful as Yani! No, she’s even stronger than Yani in some aspects, like how she easily dealt with Alati without coming into contact with it.","Zu An didn’t make a reckless move. He first examined the grayish-white death energy on Yani’s hands before placing his hand on her shoulder and channeling the Primordial Origin Sutra.","The encroaching death energy was intimidated by the Primordial Origin Sutra’s cleansing power and retreated.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. It works.","So, he grabbed Yani’s hands. He had noticed her meridians were different from a normal person's, so he figured it could be better to deal with the affected area directly.","“Careful!” Isabella warned in astonishment.","Zu An flashed a smile at her. “Don’t worry.”","He channeled his Primordial Origin Sutra. The death energy afflicting Yani’s hands melted like snow in the heat of summer and quickly vanished.","With the death energy purged, Yani swiftly regained her energy. She stretched her limbs and exclaimed in delight, “Thank you! I owe you my life.”","The crowd couldn’t believe their eyes. That fellow can control the ocean and cleanse death energy? What’s his background?","Alfred asked, “That young master over there, are you a Longevity or Reproduction worshiper?”","“Neither, I am a Deity of Memory worshiper.”","Zu An’s eyes widened as soon as he answered that question. He felt a compelling force descending upon him. The dark clouds in the sky stirred, forming a peculiar eye. A divine voice boomed in his mind, “You’re my worshiper? Why am I not aware of that?”"]},{"number":2789,"title":"Chapter 2789: Chapter 2741: Deity of Memory Meng!","paragraphs":["Zu An’s surroundings morphed. There was no frigate, bone dragon, or even ocean. He was transported into a space with data waterfalls similar to those in the Matrix flowing around him. Taking a closer look, the flowing data looked peculiar, resembling a combination of 1s and 0s yet not quite.","But Zu An wasn't in the mood to fuss over such details. Cold sweat trickled down his body.","His previous experience with Mi Li allowed him to swiftly grasp the situation. He had drawn another universal deity’s gaze, and the other party appeared to be Mi Li’s nemesis—the Deity of Memory, Meng.","He hurriedly said, “Paying respects to the great Deity of Memory. I may not be your official worshiper, but I have always looked up to you. I once met a Mirror Scribe, and through him, I learned the importance of faithfully recording historical events. I have always aspired to pursue the path of memory.”","“Oh? If that is your aspiration, why do you worship Mi Li?” an impassive voice responded amid the flickering data.","Sweat rained from Zu An. Mi Li was the Deity of Memory’s nemesis. That was readily evident from how Mirror Scribes sought to record facts, whereas Time Scribes sought to alter recorded history. They were antithetical entities to each other.","It also belatedly struck Zu An that universal deities could read minds, so he resigned himself to his fate and replied, “Mortals like us have no choice in a universal deity’s summons.”","“Are you saying that Mi Li forced you to worship her?” There was a peculiar tinge to the voice.","“I’m afraid that’s not the case. Every universal deity wields compelling power to mortals like us. I willingly accepted the Deity of Chaos and Enigma back then,” Zu An mustered his courage and replied.","He dared not talk badly about Mi Li. If Meng turned around and bragged about this matter to Mi Li, he would die a dog’s death.","“So that’s what you’re worried about. Don’t worry, I won’t report you to Mi Li. Come under me instead, and I’ll protect you from Mi Li,” the voice said teasingly.","Crap, I forgot they could read minds.","Zu An gulped. He probed, “Can I worship you while maintaining my faith in Chaos and Enigma?”","“Hm?” Terrifying pressure suddenly crushed down on Zu An. “A greedy one, aren’t you?”","Every cell in Zu An’s body was quivering, and it felt as if he could disintegrate at any moment. His soul wouldn’t even have the chance to undergo reincarnation. He added, “This will allow me to be of greater value to you. If the Deity of Chaos and Enigma learned about my betrayal, they would be guarded against me. That would prevent me from acquiring important intelligence.”","“You’re interesting. I can see why you piqued Mi Li’s attention.” A chuckle echoed as the pressure lightened. “Speak. What mission did Mi Li assign you? Let me see if you are of sufficient value or not.”","“They tasked me to worship Chaos and Enigma by altering the true history recorded by your worshipers,” Zu An carefully replied.","“That scoundrel!” The Deity of Memory was infuriated. “That bitch Mi Li is going too far!”","Zu An was speechless.","“You have done well. Continue staying on that side and provide me with intelligence.” Meng appeared to be satisfied with the intelligence.","“Yes.” Zu An bowed. He carefully probed, “But how can I convince others I’m your worshiper?”","“Are you asking for benefits? You’re a cunning one.” Meng harrumphed. “What did Mi Li give you?”","Zu An hesitated before replying, “The Deity of Chaos and Enigma made me their envoy.”","Meng was speechless","There was a long silence before a roar echoed in the distance, “That lunatic! Only that bitch Mi Li would do something like that!”","...","It was a long time later before Meng said, “Since you’re an envoy on that side, I’ll make you a Memory envoy as well.”","Zu An was overjoyed. “Thank you, Deity of Memory!”","Hehehe, there’s nothing better than to butter up these...","His heart suddenly quivered, and he hurriedly emptied his mind lest Meng overhear his blasphemous thoughts.","“You’re too weak. If you’re killed by accident, my reputation will be sullied. Very well, I shall bestow you with the ‘Eye of Truth’ and ‘Annals of History’.”","Two specks of light descended upon Zu An. One fell into his eyes, and he vaguely sensed a slight change in his vision. The other fell into his hand and morphed into a mirror.","No wonder they're called Mirror Scribes. They do indeed have mirrors.","“Your mirror is much better than the ones bestowed upon ordinary Mirror Scribes,” Meng coldly said. “This mirror is called the ‘Annals of History’. If you ever find yourself in danger, you can use the River of History as a barrier to block your enemy’s attack. No matter how strong the attack is, it can’t traverse the River of History to hurt you.”","Zu An was delighted to hear that. With this to protect me, I’ll be nigh invincible!","“Aside from that, you also have the power to unleash the River of History and randomly toss your enemy into a segment of it.”","“Is there a restriction to that ability?” Won’t I be invincible if this mirror can be used defensively and offensively?","“Of course there is. You won’t be able to trap top experts in the River of History. The stronger they are, the shorter the duration you can trap them. This item is meant to buy you time so you can escape, not for you to do other stuff.”","Zu An smiled sheepishly. Oops, my thoughts were overheard.","“The Eye of Truth allows you to see through your enemy’s illusions and disguises, lest you die without knowing how,” Meng said.","Zu An’s heart felt warm. The Deity of Memory must truly care about me to give me so many defensive artifacts. I’m touched... Even the data waterfalls didn’t look as intimidating as they were before.","“It’s good that you know. You know what you have to do from now on.”","“Thank you for the generous bestowments. I’ll devote myself to you!” Zu An raised his head and tried to use the Eye of Truth. The data waterfalls vanished, and he saw a beautiful figure.","“Hmph!” A cold harrumph echoed, and Zu An’s eyes, nose, and mouth bled.","“What are you looking at?” Meng scoffed imposingly and coldly."]},{"number":2790,"title":"Chapter 2790: Chapter 2742: Key","paragraphs":["The beautiful figure vanished, replaced by blood-red data.","Zu An withstood the terrifying pressure and hurriedly said “It may have only been a brief glimpse, but I am awe-inspired by Memory’s grandeur and divinity. It’s my utmost blessing and fortune to be a Memory envoy.”","“You have a glib tongue.” The data slowly reverted to green, and the pressure gradually receded. “Never be so brazen as to peer at a universal deity again. It’ll only bring destruction upon yourself.”","“Thank you for the lesson,” Zu An obediently replied.","“I need you to investigate a matter,” Meng said.","“It’s my honor to serve you.” Zu An wondered if he was going too far with the subservience, but then again, since he was dealing with a universal deity here, it likely wasn't excessive.","“I sense the Deity of Death’s aura at your side. There are many unrecorded details about the Deity of Death’s demise, and that violates the way of Memory. Thus, I want you to look into the matter.” Meng was displeased. She thought her Memory worshipers were good-for-nothings for failing to record such an important event.","Zu An took this chance to probe, “I heard the Deity of Death was killed by the Deity of Annihilation. Is that true?”","“It’s not that simple...” Meng suddenly paused and said, “That’s not something you should concern yourself with. Such secrets will only put you in greater danger.”","“I understand.”","“You may return now. Remember your mission.”","The scenery suddenly morphed, and Zu An found himself standing at the frigate’s bow once more. The sea breeze blew, and he belatedly realized he was soaked from head to toe.","Haa! No wonder everyone warns me against carelessly talking about universal deities. It’s fortunate I reacted fast, or else I could have died there. It was a close shave, but I obtained two special abilities from that encounter.","I'm now both Chaos and Enigma’s and Memory’s envoy. I wonder if I’ll be ripped apart if Mi Li learns about this... Hold on, Meng referred to Mi Li as a ‘bitch’ earlier. Is Mi Li a woman?","He had glimpsed Meng using the Eye of Truth, and the latter appeared to be a woman.","Are universal deities really genderless?","He shuddered and hurriedly shook off those wayward thoughts. I misspoke and summoned Meng earlier. I might not be as lucky if my thoughts wander and summon something else instead.","“Is that the Deity of Memory Meng’s gaze?”","“It does feel like Memory.”","“Brother Zu is truly Memory’s worshiper.”","“There are so many Memory worshipers in the world, but how many receive Memory’s gaze? Brother Zu is destined for great things. He might have a chance to become a Memory envoy in the future.”","...","The crowd’s attitude changed from their earlier nonchalance to amicableness.","I am already a Memory envoy.","Zu An chose not to reveal it, not because he didn’t want to brag but because he was afraid the news would reach Mi Li’s ears. He raised his head and looked around, and his expression soon tensed up.","“Big brother Zu, you saved big sister Yani earlier. Do you have a way to deal with Alati? Big sister Tingxue has scattered that bone dragon several times now, but she isn’t able to kill it,” Isabella said worriedly.","When it sensed the Deity of Memory’s divine power, Alati hadn’t dared to cause trouble, but when it realized that the Deity of Memory hadn’t descended, it quickly returned to whatever it was doing.","Had it retained its sanity, it would have retreated right away. However, it was completely driven by instinct right now, which was why it was obsessed with bringing down the people who hurt it.","Just like Yani, Tingxue could easily subdue Alati but not kill it. Even if she ground the latter’s bones to powder, it still regenerated. Is it due to the death energy, or because it was Death’s envoy?","“Let me give it a try.” Zu An flew over and looked at the ferocious bone dragon. He channeled his Primordial Origin Sutra and murmured an incantation. “Dust to dust, earth to earth. What should not remain should cease to exist...”","The roaring bone dragon suddenly became quiet. As it listened to the incantation, its twisted expression slowly became peaceful. A light breeze blew, and the grayish-white energy cloaking Alati gradually grew faint.","A middle-aged man’s silhouette manifested on Alati’s head. His fierce appearance suggested that he'd been a formidable figure back then. He cupped his hands toward Zu An and said, “Thank you, young man. I am finally free after so many years.”","“You are Death Envoy Alati?” Zu An asked curiously.","“It has been many years since I heard that name. I didn’t expect there to be someone who recognized me.” The middle-aged man sighed wistfully.","“How did you end up in... that state?” Zu An took this opportunity to gather more information.","“I was cursed.” As the middle-aged man recalled the past, a sliver of anger and fear flickered through his eyes. “Don’t ask who cursed me. Learning too much will only bring you misfortune.”","He passed a token over and said, “I have been waiting for a fated someone. Countless years have passed, and I even gave up hope. I didn’t expect to find you.”","“What is this?” Zu An examined the token. It was golden with a jade-like texture. A layer of pristine light gleamed on its surface. It was bizarrely shaped, reminiscent of a gear.","“It’s a key.”","“A key to what?”","“I can’t reveal too much. You’ll know in due time.”","Zu An wanted to curse. Argh, another riddler! But he came to terms with it when he thought about what he had just been through. It felt almost as if the universal deities and strong entities had some ‘keyword surveillance’ ability, in which uttering specific words drew their attention.","He wasn’t confident he could survive a repeat of the earlier situation.","After handing Zu An the token, the middle-aged man closed his eyes and said, “It’s finally over...”","Zu An had more questions to ask, but the silhouette began dissipating under the breeze. At the same time, the bone dragon, whom neither Yani nor Tingxue had been able to kill, disintegrated into ashes, vanishing without a trace.","The crowd rushed up to Zu An when he returned to the frigate. Yani asked, “Did he give you something?”","“He gave me a key,” Zu An replied honestly.","He figured since he had no idea what this key was for, perhaps revealing it to others could spark further intel about it.","The crowd fell into deep thought."]},{"number":2791,"title":"Chapter 2791: Chapter 2743: Devil Eye","paragraphs":["Zu An took in the crowd’s expressions. Hm, it looks like they have other motives for joining this rescue operation out in the ocean. He stowed away the key and asked, “Miss Yani, can we speed up a little?”","After being stalled by the bone dragon, he was getting increasingly worried about Firework.","Yani wanted to return the favor after being rescued by him, so she immediately took control of the frigate and went full speed ahead.","After witnessing his special abilities and close association with the Deity of Memory, many people tried to strike up a conversation with Zu An, but he was too worried about Firework, so he dealt with them perfunctorily.","The commotion from the earlier fight appeared to have frightened away the other monsters in the ocean, so they didn’t encounter any danger along the way. Soon, dense storm clouds could be spotted in the distance. Thunderous claps reverberated.","The crowd had heard about it from Zu An, but all this time, they'd thought he was exaggerating. It was only now that they realized the storm clouds were more frightening than they'd expected.","Lightning bolts as thick as pillars flashed here and there. Any normal cultivator would have been burnt to crisp upon contact.","Yani went up to Zu An and asked, “Are you sure your friend is in there?”","Zu An nodded. “She was brought in there.” That was what the ocean creatures he'd communed with told him.","“Our frigate’s defensive formation only allows us to search the outer area. I’m afraid we’ll have to turn back if we don’t find your friend there,” Yani reminded him.","Zu An turned to the crowd and said, “I’m grateful that you've come out here to help me rescue my friend, but things are only going to get more dangerous from this point on. You don’t have to risk your life with me. There are lifeboats on the frigate, so you can wait out here for us.”","“You’re being too polite. Allow me to head into the stormy region with you. It’ll help to have an extra pair of eyes looking around.”","Zu An had already proven his worth, so it wouldn’t hurt to sell him a favor.","On top of that, those gathered on this frigate were experts of their respective worlds, and they were confident in their strength. They were also curious about what lay within the stormy region, thinking there could be fortuitous encounters there.","Isabella also spoke up. “Big brother Zu, we came here to rescue your friend. It doesn’t make sense for us to back out now. You don’t have to worry about us. We’ll take care of ourselves and leave if we sense ourselves reaching our limits.”","Zu An bowed to the crowd. “Thank you!”","Yani steered the frigate toward the stormy region. They could already feel furious winds even when they were only at the borders of the stormy region, and the waves were already taller than the frigate.","Zu An used the Crown of the Ocean Deity’s ability to suppress the ocean water, allowing the frigate to steer stably into the stormy region.","Despite already knowing about this ability, the other guests were astounded.","The butler Alfred remarked, “Only a small handful of water deities and ocean deities wield such a water control ability, and none of them are... this young.”","Zu An smiled. “Are you saying I look like a kid?”","Alfred laughed. “You’re a generous person. I can see why you were given our Conglomerate’s cherished friendship emblem.”","Isabella also spoke up. “Big brother Zu, you should drop by my home after this.”","Upon hearing those words, the crowd blazed with envy. Isabella’s invitation held significance, and more importantly, she was inviting him not to her office, but her home! Is the Acadia House going to get a new son-in-law?","“I’ll have to make a trip back home first. My wives are worried about my safety,” Zu An replied. When he said those words, he couldn’t help but eye Tingxue, since she resembled Yan Xuehen a lot.","The crowd was rendered speechless. Why are you going all out to save another woman when you already have multiple wives? On top of that, you’re still flirting with Miss Tingxue and Miss Isabella. Don’t you think you’re being too greedy?!","Isabella was taken aback. “Yes, family should come first. May I visit big brother Zu’s world then? I’m sure it’s a beautiful place.”","The guests exchanged looks. They had been fawning on Isabella all this time, and while Isabella had treated them with respect, the sense of distance was unmistakable. They hadn't thought she could be this proactive.","Even Alfred frowned. Due to our big miss’ background, her words and actions are bound to invite speculation. It’s not a good idea for her to follow another man to his homeland. However, he could tell that Isabella harbored innocent thoughts, so he didn’t stop her.","Zu An smiled. “My homeland is indeed a beautiful place. It’d be my honor to host you.”","“It’s a deal!” Isabella replied with a sweet smile that could easily win anyone over. She felt like an energetic little sister that brought joy to the room.","While they were chatting, the frigate had already steered into the stormy region. Thick lightning bolts fell toward the frigate. They were almost purple in color, and it felt as if they contained calamitous power.","The crowd tensed up. Several people whipped out their weapons, ready to deflect the lightning if needed.","However, the bolts falling toward the frigate were stopped by a transparent barrier, upon which they dissipated into the surroundings as little lightning specks.","The crowd were awed by Dreamland’s wealth. To think that even an ordinary frigate would be equipped with such a formidable barrier!","Zu An examined the barrier. It ingeniously combined technology with formations, and it was designed specifically to ward off lightning. Dreamland must have tried venturing into this stormy region before.","Despite being protected by the barrier, the crowd remained tense. The visibility had abruptly plummeted in the stormy region, so much so that the experts onboard could only see several hundred meters away at most. The dense stormy clouds looming over them were suffocating.","“It resembles an apocalypse I once witnessed. The world was torn apart shortly after.”","“Was an Annihilation worshiper here?”","...","Despite its advanced technologies, Dreamland’s frigate shook like a toy in a child’s hand, seeming as if it would capsize at any moment.","Alfred suddenly spoke up. “This storm reminds me of a planet I once passed by. That planet was ravaged by a massive storm that spanned thousands of kilometers. The storm was visible even from space. For that reason, there were no living beings on that planet.”","“Why didn’t we notice this earlier when arriving at this planet?” Isabella asked.","“Big miss, our vision was obscured by the clouds. We couldn’t have noticed these storm clouds,” Alfred explained.","Isabella turned to Yani and asked, “Big sister Yani, how big is the stormy region?”","Yani replied, “These storm clouds have existed in the Dreamocean for a very long time. We call the region the Devil Eye. It wasn’t that big initially, spanning only a radius of a thousand square meters, and it was stable until several centuries ago. But in recent years, the Devil Eye began rapidly expanding at a rate that baffled even us.”"]},{"number":2792,"title":"Chapter 2792: Chapter 2744: Road of No Return","paragraphs":["The guests present here were all top experts in their respective worlds. They understood that something must have happened to cause such a change in recent centuries, and it could spell a great fortuitous encounter. Although they'd first joined this expedition to forge friendly ties with the Acadias, their interest was now piqued. A fortuitous encounter that stirred a phenomenon of this extent had to be extraordinary. It would be highly beneficial to obtain it.","Their initial intention had been to back out as soon as things looked dangerous, but now, they were determined to see to the end of the expedition no matter how dangerous it was.","The bigger the waves, the more valuable the fish!","Isabella asked, “Big brother Zu, since you can control it, why don’t we travel in the ocean?”","Before Zu An could say a word, Yani replied, “That might work elsewhere, but this region of the ocean is affected by the terrifying storm. There are countless typhoons joining the ocean to the lightning in the sky, imbuing the water with electricity. Furthermore, many hidden currents have formed underwater. It’d be more dangerous to travel in the ocean.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. “She’s right. This ocean region now contains lightning and wind. I only have sway over the ocean. It wouldn’t be easy for me to control it.”","Isabella was worried. “I didn’t think this ocean region was so violent and dangerous! If the sea monster brought big sister Firework here, she might be... Big brother Zu, you might have to mentally prepare yourself.”","Zu An’s gaze remained unwavering. “Even if she’s dead, I won’t stop until I see her corpse. I can’t give up just like that.”","The other guests agreed.","“We've already come this far. How can we give up halfway through?”","“If sea monsters can survive here, there could be a hidden safe zone, but we’ll have to explore the area to know.”","...","Isabella was perplexed. These people weren’t that enthusiastic earlier. What made them change their minds?","Yani sighed. “Young master Zu can control the ocean, while our frigate can just about defend against the lightning. It’s a pity none of us can control the wind, or else it would simplify matters.”","Isabella’s eyes lit up. She reached into her bag and fumbled for a while before pulling out a pearl. The pearl was nowhere as brilliant as other pearls, but it seemed weirdly heavy.","As soon as she pulled out the pearl, the roaring wind around them suddenly stopped. The vigorously swaying frigate also regained its stability.","“It’s the Wind Quelling Pearl! It’s said that this legendary item can suppress all winds. I didn’t expect it to exist!”","“It stopped even such terrifying typhoons! As expected of a legendary artifact!”","...","There were plenty of knowledgeable individuals on board the frigate. It didn’t take long for someone to recognize the pearl.","While gripped with excitement, some guests looked at Isabella in confusion and asked, “Miss Isabella, why didn’t you take out this pearl earlier?”","“I forgot about it.” Isabella’s face reddened. “I received this pearl as a gift when I was nine. It has been in my bag since.”","The crowd was speechless.","Their eyes fell on Isabella’s dainty bag. It’s not a joke when they say the Acadias’ wealth can rival a nation. The treasures inside that bag could be greater than most fortuitous encounters out there.","But no one in their right mind would rob the Acadias’ big miss. Given the Universal Conglomerate’s immense influence, they would only be courting their own deaths.","Zu An didn’t think that much into it. He was merely amazed that Isabella’s palm-sized bag could hold so many items. It must be a spatial artifact. Feels almost like Doraemon’s pocket.","Yani exclaimed in excitement, “With the assistance of this Wind Quelling Pearl, we’ll be able to venture deeper into the storm!”","She instructed Isabella to quell the winds in their immediate surroundings so the ocean water would remain calm. That would allow the frigate to swiftly sail further in.","Despite the devastating winds and lightning wreaking havoc in the surroundings, the narrow space around the frigate remained unharmed. The prowess of the Wind Quelling Pearl was impressive indeed.","Some time later, the frigate sailed through the terrifying storm and arrived at calm waters.","The guests on the deck were amazed. They'd never expected the center of that terrifying storm to be this peaceful.","Isabella remarked in delight, “Big brother Zu, the sea monster might have brought your friend here. We might be able to find her soon.”","“Let’s hope so.” Zu An looked at the calm waters with an ominous feeling in his heart.","It’s far too calm. How could the center of a terrifying storm be this serene?","“Hm? A fog is settling in.”","“Careful. The fog might be poisonous.”","“Don’t worry, I’ve checked. It’s not death energy.”","...","Upon realizing the fog wasn’t poisonous, the guests breathed a sigh of relief.","As the frigate ventured deeper in, the fog continued to thicken, eventually reaching a point where visibility was limited to a hundred-meter radius.","“Something is weird about the fog. It’s hindering my divine sense,” Alfred said with a frown.","The crowd hurriedly tested it out. They were appalled to realize that they couldn’t sense what was within the fog.","Experts of their caliber could spread their divine sense a far distance away as easily as eating and drinking. To have their visibility limited to a hundred meters was as good as becoming blind to them. They immediately lost their sense of security.","“The frigate’s radar isn’t working either.” Yani’s heart sank. Nothing was working, whether it be cultivation, magic, or technological tools.","“Things are getting too dangerous. I need to take responsibility for my lady’s safety. I believe we’re in grave danger, and I request for the frigate to turn back right away,” Alfred told Yani.","Even the ambitious ones who coveted the fortuitous encounter lost their courage. This place was simply too eerie. It would be wiser to return first.","Isabella was flustered. “Alfred, I’m going to continue...”","Alfred interjected before she could finish speaking. “Big miss, I can heed your words for other matters, but the old master has given me the discretion to make decisions on your behalf when your safety is at stake.”","Isabella was stunned. She looked at Zu An apologetically and said, “Big brother Zu, I...”","Yani suddenly interjected with a grim expression, “Now is not the time to be arguing about this. I’m afraid it might be impossible for us to turn back.”"]},{"number":2793,"title":"Chapter 2793: Chapter 2745: How Could it Be?","paragraphs":["“What’s wrong?” The guests were horrified.","“We have traveled through the fog for some time now. With our divine sense failing and all the frigate’s navigational tools malfunctioning, we can’t find our way back anymore,” Yani said with a frown.","“Why can’t we just turn around and return where we came from? We've been moving in a straight line all this time,” a guest suggested.","“We thought we were traveling in a straight line, but I just realized that isn’t the case at all. There’s something very off about this place.” Yani shook her head.","“So many experts are gathered on this frigate. Do you think we wouldn’t have noticed it if we steered away from our original direction? I’ll give it a try.”","Skeptical of Yani’s words, the guest flew from the frigate’s bow to around a hundred meters away before flying back. He didn’t fly further away, as he was worried he would be in danger if he strayed from the crowd’s gaze. He asked, “How is it? I flew in a straight line, right?”","The guests on the frigate stared at him in bewilderment. “Are you certain you flew in a straight line?”","“Of course! Do you think I can’t tell whether I’m flying in a straight line for a distance this short?” the guest snorted in disdain. Seconds later, he asked with a frown, “Hold on. Was I not flying in a straight line earlier?”","The other guests shook their heads. “You first flew left, then right, and at some point, you started flying in circles.”","“That’s impossible!” the guest exclaimed in disbelief. How can I not tell whether I’m flying in a straight line or not?","Someone was worried that the guest was working with Yani to fool everyone else, so he decided to verify it. He flew forth from the frigate and returned shortly after, at which he turned to Isabella and asked, “Esteemed Miss Isabella, was I flying in a straight line earlier?”","Even if he didn’t trust others, there was no way the Acadias’ first miss could be bribed to deceive him.","Isabella shook her head. “You flew haphazardly too, but there was a difference in your flight trajectory. You circled a few more rounds, and the direction of your flight was different as well.”","By this point, the other guests had already turned pale. This is terrible. Even their flight trajectories were different. That means the distortion in our senses isn't constant, making it impossible to figure out a pattern in the distortion.","Alfred spoke up. “A formidable power must have warped the fundamental laws of physics in this place, resulting in this peculiar phenomenon.”","“Could it be the Deity of Death? There was an ex-Death envoy outside.”","“That’s impossible. The Deity of Death has been dead for countless years, and no one has been able to find any traces of him. It’s too much of a coincidence for us to bump into him just like that.”","“And there’s no death energy in the vicinity either.”","...","There was another reason that no one voiced out loud. If the Deity of Death was behind this, how could the Dreamland remain oblivious to this for so many years?","“What should we do? Do we continue wandering around?” someone asked with a quivering voice.","Not only were they unable to find their way back, but even if they continued venturing forward, there was no guarantee they would find anything.","“Actually, I have something that may help us with directions.” As Isabella spoke, she reached into her bag and pulled out a glass tank with a bizarre-looking fish swimming amid corals. “This is an East Fish. It’ll always head eastward no matter how complicated the environment is.”","“I've heard legends about this fish! Having it can steeply lower the difficulty of most labyrinth dungeons!”","“This is wonderful! We can return now.”","...","Zu An was more astounded by how Isabella pulled out a living creature from her bag, considering how most spatial artifacts could only hold dead items. Could her bag contain an entire world in it?","The guests stared intently at the fish as they waited for it to point out a direction.","The East Fish swam in circles as if it couldn’t determine where east was. Perhaps stressed by all the eyes focused on it, it eventually flopped over and revealed its belly, no longer wanting to swim.","The crowd was speechless.","Isabella’s face heated up. The shower of compliments she had received from the crowd earlier turned into humiliation for her. “Why is this happening? The East Fish has never reacted like that before.”","Sensing her fluster, Zu An spoke up on her behalf, “This fog could be more than a simple labyrinth. It could be a distortion of fundamental physical laws that renders the concept of direction meaningless. Naturally, the East Fish wouldn’t be able to determine where east is.”","The others voiced their agreement. Isabella shot a grateful look at Zu An.","Alfred spoke up as well. “For even the East Fish to fail, the distortion must be severe. Does anyone have other ideas? We need to work together to overcome this crisis. We shouldn’t be holding anything back now.”","A guest scattered beans around, which grew into talisman figures. The figures scattered into the surroundings, and a thorough map of the area appeared in the air. The figures had to be extraordinary treasures.","Before the crowd could celebrate, the map flickered before abruptly vanishing. The guest smacked his chest in bitter regret as he bemoaned, “My talisman figures!”","He had lost control over all the figures.","Another guest sneered.","What an idiot! Why would you send your precious artifact into the fog when you already know something is off about it?","He pulled out an eight-trigram compass and placed his hand on it. The compass began revolving quickly. The runes on its surface drifted out into midair to construct words. That guest’s eyes lit up in excitement.","However, the runes suddenly distorted the next moment, and he groaned and spurted blood on his compass. His face turned pale, a sign that he had sustained serious internal injuries.","“It all falls on me in the end,” an old woman dressed in a mage robe snorted. She swiftly formed a series of hand seals while murmuring an obscure incantation.","“That appears to be something from a supernatural civilization.”","“Is it some kind of shamanistic ritual? Hold on, what is she using as a sacrifice?”","The knowledgeable guests were appalled. Is she going to use us as tribute?","The answer was soon revealed.","The woman’s arm was first twisted off her shoulder, then it swiftly withered, as if some invisible entity had siphoned away its blood. A spatial crack appeared in the sky, and it looked as if a mysterious entity would descend. A blood-red eye emerged from the crack. The pressure it emanated left the crowd with goosebumps.","But then, the eye suddenly widened as if it had seen something terrifying. It immediately darted back into the crack while murmuring something in a language that no one understood.","Flabbergasted, the old woman shouted, “How can you leave without doing anything after accepting my tribute...”","But the eye paid no heed to her complaint, and the spatial crack closed. The old woman had already weakened from losing her arm and a considerable amount of her blood essence, and the immense anger she felt from being betrayed caused her to pass out.","“What’s going on?” The crowd was confused. Why did the mysterious entity suddenly retreat? Was the tribute insufficient?","Zu An’s face turned grim, as he understood what that entity said before it left.","“What?! How can it be ****-”"]},{"number":2794,"title":"Chapter 2794: Chapter 2746: Destination","paragraphs":["Zu An wouldn’t have understood those words either if he hadn’t inherited Fleeting Baldie’s knowledge of languages. It was a language from a supernatural world, a powerful one that rarely interacted with the other worlds. Even Fleeting Baldie had only grasped a bit of their language.","'How can it be ****'? What could that last word be?","He couldn’t understand the last word due to his limited grasp of the language, but he could sense the mysterious entity’s extreme fear of whatever that was. Just the eye of that entity was enough to heap immense pressure on everyone on the frigate, so it was hard to imagine what could have provoked such a huge response from it.","The old woman’s lips quivered. She wanted to curse but didn’t dare to do so, and that left her feeling unbearably stifled.","The others understood how she felt. She had paid a heavy price, only for the mysterious entity to take her tribute but not do any work. Anyone in her place would have wanted to curse as well.","Isabella hurriedly took out a pill from her bag and fed it to the old woman. The flesh around the old woman’s shoulder quickly regrew, and it didn’t take long for her arm to follow.","The old woman thanked Isabella profusely. She had the means to regrow her arm as well, but that would take more time, and she would have to consume tonics to ensure a smooth recovery. Yet those problems were all circumvented with Isabella’s pill.","Isabella did live up to her reputation as the Acadias’ big miss after all.","“I still have no idea why that lord suddenly retreated. He normally gets things done after accepting my tribute.” The old woman was still confused by the earlier situation.","Zu An told the guests what he'd heard from the mysterious entity.","Isabella looked at Zu An with surprised eyes. She was impressed that on top of all the abilities he had already displayed, he also understood that supernatural world’s language.","The guests were appalled. What could have struck fear in an entity of that level? Could this place truly be related to the Deity of Death?","Since they couldn’t even figure out the directions, neither advancing nor retreating was an option for them. This put the crowd at a loss.","Just then, Yani turned to Zu An and asked, “Didn’t Alati hand you a key earlier? Could that be a clue?”","Zu An took out the uniquely-shaped key. He'd found nothing special about it when he examined it earlier, but right now, the key was emanating a white light, as if resonating with something.","The light converged in the sky and slowly formed a map.","“This...” The previously fearful crowd suddenly trembled in excitement and greed. They realized they might have truly stumbled upon a fortuitous encounter. Under normal circumstances, they wouldn’t have found a fortuitous encounter even if they had devoted their lives to searching for it, but it just so happened that Zu An had the map.","We’re on the same boat now. Surely he can’t lock us out after we find the fortuitous encounter? As per convention in the Myriad Worlds, once we find it, it’ll be up to the individual to obtain whatever they can from it.","Something guarded by the ex-Death envoy Alati and this law-warping labyrinth was bound to be extraordinary. Thus, the guests urged Yani to follow the map.","Yani said, “Since we can’t retreat anymore, we’ll have to advance. We might find another way out of this place.”","Zu An frowned. “I came here to rescue my friend.”","The other guests tried to persuade Zu An. “There’s not a single living being around us. It’s unlikely that you’ll find Miss Firework by wandering aimlessly in this fog labyrinth. It’d be wiser for us to follow the map. Think about it. The sea monster should be familiar with this region for it to bring Miss Firework here, so she could be at the location indicated on the map.”","Zu An thought those words made sense. He'd tried communicating with the sea creatures in the vicinity, only to find there were no living beings around them. Their only clue was the map, so their best bet was to try their luck there.","Yani began sailing the frigate according to the map's directions. Said map also contained an arrow that always pointed in the right direction despite the distortion.","Often, when the crowd thought they should continue heading forward, the arrow told them to head in the opposite direction. So in the end, Yani ordered her subordinates to close their eyes and just blindly follow her instructions, lest they be fooled by their senses. As a result, the frigate kept changing directions, sometimes even circling non-stop on the spot.","Yet the crowd felt themselves approaching their destination.","Alfred, who was standing in front of Isabella to guard her, sent her a telepathic message. “Big miss, please make sure to keep close to me. A place guarded by an ex-Death envoy is bound to be fraught with dangers.”","He didn’t want to come here, as it would expose Isabella to too much danger, but unfortunately, he didn’t have a choice. They had an artifact to create a ship, but they wouldn’t be able to navigate their way out of an ocean region where even the East Fish had given up. It would be courting death to leave the frigate now, so they could only follow the others and hope for the best.","Isabella maintained her graceful smile while replying telepathically, “Uncle Alfred, it should be safest for us to stay close to big brother Zu.”","Alfred frowned. “Big miss, you can know a person but not their heart. It hasn’t been long since you met him...”","Isabella shook her head. “Big brother Zu is willing to take such a huge risk to rescue a friend whom he has only just met; he is a trustworthy person. Of everyone on this frigate, he has the purest motive.","“Not to forget, he has obtained Alati’s key and received the Deity of Memory’s favor. This shows he is blessed with luck. Staying with someone who is upright and has luck on his side increases our chances of surviving this crisis.”","“Our big miss has grown up.” Alfred was moved. Our big miss is kind but not foolish. If anything, she is sharper than most people.","The frigate continued advancing. By the time their location pin overlapped with their destination on the map, the bizarre fog had already vanished, revealing a vast ocean region.","“Huh? Why is there nothing here?”","The crowd was baffled. There was nothing but water surrounding them.","Just then, Zu An’s key suddenly glowed rhythmically. The calm ocean began twirling, instantaneously forming a massive whirlpool that they couldn’t see the end of. The frigate’s engines couldn’t struggle free of the whirlpool and was sucked into it.","Even if they somehow survived falling into the ocean’s unfathomable depths, they would still be flattened by the terrifying pressure down there. Several frightened guests tried to fly away from the frigate, hoping that they could escape the whirlpool’s suction force while they were still on its outer perimeter.","As soon as they rose into the sky, however, their faces suddenly warped in horror. They plummeted into the whirlpool faster than the frigate and vanished instantly, leaving behind nothing but miserable cries."]},{"number":2795,"title":"Chapter 2795: Chapter 2747: Beneath the Ocean","paragraphs":["Those who had tried flying away from the frigate weren’t weak by any means, but that only made their miserable cries as they plummeted into the whirlpool even more chilling.","After witnessing their plight, no one else dared to make a reckless move. It had been made clear that after leaving the frigate, none could resist the whirlpool’s suction force. They were only holding on thanks to the frigate’s defensive system. Even so, they were still toppling over.","Yani shouted, “Grab something! Don’t get flung off the frigate!”","Everyone was already doing that even without her reminder, but the whirlpool’s suction force was so strong that the frigate’s defensive formation began to unravel. Some crew members failed to hold on and were flung off.","The guests were strong enough to maintain their grip on the railings, but the whirlpool was simply so strong that some of the railings suddenly snapped off. Several of them were caught off guard and were flung off as well. Fortunately, they had exceptional skills such as extending their arms or hurling out hooks to grab onto another part of the frigate, thus barely remaining onboard.","Alfred fended the waves away from Isabella while shouting, “Big miss, make sure to hold on tight!”","The pale-faced Isabella nodded as she clutched onto the railings. She faced less stress compared to the other guests as Alfred warded off most of the dangers headed her way.","Zu An and Tingxue were at the frigate’s bow. Tingxue’s feet were firmly planted on the deck as if nailed to it. She remained unfazed, no matter how strong the whirlpool was. She asked, “Can’t you control the ocean?”","Zu An shook his head. “The water has been imbued with some kind of energy. I can’t control it.”","All of a sudden, there was a crack. A rope on the deck abruptly snapped through the air like a roaring whip. Several crew members were caught off guard and sliced in two. The ropes used on a war frigate were very heavy, capable of unleashing great destruction when flung around; the whirlpool turned them into devastating weapons.","The rope swung toward Isabella, and Alfred was appalled. He quickly stood in front of Isabella and crossed his arms. A tortoise-shell avatar manifested around him.","Pah!","Alfred blocked the whip, but he spewed blood as well. He was shocked by how powerful the whip was.","Another crisis happened right after.","It turned out the snapping rope was just the first sign that the frigate had reached its limit. This time, the frigate snapped right in half, and its back half was immediately dragged down into the whirlpool.","“Big miss!” Alfred had barely deflected a lethal blow and didn’t have the time to muster his strength anew yet. He couldn’t react at all.","Isabella panicked. She tried grabbing onto something, but to no avail. Her scream for help only lasted for an instant before it vanished amid the roaring waves.","Without any hesitation, Zu An used his position swap skill to trade places with Isabella.","Isabella appeared at the frigate’s bow. It was so abrupt that she struggled to keep her balance. Fortunately, the sharp-eyed Tingxue reacted fast and supported her.","When Isabella finally realized what had happened, she anxiously looked at the back half of the frigate, only to see it had been ripped into shreds. Tears flowed from her eyes as she shouted, “Big brother Zu!”","Tingxue ripped off a section of the railing. It vanished, and Zu An reappeared on the frigate. She quickly grabbed his arm so he could regain his balance.","Zu An looked at Tingxue gratefully. “Thank you!”","Everything had happened so fast that he hadn’t had time to think. It was by sheer instinct that he'd moved to save Isabella, but he'd forgotten to check beforehand if there was anything on the frigate's bow for him to swap back.","All the miscellaneous objects had been flung off the frigate. The only things he could position swap with were the entire frigate or other guests. If not for Tingxue quickly ripping off a section of the railing for him, he wouldn’t have been able to swap back.","It was amazing how Tingxue, despite it being her first time witnessing his position swap, had been able to figure out the principles behind how it worked and react right away. Her wits were truly impressive.","Tingxue nodded in acknowledgment.","A tearful Isabella embraced Zu An. “Thank you, big brother Zu! I was scared to death when you nearly disappeared earlier!”","Zu An looked at Tingxue awkwardly. The latter resembled Yan Xuehen so much that he felt strange, as if he'd been caught cheating by Yan Xuehen.","Tingxue turned away as if she hadn’t seen anything.","Alfred anxiously rushed over. “Thank you, sir!” He was so gripped by the fear of almost losing the big miss that he didn’t even realize that Isabella tightly embracing a young man was contrary to noble etiquette.","“It’s a pity I wasn’t able to save the others.” Zu An looked at the shattered bits of the frigate plummeting into the whirlpool. Even he had nearly died in the whirlpool.","The other guests consoled him, knowing he couldn’t be blamed for that. It was also then that someone asked out of curiosity, “Why was the other half of the frigate immediately ripped into bits, but our half remained fine?”","That’s true. There would have been more time for those on the back half of the frigate to react if it hadn’t been ripped to shreds right away. But why was it that the back half met with such a fate, but the front half remained intact?","“It’s probably because of his key. That key protects everything within a radius, but the frigate exceeds that radius. That’s why the back half snapped off and was destroyed shortly after.”","The crowd widened their eyes in shock. They hurriedly made their way closer to Zu An to ensure they wouldn’t fall outside of the key’s protection radius.","Despite the key’s protection, the whirlpool was still a fearsome adversary. The frigate’s remaining half continued twirling around like a shirt in a washing machine. The remaining survivors were experts who could still hold on, but the relentless spinning still left them dizzy.","Isabella’s mind blanked out in fear. She tightly hugged Zu An as that was the only way she could find any sense of security.","After an unknown period of time, Zu An woke up to find himself soaked in water, surrounded by the frigate’s shattered remnants.","He raised his head and saw not the ocean, but the blue sky... or at least that was what he thought, until he saw gigantic figures swimming in the ‘sky’. It turned out he was at the bottom of the ocean, and the 'sky’ he saw was water."]},{"number":2796,"title":"Chapter 2796: Chapter 2748: I’ll Vanquish It Right Away!","paragraphs":["This wasn't Zu An’s first experience with such a situation. The Ocean races’ Crystal Palace was also a city encapsulated in a transparent light barrier.","However, this place was much deeper than the Ocean races’ Crystal Palace. Perhaps he'd passed out at some point, but he had a vivid impression of that enormous whirlpool. He had to be at least a hundred thousand kilometers deep now.","Even Earth’s deepest ocean trench was only eleven kilometers deep, and that was already a depth that humans struggled to conquer. Meanwhile, he was now tens of thousands of times deeper. Any expert would be crushed to death if the ocean water fell on them.","Zu An took another look at the transparent barrier above him. He couldn’t imagine the power that would be needed to create such a huge space so deep in the ocean.","Just then, he heard a moan. Only then did he realize that Isabella was still in his arms. She'd grabbed him when the frigate was dragged into the whirlpool.","Zu An felt her trembling body and couldn’t bring himself to abandon her, so he embraced her. He hadn’t expected them to remain together despite having fallen this far down.","Just then, Isabella regained consciousness and realized that her hands and legs were still wrapped around Zu An. Her face reddened, and she mumbled as she unwrapped herself from his body, “B-big brother Zu, t-thank you.”","Zu An didn’t mind it. “Thank your luck instead of me. I’m surprised we’re fine despite having fallen so deep into the ocean.”","Before he passed out, he vaguely sensed a flowing current propping up his body. That could be why they hadn't been smashed to bits.","Just then, he heard groans as more people emerged from the water and slowly regained consciousness. They warily surveyed their surroundings, and they couldn’t help but be amazed by the ocean ceiling above them.","A horrified Alfred frantically looked around. When he spotted Isabella, he anxiously ran over and exclaimed, “Big miss, I can’t be more relieved that you’re safe!”","Isabella eyed Zu An in embarrassment. “Big brother Zu saved me.”","Alfred grabbed Zu An’s hand and shook it vigorously. “You’re truly the savior of our Universal Conglomerate. I don’t know how many times you have saved our big miss now. I’ll report this matter to my superiors. You’ll be the most esteemed friend of our Universal Conglomerate.”","Zu An smiled. “It’s thanks to Isabella’s great fortune that we survived such a huge fall.”","Zu An’s humility only made Alfred more fond of him. Our big miss happens to be of a marriageable age, and our old master is looking for a son-in-law. It’d be perfect if the two of them could get together. It’s a pity he has wives back in his world, but that isn’t a big problem. We’ll accept his current wives as concubines...","After answering Alfred’s question, Zu An anxiously searched the area. When he finally spotted the person he was looking for standing not too far away, he breathed a sigh of relief. He walked over and asked, “When did you regain consciousness?”","Tingxue was dry despite having been caught inside the whirlpool. Her clothes were artifacts, which had a certain level of resistance against water and fire. But even if they weren’t water-resistant, she could easily dry her clothes just by channeling her ki.","“I woke up slightly earlier than you,” she replied impassively.","“You should have woken me up. Did you find anything?” Zu An asked as he assessed their surroundings.","Tingxue eyed Isabella. “The two of you were hugging so tightly. I didn’t want to get in your way.”","Zu An was speechless. He was surprised as this was Tingxue’s first time showing interest in something unrelated to her.","“We should be on the ocean bed. There are some buildings in the distance. I was thinking of heading over to take a look after you regained consciousness,” Tingxue said.","Zu An looked over and saw structures that resembled buildings, but they were so far away that he couldn’t be certain.","Meanwhile, more people arrived on shore.","Yani did a head count. They had lost more than half of the crewmates—given their weak cultivation, it would be hard for them to survive. Most of the guests, except for the unlucky ones who had been on the other side of the frigate, had survived.","The others also noticed the buildings in the distance and decided to investigate them.","Yani instructed the remaining crewmates to remain in the vicinity and construct a temporary camp, so they would have a place to retreat to should they encounter trouble ahead. The guests had no qualms with this course of action; they even complimented her meticulousness.","Thus, Zu An and the others began their adventure.","“Uncle Alfred, why is the ocean water not falling? Is it some kind of formation?” Isabella asked.","“This exceeds the scope of formations and technology. The only ones who can pull off such a feat are water-type deities and those who possess ocean control powers like young master Zu.”","Zu An shook his head. “I might be able to create such a pocket temporarily, but this place has clearly been around for ages. I can’t maintain one for that long.”","He could control the ocean with the Crown of the Ocean Deity, but it would also deplete his ki. There was no way he could maintain such a pocket in the long run.","Their conversation sparked thoughts in the other guests. Chances are that there is some water-type divine artifact here. It’ll be a jackpot if I can obtain it...","But Yani poured a pail of cold water over them. “There’s another possibility. A universal deity could be behind this.”","The hearts of the guests shuddered. Indeed, a universal deity could easily perform such a feat. They thought about their earlier encounter with Death Envoy Alati. Could this be where the Deity of Death died?","But there was no death energy in the vicinity.","Despite being under the ocean, their surroundings looked no different from being on land; it was just that the forests were made up not of trees, but fossils of ocean plants. Along the way, they saw a lot of bizarrely-shaped skerries[1] that induced chills in them.","Isabella instinctively grabbed Zu An’s hand and leaned toward him. This was the only way she could feel any sense of security. Alfred quietly chuckled at that sight while walking behind them.","Tingxue suddenly halted. “Do you hear that?”","Yani replied, “I hear chirping sounds.”","The other guests heightened their wariness. They didn’t dare to let their guard down in this environment, though they didn’t think any monster could pose a threat, given the experts present here.","A black beetle emitting a golden luster suddenly appeared amid the skerries. It seemed to be examining them curiously.","“It’s just a little bug.” Many guests breathed a sigh of relief.","Alfred, on the other hand, first narrowed his eyes in uncertainty before extreme fear gripped his heart. “Run! It is a Soul Gnawing Beetle!” As he cried out, he grabbed Isabella and dashed off.","Due to Isabella grabbing his arm, Zu An was dragged along.","A brawny guest frowned. “It’s just a measly bug. Watch as I vanquish it!”","He grabbed the bug and torched it with a flame. The fire was so intense that it could have instantly incinerated any beetle.","But a mere instant later, his smile froze. He first noticed his flame diminishing, then felt a sharp pain in his palm. A lump beneath his skin traveled up his arm, and wherever it passed, the corresponding part of his body withered.","1. small rocky island ☜"]},{"number":2797,"title":"Chapter 2797: Chapter 2749: Slashing Out a Nebula","paragraphs":["The brawny man screamed. Flames ignited all over his body, leaving no question that he was a fire wielder. He'd been helpless earlier when they were surrounded by ocean water, so he'd thought he ought to reveal a hand here to show his worth. Little had he expected this damned beetle to be this formidable.","He quickly severed his withered arm, but he was still a step too slow. The beetle had already slipped into his body.","He anxiously channeled his fire ability to its full extent in hopes that the intense heat would incinerate the beetle, but to his horror, the raging flames he channeled swiftly extinguished. It was as if there was a black hole in his body devouring his flames.","It went without saying that the terrifying beetle was the culprit.","How is this possible? How can my almighty flames fail to incinerate a mere bug?","He would never get an answer to that question. His screams died down, and it came to a point where his withered body could no longer support its weight and fell to the ground.","“What’s that?!” the old shaman woman exclaimed in horror.","Alfred grimly replied, “It’s a Soul Gnawing Beetle. It devours all energies, be it ki or mana. That fellow tried to incinerate the Soul Gnawing Beetle, but his flames did nothing but nourish it.”","The others gulped. A being that can devour all energies? Isn’t it invincible then?!","“Does that beetle have no weaknesses?” Isabella asked.","“All beings are bound to have a weakness, but no one knows the Soul Gnawing Beetle’s weakness because no one has ever survived after encountering them.”","More chirping sounds echoed.","Pah!","The brawny man’s chest suddenly burst open. A black beetle crawled out, followed by a huge army of little beetles.","The crowd felt chills run down their spine. It reproduced so much within such a short time?","The Soul Gnawing Beetle flapped its wings, producing sharp whistling sounds.","A moment later, similar sounds came from the other skerries. More black beetles emerged from the cracks within the rock, creating a hellish sight for anyone who suffered from trypophobia[1]. Isabella nearly passed out from the sight.","The other guests dared not dawdle anymore and immediately fled. They regretted not being born with more limbs so that they could flee faster.","The Soul Gnawing Beetles were alarmed by the crowd’s movements and charged over. There were so many beetles that it was impossible to avoid all of them. It didn’t take long for a guest to be rushed down by the beetles.","It was the person who had attempted to scout the way earlier with talisman figures. He hurriedly conjured an army of birds to devour the Soul Gnawing Beetles.","But there were so many beetles that they overran the birds in a mere second. The birds cried in agony as they transformed back into paper talismans and were devoured clean. The talisman user also let out a miserable scream as a wave of Soul Gnawing Beetles washed over him.","Several guests tried to rescue him. Despite having heard from Alfred that the Soul Gnawing Beetles could devour all energies, they still wanted to give it a try.","The results were disappointing, though. The Soul Gnawing Beetles devoured all the attacks without a hitch. In the meantime, the beetles got to another guest and siphoned her dry.","But their efforts weren't all futile. They discovered that physical attacks worked on the beetles, but the attacks had to involve direct physical contact. Sword ki and the like wouldn’t work.","Unfortunately, there were simply too many Soul Gnawing Beetles, and these beetles were capable of gnawing through weapons as well. Several guests lost their weapons in such a manner and burst into tears.","Zu An was glad he hadn’t whipped out the Tai’e Sword. Otherwise, Mi Li could have lost her home. He'd dealt with enemies with such traits before, but none of them had been as formidable as the Soul Gnawing Beetles.","The guests gathered here were from different worlds, and their attacks were of all kinds and patterns, but the Soul Gnawing Beetles still devoured them with ease.","All of a sudden, the crowd grimly halted their footsteps. The path ahead had been blocked by Soul Gnawing Beetles. In fact, they were completely surrounded.","Cornered, the guests unleashed all their methods. Isabella even whipped out all sorts of artifacts from her bag, but none of them worked against the Soul Gnawing Beetles.","Zu An’s heart quivered. I do have an idea, but I don’t know if it’ll work.","Faced with the encroaching Soul Gnawing Beetles, Tingxue said, “I’ll deal with them.” She took a step forward.","That provoked the Soul Gnawing Beetles, and they furiously charged at her.","“Be careful!” Zu An was worried. How could he not be after witnessing other guests being siphoned dry by the Soul Gnawing Beetles?","With a crisp reverberation, Tingxue drew her sword. It sliced through the world, tearing open a void.","The crowd suddenly felt cold and desolate, as if there was no meaning to life. By the time they snapped out of their trance, the terrifying Soul Gnawing Beetles were nowhere to be seen.","“Where did those beetles go?” Isabella asked in astonishment.","“I have exiled them to another dimension,” Tingxue calmly replied.","The crowd frowned. That didn’t feel like any normal dimension—it resembles the nebula. In the nebula’s voidlike space, the Soul Gnawing Beetles won’t have anything to devour.","The crowd looked at Tingxue in shock. What’s her background? How can she slice open a pathway to the nebula just like that?","Yani clenched her fists. She was tempted to spar with Tingxue, but she dropped that thought, knowing they weren’t out of danger yet.","Tingxue walked at the forefront, and the other guests followed her. There was no reason not to clutch onto that extra thick thigh dangling in front of them.","Isabella remained by Zu An’s side. She whispered, “Big brother Zu, you’re incredible to have befriended someone like that.”","Alfred was speechless. That’s a pair of absurdly rose-tinted glasses you’re wearing, big miss. You’re crediting that to him, too?","“I don’t know if she thinks of me as a friend.” Zu An sighed. She’s even colder than Yan Xuehen.","After the earlier crisis, the guests were exceptionally vigilant.","Some time later, Tingxue suddenly stopped. Yani frowned as well.","“Haven’t we been here before?”","1. Trypophobia is an aversion to the sight of repetitive patterns of holes or bumps, triggering intense feelings of disgust, fear, or discomfort ☜"]},{"number":2798,"title":"Chapter 2798: Chapter 2750: Disappearance","paragraphs":["“You’re right. We have been here.”","The guests gathered here were top-notch experts. Despite the difficulty in distinguishing the skerries, they still swiftly spotted the resemblance in their surroundings.","“No wonder these skerries look so weird. It’s a labyrinth.” The guests turned to Zu An, wondering if his key would provide them guidance once more.","Zu An shook his head as he waved the key around. “It’s not providing guidance anymore. Its purpose could be to guide us out of that fog, trigger the whirlpool, and bring us into this space.”","Another guest asked, “Miss Isabella, what about the East Fish?”","Isabella pulled out a fish tank from her bag. The East Fish was still lying belly-up in the water. She felt so embarrassed and awkward that she was tempted to smash the fish tank on the floor.","Yani suggested, “Why don’t we split up and explore the area? Those who reach a dead end can just return here.”","Zu An frowned. “It’s dangerous to split up in a labyrinth.”","He hadn’t watched so many horror movies in his previous life for nothing. It was always the same pattern. As soon as the protagonist’s party split up, the monster lurking in the shadows would tear them apart one by one.","Yani replied, “We can split into groups. With our cultivation, we can look out for one another as long as we don’t stray too far away.”","Isabella spent a moment in thought before pulling out a bunch of communication devices from her bag. “Each group will take one communicator. This will allow us to remain in contact and alert one another of danger right away. These communicators are resistant to interference, and each one has enough energy to last a decade in adverse environments.”","Yani took a communicator. “I’ll go alone and scout the way up front.” She had proven her strength. No one was opposed to her going solo.","Seeing that, Tingxue also said, “Then I’ll scout this path.” She grabbed a communicator and headed down another path.","Zu An wanted to go with Tingxue, but there were many other people remaining who needed to be grouped up. He could only put aside his personal feelings. In the end, he formed a group with Alfred and Isabella.","The other guests also formed groups of their own and began exploring the area. They remained in contact via the communicators, reporting their movements.","Zu An observed the surroundings along the way. He noticed that the skerries resembled formations, but they weren’t quite complete. Despite his high proficiency in formations, he was still unable to decipher them right away.","Just then, Isabella suddenly remarked, “Hasn’t it been a while since we last heard from big sister Tingxue?”","Zu An was startled.","Unlike the others, who were afraid of encountering danger and reported in every few steps, the reticent Tingxue only reported in once in a while. He had already gotten used to it and didn’t pay much attention to it anymore. It was only when Isabella pointed that out that it struck him that it had been a long while since he last heard from Tingxue.","So, he tried calling for Tingxue via the communicator, but the latter didn’t reply. His heart sank. Tingxue might be cold, but she won’t ignore me under such circumstances. Something must have happened to her.","He quickly headed back and traced Tingxue’s footsteps to find her.","Isabella quickly chimed in, “Don’t worry, big brother Zu. The communicators are able to locate one another.”","She fiddled with the communicator, and a minimap appeared on screen. It indicated the locations of the other communicators. Two communicators were swiftly approaching them, whereas Tingxue’s remained still.","Zu An’s expression turned even more grim. He continuously used his continuous movements skill until he arrived at the location corresponding to Tingxue’s communicator.","It was a circular clearing surrounded by a wall made up of skerries. There was no way out of here aside from the path he'd entered through. Tingxue’s communicator was lying in front of the wall.","“What happened?”","“Is Miss Tingxue all right?”","The other groups arrived just then.","Zu An ignored them and headed up to the skerry wall to examine the area. Meanwhile, Isabella filled the others in about the situation.","“How could she disappear without any warning?” A guest was perplexed.","“We didn’t hear anything.”","Yani walked up to Zu An and asked, “Did you find anything?”","Zu An shook his head. “There don’t seem to be any mechanisms here.” So, he drew his sword, intending to blast open the skerry wall in front of him.","Yani stepped forward. “Let me do it instead.”","Having witnessed Yani’s strength, the others had no qualms with letting her do the work.","Yani took a breath so deep her chest puffed up, then hurled a fist. The force behind her punch appeared to vacuum away all the air in the area. The crowd narrowed their eyes in fear, knowing they couldn’t have survived this punch if it was directed at them.","But something even more shocking happened—the skerry wall didn’t budge! Instead, Yani’s arm fractured with a crack, and her fist turned bloody.","Isabella yelped in horror. She reached into her bag and pulled out a few pills. “Big sister Yani, take this!”","“Thank you.” Yani took the pills. Her arm was soon as good as new. She turned to the crowd and explained, “The wall is imbued with a mysterious power of high stature. It’s not limited to just this wall, but all the skerries we passed by along the way.”","None of the guests were fools. Why would they observe the rules of a labyrinth if they could have just smashed their way out of it? They had tried smashing the skerries, but couldn’t break them.","Zu An frowned. He inspected the other wall surfaces, but he couldn’t gather any clues from them.","Yani walked over and said, “Don’t worry too much. Miss Tingxue is strong. I’m sure she can protect herself.”","The other guests voiced their agreement. Even Isabella and Alfred nodded as well.","Tingxue’s feat of slashing open the nebula had been too astonishing. Even the strongest experts they had met were, at most, on par with her. It was unlikely anyone could corner her, unless she encountered a universal deity.","Zu An finally calmed down. Yes, Tingxue isn’t Yan Xuehen. She’s an expert, even in the vast Myriad Worlds. She might be in a quandary right now, but that doesn’t mean she’s in danger. She’s a Nebula envoy. If it comes to that, she can just open the nebula and leave.","“We found something, and we believe it will lead us to the exit,” the guest with the golden compass said with a smile. “The way in reveals the way out. When we stepped back and took a second look at the skerries, we noticed their arrangement utilizes 256-bit encryption. We have ideas on how to decrypt it, but we rushed here after hearing your shouts. With more time, I’m sure we can find the way out.”"]},{"number":2799,"title":"Chapter 2799: Chapter 2751: Waking Up","paragraphs":["Since Tingxue was nowhere to be found, the crowd decided to leave the labyrinth first before deciding their next step.","Zu An had no choice but to go with them. He left marks along the way, hoping Tingxue could follow his lead and escape once she was freed from her quandary.","Soon, the crowd returned to where they had been. There, they noticed some changes in the skerries compared to before.","One guest lifted his golden compass, and the runes on its surface began to change endlessly. He said, “Such an encryption method might stump most civilizations, but it isn’t a problem for me.”","He had been injured on the frigate, but thanks to Isabella’s pills, he'd recovered swiftly. I embarrassed myself in front of the big miss once. This is my chance to restore my reputation!","His hands swiftly rearranged the floating golden runes so quickly that they left afterimages. The surrounding skerries, influenced by his movements, began moving around. As they shuffled around, a path slowly emerged; afterward, the skerries vanished.","“You’re amazing!” Isabella exclaimed in amazement.","“It’s my honor to receive Miss Isabella’s admiration.” The guest performed a knight’s bow. Fearing Isabella had forgotten him, he introduced himself once more. “It’s all thanks to Miss Isabella’s medicine. If not for that, I, Divine Calculator, wouldn’t have recovered that quickly otherwise.”","Isabella replied with a sweet smile, “We’re in the same boat now. It’s only right for us to help each other out.”","Disappointment flickered through Divine Calculator’s eyes. He looked at how intimately Isabella was holding Zu An’s arm. She’s treating me no differently from other guests. She favors him more right now because he hogged the limelight earlier, but if I prove myself, I should catch her eye as well.","Thus, Divine Calculator said, “I’ll lead the way. This is my field of specialty.” Without waiting for Isabella’s answer, he strutted forth.","Isabella turned to Zu An and sighed. She had encountered far too many of these situations.","The others wouldn’t object to someone scouting the path for them, though.","Of course, Divine Calculator wasn't a reckless person. He understood the dangers of leading the way, so he fiddled with his compass and scanned the path forward with rays of golden light. He turned back to smile at Isabella. “Big miss, I am known for my prophetic ability. The compass will warn me if there are any dangers ahead.”","Zu An frowned. He suddenly felt uneasy, but Divine Calculator wasn’t reacting in the slightest. Am I overthinking things?","Just then, Divine Calculator suddenly stopped for no reason. He turned around in confusion. “Huh? Is there no more road...”","He looked forward and saw there was still a road ahead. Confusion first flickered through his eyes, then his pupils widened in horror. “What the hell! Why did I stop moving?”","The others were hurriedly stopped in horror. “What’s wrong?”","Divine Calculator was flailing his limbs around even though there was nothing there.","“I feel something gluing...” Before Divine Calculator could finish speaking, he was suddenly dragged into the sky.","The crowd hurriedly looked up, but the sky above them was pitch-black. They couldn’t see anything at all.","“Be careful!” Yani shouted.","The others also got into battle stances.","The next second, Divine Calculator reappeared before the crowd.","“What the hell, Divine Calculator?!” a guest roared.","No one among the crowd had sensed anything amiss earlier, and Divine Calculator had returned safely by himself. It felt as if he was playing a prank on them.","Divine Calculator began walking toward the guest.","“What are you doing? Don’t come here!” the guest shouted in fright.","There was something weird in the way Divine Calculator walked. It felt unnerving.","Zu An said, “Be careful. He’s dead.” As the master of the Netherworld, he was particularly attuned to death.","“What?”","The crowd was startled, as Divine Calculator looked no different from before, and he was still moving normally.","Just then, Divine Calculator revealed an eerie smile and lurched at the guest.","Luckily, the guest had prepared himself after hearing Zu An’s warning, and knocked Divine Calculator back with a stick.","But while Divine Calculator was flying backward, he suddenly defied physics and lurched forward once more. His head bent toward his back and his limbs curved unnaturally as he charged the guest at a shocking speed.","Pah!","Yani bashed her fist into Divine Calculator, causing his body to be smashed into many bits.","But the shattered fragments suddenly stitched back together into his ragged form. Despite Divine Calculator's unseemly condition, he relentlessly charged at the guest who had berated him.","The sight left the crowd with goosebumps. Isabella even shrieked in horror.","“Be careful!” Alfred shouted as he shoved Isabella aside.","The next second, however, Alfred disappeared as well.","“Uncle Alfred!” Isabella shouted in horror.","“There’s something above us!” Zu An warned the others with a shout.","Unfortunately, their divine sense was unable to perceive what was above them.","Isabella hurriedly reached into her bag and pulled out something resembling a torchlight. She flicked it on, and a brilliant light illuminated the area.","The crowd finally saw what was above them. It was a colorful spider that spanned the size of a football field! The area was covered in transparent spiderwebs that, for some reason, could be seen clearly under Isabella’s light.","Thus, they finally understood why Divine Calculator was behaving in such a bizarre manner. Those transparent threads were controlling him!","The crowd saw Alfred with swollen muscles like the Hulk, looking nothing like the sickly old man he was a second ago. He was fighting desperately to prevent the threads from wrapping around him, but despite his best efforts, he could only slow the process. He was unable to save himself.","Isabella quickly reached into her bag, pulled out a pistol, and fired at the spiderweb.","The pistol was small, but the bullet it fired emanated a phoenix’s cry as a gigantic fiery bird lurched at the spider. The webs it touched along the way melted.","The other guests were stunned. The sheer power of the pistol was comparable to the forbidden fire spells of magic worlds.","“DON’T!” Yani shouted, but it was too late.","Pah!","The fiery bird crashed into the spider, raising a fiery inferno. But it was swiftly extinguished without leaving the slightest singe on the spider’s fur.","The spider opened dozens of eyes all along its body, and terrifying pressure crashed down from above.","Everyone shuddered in fear. It felt as if a universal deity had descended before them."]},{"number":2800,"title":"Chapter 2800: Chapter 2752: Finding a Way out of Danger","paragraphs":["When they saw the spider above them, the crowd was initially startled, but they weren’t too frightened. The guests who had joined this expedition were experts from the Myriad Worlds, wielding skills surpassing their peers. They had encountered all kinds of monsters before.","It was creepy to see Divine Calculator being controlled by the spiderwebs, but it wasn't beyond what they had already seen before. Besides, the spider had caught Divine Calculator off guard, so it wasn't too surprising for its ambush to have succeeded.","It was only when Isabella fired that bullet at the spider that the crowd realized they had underestimated their enemy. It turned out that the spider had been asleep, and it had killed Divine Calculator out of sheer instinct.","Now that it was awake, the pressure it emanated was cataclysmic.","These guests would still consider putting up a fight against the ex-Death Envoy Alati, but they couldn’t muster the courage to fight this spider. Just looking at it made their souls tremble. Thus, those who remained turned tail and fled. No matter how powerful the Universal Conglomerate and the Acadias were, those groups couldn’t be more important than their lives.","Their abrupt movements alarmed the spider, however. They were quickly bound by threads, and the more they struggled, the tighter the threads became. They screamed in horror, “Save me!”","But no one had the spare capacity to save anyone right now.","Zu An was desperately trying to avoid the transparent threads flying around. If not for the predictions from the Book, he would have been caught by spider threads by now.","Isabella wanted to pull out other weapons from her bag, but the spider above had already recognized her as the one who had fired at it earlier. Its chelicerae[1] fell down upon her from the sky. In that instant, she looked like an ant facing a giant’s fist. She froze in place, gripped by extreme fear that rendered her incapable of reacting.","Zu An used the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra to pull her over to his side, but the chelicerae followed her as if they had already locked onto her. At this moment, he understood why Isabella had stopped moving earlier. It felt as if the entire world was crushing him, sealing off his vitality, stamina, blood, and heartbeat. The only thing that could function was his mind.","But such a state would only plunge one further into despair.","Just then, Yani hurled her fist at the chelicerae with a roar. It was a fist that could tear even space, but the chelicerae only shook a little.","Fortunately, this disturbance was enough for Zu An to regain his mobility. He quickly retreated with Isabella via instantaneous movement.","Yani hurled her fist once more to strike the spider directly, but her arm got caught in the transparent webs instead. She was temporarily stuck in place, during which the spider wrapped her limbs with more spider threads. Soon, she couldn’t budge anymore.","“Brother, please escape with our big miss!” Alfred struggled with all his might, but he couldn’t break free of his restraints. He was wrapped in a thick cocoon and shouted his final words before being fully sealed.","The other guests were already wrapped so tightly that they couldn’t let out any noise.","“Uncle Alfred!” Tears streamed down Isabella’s face. She'd thought that given their strength and the treasures they had on hand, this trip would just be another interesting experience. She hadn't thought they would encounter such a powerful monster that would cost Alfred his life.","Zu An grabbed her hand and fled. Isabella exclaimed, “Big sister Yani is still there...”","Zu An turned around and saw Yani struggling in the spiderweb. “We can’t save her now. If we don’t run now, all of us will die.”","Isabella bit her lip, knowing they couldn’t do aynthing to save the others. She whipped out a few items from her bag to construct layers of barriers against the spider.","But the spider’s chelicerae continued to reach directly toward her. Isabella’s array of defensive artifacts were top-notch, but the chelicerae pierced through them like hot knife slicing through butter.","Isabella felt the same despair she'd experienced earlier. Her body froze in place. She desperately wanted to escape but was unable to do so. She couldn’t even close her eyes out of fear.","However, Zu An was still able to move.","A beautiful river reflecting countless civilizations suddenly appeared behind them, standing in the way of the chelicerae thrusting toward them. The chelicerae struck the river, but were unable to pierce through it. A light, fleeting hum echoed—it didn’t sound human.","Zu An made use of this opportunity to escape with Isabella.","The spider was infuriated, but its chelicerae were stuck in that bizarre river. It could only roar angrily. Just then, however, the hair on its chelicerae fell onto the ground and transformed into countless smaller spiders that frenziedly chased the duo.","“Big brother Zu, what’s that ability? How did you stop that monster?” Isabella was awed.","Zu An was surprised as well. That had been the Annals of History, one of the two abilities he had received from Deity of Memory Meng not too long ago. It allowed him to use the river of history to block an enemy’s fatal attack. If not for that, they would have been in danger.","He was about to answer that question when Isabella suddenly yelped. Her torchlight had revealed countless small spiders chasing after them. Thus, Zu An quickly lifted Isabella up and escaped via Rainbow Morph.","But somehow, the small spiders persistently followed him no matter how he flitted around. He couldn’t shake them off no matter how he tried.","Just then, a voice echoed from the shadows, “Head in my direction!”","Hearing a feminine voice in an empty, dark space sent shivers down Isabella’s spine. Is it a ghost? But on second thought, the spider was far more terrifying than any ghost.","Even so, Zu An didn’t hesitate to run toward the voice.","An arm suddenly emerged from the darkness and dragged him in. The shadows rippled as if they were passing through a spatial passageway. After they passed through, the ripples vanished, and the shadow melded into the surrounding darkness.","Dozens of spiders scuttled over and combed the surroundings, but they could no longer sense their target’s aura.","Meanwhile, Zu An and Isabella found themselves in a cave that had a high ceiling over fifty meters high. They sensed a presence with them and switched on the torchlight.","The third party stared intently at Isabella and Zu An’s linked arms and remarked, “You’re a heartless man. It hasn’t even been that long, but you've already gotten together with another woman.”","Isabella hurriedly retracted her hand, and her face flushed red.","Zu An stared at the other party and huffed, “I need an explanation.”","The person before him was none other than Firework.","—","Translator Thought:","The Book (The Book of Prophecies) existed in history, too.","Lu Sheng was an official tasked by Qin Shihuang (Ying Zheng) to find the elixir of immortality, but he failed. So, he created the Book of Prophecies and presented it to Qin Shihuang, saying that it had come from beyond the seas and possessed mystical powers.","1. The mouthparts of a spider. ☜"]}]);
